{"number": 153, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S4.3i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [152], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests"], "how_to": "Saving and loading a scene write and read its kit file (the S4.3 brief; 001 §P: every user step is a semantic message, and the same messages back the buttons; .spec-md §4 'UI'). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `sceneName : ControlCaption` (the scene name being typed, raw text until `SceneName.tryCreate` validates it at save, as the draft's label is) and `savedScenes : Scene.SceneName list` (the kit's scenes, by name), each with a one-line doc. `initWith` sets them to `ControlCaption \"\"` and `[]`; `loadKit` (step 152) sets `savedScenes` to `opened.scenes`. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each with a one-line doc: `SceneSetName of ControlCaption` (edit the name), `SceneSave` (save the table as a scene of that name in the kit) and `SceneLoad of Scene.SceneName` (put the kit's scene of that name on the table). (3) Arms. `SceneSetName name` sets `sceneName`. `SceneSave`: `SceneName.tryCreate model.sceneName.value` (`Scene.fs:SceneName`); a blank name sets `kitStatus` to `Save failed — <reason>` and writes nothing. Otherwise `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordScene name model.captureScene` (step 149; `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:captureScene`): on `Ok` `savedScenes` holds the name once, in ordinal order, and `kitStatus` is `Saved scene '<name>'.`; on `Error e` nothing else changes and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `SceneLoad name`: `model.kit.proxy.readScene name` (step 148); `Ok scene` is `restoreScene scene model` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:restoreScene`) with `kitStatus` `Loaded scene '<name>'.`; `Error e` leaves the table alone and sets `kitStatus` to `Load failed — <e.describe>`. (4) The view: `collectionBuilderView` shows first, under the heading `Scene:`, one horizontal row: the name field, a `TextBox` carrying `ConstructorUiId.sceneNameField` that dispatches `SceneSetName` on Enter and on lost focus (the old collection name field's commit), and the `workbenchButton` `Save scene` (`ConstructorUiId.saveSceneButton`, dispatching `SceneSave`); then the `kitStatus` line (step 152); then, when `savedScenes` is not empty, `Saved scenes:` and a `WrapPanel` named `ConstructorUiId.savedScenes` holding one `workbenchButton` per name (`ConstructorUiId.savedScene name`, captioned by the name, dispatching `SceneLoad name`); then the inverse `Data files:` section. It shows in both modes. (5) Ids. `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, beside `kitStatus` (step 152), under one doc line naming the scene row: `sceneNameField` (`\"SceneNameField\"`), `saveSceneButton` (`\"SaveSceneButton\"`) and `savedScenes` (`\"SavedScenes\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, where `savedCollection` and the collection caption stood: `static member savedScene (name : Scene.SceneName) : ConstructorUiId` (`SavedScene_<name>`) and `type Scene.SceneName with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, each with a one-line doc. No other message, field or id is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SceneSaveLoadTests.fs`, `module SceneSaveLoadTests`, compiled directly after `InverseConstructorTests.fs` with no comment. Its model is `initMain ()` loaded through `loadKit (TestAppScope.openedKitIn (FolderName \"SceneSaveLoadTests\") m.catalogueImports)` (step 152), whose import seam holds the Built-in catalogue. `a saved scene is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table`: with a linear polarizer added (`AddElement Placement.LinearPolarizer`, pre-bound to its preset), `SceneSetName (ControlCaption \"Bench: A\")` then `SceneSave` makes `savedScenes` `[ Bench: A ]` and `kitStatus` `Saved scene 'Bench: A'.`; the kit folder holds `Bench_ A.setup-json` and the preset's snapshot under `library/`; after `RemoveSelected`, `SceneLoad` of that name puts back the saved elements; and a model loaded from the same folder opened again (the first kit closed) lists `Bench: A`. `saving a scene with a blank name reports a typed status and writes nothing`: `SceneSetName (ControlCaption \"   \")` then `SceneSave` sets `kitStatus` to a text starting `Save failed`, leaves `savedScenes` empty and writes no setup file. `loading a scene the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone`: `SceneLoad (SceneName \"nowhere\")` sets `kitStatus` to a text starting `Load failed` and leaves `elements` as they were. `the scene row renders its name field, Save scene and the saved scenes` (trait `ui-smoke`): `mainView` over a model with one saved scene and the Experiments bay selected renders headless without throwing, holding `sceneNameField`, `saveSceneButton`, `savedScenes` and the scene's `savedScene` button.", "acceptance": "After scene save and load land, `SceneSave` MUST record the table as a setup file of the kit with its library snapshots and `SceneLoad` MUST restore a kit scene onto the table, each reporting a refusal in `kitStatus`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the scene row renders its name field, Save scene and the saved scenes`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a saved scene is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table`, `saving a scene with a blank name reports a typed status and writes nothing`, `loading a scene the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "sui