{"number": 262, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S82h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [261], "how_to": "The setup row saves the active setup and shows which setup the table draws (the S8.2 brief: 'the constructor's scene save / load becomes setup save / load'; 'The constructor model keeps the active setup and writes it through KitProxy'; 'editing a setup that an experiment uses mints the next revision'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `SaveSetup`, with a one-line doc: write the table over the active setup. (b) Its arm is refused by the read-only guard of step 185 like `CreateSetup`. With `activeSetupOpt = None` it writes nothing and sets `kitStatus` to `No setup is active: create one first.`. With `Some active`, the revised setup is `active.revisedWith (model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.recordedWith model.kitItems)) (active.pinFor model.experimentCollection.experiments)` (steps 256, 258 and 261): when it equals `active` nothing is written and `kitStatus` is `Setup '<name>' is unchanged.`; otherwise it is recorded through `recordSetup` (step 260): on `Ok`, `kitSetups` holds it in place of its name's, `activeSetupOpt` is `Some` it and `kitStatus` is `Saved setup '<name>', revision <n>.`; on `Error e` nothing else changes and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. (c) The view: the setup row (step 260) shows first, in a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.activeSetupText`, `Active setup: <name>, revision <n>` or, with none, `The table is not a setup of the kit yet.`; after `Create setup`, the `workbenchButton` `Save setup` (`ConstructorUiId.saveSetupButton`, dispatching `SaveSetup`), withheld (`availableWorkbenchButton`, step 185) when no setup is active or the kit is open read-only. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, beside step 260's setup-row ids, each with a one-line doc: `activeSetupText` (`\"ActiveSetupText\"`) and `saveSetupButton` (`\"SaveSetupButton\"`). No other message, field or id is added. Tests. `SetupModelTests` (step 260): `SaveSetup writes the active setup in place until an experiment references its revision, then mints the next`: after `CreateSetup` of `Bench` and the polarizer turned (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 30.0)`), `SaveSetup` leaves `Bench` at revision 1 holding the turned slots; after `ExpChooseElement` of the polarizer and an `ExpCommit` over it (the table unchanged, so `Bench` stays at revision 1) and the polarizer turned again, `SaveSetup` gives `Bench` revision 2 with revision 1 in its history, the experiment still referencing revision 1, and `kitStatus` `Saved setup 'Bench', revision 2.`. `SaveSetup with no active setup, or over an unchanged table, writes nothing and says why`: with no active setup `SaveSetup` writes no setup file and sets `No setup is active: create one first.`; over an unchanged table it rewrites nothing (the file's bytes are unchanged) and sets `Setup 'Bench' is unchanged.`. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 185): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `SaveSetup` after a setup is active, with the same assertions. `SetupSaveLoadTests` (step 260): `the setup row renders its name field, Create setup and the saved setups` (trait `ui-smoke`) becomes `the setup row renders the active setup, its name field, Create setup, Save setup and the saved setups`, also holding `activeSetupText` and `saveSetupButton`; and `Save setup over a table an experiment uses keeps the earlier revision in the setup's kit file`: through the setup row's buttons and the Experiments bay's commit, a setup created, committed over and then saved changed holds both revisions in its `.setup-json`, read back through `readSetups`. `KitWindowTests` (step 185): `a read-only window withholds every write control` also finds no `saveSetupButton`.", "acceptance": "After Save setup lands, `SaveSetup` MUST write the table over the active setup, in place until an experiment references its revision and as the next revision after, and refuse to write with no active setup, over an unchanged table or under a read-only kit, the setup row showing the active setup; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SaveSetup writes the active setup in place until an experiment references its revision, then mints the next`, `SaveSetup with no active setup, or over an unchanged table, writes nothing and says why` and `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the setup row renders the active setup, its name field, Create setup, Save setup and the saved setups`; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `Save setup over a table an experiment uses keeps the earlier revision in the setup's kit file` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupSaveLoadTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.SaveSetup writes the active setup in place until an experiment references its revision, then mints the next", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.SaveSetup with no active setup, or over an unchanged table, writes nothing and says why", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests.the setup row renders its name field, Create setup and the saved setups", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupSaveLoadTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests.the setup row renders the active setup, its name field, Create setup, Save setup and the saved setups", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests.Save setup over a table an experiment uses keeps the earlier revision in the setup's kit file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupSaveLoadTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SaveSetup", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.activeSetupText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.saveSetupButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SAVE-SETUP"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number": 263, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S82i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [262], "how_to": "Putting a kit item into a slot of the table, as a semantic message (001 §P `AssignSlot`; 001 §J 'each holding an item or nothing'; the S8.2 brief: 'Placing an element binds a slot … Messages CreateSetup, AssignSlot and SwapSlot are pure updates with tests'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) On the model extension holding `itemModelCaption` (step 238): `member model.tryItemModelChoice (item : Item) : ItemModelChoice option`, the model as the window's stores resolve it: a `PresetInstance id` whose `model.library.tryGetEntry id` answers a `SourceItem` or a `PolarizerItem` is its `SourcePresetChoice` or `PolarizerPresetChoice`; a `SampleInstance v` whose `model.samples.resolveVersion v` answers a sample is `StackSampleChoice (v, sample)`; an `ItemModelVersionInstance v` whose `model.itemModels.resolveItemModelVersion v` answers a version is its `LibraryModelChoice` (step 223); anything else, `None` or an error, is `None`. `itemModelCaption` becomes the resolved choice's `caption` (step 238) or `(model not in the library)`, its three store reads replaced by this one resolution, so its texts are unchanged. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `AssignSlot of Library.ElementId * ItemId option`, with a one-line doc: put a kit item, or nothing, into that slot of the table. (3) Its arm writes nothing, so a read-only kit takes it too. A slot id the table lacks sets `kitStatus` to `Not assigned — <describe>` of `UnknownSetupSlotErr` naming it. `None` makes the slot `withoutItem` (step 258). `Some id` takes the item of that id in `kitItems` (else `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the id) and its `tryItemModelChoice` (else `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the item's label and that its model is not in the library), and the slot becomes `slot.withItem item choice` (step 258); a refusal sets `kitStatus` to `Not assigned — <e.describe>` and changes nothing else; on success the slot is replaced in `elements` and `kitStatus` is `None`. The setup records the slot at the next CreateSetup, SaveSetup or commit (steps 260-262). No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (step 260), whose kit holds items added through `AddItem` (step 236): `LP1` (the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` preset, `FixedMounting`), `QZ` (the glass plate at version 1), `Laser` (the HeNe preset) and `LPd` (that polarizer preset, `DialMounted DialNegative`, its `dialZero` set to 10° through `SetParameterState`, step 237). `AssignSlot puts a kit item into a table slot bound to its library entry, and AssignSlot of nothing empties it`: with a linear polarizer and a sample added, `AssignSlot (polarizer, Some LP1)` holds `ItemInSlot (LP1, PlacementTurn)` bound to the preset, `AssignSlot (sample, Some QZ)` binds the glass plate with its supported emission, and `AssignSlot (polarizer, None)` holds `EmptySlotContent` with the binding kept; no kit file changes. `AssignSlot of an item that does not fit the slot, that the kit lacks, or whose model the library lacks is told and changes nothing` : `Laser` into the polarizer slot sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not assigned` and naming `Laser`; an id the kit lacks, a slot id the table lacks, and a test-local item put in `kitItems` whose sample version the store lacks each do so too, and `elements` are unchanged. `a dial-mounted item is recorded with its reading and drawn through its current zero`: `LPd` assigned to the polarizer at R1 30° and `CreateSetup` of `Dial` write a `DialTurn` of −20° (10° − 30°); after `LPd`'s `dialZero` is set to 20°, `ActivateSetup (SetupName \"Dial\")` draws the polarizer at R1 40°, within 1e-12. `ItemsPanelModelTests` and `ItemsPanelTests`' facts on the model caption pass unchanged.", "acceptance": "After AssignSlot lands, `model.tryItemModelChoice` MUST resolve an item's model through the window's stores, `itemModelCaption` MUST read it, and `AssignSlot` MUST put a fitting kit item into a table slot bound to its library entry, empty a slot, and refuse an item that does not fit or is unavailable, writing nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `AssignSlot puts a kit item into a table slot bound to its library entry, and AssignSlot of nothing empties it`, `AssignSlot of an item that does not fit the slot, that the kit lacks, or whose model the library lacks is told and changes nothing` and `a dial-mounted item is recorded with its reading and drawn through its current zero`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ItemsPanelTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.AssignSlot puts a kit item into a table slot bound to its library entry, and AssignSlot of nothing empties it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-ASSIGN-SLOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.AssignSlot of an item that does not fit the slot, that the kit lacks, or whose model the library lacks is told and changes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-ASSIGN-SLOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a dial-mounted item is recorded with its reading and drawn through its current zero", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-ASSIGN-SLOT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.tryItemModelChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S82-ASSIGN-SLOT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.itemModelCaption", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S82-ASSIGN-SLOT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.AssignSlot", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S82-ASSIGN-SLOT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number": 264, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S82j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [263], "how_to": "The quick swap as a semantic message: another item into one slot is another setup, an existing one or a new one (001 §J 'Quick swap: … choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one'; 001 §P `SwapSlot`; the S8.2 brief). The slot bar that sends it is S8.4's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `SwapSlot of Library.ElementId * ItemId`, with a one-line doc: the table as the setup that holds this item in that slot. (2) Its arm resolves the slot, the item and its choice and refuses as `AssignSlot` does (step 263), with `Not swapped — <e.describe>`. The swapped slots are the table's with that slot `withItem item choice` (step 258), each `recordedWith model.kitItems`; the fresh name is `active.name.nextFreeAmong` the kit's setup names for `activeSetupOpt = Some active` and `SetupName.firstFree` of them otherwise (step 255). `Setup.swapTarget swapped model.kitSetups fresh` (step 258): `SwitchToHeldSetup s` is `ActivateSetup s.name`'s update (step 260) and writes nothing, so a read-only kit takes it; `CreateSwappedSetup s` is refused by the read-only guard of step 185, and otherwise recorded through `recordSetup` (step 260): on `Ok`, `kitSetups` holds it in name order, `activeSetupOpt` is `Some s`, `elements` are the swapped slots and `kitStatus` is `Created setup '<name>' by the swap.`; on `Error e` nothing else changes and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. The setup swapped from is never written. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 260, 263), whose kit holds `QZ` (the glass plate at version 1) and `QZ2` (the 2 mm plate at version 1) and a table of a source, a sample and the seeded detector: `SwapSlot switches to the kit's setup that holds the swapped content and writes nothing`: with `Bench A` created holding `QZ` and `Bench B` holding `QZ2` (each through `AssignSlot` then `CreateSetup`), and `Bench A` made active again (`ActivateSetup`), `SwapSlot (sample, QZ2)` makes `Bench B` active and the table its slots, and no kit file's bytes change. `SwapSlot to content no setup holds creates and activates a setup of the next free name, leaving the swapped-from setup as it was`: with only `Bench A` held and active, `SwapSlot (sample, QZ2)` writes `Bench A (2).setup-json` holding `QZ2` at revision 1, makes it active, and `Bench A`'s file is unchanged; from a table that is no setup yet, the swap creates `Setup 1`. `a kit opened read-only switches setups by a swap but creates none`: over the folder reopened read-only, the swap to `Bench B` switches, and the swap to new content sets `kitStatus` to `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.` and leaves the table, `kitSetups` and every file as they were.", "acceptance": "After SwapSlot lands, `SwapSlot` MUST switch to the kit's setup holding the swapped content without writing, and otherwise create, record and activate a setup of the next free name, never writing the setup swapped from and creating nothing under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SwapSlot switches to the kit's setup that holds the swapped content and writes nothing`, `SwapSlot to content no setup holds creates and activates a setup of the next free name, leaving the swapped-from setup as it was` and `a kit opened read-only switches setups by a swap but creates none`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.SwapSlot switches to the kit's setup that holds the swapped content and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SWAP-SLOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.SwapSlot to content no setup holds creates and activates a setup of the next free name, leaving the swapped-from setup as it was", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SWAP-SLOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a kit opened read-only switches setups by a swap but creates none", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SWAP-SLOT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SwapSlot", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SWAP-SLOT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number": 265, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S82k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [264], "how_to": "The run law reads the setup's slots: a slot holding an item is evaluated through that item's model and its own parameters (the S8.2 brief: 'S8.1's run law reads the setup's slots in light order'; 001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; the S8.1 mapper's request: Prep and Analyzer slots become `ElementStep`s and Object slots `ObjectStep`s through `ItemModelChoice.boundWith` / `BoundOpticalElement.muellerAt` at the slot's R1, its drawn incidence and its path branch). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `chartForRun` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun`, as step 252 left it): a path step's element whose `content` is `ItemInSlot (id, _)` is built from the item of that id in `kitItems`, its `tryItemModelChoice` (step 263) and `choice.boundWith model.materials (ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters)` (steps 245, 251), bound once per path step, and evaluated by `muellerAt` at each point exactly as step 252 evaluates a bound preset or sample: `{ rotation = its R1, or the swept x when its R1 is varied; incidence = its drawn incidence, or the swept x under VaryR2; branch = the path step's branch }` and the point's wavelength. It is an `ObjectStep` for a `Sample` slot and an `ElementStep` for any other. Its R1 is the drawn one, which a dial reading set (step 258's `drawnWith`). An evaluation error shows step 252's failure chart, `The run cannot be evaluated` with the error's `describe`, `SampleMaterialErr` keeping its own title; an item the kit lacks, or whose model does not resolve, shows that chart with the `describe` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming it (step 255). A slot of `EmptySlotContent` is built from its library binding exactly as step 252 builds it. (2) `model.objectIds` (step 254) answers the `Sample` slots that hold an item or are bound to a library sample, in table order, so a sample item is an object of the capture rule. (3) `chartForRun`'s no-analyzer check (`noPolarizerOnPath`) counts a polarizer slot that holds an item as a polarizer, and its 'nothing bound to the varied element' check passes a varied slot that holds an item. Each doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. Nothing else changes: with no item in any slot every chart is step 252's, so `FsxAcceptanceTests` and the chart classes run as they are. Tests, in `ExperimentControlsTests` (step 252), each over `initMain ()` with items added through `AddItem` (step 236) and put in slots through `AssignSlot` (step 263), at 600 nm with the seeded intensity detector: `a slot's item is run through its own parameters: a real polarizer item's leakage passes crossed light`: a linear polarizer at R1 0° bound to its preset in front of a second linear polarizer holding a real-LP item (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`, `ExtinctionRatioLeakage`) whose `extinctionRatio` is set to 0.01 (`SetParameterState`, step 237), the second varied over R1 0 … 180° in 5 points: each S₀ equals that of the item's `BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm` at the point's rotation applied to `Propagation.inputStokes IdealLinear (0°)` within 1e-12, and at 90° it is above 1e-4 while the same table with the preset in place of the item reads below 1e-12. `a sample item is solved at its own thickness, as the item evaluator solves it`: a sample holding a glass-plate item (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1) whose `substrate.thickness` is set to 2e-3 m, varied over R2 0 … 60° in 7 points with capture T: each S₀ equals that of `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample` over the item's values (step 249) on `BranchTransmitted` at the point's incidence, spin 0, applied to `Propagation.unpolarizedStokes`, within 1e-12. `a dial-mounted item is run at the angle its reading draws`: behind a first linear polarizer bound to its preset, a second polarizer at R1 30° holding a `DialMounted DialNegative` item of the linear-polarizer preset whose `dialZero` is 10° (so its reading is −20°, step 258) is recorded by `CreateSetup`; the item's `dialZero` is then set to 20° and the setup activated (`ActivateSetup`, step 260), which draws the second polarizer at R1 40°; the chart of a sweep of the first polarizer over R1 0 … 90° in 4 points equals, within 1e-12, that of a table whose second polarizer is the bare preset at R1 40°.", "acceptance": "After the run law reads the slots' items, `chartForRun` MUST evaluate a slot holding an item through the item's model and parameters at its drawn orientation, as an object for a sample slot, `model.objectIds` MUST count sample items, and every chart with no item MUST be unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a slot's item is run through its own parameters: a real polarizer item's leakage passes crossed light`, `a sample item is solved at its own thickness, as the item evaluator solves it` and `a dial-mounted item is run at the angle its reading draws`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a slot's item is run through its own parameters: a real polarizer item's leakage passes crossed light", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-RUN-SLOT-ITEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a sample item is solved at its own thickness, as the item evaluator solves it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-RUN-SLOT-ITEMS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a dial-mounted item is run at the angle its reading draws", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-RUN-SLOT-ITEMS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S82-RUN-SLOT-ITEMS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number": 266, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S82l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [265], "how_to": "The source slot's item is the run's source: it emits its own Stokes state times its intensity scale (001 §N 'The source is real: a source item with a Stokes state and an intensity scale'; the S8.1 mapper's request: the source slot's item emits through `emissionWith (ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters)`; step 252 (c): every chart reads the default parameter set until S8.2's source slot gives a source item's own values). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) On the model extension holding `tryItemModelChoice` (step 263): `member model.runEmission : Result<SourceEmission, ControlCaption>`, the error being the text the failure chart shows. For the first `LightSource` slot of the table holding an item whose `tryItemModelChoice` resolves, it is `choice.emissionWith (ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters)` (step 246), an `ItemEvaluationError` answering its `describe`; for such a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve, the `describe` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming it (step 255); and otherwise `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)`, step 252's default. (2) `chartForRun` reads every point with `model.runEmission` where it read the default emission, an `Error text` showing step 252's `The run cannot be evaluated` chart with that text. The wavelength stays the bound preset's (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:boundSource`), because a source item's slot is bound to its preset (step 258). Each doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. With no source item every chart is step 252's. Tests, in `ExperimentControlsTests`, over `initMain ()` whose source slot holds a `Laser` item of the HeNe preset (`AddItem`, `AssignSlot`), with one linear polarizer bound to its preset between it and the seeded intensity detector, varied over R1 0 … 180° in 7 points: `a source item emits its own polarization through the run`: with `degreeOfPolarization` 1 and `azimuth` 30° (`SetParameterState`, step 237) each S₀ is 1 + cos(2(x − 30°)) within 1e-12 (the polarizer is the intensity reference, r = 2, step 252), and with the item's defaults each S₀ is 1, as the default source reads. `a source item whose parameters the run cannot evaluate shows that the run cannot be evaluated`: with `degreeOfPolarization` set to 1.5 the chart's title is `The run cannot be evaluated` and its description names `degreeOfPolarization` (`ParameterOutOfRangeErr`, step 245).", "acceptance": "After the source slot emits, `model.runEmission` MUST be the source item's emission through `emissionWith` over its own parameters, the default parameter set without one, and `chartForRun` MUST read with it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a source item emits its own polarization through the run` and `a source item whose parameters the run cannot evaluate shows that the run cannot be evaluated`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a source item emits its own polarization through the run", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SOURCE-SLOT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a source item whose parameters the run cannot evaluate shows that the run cannot be evaluated", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S82-SOURCE-SLOT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.runEmission", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S82-SOURCE-SLOT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S82-SOURCE-SLOT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.2 -- Setups as slots"}
{"number": 267, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [266], "how_to": "The naming template becomes a field of the kit file, stored as the text the lab writes (001 §J 'Naming template: each kit carries one (e.g. `{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}`)'; 001 §A 'the kit: id, name, author, notes, naming template, import profiles, sendExclude'; step 122: 'S8.3 adds the naming template'). The grammar, the reading and the writing are steps 268-271's; this step adds the stored shape and its default. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, directly before `KitFile` (step 122): `NamingTemplate of string` with `.value`, the kit's naming template as its text, and `static member standard : NamingTemplate`, which is `NamingTemplate \"{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}\"`: 001 §J's template, the one place that text is written, every new kit's template and the grammar of the reference pipeline's labels (step 270). It is not validated here: the grammar is `NamingTemplates.fs`'s (step 268), and every use of a template answers a `Result`. (2) `KitFile` gains `namingTemplate : NamingTemplate` after `sendExclude`, and `KitFile.create` sets it to `NamingTemplate.standard`, so `KitFolder.namedKitFile` (step 145) and `scratchKit` (step 150), which call `create`, take it with no change. The shared serializer options unwrap a single-case union (`ProjectJson.fs:142`, `WithUnionUnwrapSingleCaseUnions`, moved into `CanonicalJson.fs` by step 21), so the template is written as a JSON string. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json` (step 124): under `if` `schemaVersion` is 1, `namingTemplate` joins the required keys and the properties as a string, and `additionalProperties: false` stays. The schema version stays 1: kit files of the old shape exist only under test output folders (.spec-md §7: kit file shapes change in later parts and no migration is needed). No up-converter, default-on-read or other member is added. Tests. In `KitTests` (step 122): `a kit's naming template keeps its text, and a new kit takes the standard one`: `(NamingTemplate \"{obj1}\").value` is `{obj1}`, `NamingTemplate.standard.value` is `{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}`, and `KitFile.create` over step 122's id, name, author and instant holds `NamingTemplate.standard`. In `KitFileJsonTests` (step 124), whose kit file now also holds `namingTemplate = NamingTemplate \"{source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}-({obj1}#{phi1})-{analyzer:CPL2=CPL}\"`: `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text` lists the top-level keys `author`, `created`, `id`, `modified`, `name`, `namingTemplate`, `notes`, `schemaVersion` and `sendExclude` in that order and writes the template's text verbatim as the string value of `namingTemplate`; `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds` also refuses the text without `namingTemplate`, and with `namingTemplate` set to the number `7`, each with `SchemaValidationErr`. Every other kit-file fact passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the kit file gains its naming template, `NamingTemplate` MUST exist in `Kit.fs` with `NamingTemplate.standard` holding 001 §J's text, `KitFile` MUST carry `namingTemplate`, `KitFile.create` MUST set the standard template and `kit.schema.json` MUST require it as a string; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit's naming template keeps its text, and a new kit takes the standard one` and the changed `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text` and `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a kit's naming template keeps its text, and a new kit takes the standard one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-KIT-TEMPLATE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests.a kit file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S83-KIT-TEMPLATE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S83-KIT-TEMPLATE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.NamingTemplate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S83-KIT-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitFile", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S83-KIT-TEMPLATE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 268, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [267], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests"], "how_to": "The naming template's grammar as pure Domain: the pieces a template's text holds, and the refusal of a text that is none (001 §J 'Naming template … It names setups and experiments, and PARSES names back to match imported data'; .spec-md §5 'Setup, SetupName, slots, NamingTemplate'). The template speaks the polarimeter's words, as 001 §J's example and 001 §O's experiment matrix ('rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer') do: the source is the polarization source, S8.2's Prep slots (step 257), and the light is the light source, S8.2's Source slot; this is what makes 001's example name a setup whose Prep 1 holds `CPL1` `CPL-(…)-CPL`, as 001 §A's kit layout does. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs`: `module NamingTemplates` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `Setups.fs` (step 256), because a placeholder names a `SlotRole` (step 257): one `<Compile Include=\"NamingTemplates.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the kit's naming template, its grammar, and the names it writes and reads (spec 0050 S8.3). It opens `Kit` and `Setups`. (2) `NamePart of string` with `.value`: one piece of text a name holds (an item's name, the note, or the literal text between placeholders). (3) `NameAlias = { label : ItemLabel; part : NamePart }`: in its placeholder, the kit item of that label is written as `part` (001 §A: the items `CPL1` and `CPL2` of a kit whose setups are named `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`). (4) `PlaceholderNeed` = `RequiredPlaceholder` | `OptionalPlaceholder`. (5) `TemplatePlaceholder` = `SlotPlaceholder of SlotRole` | `AnglePlaceholder of SlotPosition` | `NotePlaceholder`. `member this.text : string` is the placeholder's word with its number: `light` (`SourceSlotRole`), `source<k>` (`PrepSlotRole k`), `obj<k>` (`ObjectSlotRole k`), `analyzer<k>` (`AnalyzerSlotRole k`), `detector<k>` (`DetectorSlotRole k`), `phi<k>` (the angle of Obj k) and `note`. `member this.need : PlaceholderNeed` is `OptionalPlaceholder` for a slot or angle of position 2 or more and for the note, and `RequiredPlaceholder` for `light` and for the first slot of each role and its angle. A placeholder is never stored apart from the template's text, so it carries no wire tag. (6) `TemplateValue = { placeholder : TemplatePlaceholder; aliases : NameAlias list }` and `TemplatePiece` = `LiteralPiece of NamePart` | `ValuePiece of TemplateValue`. (7) `NamingTemplateError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the template's text, the placeholder or the name: `TemplateSyntaxErr` (a brace without its partner, a word or number that names no placeholder, a malformed alias, or an alias on an angle or the note), `DuplicatePlaceholderErr` (one placeholder twice, `{source}` with `{source1}` included), `AdjacentPlaceholdersErr` (two placeholders with no text between them, which no name could tell apart), `DuplicateAliasErr` (one placeholder aliasing one label twice, ignoring case, or two labels as one part), `MissingNameValueErr` (a required placeholder holds nothing, steps 269 and 271), `NameMismatchErr` (a name the template does not fit, step 269) and `UnknownNameItemErr` (a part names no kit item, step 271); `member this.describe : string` renders them `the naming template is not valid: <reason>`, `the naming template names a placeholder twice: <reason>`, `the naming template has two placeholders with nothing between them: <reason>`, `the naming template aliases an item twice: <reason>`, `the name has nothing for a placeholder it needs: <reason>`, `the name does not fit the naming template: <reason>` and `the name names no item of the kit: <reason>`. (8) `type NamingTemplate with`: `member this.pieces : Result<TemplatePiece list, NamingTemplateError>` reads the text left to right. Text outside braces is a `LiteralPiece` (a run of it is one piece, and an empty one is never made). A `{` opens a placeholder that runs to the next `}` and holds a word (`light`, `source`, `obj`, `phi`, `analyzer`, `detector` or `note`), then an optional number (ASCII digits not starting with `0`; `light` and `note` take none; no number is 1, so `{source}` is Prep 1 and `{analyzer}` is Analyzer 1), then, after a `:`, a comma-separated list of `label=part` aliases, each label and part non-empty and holding none of `{`, `}`, `:`, `=` and `,`, the label made by `ItemLabel.tryCreate` (step 220), aliases being allowed on a slot placeholder only. A `}` outside a placeholder or a `{` inside one is `TemplateSyntaxErr`. It then refuses a placeholder that appears twice, two `ValuePiece`s with no `LiteralPiece` between them, and an alias list that repeats a label (its text ignoring case) or a part. `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<NamingTemplate, NamingTemplateError>` answers `NamingTemplate text` when its `pieces` answer `Ok`, and their error otherwise. The scanning is done by locals inside these members, so no module-level signature carries a primitive (ELEV003P, ELEV010P). No regular expression, cache or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs`, `module NamingTemplateTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. `the standard template is the lab's: the source, two objects at their angles, the analyzer and the note`: `NamingTemplate.standard.pieces` answers, in order, the values `SlotPlaceholder (PrepSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))`, then `ObjectSlotRole 1`, `AnglePlaceholder 1`, `ObjectSlotRole 2`, `AnglePlaceholder 2`, `AnalyzerSlotRole 1` and `NotePlaceholder`, none with an alias, with the literals `-(`, `#`, `-`, `#`, `)-` and `-` between them; Prep 1, Obj 1, its angle and Analyzer 1 are `RequiredPlaceholder`, and Obj 2, its angle and the note `OptionalPlaceholder`. `a placeholder without a number names the first slot of its role, and each role has its word`: the pieces of `{light}/{source2}/{obj3}/{phi3}/{analyzer}/{detector2}/{note}.csv` hold, between the literals `/` and ending with `.csv`, the placeholders `SourceSlotRole`, `PrepSlotRole 2`, `ObjectSlotRole 3`, `AnglePlaceholder 3`, `AnalyzerSlotRole 1`, `DetectorSlotRole 2` and `NotePlaceholder`, whose `text`s are `light`, `source2`, `obj3`, `phi3`, `analyzer1`, `detector2` and `note`. `an alias writes a kit item under another name in its placeholder`: `{source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}` holds `PrepSlotRole 1` with the aliases `CPL1` as `CPL` and `LP1` as `LP`, in that order. `a text that is no naming template is refused with its reason`: `{sauce}`, `{obj0}`, `{obj01}`, `{light1}`, `{obj1`, `obj1}`, `{ob{j1}`, `{phi1:A=B}`, `{note:A=B}`, `{source:CPL1}` and `{source:=CPL}` answer `TemplateSyntaxErr`; `{source}-{source1}` `DuplicatePlaceholderErr`; `{obj1}{phi1}` `AdjacentPlaceholdersErr`; `{source:CPL1=CPL,cpl1=C}` and `{source:A=CPL,B=CPL}` `DuplicateAliasErr`; `tryCreate` of each answers the same error, and `tryCreate` of the standard text answers `NamingTemplate.standard`. `every naming template error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it.", "acceptance": "After the grammar lands, `NamingTemplates.fs` MUST hold `NamePart`, `NameAlias`, `PlaceholderNeed`, `TemplatePlaceholder`, `TemplateValue`, `TemplatePiece` and `NamingTemplateError`, `NamingTemplate.pieces` MUST read 001 §J's template into its values and literals and `tryCreate` MUST refuse every malformed text with its typed error; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the standard template is the lab's: the source, two objects at their angles, the analyzer and the note`, `a placeholder without a number names the first slot of its role, and each role has its word`, `an alias writes a kit item under another name in its placeholder`, `a text that is no naming template is refused with its reason` and `every naming template error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.the standard template is the lab's: the source, two objects at their angles, the analyzer and the note", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.a placeholder without a number names the first slot of its role, and each role has its word", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.an alias writes a kit item under another name in its placeholder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.a text that is no naming template is refused with its reason", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.every naming template error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamePart", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NameAlias", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.PlaceholderNeed", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.TemplatePlaceholder", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.TemplateValue", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.TemplatePiece", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplateError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.pieces", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.tryCreate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-GRAMMAR"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 269, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [268], "how_to": "A name read through a template and written back, at the level of its text (001 §J 'It names setups and experiments, and PARSES names back to match imported data'; 'their cases become the template engine's first test cases': `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:parsed`) reads the lab's labels by `experimentRegex` and `objectRegex` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:experimentRegex`, `:objectRegex`), and step 270 re-points its callers here). In `NamingTemplates.fs`, after step 268's declarations; each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `NameText of string` with `.value`: a whole name as text, a setup's or an experiment's name or a label a lab file carries. (2) `SlotPart = { role : SlotRole; part : NamePart }`, `ObjectAngle = { position : SlotPosition; angle : Angle }` and `NameReading = { parts : SlotPart list; angles : ObjectAngle list; noteOpt : NamePart option }`, the values a name holds, each list in its template's order, with `member this.tryFindPart (role : SlotRole) : NamePart option` and `member this.tryFindAngle (position : SlotPosition) : Angle option`. (3) An angle is written as its degrees rounded to three decimals, in the invariant culture, with no exponent, no trailing zero and no sign on zero (`45`, `-22.5`, `0.333`, `0`); it is read as an optional `-`, ASCII digits and an optional `.` followed by ASCII digits, and becomes `Angle.degree` of that number (`Geometry.fs:degree`). (4) Each placeholder of a template owns the literal text directly before it, back to the placeholder before it; the literal after the last placeholder is the template's tail. The optional placeholders of one object, `{obj<k>}` and `{phi<k>}`, form one group, and every other optional placeholder is a group alone. (5) `type NamingTemplate with member this.writeName (reading : NameReading) : Result<NameText, NamingTemplateError>` writes, in the template's order, each placeholder's value after the text it owns: a `SlotPlaceholder` the reading's part of its role, an `AnglePlaceholder` the angle of its position, `NotePlaceholder` the note. An optional placeholder the reading lacks is left out with the text it owns; a required one answers `MissingNameValueErr` naming the placeholder's `text`. The tail ends the name. (6) `member this.readName (name : NameText) : Result<NameReading, NamingTemplateError>` tries the ways of leaving out the optional groups in one fixed order, binary counting over the groups in template order with the last group the lowest digit and a left-out group a one: every group kept comes first, and an earlier group is kept longest. One way reads the name left to right. Each kept placeholder's owned text must stand at the reading point. Its value runs from there to the first place, at least one character on, where the text that follows it in this way stands (the next kept placeholder's owned text, or the tail), or to the end of the name when that text is empty. A value is never empty, an angle's value must read as an angle, and after the last value the rest of the name must be the tail exactly. The first way that reads answers the reading; when none does, the answer is `NameMismatchErr` naming the name and the template. The scanning is done by locals inside the members (ELEV003P, ELEV010P). No regular expression, backtracking within a way, cache or other member is added. So the lab's labels read as `parsed` reads them: `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2` holds the analyzer `CPL` and the note `2`, because keeping the note is tried before leaving it out, and `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` keeps its sign, because a value runs at least one character before the next owned text. Tests, in `NamingTemplateTests` (step 268), over `NamingTemplate.standard` and each label as a `NameText`: `the lab's labels read into their source, objects, angles, analyzer and note`: `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL` reads the source part `CPL` (`PrepSlotRole 1`), the objects `QZ` and `LR` with the angles 90° and 90°, the analyzer part `CPL` and no note; `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL` the object `AIR` at 0° and no second object; `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2` the source `LP`, the analyzer `CPL` and the note `2`; `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR` the note `BR`; `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` the angle −45°; and `LP-(QZ#22.5)-LP` 22.5°; each angle equals `Angle.degree` of its number exactly. `a name that does not fit the template is refused naming it`: `Darkness`, `BullshitCheck`, `BullshitCheck-2`, `LP-(Darkness)-CPL2`, `CPL-(QZ#ab)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#90-LR)-CPL` and the empty name each answer `NameMismatchErr` whose reason holds the name. `writing a reading back gives the name it was read from`: for `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL`, `CPL-(QZ#0-LR#0)-LP-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR`, `LP-(LR#45)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` and `LP-(QZ#22.5)-LP`, `writeName` of the `readName` answers the same text. `a reading writes each value in its place and leaves out an optional one it lacks with the text it owns`: the test-local reading of the source `CPL`, the object `QZ` at 45° and the analyzer `CPL` writes `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`; with the note `2`, `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL-2`; with a second object `LR` at 45°, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`; an angle of 1/3° is written `0.333` and one of −0.0001° `0`; and the reading without the analyzer answers `MissingNameValueErr` naming `analyzer1`.", "acceptance": "After names are read and written, `NameText`, `SlotPart`, `ObjectAngle` and `NameReading` MUST exist in `NamingTemplates.fs`, `NamingTemplate.readName` MUST read the lab's labels as `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed` reads them and refuse a name the template does not fit, and `writeName` MUST write a reading back to the name it was read from; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the lab's labels read into their source, objects, angles, analyzer and note`, `a name that does not fit the template is refused naming it`, `writing a reading back gives the name it was read from` and `a reading writes each value in its place and leaves out an optional one it lacks with the text it owns`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.the lab's labels read into their source, objects, angles, analyzer and note", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.a name that does not fit the template is refused naming it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.writing a reading back gives the name it was read from", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.a reading writes each value in its place and leaves out an optional one it lacks with the text it owns", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NameText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.SlotPart", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.ObjectAngle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NameReading", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.writeName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.readName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-NAME-READING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 270, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [269], "how_to": "The reference pipeline reads its labels through the naming template, and the label regular expressions go (001 §J 'It replaces `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed` and its `experimentRegex`'; 001 §R; 001 §T 'From section 8: `git grep -n -F \"experimentRegex\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing', which this step makes true). `MuellerReconstructionTests`' numbers are unchanged. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: (1) Deleted: `experimentRegex` and `objectRegex` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:experimentRegex`, `:objectRegex`), the `MuellerExperimentLabel` extension holding `parsed` (`:parsed`), `ParsedExperiment` (`:ParsedExperiment`), `ParsedObject` (`:ParsedObject`) and `MuellerLabelToken` (`:MuellerLabelToken`), whose only readers are each other, `buildDesign` and `MuellerReconstructionTests` (the census names no other), with the doc and comment lines that describe them; and `open System.Text.RegularExpressions` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:3`), which nothing else reads. The file opens `Kit`, `Setups` and `NamingTemplates`. (2) `MuellerExperimentLabel` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerExperimentLabel`) gains `member this.nameText : NameText`, its text as a name (step 269); its doc says a label reads through `NamingTemplate.standard` (step 267). (3) After `MatrixKind` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixKind`), `type NameReading with`, the reference pipeline's reading of a label, moved from `ParsedExperiment` with its rules unchanged: `member this.family : Family` takes a part as the circular family when its text contains `CPL` (the reference `canonical_polarizer`), over the source part (`tryFindPart (PrepSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))`) and the analyzer part (`AnalyzerSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)`), an absent part being linear; `member this.objectRotation : Angle * MatrixKind` takes the objects as the reading's `ObjectSlotRole` parts that have an angle of their position, in position order: none is `Angle.zero, Air`; one is its angle and, by its text upper-cased (`ToUpperInvariant`), `Qz` for `QZ`, `Lr` for `LR` and `Air` otherwise; two or more are the first's angle and `QzLrProduct`; `member this.matrixKind : MatrixKind` and `member this.objectPhi : Angle` are its halves. (4) `buildDesign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:buildDesign`) keeps a row whose label `NamingTemplate.standard.readName r.experiment.nameText` reads with a `matrixKind` equal to `kind`, a label the template does not read being never kept, and otherwise filters as it does; its doc says so. Every science label of the lab's files reads (`CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`, …), so every design holds the same rows in the same order. The one reading that differs is a darkness label such as `CPL-(Darkness)-LP-2`, which `parsed` read as `Air` and the template does not read; no design selects `Air`. (5) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit`. Its fact `parseExperiment decodes CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:559`) becomes `the standard naming template reads CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL as the CPL-CPL family and the QZ LR product at phi 90, and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)`: the label is read by `NamingTemplate.standard.readName (MuellerExperimentLabel \"CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL\").nameText`, an `Error` failing the fact with its `describe`, and its assertions are unchanged. In the section 7.2 fact, `prepareRow` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:945`) takes `phi` as that reading's `objectPhi` in the same way. Tests. `NamingTemplateTests` (it opens `MuellerReconstruction`) gains `a lab label's reading names its reference family, matrix kind and object angle`: `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL` is `CplCpl`, `QzLrProduct` and 90°; `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL` `CplCpl`, `Air` and 0°; `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2` `LpCpl`, `Lr` and 90°; `CPL-(QZ#45)-LP-2` `CplLp`, `Qz` and 45°; and `LP-(QZ#0)-LP-2R` `LpLp`, `Qz` and 0°. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' facts pass with their numbers unchanged, `buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)` and the section 7.2 fact included.", "acceptance": "After the reference pipeline reads its labels through the template, `experimentRegex`, `objectRegex`, `MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed`, `ParsedExperiment`, `ParsedObject` and `MuellerLabelToken` MUST be gone and `git grep -n -F \"experimentRegex\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing, and `buildDesign` and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST read labels through `NamingTemplate.standard` and the moved `NameReading.family`, `matrixKind` and `objectPhi`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a lab label's reading names its reference family, matrix kind and object angle`, the count rising by 1; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its fact renamed to `the standard naming template reads CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL as the CPL-CPL family and the QZ LR product at phi 90, and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)` and its numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.a lab label's reading names its reference family, matrix kind and object angle", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.parseExperiment decodes CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "successor": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the standard naming template reads CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL as the CPL-CPL family and the QZ LR product at phi 90, and the +90 / -90 object rotation is inert (R(2 phi) invariance)", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.experimentRegex", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.objectRegex", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerExperimentLabel.parsed", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.ParsedExperiment", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.ParsedObject", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerLabelToken", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerExperimentLabel.nameText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.NameReading.family", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.NameReading.objectRotation", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.NameReading.matrixKind", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.NameReading.objectPhi", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S83-LABELS-THROUGH-TEMPLATE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 271, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [270], "how_to": "A setup's name written from its slots, and read back into its items and angles (001 §J 'It names setups and experiments, and PARSES names back to match imported data'; the S8.3 brief: it 'FORMATS a setup or experiment name from its slots and angles, and PARSES a name back into slot items and angles'). In `NamingTemplates.fs`, after step 269's declarations; each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `type ItemLabel with member this.namePart : NamePart`, a label as a name part (step 220), and `type NameText with member this.toSetupName : Result<SetupName, SetupError>`, `SetupName.tryCreate` of its text (step 255); no member converts back (ELEV006). (2) `SlotItem = { role : SlotRole; item : ItemId }`. (3) `type NamingTemplate with`: (a) `member this.nameReadingOf (slots : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) (noteOpt : NamePart option) : Result<NameReading, NamingTemplateError>` lays the slots out in light order (`SetupSlot.inLightOrder`, step 257) and takes, for each placeholder of `pieces` in order: for a `SlotPlaceholder role`, when the slot of that role holds an item of `items` (`SlotContent.itemOpt`, step 256), the part of the placeholder's first alias whose label equals the item's label ignoring case, or else the item's `label.namePart`; for an `AnglePlaceholder k`, when Obj k holds an item, its angle: the reading of a `DialTurn reading` slot, the placement's R1 for `PlacementTurn` (S8.2's rule, after 001 §I: experiments record raw dial readings); for `NotePlaceholder`, `noteOpt`. A role the layout has no slot of, a slot holding nothing and an item `items` lacks give no value. A template whose `pieces` fail answers their error. (b) `member this.itemsOf (reading : NameReading) (items : Item list) : Result<SlotItem list, NamingTemplateError>` answers, for each part in order, the item it names in its placeholder: when an alias of the placeholder has that part (ordinal), the item whose label equals the alias's label ignoring case; otherwise the item whose label equals the part ignoring case. A part naming no item answers `UnknownNameItemErr` naming the part and the placeholder's `text`. Item labels are unique by file stem ignoring case (step 223), so at most one item matches. (c) `member this.setupNameOf (slots : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) : Result<SetupName, NamingTemplateError>` is `writeName` of `nameReadingOf slots items None`, made a `SetupName` by `toSetupName`; a blank name answers `MissingNameValueErr` naming the template. (d) `member this.setupNameAmong (slots : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) (taken : SetupName list) (unnamed : SetupName) : SetupName` is `setupNameOf`'s name made free among `taken` by `nextFreeAmong` (step 255), or `unnamed` when the template cannot name the slots. It names every new setup the window and the grid make (steps 272 and 276), `unnamed` being S8.2's name for it. Setups and experiments keep their names when the template changes: a template names what is made after it is saved. No other member, cache or option is added. Tests, in `NamingTemplateTests`, over slots made as `SetupTests` makes them (steps 256-258): `src` (a `LightSource` at `RayModel.defaultSourcePoint`), `lpA` (a `LinearPolarizer` at x −0.3 m), `sampleA` (a `Sample` at x −0.1 m), `sampleB` (a `Sample` at x 0.1 m), `lpB` (a `LinearPolarizer` at x 0.3 m) and `det` (a `Detector` at `RayModel.defaultDetectorPoint`), all on the main beam; test-local items made through `ItemDraft` (step 223), each `FixedMounting` unless named: `Laser` (`PresetIds.heNe633`), `CPL1` and `CPL2` (`ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId`), `QZ`, `LR` and `QZd` (`ItemModelIds.blackBoxMuellerModelId`, `QZd` `DialMounted DialNegative` with its `dialZero` known at 10°), each put in its slot by `withItem` (step 258) after the slot's R1 is set; and the template `lab` = `tryCreate \"{source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer:CPL2=CPL,LP2=LP}-{note}\"`. `a setup's name is written from its slots in light order, its items under their aliases and its objects at their angles`: `src` holding `Laser`, `lpA` `CPL1`, `sampleA` `QZ` at R1 45°, `sampleB` `LR` at 45°, `lpB` `CPL2` and `det` nothing is named `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` by `lab` and `CPL1-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL2` by `NamingTemplate.standard`; with `sampleB` holding nothing, `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`; with `QZd` in `sampleA` at R1 30° (its reading −20°, step 258) and `sampleB` holding nothing, `CPL-(QZd#-20)-CPL`; and `nameReadingOf` with the note `2`, written by `writeName`, is `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`. `a name reads back into the items of its slots and their angles`: `itemsOf` of `lab`'s reading of `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` over those items is `CPL1` at `PrepSlotRole 1`, `QZ` at `ObjectSlotRole 1`, `LR` at `ObjectSlotRole 2` and `CPL2` at `AnalyzerSlotRole 1`, with the angles 45° and 45°; the object part `qz` reads as `QZ`; and `CPL-(XX#45)-CPL` answers `UnknownNameItemErr` naming `XX` and `obj1`. `writing a setup's name and reading it back gives its items and angles`: for each slot list of the first fact and for one with `sampleA` at 22.5°, the slots' items by role equal `itemsOf` of the `readName` of their `setupNameOf`, and each object's angle equals the read angle within 1e-12. `a setup the template cannot name says which placeholder is empty, and a new setup takes the template's name made free, or the name it is given`: with `lpA` holding nothing, `setupNameOf` answers `MissingNameValueErr` naming `source1` and `setupNameAmong … [] (SetupName \"Setup 3\")` answers `Setup 3`; the full slots among `[]` answer `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`, and among `cpl-(qz#45-lr#45)-cpl` `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL (2)`.", "acceptance": "After names come from slots, `NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf`, `itemsOf`, `setupNameOf` and `setupNameAmong`, `SlotItem`, `ItemLabel.namePart` and `NameText.toSetupName` MUST exist in `NamingTemplates.fs`, a setup's name MUST be written from its slots in light order under the template's aliases and read back into the same items and angles; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a setup's name is written from its slots in light order, its items under their aliases and its objects at their angles`, `a name reads back into the items of its slots and their angles`, `writing a setup's name and reading it back gives its items and angles` and `a setup the template cannot name says which placeholder is empty, and a new setup takes the template's name made free, or the name it is given`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.a setup's name is written from its slots in light order, its items under their aliases and its objects at their angles", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.a name reads back into the items of its slots and their angles", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.writing a setup's name and reading it back gives its items and angles", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.a setup the template cannot name says which placeholder is empty, and a new setup takes the template's name made free, or the name it is given", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.ItemLabel.namePart", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NameText.toSetupName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.SlotItem", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.itemsOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.setupNameOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.setupNameAmong", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S83-SLOT-NAMES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 272, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [271], "how_to": "The window names every new setup by the kit's naming template (001 §J 'It names setups and experiments'; S8.2 interpretation 8: a table that is no setup yet takes `Setup <n>` at a commit or a swap, a swap from an active setup `<name> (2)`, and 'S8.3's template replaces these names'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, which opens `NamingTemplates`: (1) `ExpCommit` on a table that is no setup yet (step 261 (8)(b)): the setup is `Setup.create name slots model.kitSetups` with `name` = `model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate.setupNameAmong slots model.kitItems taken (SetupName.firstFree taken)` (step 271), `taken` being the names of `kitSetups` and `slots` the recorded table step 261 builds; `nextFreeAmong` keeps the name free, so `create` refuses none. (2) `SwapSlot` (step 264): the fresh name of a `CreateSwappedSetup` is `setupNameAmong swapped model.kitItems taken <step 264's fresh name>`, so a swapped table the template names takes that name and one it cannot name keeps `<active> (2)` or `Setup <n>`. (3) Nothing else is named here: `CreateSetup` keeps the typed name (step 260), and a copied setup keeps its own (step 261). The template is read from the kit file the window holds (`KitContext.kitFile`, step 131), so a template saved in the window names the next setup (step 273). No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 260, 263, 264), whose kit holds step 263's items `LP1`, `QZ`, `Laser` and `LPd` and step 264's `QZ2`, and whose kit file holds `NamingTemplate.standard`: `a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name`: with a linear polarizer, a sample and a second linear polarizer added, as step 263's facts add elements, so that the light meets them in that order before the seeded detector; `LP1` assigned to the first, `QZ` to the sample, turned to R1 45° (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 45.0)` with it selected), and `LPd` to the second, each by `AssignSlot` (step 263); the first polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`) and `ExpCommit`: the kit holds `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json` at revision 1, `E1` references it, and `activeSetupOpt` is that setup. `a swap to content no setup holds takes the template's name of the swapped table`: after that commit, `SwapSlot (sample, QZ2)` writes `LP1-(QZ2#45)-LPd.setup-json`, makes it active, and leaves the bytes of `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json` unchanged. Step 261's and 264's facts keep their names (`Setup 1`, `Bench A (2)`), and so do the UI facts that find `Setup 1.setup-json` (step 261): their tables hold no item in Prep 1, Obj 1 or Analyzer 1, which `NamingTemplate.standard` requires (step 268).", "acceptance": "After the window names new setups by the template, a commit on a table that is no setup yet and a swap to content no setup holds MUST name the new setup by the kit's naming template made free, and keep S8.2's name for a table the template cannot name; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name` and `a swap to content no setup holds takes the template's name of the swapped table`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-WINDOW-NAMES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a swap to content no setup holds takes the template's name of the swapped table", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-WINDOW-NAMES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 273, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [272], "how_to": "The kit's naming template is shown and saved in the kit bar, through semantic messages (001 §J 'Naming template: each kit carries one'; 001 §P and .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message, and the button and the test send the same one; S12.1 builds its kit with the lab's template). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type Kit.NamingTemplate with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, the template's text, with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the kit bar group (step 188), each with a one-line doc: `namingTemplateField` (`\"NamingTemplateField\"`) and `saveNamingTemplateButton` (`\"SaveNamingTemplateButton\"`). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) The model gains `namingTemplateText : ControlCaption`, the template being typed, with a one-line doc; it is the kit file's `namingTemplate.caption` wherever the model takes a kit file: `initWith`, the open's `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` (step 187), so a reload shows a template another writer saved. (b) Messages, each with a one-line doc: `SetNamingTemplateText of ControlCaption` (the field's text) and `SaveNamingTemplate` (the kit's naming template becomes the field's). (c) Arms. `SetNamingTemplateText text` sets `namingTemplateText`. `SaveNamingTemplate` is refused by the read-only guard of step 185, as `SaveSetup` is (step 262). Otherwise `NamingTemplate.tryCreate model.namingTemplateText.value` (step 268): `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved — <e.describe>` and writes nothing; a template equal to `model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate` sets `The naming template is unchanged.` and writes nothing; any other is written by `model.kit.saveKitFile { model.kit.kitFile with namingTemplate = template }` (step 131), whose `Ok kit` makes `model.kit` that context and `kitStatus` `Saved the naming template.`, and whose `Error e` keeps the model and sets `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. The window's own write is not a change offered for reload (step 130), and no setup or experiment is renamed (step 271). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs` (step 188): after the Kit menu's `WrapPanel` (step 188 (2)(b)), a `DockPanel` whose left child is the semi-bold `TextBlock` `Naming template:`, whose right child is the `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` `Save template` carrying `saveNamingTemplateButton` and sending `SaveNamingTemplate`, present only while the kit's writes are offered (`model.kitWrites`, step 185), and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `namingTemplateField` that shows `namingTemplateText` and sends `SetNamingTemplateText` at every change of its text. No other message, field, id or option is added. Tests. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 184-187), over a folder kit: `Save template writes the typed naming template into the kit file`: `SetNamingTemplateText (ControlCaption \"{source:CPL1=CPL}-({obj1}#{phi1})-{analyzer:CPL2=CPL}\")` and `SaveNamingTemplate` leave that template in `model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate`, `model.kit.proxy.readKitFile ()` answers a kit file holding it, `kitStatus` is `Saved the naming template.` and `CheckKitChanges KitCheckOnRequest` offers no change. `a naming template that does not parse, or the kit's own, is told and writes nothing`: the text `{sauce}` sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not saved` and holding `the naming template is not valid`, and the standard text sets `The naming template is unchanged.`; the bytes of `.kit-json` are unchanged by both. `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` (step 185) also sends `SaveNamingTemplate` after a template is typed, with the same assertions. `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer` (step 187) also has the other writer save a kit file whose template is `{obj1}`, and after Reload `namingTemplateText` is `{obj1}`. `KitWindowTests` (step 188): `the kit bar shows the kit's naming template with Save template beside it`: `namingTemplateField` shows the kit's template text, `saveNamingTemplateButton` is present with its left beyond the field's right, and the ids' texts are `NamingTemplateField` and `SaveNamingTemplateButton`; `a read-only window withholds every write control` (step 185) also finds no `saveNamingTemplateButton`. `ScrollExtentTests`' kit-window fact passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the template is edited in the kit bar, `SetNamingTemplateText` and `SaveNamingTemplate` MUST set and save the kit's naming template through `KitContext.saveKitFile`, refusing a text that does not parse, an unchanged template and a read-only kit with nothing written, and the kit bar MUST show the template's field and Save template; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Save template writes the typed naming template into the kit file` and `a naming template that does not parse, or the kit's own, is told and writes nothing` and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` and `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the kit bar shows the kit's naming template with Save template beside it` and the changed `a read-only window withholds every write control`; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Save template writes the typed naming template into the kit file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a naming template that does not parse, or the kit's own, is told and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.the kit bar shows the kit's naming template with Save template beside it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.NamingTemplate.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.namingTemplateField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.saveNamingTemplateButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.namingTemplateText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetNamingTemplateText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SaveNamingTemplate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitWindowView.kitWindowView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S83-TEMPLATE-EDIT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 274, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [273], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests"], "how_to": "The grid generator as pure Domain: options per slot, their product, the combinations unticked, and every setup made at once and named by the template (001 §J 'Grid generator: a set of options per slot → their product, with impossible or unwanted combinations unticked → all setups and experiments created at once'; 001 §P `GenerateSetupGrid`, whose message is step 276 and whose controls are S8.4's). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`: `SetupError` (step 255) gains `SlotItemTwiceErr of reason : string`, one item in two slots (one physical piece is in one place, 001 §I), rendered `the item is in two slots: <reason>`. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs`: `module SetupGrids` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `NamingTemplates.fs` (step 268): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the grid generator, every combination of a table's slot options made a setup at once (spec 0050 S8.3). It opens `Kit`, `ItemModels`, `Setups` and `NamingTemplates`. (a) `SlotChoice = { itemOpt : ItemId option; r1 : Angle }`: the slot holds that item, or nothing, turned to `r1`. (b) `SlotOptions = { slot : Library.ElementId; choices : SlotChoice list }`, one axis: a slot of the table and its options in order. (c) `SlotPick = { slot : Library.ElementId; choice : SlotChoice }` and `GridCombination = { picks : SlotPick list }`, one pick per axis in axis order, with `member this.slotsOver (table : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) : Result<SetupSlot list, SetupError>`: the table's slots in order, each picked slot first turned (its placement's `r1` set to the choice's) and then made `withoutItem` for `None`, or `withItem item choice` (step 258) for `Some id`, the item taken from `items` (else `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the id) and its choice from `choiceOf` (else `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the item's label and that its model is not in the library), as `AssignSlot` resolves an item (step 263). A pick of a slot the table lacks answers `UnknownSetupSlotErr`, and one item in two picked slots `SlotItemTwiceErr` naming its label. Every slot is then `recordedWith items` (step 258), as a commit records the table (step 261). (d) `SetupGrid = { axes : SlotOptions list; unticked : GridCombination list }`, with: `member this.combinations : GridCombination list`, the product of the axes' choices, the first axis varying slowest (no axis gives one empty combination); `member this.ticked : GridCombination list`, those not in `unticked`, in order; `member this.untick (combination : GridCombination) : SetupGrid`, which adds it to `unticked` once, and `member this.tick (combination : GridCombination) : SetupGrid`, which removes it; `static member create (axes : SlotOptions list) (table : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) : SetupGrid`, the grid over `axes` whose `unticked` holds, in order, every combination whose `slotsOver` answers an error, so the impossible ones start unticked (001 §J); and `member this.generate (table : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) (template : NamingTemplate) (held : Setup list) : Result<Setup list, SetupError>`, one setup per ticked combination, in order: the setup of `held`, or one made earlier in the same run, whose current slots equal the combination's `slotsOver`; else `Setup.create` (step 256) of `template.setupNameAmong slots items taken (SetupName.firstFree taken)` (step 271), `taken` being the names of `held` and of the setups made before it. The first combination whose `slotsOver` fails refuses the whole grid with that error, so nothing half-made is answered. Nothing is written: the host records (step 276). No cache, sort, size limit or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs`, `module SetupGridTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over step 271's fixture as test-local copies: the slots `src`, `lpA`, `sampleA`, `lpB` and `det`, the items `Laser`, `CPL1`, `CPL2`, `QZ` and `LR`, the template `lab` = `tryCreate \"{source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer:CPL2=CPL,LP2=LP}-{note}\"`, and a test-local `choiceOf` answering each item's choice (`SourcePresetChoice` for `Laser`, `LibraryModelChoice` of its model for the others) and `None` for `Ghost`, an item whose model no library holds. `a grid lists the product of its slots' options, the first slot slowest, and leaves out what is unticked`: the axes `lpA` {`CPL1` at 0°, nothing at 0°} and `sampleA` {`QZ` at 0°, `QZ` at 45°, `LR` at 90°} list six combinations in the order (`CPL1`, `QZ` 0°), (`CPL1`, `QZ` 45°), (`CPL1`, `LR` 90°), (nothing, `QZ` 0°), (nothing, `QZ` 45°), (nothing, `LR` 90°); unticking (`CPL1`, `QZ` 45°) leaves the other five ticked in that order, unticking it again changes nothing, and ticking it lists six again. `a grid starts with the combinations it cannot make unticked`: `create` over the axes `lpA` {`CPL1`, `Laser`, `Ghost`, an id no item has} and `sampleA` {`QZ`} unticks the three last combinations, and over `lpA` {`CPL1`} and `lpB` {`CPL1`, `CPL2`} unticks (`CPL1`, `CPL1`). `a grid's setups take the template's names, and a combination a held setup holds is that setup`: over `lpA` {`CPL1`}, `sampleA` {`QZ` at 0°, `QZ` at 45°} and `lpB` {`CPL2`} with `lab`, `generate` with no held setup answers `CPL-(QZ#0)-CPL` and `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL` at revision 1; with the first held, it answers that held setup itself and the second as before; with a held `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL` of other slots, the second is `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL (2)`; and over the same grid with `lpA` no axis and holding nothing, which `lab` cannot name, the setups are `Setup 1` and `Setup 2`. `a ticked combination the grid cannot make refuses the whole grid`: the record `{ axes = …; unticked = [] }` over `lpA` {`CPL1`, `Laser`} and `sampleA` {`QZ`} answers `IncompatibleSlotItemErr` naming `Laser`; one putting `CPL1` in `lpA` and `lpB` answers `SlotItemTwiceErr` naming `CPL1`; and an axis of a slot the table lacks answers `UnknownSetupSlotErr`. `KitTests`' `every setup error renders its condition and its payload` (step 255) also covers `SlotItemTwiceErr`.", "acceptance": "After the grid generator lands, `SetupGrids.fs` MUST hold `SlotChoice`, `SlotOptions`, `SlotPick`, `GridCombination` and `SetupGrid`, a grid MUST list the product of its options less the unticked ones, start with its impossible combinations unticked, and generate one setup per ticked combination named by the template, a held one reused, or refuse the whole grid; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a grid lists the product of its slots' options, the first slot slowest, and leaves out what is unticked`, `a grid starts with the combinations it cannot make unticked`, `a grid's setups take the template's names, and a combination a held setup holds is that setup` and `a ticked combination the grid cannot make refuses the whole grid` and the changed `every setup error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests.a grid lists the product of its slots' options, the first slot slowest, and leaves out what is unticked", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests.a grid starts with the combinations it cannot make unticked", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests.a grid's setups take the template's names, and a combination a held setup holds is that setup", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests.a ticked combination the grid cannot make refuses the whole grid", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every setup error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.SetupError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.SetupGrids.SlotChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.SetupGrids.SlotOptions", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.SetupGrids.SlotPick", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.SetupGrids.GridCombination", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.SetupGrids.GridCombination.slotsOver", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.SetupGrids.SetupGrid", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GRID"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 275, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [274], "how_to": "One experiment of the draft over each of several setups, the experiments half of the grid (001 §J 'all setups and experiments created at once'). In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, after `commit` (`Experiments.fs:commit`), with a doc of one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3: `commitOverSetups (references : SetupReference list) (c : ExperimentCollection) : ExperimentCollection`. When the draft can be committed (`ExperimentCollection.canCommit`, `Experiments.fs:canCommit`: an element and a variable are chosen) it appends, for each reference in order, the experiment `commit` (step 261) appends over it from the draft editing nothing: each takes the next id and holds the draft's varied element, capture, range and wavelength, and no data file. The answer's draft is the draft editing nothing, so a later commit appends. An incomplete draft appends nothing, as `commit` does. Its body folds `commit`, so no second experiment builder is written (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). No other function or option is added. Tests, in `ExperimentProxyTests`: `committing the draft over setups appends one experiment over each, and an incomplete draft appends none`: over a collection holding `E1` whose draft edits `E1` and varies a polarizer's R1 over 0 … 90°, `commitOverSetups` of the test-local references `A` revision 1 and `B` revision 2 appends `E2` over `A` revision 1 and `E3` over `B` revision 2, each with the draft's variable, range and capture and no data file, leaves `E1` unchanged and the draft editing nothing; over `ExperimentDraft.empty` it answers the collection unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the draft can be committed over several setups, `Experiments.commitOverSetups` MUST append one experiment of a committable draft over each reference in order through `commit`, leave the draft editing nothing and append nothing for an incomplete draft; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `committing the draft over setups appends one experiment over each, and an incomplete draft appends none`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.committing the draft over setups appends one experiment over each, and an incomplete draft appends none", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GRID-EXPERIMENTS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.commitOverSetups", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GRID-EXPERIMENTS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 276, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S83j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [275], "how_to": "`GenerateSetupGrid` as a semantic message: every ticked combination becomes a setup of the kit, with an experiment of the draft over each, at once (001 §J 'all setups and experiments created at once'; 001 §P `GenerateSetupGrid`; the grid's controls, `SetupGridGenerateButton`, are S8.4's). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `GenerateSetupGrid of SetupGrids.SetupGrid`, with a one-line doc: every ticked combination of the grid over the table, as setups and experiments of the kit. Its arm is refused by the read-only guard of step 185. Otherwise it calls `grid.generate model.elements model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate model.kitSetups` (steps 274, 263): `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `Not generated — <e.describe>` and writes nothing. `Ok setups`: each setup not in `kitSetups` (by equality) is recorded through `recordSetup` (step 260), in order; then, when the draft has a capture (`model.draftCapture`, as `ExpCommit` reads it), the collection takes it (`chooseMeasurement`) and `commitOverSetups` (step 275) over the setups' references in order, and each experiment it appends is recorded as `ExpCommit` records one (step 261). The first write that fails stops the run: `kitSetups` and the collection hold what was written, and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. On success `kitSetups` holds the new setups in name order and `kitStatus` is `Generated <n> setups (<m> new) and <k> experiments.`. The table, `activeSetupOpt` and the draft's fields are unchanged. (2) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'The table is the active setup' (step 261), one bullet of at most six lines: **Names come from the kit's naming template** (`NamingTemplates.fs`, spec 0050 S8.3): `{source}` is the polarization source (Prep 1), `{light}` the light source, `{obj<k>}` / `{phi<k>}` the objects and their angles (a dial reading or R1), then `{analyzer}`, `{detector}` and `{note}`; a second or later slot of a role and the note are left out with the text before them, and `{source:CPL1=CPL}` writes an item under another name. A new setup takes the template's name made free (`setupNameAmong`), and one the template cannot name keeps `Setup <n>`; the reference pipeline reads the lab's labels through `NamingTemplate.standard`, and the grid generator is `SetupGrids.fs`. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests`, over step 272's table (`LP1`, the sample, `LPd`) with the first polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`) and a grid made by `SetupGrid.create` over the sample's options `QZ` at 0°, `QZ` at 45° and `QZ2` at 0° with (`QZ2`, 0°) unticked: `GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each`: the kit holds `LP1-(QZ#0)-LPd.setup-json` and `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json` at revision 1 and `E1` and `E2` referencing them in that order, with the draft's variable; `kitStatus` is `Generated 2 setups (2 new) and 2 experiments.`; and `elements` and `activeSetupOpt` are as they were. `a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing`: the same grid again leaves both setup files' bytes unchanged, records `E3` and `E4` over them and sets `Generated 2 setups (0 new) and 2 experiments.`; a grid record whose sample options hold `Laser` and whose `unticked` is empty sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not generated` and naming `Laser`, and no kit file changes. `a grid over a draft that cannot be committed records its setups and no experiment`: after `ExpNew` (no element chosen) the grid writes the two setups and no experiment file and sets `Generated 2 setups (2 new) and 0 experiments.`. `a kit opened read-only generates nothing`: over the folder reopened read-only, the grid sets `kitStatus` to `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.` and every file is as it was.", "acceptance": "After `GenerateSetupGrid` lands, the message MUST record every ticked combination's setup not yet held, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of a committable draft over each, refuse an impossible grid and a read-only kit with nothing written, and `AGENTS.md` MUST carry the naming-template gotcha; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each`, `a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing`, `a grid over a draft that cannot be committed records its setups and no experiment` and `a kit opened read-only generates nothing`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GENERATE-SETUP-GRID"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GENERATE-SETUP-GRID"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a grid over a draft that cannot be committed records its setups and no experiment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GENERATE-SETUP-GRID"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a kit opened read-only generates nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S83-GENERATE-SETUP-GRID"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.GenerateSetupGrid", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S83-GENERATE-SETUP-GRID"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.3 -- The naming template and the grid generator"}
{"number": 277, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S84a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [276], "how_to": "The pure halves of the slot bar: which kit items a slot's chip lists, which one a typed letter picks, and the angle an object's chip shows (001 §J 'Quick swap: a slot bar above the table shows one chip per slot (… Obj 1: QZ ▾ @ 45° ▾ …); each dropdown lists compatible items only; … keyboard: Tab between chips, letters pick'; the S8.4 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`, after step 261's members: (1) `PickLetter of char` with `.value`, a letter typed on a chip, and `static member tryCreate (text : string) : PickLetter option`: the first character of the text, upper-cased in the invariant culture, when `Char.IsLetterOrDigit` holds for it, and `None` for an empty text or any other first character. (2) `type SetupSlot with`: (a) `member this.turnAngle : Angle`, the reading of a `DialTurn reading` slot and the placement's R1 otherwise (`PlacementTurn`, or a slot holding nothing): the rule `NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf` applies to an `AnglePlaceholder` (step 271), moved here; that arm in `NamingTemplates.fs` calls it and keeps its condition (Obj k holds an item), so every name it writes is unchanged. (b) `member this.fittingItems (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) : Item list`: the items of `items`, in their order, whose `choiceOf` answers a choice whose `slotKinds` (step 258) holds the slot's `placement.catalogueKind`; an item `choiceOf` cannot resolve is left out. It is the rule `withItem` checks (step 258), applied before the choice, so a chip lists exactly what `SwapSlot` accepts. (c) `member this.pickedByLetter (letter : PickLetter) (fitting : Item list) : Item option`: among `fitting`, the items whose label's first character, upper-cased in the invariant culture, is the letter; when the slot holds one of them (`content.itemOpt`, step 256), the next of them after it, wrapping to the first; otherwise the first of them; and `None` when none is, or when that pick is the item the slot already holds, so a letter never swaps a slot to its own content. No cache, wildcard arm or other member is added. Tests, in `SetupTests` (steps 256-258, 261), over its slots `src`, `lpA`, `sampleA` and `det` (steps 256, 257) and test-local items made as step 258's facts make them, each `FixedMounting` unless named: `Laser` (`SourcePresetChoice` of `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633`), `LP1` and `LP2` (the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` polarizer), `CPL1` (`LibraryModelChoice` of the circular polarizer's built-in item model, `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel`, step 217), `QZ` (`StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1), `QZd` (the glass plate, `DialMounted DialNegative`, its `dialZero` known at 10°) and `Ghost`, which the test-local `choiceOf` answers `None` for. `a slot lists the kit's items that fit it, in their order`: over the items `Laser`, `LP1`, `QZ`, `CPL1`, `Ghost` and `LP2`, in that order, `lpA.fittingItems` is `LP1`, `CPL1`, `LP2`, `sampleA`'s is `QZ`, `src`'s `Laser` and `det`'s none. `a typed letter picks the next fitting item whose label starts with it, wrapping, and never the slot's own`: over `lpA`'s fitting `LP1`, `CPL1`, `LP2`: holding `LP1`, `l` picks `LP2` and `c` picks `CPL1`; holding `LP2`, `L` picks `LP1` (wrapping); holding nothing, `l` picks `LP1`; holding `CPL1`, `c` picks nothing (no other label starts with it); `x` picks nothing; and `PickLetter.tryCreate` of `q` and of `qz` is `PickLetter 'Q'`, and of the empty text, ` ` and `-` is `None`. `an object's angle is its dial reading, or its R1`: `sampleA` holding `QZd` put in by `withItem` at R1 30° turns at −20° (its reading, step 258), holding `QZ` at R1 45° at 45°, and holding nothing at R1 15° at 15°, each within 1e-12. `NamingTemplateTests`' facts pass unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the slot bar's pure halves land, `PickLetter` MUST exist in `Setups.fs`, `SetupSlot.fittingItems` MUST list the items whose model fits the slot, `pickedByLetter` MUST pick the next fitting item whose label starts with the typed letter and never the slot's own, and `turnAngle` MUST be the one angle rule `NamingTemplate.nameReadingOf` calls; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot lists the kit's items that fit it, in their order`, `a typed letter picks the next fitting item whose label starts with it, wrapping, and never the slot's own` and `an object's angle is its dial reading, or its R1`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a slot lists the kit's items that fit it, in their order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-PICKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a typed letter picks the next fitting item whose label starts with it, wrapping, and never the slot's own", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-PICKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.an object's angle is its dial reading, or its R1", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-PICKS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.PickLetter", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-PICKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.turnAngle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-PICKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.fittingItems", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-PICKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.pickedByLetter", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-PICKS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.4 -- The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem"}
{"number": 278, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S84b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [277], "how_to": "`RecordExperiment` as a semantic message: a new experiment of the draft over the active setup, however many the setup already has (001 §P `RecordExperiment`; 001 §J 'Direct problem: several experiments over one setup, saved in the kit'; 001 §O 'Slot bar over the table (§J), with \"Record experiment\"'). The slot bar's button that sends it is step 280's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `ExpCommit`'s two halves (steps 152, 261 (8)(b), 272) become two private functions of the update, so no second copy of either is written (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'): the table recorded as the active setup (the recorded slots, `revisedWith` over `pinFor` when a setup is active or the template's name made free otherwise, `recordSetup` unless the setup is unchanged, then `kitSetups` and `activeSetupOpt`), and the recording of the experiments a commit appended (`recordExperiment`, step 261 (7)(b)). `ExpCommit` and `GenerateSetupGrid` (step 276, which records each appended experiment as `ExpCommit` records one) call them, every text and outcome unchanged. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `RecordExperiment`, with a one-line doc: a new experiment of the draft over the active setup. (3) Its arm is refused by the read-only guard of step 185, which every write message calls. Otherwise a draft that cannot be committed (`ExperimentCollection.canCommit`, `Experiments.fs:canCommit`: no element or no variable chosen) sets `kitStatus` to `Not recorded — choose the element and the variable to vary in the Experiments bay first.` and writes nothing, and with no capture (`model.draftCapture`, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1555`: no detector captures the table) `Not recorded — no detector captures this table.` and writes nothing. Else the table is recorded as the active setup through the first function, whose error keeps the model with `ExpCommit`'s `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`; then the collection takes the capture (`Experiments.chooseMeasurement`) and `Experiments.commitOverSetups [ setup.reference ]` (step 275), which appends the draft as a new experiment over that one reference whether or not the draft edits one and leaves the draft editing nothing, and the appended experiment is recorded through the second function, whose error keeps the collection with the same text. On success `kitStatus` is `Recorded <the experiment's id> over <setup.reference.describe>.` (`Recorded E2 over 'Bench' revision 1.`). So the direct problem is any number of experiments over one setup, each its own `<id>.experiment-json`, and a table changed since its setup was recorded is recorded first, as a commit records it. `ExpCommit` keeps editing the experiment its draft edits; `RecordExperiment` never edits one. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 260-264), over its folder kit: `RecordExperiment appends a new experiment over the active setup each time, so one setup holds several experiments`: with a linear polarizer added, `SetSetupName (ControlCaption \"Bench\")` and `CreateSetup`, the polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`), then `RecordExperiment`, the range's maximum changed (`ExpSetRangeMax`) and `RecordExperiment` again: the folder holds `E1.experiment-json` and `E2.experiment-json`, both referencing `'Bench' revision 1`, `E1` with the first range and `E2` with the changed one; the bytes of `Bench.setup-json` are those `CreateSetup` wrote; `kitStatus` is `Recorded E2 over 'Bench' revision 1.`; and the draft edits nothing. `RecordExperiment over a draft that edits an experiment appends another and leaves the edited one as it was`: after `E1` is recorded, `ExpEdit E1`, the range's maximum changed and `RecordExperiment` append `E2` with the changed range, and the bytes of `E1.experiment-json` are unchanged. `RecordExperiment records the table as ExpCommit does: a first setup for a table that is no setup yet, and the next revision over one an experiment references`: on a table that is no setup yet, with the polarizer chosen, `RecordExperiment` writes `Setup 1.setup-json` and `E1` over `'Setup 1' revision 1` and makes `Setup 1` active; the polarizer turned (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 30.0)`, it being selected) and `RecordExperiment` again give `Setup 1` revision 2 with revision 1 in its history and `E2` over revision 2, `E1` still referencing revision 1. `RecordExperiment without a chosen element and variable is told and writes nothing`: after `ExpNew`, with nothing chosen, `RecordExperiment` sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not recorded` and the folder holds no experiment file. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 185, 262, 273): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `RecordExperiment`, with the same assertions. Every `ExpCommit` and `GenerateSetupGrid` fact passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After `RecordExperiment` lands, it MUST record the table as `ExpCommit` records it and append a new experiment of the draft over the active setup each time, never editing the draft's own, and refuse a draft that cannot be committed and a read-only kit with nothing written, `ExpCommit` and `GenerateSetupGrid` sharing its two halves unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `RecordExperiment appends a new experiment over the active setup each time, so one setup holds several experiments`, `RecordExperiment over a draft that edits an experiment appends another and leaves the edited one as it was`, `RecordExperiment records the table as ExpCommit does: a first setup for a table that is no setup yet, and the next revision over one an experiment references` and `RecordExperiment without a chosen element and variable is told and writes nothing` and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`, the count rising by 4; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.RecordExperiment appends a new experiment over the active setup each time, so one setup holds several experiments", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-RECORD-EXPERIMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.RecordExperiment over a draft that edits an experiment appends another and leaves the edited one as it was", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-RECORD-EXPERIMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.RecordExperiment records the table as ExpCommit does: a first setup for a table that is no setup yet, and the next revision over one an experiment references", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-RECORD-EXPERIMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.RecordExperiment without a chosen element and variable is told and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-RECORD-EXPERIMENT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S84-RECORD-EXPERIMENT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.RecordExperiment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-RECORD-EXPERIMENT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.4 -- The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem"}
{"number": 279, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S84c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [278], "how_to": "The slot bar's state in the window model: which chip's list is open and what each chip lists (001 §J 'each dropdown lists compatible items only; choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one'; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message). The bar that shows it is step 280's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `slotChipOpenOpt : Library.ElementId option`, the slot whose chip's list is open, with a one-line doc; `initWith` sets it to `None`. (2) On the model extension holding `tryItemModelChoice` (step 263): `member model.slotChipItems (slot : Setups.SetupSlot) : Item list` is `slot.fittingItems model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice` (step 277), what that slot's chip lists. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `ToggleSlotChip of Library.ElementId`, with a one-line doc: open that slot's chip list, or close it when it is the open one. Its arm writes nothing, so a read-only kit takes it: for a slot of `elements` it sets `slotChipOpenOpt` to `Some` the id, or to `None` when that id is the open one; an id the table lacks leaves the model as it is. (4) `SwapSlot`'s arm (steps 264, 272) also sets `slotChipOpenOpt` to `None` on every outcome, so a pick closes the list whether the swap switched, created or was refused. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 263, 264), whose kit holds the items `LP1`, `QZ`, `Laser`, `LPd` and `QZ2`: `a slot's chip lists the kit's items that fit it`: with a linear polarizer and a sample added, `slotChipItems` of the polarizer's slot is exactly `LP1` and `LPd`, in the order `kitItems` holds them, of the sample's `QZ` and `QZ2`, of the light source's `Laser` and of the seeded detector's none. `ToggleSlotChip opens one chip's list at a time, and a swap closes it`: `ToggleSlotChip` of the sample sets `slotChipOpenOpt` to it, of the polarizer moves it there, and of the polarizer again closes it; `ToggleSlotChip` of an id the table lacks changes nothing; the toggles change no kit file; and with the sample's list open, `SwapSlot (sample, QZ2)` closes it.", "acceptance": "After the chip state lands, `model.slotChipItems` MUST list the kit items that fit a slot, `ToggleSlotChip` MUST open one chip's list at a time and close the open one, writing nothing, and `SwapSlot` MUST close the list; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot's chip lists the kit's items that fit it` and `ToggleSlotChip opens one chip's list at a time, and a swap closes it`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a slot's chip lists the kit's items that fit it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-CHIP-STATE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.ToggleSlotChip opens one chip's list at a time, and a swap closes it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-CHIP-STATE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.slotChipOpenOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-CHIP-STATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.slotChipItems", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-CHIP-STATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ToggleSlotChip", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-CHIP-STATE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SwapSlot", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-CHIP-STATE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.4 -- The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem"}
{"number": 280, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S84d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [279], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests"], "how_to": "The slot bar above the table, in a file of its own (001 §J 'Quick swap: a slot bar above the table shows one chip per slot (`Source: Laser | Prep: CPL1 ▾ | Obj 1: QZ ▾ @ 45° ▾ | … | Detector: Phone`); each dropdown lists compatible items only; choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one; keyboard: Tab between chips, letters pick'; 001 §O 'Slot bar over the table (§J), with \"Record experiment\"' and 'Automation': `SlotChip_<slot>`; the S8.4 brief; .spec-md §4 'UI'). The bar sits inside the main page directly above the table, so it is compiled before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` as a projection of its own state and handler records, the shape of the Experiments bay (`ExperimentControls.fs:experimentControlsView`, over the handlers `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:experimentHandlers` builds), and the main view docks it. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the flow-strip group (step 239), `// --- The slot bar over the table (SlotBarView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `slotBar` (`\"SlotBar\"`), `slotChipChoiceList` (`\"SlotChipChoiceList\"`) and `recordExperimentButton` (`\"RecordExperimentButton\"`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each declaration with a one-line doc: `type Setups.SlotRole with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey`, the role's `text` (step 257) without its spaces (`Source`, `Prep1`, `Obj2`, `Analyzer1`, `Detector1`); on the `ConstructorUiId` extension that holds `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:elementHover`, `static member slotChip (role : Setups.SlotRole) : ConstructorUiId` (`SlotChip_<role.uiKey>`) and `static member slotChipChoice (role : Setups.SlotRole) (item : Kit.ItemId) : ConstructorUiId` (`SlotChipChoice_<role.uiKey>_<the item's GUID>`); `type Kit.ItemLabel with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, the label's text; `type Angle with member this.degreeCaption : ControlCaption`, its degrees as the rotation bar writes them (`RotationControls.fs:51`, `BarDegrees.text`: at most two decimals, invariant culture) followed by `°`; and `type Setups.RoledSlot with member this.chipCaption (items : Kit.Item list) : ControlCaption`: `<role.text>: <the label of the item the slot holds>`, `<role.text>: —` when it holds nothing and `<role.text>: (not in this kit)` when `items` lacks its item, an `ObjectSlotRole` holding an item adding ` @ <slot.turnAngle.degreeCaption>` (step 277), the angle the naming template writes for it (step 271). (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.SlotBarView`, compiled directly before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj` and no comment, and a module doc of one to three lines. It declares, each with a one-line doc: `SlotChipState = { roled : Setups.RoledSlot; caption : ControlCaption; fitting : Kit.Item list }`, one chip; `SlotBarState = { chips : SlotChipState list; openOpt : Library.ElementId option; recordAvailability : ControlAvailability }`; and `SlotBarHandlers = { toggleChip : Library.ElementId -> unit; swapSlot : Library.ElementId -> Kit.ItemId -> unit; pickByLetter : Library.ElementId -> Setups.PickLetter -> unit; recordExperiment : unit -> unit }`; and `slotBarView (state : SlotBarState) (handlers : SlotBarHandlers) : IView`, documented in one to three lines. The view is a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `slotBar`, margin 8, 4, holding: (a) a `WrapPanel` (in a vertical block, AGENTS.md) of one chip per `chips` entry, in order, then, when `recordAvailability` is `ControlOffered`, the verb `Record experiment` (`MaterialsWindowView.verbButton`, public since step 107, carrying `recordExperimentButton`, calling `recordExperiment`). A chip is a `Border` carrying `slotChip roled.role`, focusable and a tab stop, in the box look of `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` (on `positiveBackground` while its list is open), whose child reads `<caption> ▾`; a press focuses it and calls `toggleChip` with its slot; a text typed while it has the focus is read by `PickLetter.tryCreate` (step 277), an answer calling `pickByLetter` with its slot, the event handled. So Tab moves between the chips in light order and a letter picks. (b) While `openOpt` names a chip's slot: a `WrapPanel` carrying `slotChipChoiceList` holding, for each item of that chip's `fitting`, a box carrying `slotChipChoice role item.id` with `item.label.caption`: the item the slot holds an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` that calls `toggleChip` (closing the list: there is nothing to swap), every other a `verbButton` that calls `swapSlot` with the slot and the item; with no fitting item, the line `No item of this kit fits <role.text>.`. Every id is an AutomationId. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: on the model extension holding `slotChipItems` (step 279), `member model.slotBarState : SlotBarView.SlotBarState`: a chip per `SetupSlot.inLightOrder model.elements` (step 257), in that order, captioned by `chipCaption model.kitItems` and listing `model.slotChipItems slot`; `openOpt` is `slotChipOpenOpt`; and `recordAvailability` is `model.kitWrites` (step 185). A private `slotBarHandlers (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : SlotBarView.SlotBarHandlers` beside `experimentHandlers` dispatches `ToggleSlotChip`, `SwapSlot` and `RecordExperiment`, and resolves `pickByLetter` against the model: the slot of that id in `elements`, its `pickedByLetter letter (model.slotChipItems slot)` and `SwapSlot` of the picked item, no pick dispatching nothing. `mainView`'s table surface (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3944`, `tableSurface`) becomes a `DockPanel` whose top is `SlotBarView.slotBarView model.slotBarState (slotBarHandlers model dispatch)` and whose fill is the panel it holds today, so the canvas, its gestures, the element menu overlay and the page's scrolling are unchanged; a full-surface bay shows no table and no bar. The comment above it gains, in no more words than it needs, that the slot bar sits above the table. No other message, field, id or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs`, `module SlotBarTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, mounting `mainView` in a `HostWindow` as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` (`:107`) mounts it, headless at 1000 × 900, over `initMain ()` driven through its messages: its scratch kit holds the items `Laser` (the HeNe preset), `LP1` and `LP2` (the linear-polarizer preset, `FixedMounting`), `QZ` and `QZ2` (the glass plates at version 1), added through the Items panel's messages (`OpenAddItemForm`, `ChooseNewItemModel`, `SetNewItemLabel`, `AddItem`, step 236), and a linear polarizer and a sample are added (`AddElement`) so that the light meets them in that order before the seeded detector. Without a trait: `the slot bar UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the three fixed ids' texts; `slotChip` of `SourceSlotRole`, `PrepSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)`, `ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 2)`, `AnalyzerSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)` and `DetectorSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)` is `SlotChip_Source`, `SlotChip_Prep1`, `SlotChip_Obj2`, `SlotChip_Analyzer1` and `SlotChip_Detector1`; and `slotChipChoice (ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))` of a test-local item id is `SlotChipChoice_Obj1_<its GUID>`. `the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle`: with `Laser`, `LP1` and `QZ` assigned to the source, the polarizer and the sample (`AssignSlot`, step 263) and the sample turned to R1 45° (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 45.0)`, it being selected), the chips of Source, Prep 1, Obj 1 and Detector 1 are present left to right on one row, reading `Source: Laser ▾`, `Prep 1: LP1 ▾`, `Obj 1: QZ @ 45° ▾` and `Detector 1: — ▾`, and the bar's bottom is above the top of `tableElementCanvas`. `an open chip lists only the kit's items that fit its slot`: after `ToggleSlotChip` of the polarizer, `slotChipChoiceList` holds the boxes `slotChipChoice` of `LP1` and `LP2` and none of `Laser`, `QZ` or `QZ2`; after `ToggleSlotChip` of the detector it holds the line `No item of this kit fits Detector 1.`. `Tab moves between the chips in light order, and a typed letter picks the next fitting item`: over `the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle`'s model, with the Prep 1 chip focused, one Tab (`KeyPressQwerty` then `KeyReleaseQwerty` of `PhysicalKey.Tab`, as `EmbeddedChartTests.fs:156` presses Enter) leaves the Obj 1 chip focused (the window's `FocusManager`), and a second the Detector 1 chip; with the Obj 1 chip focused, `window.KeyTextInput(\"q\")` (as `FacetedTreeControlsTests.fs:403` types) makes the sample hold `QZ2`; with it focused again, a second `q` makes it hold `QZ`, and `x` changes nothing. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing boxes at their centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` (`:69`) does: `pressing a chip and an item swaps the table to a kit setup that holds it`: over `the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle`'s model, pressing the Obj 1 chip shows `slotChipChoiceList`, and pressing `QZ2`'s box closes it, the chip reading `Obj 1: QZ2 @ 45° ▾` and the scratch kit's `readSetups ()` answering one setup whose sample slot holds `QZ2`. `pressing Record experiment twice records two experiments over the active setup`: with `SetSetupName (ControlCaption \"Bench\")`, `CreateSetup` and the polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`), pressing `recordExperimentButton` twice leaves the scratch kit's `readExperiments ()` answering `E1` and `E2`, both over `'Bench' revision 1`. `KitWindowTests` (steps 185, 262): `a read-only window withholds every write control` also finds no `recordExperimentButton`.", "acceptance": "After the slot bar lands, `SlotBarView.slotBarView` MUST show, directly above the table, one focusable chip per slot in light order under `ConstructorUiId.slotChip`, each naming its item and an object its angle, the open chip's list of fitting items under `slotChipChoice` sending `SwapSlot`, Tab moving between the chips and a typed letter picking, and `Record experiment` sending `RecordExperiment`, withheld under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing a chip and an item swaps the table to a kit setup that holds it` and `pressing Record experiment twice records two experiments over the active setup`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the slot bar UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle`, `an open chip lists only the kit's items that fit its slot` and `Tab moves between the chips in light order, and a typed letter picks the next fitting item` and the changed `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests.the slot bar UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests.the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests.an open chip lists only the kit's items that fit its slot", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests.Tab moves between the chips in light order, and a typed letter picks the next fitting item", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests.pressing a chip and an item swaps the table to a kit setup that holds it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests.pressing Record experiment twice records two experiments over the active setup", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a read-only window withholds every write control", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.slotBar", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.slotChipChoiceList", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.recordExperimentButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.SlotRole.uiKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.slotChip", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.slotChipChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ItemLabel.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.Angle.degreeCaption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.RoledSlot.chipCaption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SlotBarView.SlotChipState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SlotBarView.SlotBarState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SlotBarView.SlotBarHandlers", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SlotBarView.slotBarView", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.slotBarState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-SLOT-BAR-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.4 -- The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem"}
{"number": 281, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S84e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [280], "how_to": "The grid generator's editable options as pure Domain, so the panel that edits them holds no rule of its own (001 §J 'Grid generator: a set of options per slot → their product, with impossible or unwanted combinations unticked → all setups and experiments created at once'; S8.3's grid, step 274, whose controls are S8.4's; AGENTS.md 'State is separable from the UI'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs`, after `SetupGrid` (step 274): (1) `GridSlotDraft = { slot : Library.ElementId; items : ItemId list; angles : Angle list }`, one slot's options as the panel edits them: the items tried in it and the R1 angles each is tried at. (2) `SetupGridDraft = { slots : GridSlotDraft list; unticked : GridCombination list }`, every edited slot's draft in the order first edited and the combinations the user unticked, with: `static member empty : SetupGridDraft` (no slot, nothing unticked); `member this.slotDraft (slot : Library.ElementId) : GridSlotDraft`, the slot's draft, or one with no item and no angle; `member this.withItemToggled (slot : Library.ElementId) (item : ItemId) : SetupGridDraft`, the item appended to the slot's items, or removed when they hold it; `member this.withGridAngle (slot : Library.ElementId) (angle : Angle) : SetupGridDraft`, the angle appended to the slot's angles when they do not hold it; `member this.withoutGridAngle (slot : Library.ElementId) (angle : Angle) : SetupGridDraft`, the angle removed; `member this.withCombinationToggled (combination : GridCombination) : SetupGridDraft`, the combination removed from `unticked` when it holds it and appended otherwise; and `member this.gridOver (table : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) : SetupGrid`. A slot draft left with no item and no angle is dropped from `slots`, so an edit undone leaves the draft as it was. `gridOver` takes one axis per slot of `SetupSlot.inLightOrder table` (step 257), in that order, whose draft holds an item: its `choices` are, for each item in order, a `SlotChoice` of `Some item` at each angle in order, or at the slot's `placement.r1` when the draft lists no angle; a draft of a slot the table lacks gives no axis. The grid is `SetupGrid.create` over those axes (step 274), so its impossible combinations start unticked, its `unticked` then extended by the draft's `unticked` combinations that it lists and does not already hold, in the draft's order. Editing a slot's options re-lists the combinations, so an untick lasts while its combination is listed. Nothing is written. No cache, sort or other member is added. Tests, in `SetupGridTests` (step 274), over its fixture (the slots `src`, `lpA`, `sampleA`, `lpB` and `det`, the items `Laser`, `CPL1`, `CPL2`, `QZ` and `LR`, `Ghost` and `choiceOf`): `a grid draft tries each ticked item of a slot at each of its angles, its slots in light order`: a draft that toggles `CPL2` into `lpB` and then `QZ` and `LR` into `sampleA` with the angles 0° and 45° lists, through `gridOver`, the axes `sampleA` {`QZ` 0°, `QZ` 45°, `LR` 0°, `LR` 45°} and then `lpB` {`CPL2` at `lpB`'s R1}, and four combinations, each with `CPL2`. `ticking an item or adding an angle twice changes nothing more, removing undoes it, and a slot with no item is no axis`: toggling `QZ` into `sampleA` twice leaves `SetupGridDraft.empty`; `withGridAngle` of 0° twice lists 0° once and `withoutGridAngle` of it then lists none; a slot with an angle and no item gives no axis; a draft of an id the table lacks gives no axis; and `slotDraft` of a slot never edited holds no item and no angle. `a draft's unticked combinations stay unticked beside the impossible ones while they are listed`: over `sampleA` {`QZ`, `Ghost`} at its R1, the grid starts with `Ghost`'s combination unticked; `withCombinationToggled` of `QZ`'s makes the grid's `unticked` `Ghost`'s then `QZ`'s and its `ticked` empty; toggling it again ticks it; and after `QZ` is toggled out of the slot, the grid's `unticked` holds `Ghost`'s alone.", "acceptance": "After the grid draft lands, `SetupGrids.fs` MUST hold `GridSlotDraft` and `SetupGridDraft`, whose edits toggle items, angles and unticked combinations and whose `gridOver` MUST make, in light order, one axis per slot holding an item, each item at each angle, through `SetupGrid.create` with the user's unticks kept while listed; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a grid draft tries each ticked item of a slot at each of its angles, its slots in light order`, `ticking an item or adding an angle twice changes nothing more, removing undoes it, and a slot with no item is no axis` and `a draft's unticked combinations stay unticked beside the impossible ones while they are listed`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests.a grid draft tries each ticked item of a slot at each of its angles, its slots in light order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-DRAFT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests.ticking an item or adding an angle twice changes nothing more, removing undoes it, and a slot with no item is no axis", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-DRAFT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests.a draft's unticked combinations stay unticked beside the impossible ones while they are listed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupGridTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupGridTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-DRAFT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.SetupGrids.GridSlotDraft", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-DRAFT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.SetupGrids.SetupGridDraft", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/SetupGrids.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-DRAFT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.4 -- The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem"}
{"number": 282, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S84f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [281], "how_to": "The grid generator's edits as semantic messages over the window model (001 §J 'Grid generator'; 001 §P `GenerateSetupGrid`, step 276's message, which the panel sends; .spec-md §4 'UI'). The panel that sends them is step 283's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `setupGridOpt : SetupGrids.SetupGridDraft option`, the grid panel's draft while the panel is open, with a one-line doc; `initWith` sets it to `None`. (2) On the model extension holding `slotChipItems` (step 279): `member model.setupGrid : SetupGrids.SetupGrid option`, the open draft's `gridOver model.elements model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice` (step 281), `None` while the panel is closed. (3) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each with a one-line doc: `OpenSetupGrid` (open the grid panel), `CloseSetupGrid` (close it, forgetting its draft), `ToggleSetupGridItem of Library.ElementId * ItemId` (try the item in that slot, or stop trying it), `AddSetupGridAngle of Library.ElementId * RotationControls.BarDegrees` (try that slot's items at this R1 too), `RemoveSetupGridAngle of Library.ElementId * Angle` (stop trying that R1) and `ToggleSetupGridCombination of SetupGrids.GridCombination` (untick a ticked combination, or tick it again). (4) Arms. None writes, so a read-only kit takes them all. `OpenSetupGrid` sets `setupGridOpt` to `Some SetupGridDraft.empty`, keeping a draft already open; `CloseSetupGrid` sets it to `None`. With a draft open, `ToggleSetupGridItem (slot, item)` sets it to `withItemToggled slot item`, `AddSetupGridAngle (slot, d)` to `withGridAngle slot d.wrappedAngle` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:815`, the table's angle convention), `RemoveSetupGridAngle (slot, a)` to `withoutGridAngle slot a` and `ToggleSetupGridCombination c` to `withCombinationToggled c`; with none open each leaves the model as it is. An item that does not fit its slot is the grid's to refuse: its combinations start unticked (step 274) and the panel shows why (step 283). `GenerateSetupGrid` (step 276) is unchanged: the panel sends it with `model.setupGrid`, and the draft stays open, so a grid can be edited and generated again. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (steps 272, 276), over step 272's table (`LP1` in the first linear polarizer, the sample, `LPd` in the second) and its kit's items: `the grid panel's draft lists the product of the items and angles tried in a slot, and writes nothing`: `OpenSetupGrid` gives a grid with no axis; `ToggleSetupGridItem` of the sample with `QZ` and `QZ2` and `AddSetupGridAngle` of the sample with `BarDegrees 0.0` and `BarDegrees 45.0` list (`QZ`, 0°), (`QZ`, 45°), (`QZ2`, 0°), (`QZ2`, 45°), all ticked; `RemoveSetupGridAngle` of 45° leaves (`QZ`, 0°) and (`QZ2`, 0°); toggling `QZ2` again leaves (`QZ`, 0°); `AddSetupGridAngle` of `BarDegrees -45.0` adds 315°; and no kit file's bytes change. `unticking a combination in the panel leaves it out, and closing the panel forgets the draft`: `ToggleSetupGridCombination` of (`QZ2`, 0°) leaves the other three ticked, and again all four; `CloseSetupGrid` makes `setupGridOpt` and `model.setupGrid` `None`, and `OpenSetupGrid` then opens an empty draft. `the panel's grid generates its ticked setups through GenerateSetupGrid and stays open`: with the first polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`) and a draft of `QZ` and `QZ2` at 0° and 45° with (`QZ2`, 45°) unticked, `GenerateSetupGrid` of `model.setupGrid` leaves the kit holding `LP1-(QZ#0)-LPd.setup-json`, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json` and `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd.setup-json` and `E1` to `E3` over them in that order, `kitStatus` `Generated 3 setups (3 new) and 3 experiments.`, and the draft still open.", "acceptance": "After the grid messages land, `OpenSetupGrid`, `CloseSetupGrid`, `ToggleSetupGridItem`, `AddSetupGridAngle`, `RemoveSetupGridAngle` and `ToggleSetupGridCombination` MUST edit the open grid draft through its Domain members, writing nothing, and `model.setupGrid` MUST be the draft's grid over the table, which `GenerateSetupGrid` records; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the grid panel's draft lists the product of the items and angles tried in a slot, and writes nothing`, `unticking a combination in the panel leaves it out, and closing the panel forgets the draft` and `the panel's grid generates its ticked setups through GenerateSetupGrid and stays open`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupSaveLoadTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.the grid panel's draft lists the product of the items and angles tried in a slot, and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.unticking a combination in the panel leaves it out, and closing the panel forgets the draft", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.the panel's grid generates its ticked setups through GenerateSetupGrid and stays open", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.setupGridOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.setupGrid", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.OpenSetupGrid", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.CloseSetupGrid", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ToggleSetupGridItem", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.AddSetupGridAngle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.RemoveSetupGridAngle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ToggleSetupGridCombination", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-MESSAGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.4 -- The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem"}
{"number": 283, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S84g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [282], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests"], "how_to": "The grid generator's panel, a surface in a file of its own, opened from the slot bar and shown between it and the table (001 §O 'Slot bar over the table (§J), with \"Record experiment\"; the grid generator' and 'Automation': `SetupGridGenerateButton`; 001 §J 'Grid generator'; the S8.4 brief: 'The grid-generator UI (SetupGridGenerateButton) runs over S8.3'; .spec-md §4 'UI', §10.5). Like the slot bar (step 280) it is compiled before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` as a projection of its own state and handler records. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: in the slot-bar group (step 280), `setupGridOpenButton` (`\"SetupGridOpenButton\"`); and a new group after it, `// --- The setup grid generator (SetupGridView). ---`: `setupGridPanel` (`\"SetupGridPanel\"`), `setupGridCombinationList` (`\"SetupGridCombinationList\"`), `setupGridGenerateButton` (`\"SetupGridGenerateButton\"`, 001 §O's id), `setupGridCloseButton` (`\"SetupGridCloseButton\"`) and `static member setupGridCombination (position : ConstructorUiPosition) : ConstructorUiId` (`SetupGridCombination_<n>`, over `UiIds.fs:ConstructorUiPosition`), each with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: on the `ConstructorUiId` extension, `static member setupGridItemChoice (role : Setups.SlotRole) (item : Kit.ItemId) : ConstructorUiId` (`SetupGridItem_<role.uiKey>_<the item's GUID>`), `static member setupGridAngleField (role : Setups.SlotRole) : ConstructorUiId` (`SetupGridAngleField_<role.uiKey>`) and `static member setupGridAngle (role : Setups.SlotRole) (angle : Angle) : ConstructorUiId` (`SetupGridAngle_<role.uiKey>_<the angle's degrees as degreeCaption writes them, without the °>`); and `type SetupGrids.GridCombination with member this.caption (table : Setups.SetupSlot list) (items : Kit.Item list) : ControlCaption`: each pick, in order, as `<the role.text of its slot in the table's light order>: <the item's label> @ <r1.degreeCaption>` (`—` for nothing, `(not in this kit)` for an item `items` lacks), joined by `, `, and `The table as it is` for a combination of no pick. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.SetupGridView`, compiled directly after `SlotBarView.fs` and before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment, and a module doc of one to three lines. It declares, each with a one-line doc: `GridCombinationMark` = `CombinationTicked` | `CombinationUnticked` | `CombinationImpossible of reason : ControlCaption`, never stored, so with no wire tag; `GridCombinationState = { combination : SetupGrids.GridCombination; caption : ControlCaption; mark : GridCombinationMark }`; `SetupGridSlotState = { roled : Setups.RoledSlot; fitting : Kit.Item list; draft : SetupGrids.GridSlotDraft }`; `SetupGridState = { grid : SetupGrids.SetupGrid; slots : SetupGridSlotState list; rows : GridCombinationState list; generateAvailability : ControlAvailability }`; and `SetupGridHandlers = { toggleItem : Library.ElementId -> Kit.ItemId -> unit; addAngle : Library.ElementId -> RotationControls.BarDegrees -> unit; removeAngle : Library.ElementId -> Angle -> unit; toggleCombination : SetupGrids.GridCombination -> unit; generateGrid : SetupGrids.SetupGrid -> unit; closeGrid : unit -> unit }`; and `setupGridView (state : SetupGridState) (handlers : SetupGridHandlers) : IView`. The view is a `Border` carrying `setupGridPanel`, margin 8, 0, 8, 4, over a vertical `StackPanel` holding: (a) the semi-bold `Setup grid` and the wrapping line `Choose the items and the R1 angles to try in each slot. Every ticked combination becomes a setup of the kit, with an experiment of the draft over each.`; (b) for each of `slots`, a `DockPanel` whose left is `<role.text>:` and whose fill is a `WrapPanel` holding each `fitting` item as a box carrying `setupGridItemChoice role item.id` with `item.label.caption`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` while the draft holds the item and a `verbButton` otherwise, either calling `toggleItem`; then `R1 (°):` and a `TextBox` carrying `setupGridAngleField role`, width 60, whose text on Enter or losing focus is read by `BarDegrees.tryCreate` (`RotationControls.fs:60`) and, when it reads, passed to `addAngle` and the field cleared, an unreadable text being left as typed and ignored (the rotation bar's field rule, `RotationControls.fs:236`); then each of the draft's angles as a box carrying `setupGridAngle role angle` reading `<angle.degreeCaption> ×` and calling `removeAngle`; (c) `Combinations:` over a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `setupGridCombinationList`, one line per `rows` entry in order carrying `setupGridCombination` of its 1-based position: a ticked one a box reading `☑ <caption>`, an unticked one `☐ <caption>`, either calling `toggleCombination` (the element menu's marks, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3733`), and an impossible one a `TextBlock` reading `✗ <caption> — <reason>` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`, which takes no press; (d) one horizontal `StackPanel` of `Generate` (`setupGridGenerateButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` calling `generateGrid grid`, present only when `generateAvailability` is `ControlOffered`) and `Close` (`setupGridCloseButton`, on `negativeBackground`, calling `closeGrid`), the action box's right margin being the gap (.spec-md §10.5). Every id is an AutomationId. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs` (step 280): `SlotBarHandlers` gains `openSetupGrid : unit -> unit`, and the chip row ends, after `Record experiment`, with the verb `Setup grid…` (`setupGridOpenButton`) calling it; the grid's edits write nothing, so it is offered under a read-only kit too. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: on the model extension holding `setupGrid` (step 282), `member model.setupGridState : SetupGridView.SetupGridState option`, `None` while `setupGrid` is: its `slots` one per `SetupSlot.inLightOrder model.elements` with `model.slotChipItems slot` and the draft's `slotDraft slot.id`; its `rows` one per `grid.combinations`, captioned by `caption model.elements model.kitItems` and marked `CombinationImpossible` with the `describe` of `combination.slotsOver model.elements model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice`'s error (step 274), else `CombinationTicked` when `grid.ticked` holds it and `CombinationUnticked` otherwise; and `generateAvailability` `ControlOffered` when `model.kitWrites` is (step 185), the grid has an axis and `ticked` is not empty, and `ControlWithheld` otherwise. A private `setupGridHandlers (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : SetupGridView.SetupGridHandlers` beside `slotBarHandlers` dispatches `ToggleSetupGridItem`, `AddSetupGridAngle`, `RemoveSetupGridAngle`, `ToggleSetupGridCombination`, `GenerateSetupGrid` (step 276) and `CloseSetupGrid`, and `slotBarHandlers` gains `openSetupGrid` dispatching `OpenSetupGrid`. The table surface's `DockPanel` (step 280) docks, below the slot bar and above the table, `SetupGridView.setupGridView state (setupGridHandlers dispatch)` while `setupGridState` is `Some state`. No other message, field, id or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupGridPanelTests.fs`, `module SetupGridPanelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, mounting `mainView` as `SlotBarTests` does (step 280), over `initMain ()` whose scratch kit holds `LP1`, `LP2`, `QZ` and `QZ2` added through the Items panel's messages, with a linear polarizer, a sample and a second linear polarizer added so that the light meets them in that order before the seeded detector, `LP1` in the first and `LP2` in the second (`AssignSlot`). Without a trait: `the setup grid UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the five fixed ids' texts, `setupGridCombination (ConstructorUiPosition 2)` (`SetupGridCombination_2`), `setupGridItemChoice (ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))` of a test-local item id (`SetupGridItem_Obj1_<its GUID>`), `setupGridAngleField (AnalyzerSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))` (`SetupGridAngleField_Analyzer1`) and `setupGridAngle (ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)) (Angle.degree 22.5)` (`SetupGridAngle_Obj1_22.5`). `the grid panel sits between the slot bar and the table, offers each slot's fitting items and angles, and marks each combination ticked, unticked or impossible`: after `OpenSetupGrid`, `setupGridPanel`'s top is below the bar's bottom and its bottom above the canvas's top, with a row for Source, Prep 1, Obj 1, Analyzer 1 and Detector 1, Obj 1's offering `QZ` and `QZ2` and Prep 1's `LP1` and `LP2`; after `ToggleSetupGridItem` of the sample with `QZ` and `QZ2`, `AddSetupGridAngle` of 0° and 45° and `ToggleSetupGridCombination` of (`QZ2`, 45°), `setupGridCombinationList` reads, in order, `☑ Obj 1: QZ @ 0°`, `☑ Obj 1: QZ @ 45°`, `☑ Obj 1: QZ2 @ 0°` and `☐ Obj 1: QZ2 @ 45°`; and with Prep 1 trying `LP1` and `LP2` and Analyzer 1 trying `LP2`, each combination putting `LP2` in both is a line starting `✗ ` and ending `the item is in two slots: ` and the reason naming `LP2` (`SlotItemTwiceErr`, step 274). `Generate and Close share a row, Close to the right, and Generate needs a ticked combination over a slot`: with the panel open and no axis, `setupGridGenerateButton` is absent and `setupGridCloseButton` present; with an item tried, `Generate` and `Close` have equal tops, `Close`'s left beyond `Generate`'s right; and pressing `setupGridCloseButton` removes the panel. `a kit opened read-only offers the grid but no Generate`: with the model's kit replaced, by record update, by the read-only view of its scratch kit (step 131), as `ItemsPanelTests`' read-only fact builds its model (step 238), and the grid open with `QZ` tried in the sample, `setupGridOpenButton` and `setupGridPanel` are present and `setupGridGenerateButton` absent. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing boxes at their centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` (`:69`) does: `pressing Setup grid, items, an angle and Generate records the grid's setups in the kit`: pressing `setupGridOpenButton`, Obj 1's `QZ` and `QZ2` boxes, typing `45` into Obj 1's angle field followed by Enter, and pressing `setupGridGenerateButton` leaves the scratch kit's `readSetups ()` holding `LP1-(QZ#45)-LP2` and `LP1-(QZ2#45)-LP2`. `ScrollExtentTests`: `the Main page with the setup grid open leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable \"MainSetupGrid\"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:89`) over `constructorWindow` (`:107`) of `filledExperiments ()` with the grid open (`OpenSetupGrid`) and the R1 angles 0°, 45° and 90° added to the polarizer's options. `SlotBarTests` (step 280): `the slot bar UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also checks `setupGridOpenButton`.", "acceptance": "After the grid panel lands, `SetupGridView.setupGridView` MUST show, between the slot bar and the table, each slot's fitting items and R1 angles, the combinations ticked, unticked or impossible with the reason, and `Generate` beside `Close`, Generate sending `GenerateSetupGrid` and offered only for a ticked combination over a slot under a writable kit, and the slot bar MUST open it with `Setup grid…`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Setup grid, items, an angle and Generate records the grid's setups in the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the setup grid UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the grid panel sits between the slot bar and the table, offers each slot's fitting items and angles, and marks each combination ticked, unticked or impossible`, `Generate and Close share a row, Close to the right, and Generate needs a ticked combination over a slot`, `a kit opened read-only offers the grid but no Generate` and `the Main page with the setup grid open leaves everything reachable` and the changed `the slot bar UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupGridPanelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests.the setup grid UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupGridPanelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests.the grid panel sits between the slot bar and the table, offers each slot's fitting items and angles, and marks each combination ticked, unticked or impossible", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupGridPanelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests.Generate and Close share a row, Close to the right, and Generate needs a ticked combination over a slot", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupGridPanelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests.a kit opened read-only offers the grid but no Generate", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupGridPanelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests.pressing Setup grid, items, an angle and Generate records the grid's setups in the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupGridPanelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the Main page with the setup grid open leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests.the slot bar UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.setupGridOpenButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.setupGridPanel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.setupGridCombinationList", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.setupGridGenerateButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.setupGridCloseButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.setupGridCombination", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.setupGridItemChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.setupGridAngleField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.setupGridAngle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.GridCombination.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SetupGridView.GridCombinationMark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SetupGridView.GridCombinationState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SetupGridView.SetupGridSlotState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SetupGridView.SetupGridState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SetupGridView.SetupGridHandlers", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SetupGridView.setupGridView", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SlotBarView.SlotBarHandlers", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.setupGridState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S84-GRID-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.4 -- The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem"}
{"number": 284, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S84h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [283], "how_to": "The direct problem and the quick swap proved through the constructor window itself, and the slot bar named where every agent reads first (001 §J 'Quick swap', 'Direct problem: several experiments over one setup, saved in the kit'; .spec-md §9 'UI tests'). The window's composition is unchanged: `kitWindowView` shows `mainView` for the Setups and Experiments steps (step 239), so the slot bar (step 280) and the grid panel (step 283) are in every constructor window already. (1) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'Names come from the kit's naming template' (step 276), one bullet of at most six lines: **The slot bar is the quick swap** (`SlotBarView.fs`, spec 0050 S8.4): one chip per slot in light order, directly above the table, each listing the kit items that fit its slot (`SetupSlot.fittingItems`); choosing one is `SwapSlot` (the held setup of that content, else a new one), Tab moves between chips and a typed letter picks (`pickedByLetter`). `Record experiment` is `RecordExperiment`, a new experiment of the draft over the active setup every time (the direct problem), while `ExpCommit` edits the draft's own; `Setup grid…` opens `SetupGridView.fs` over `SetupGridDraft`, whose Generate is `GenerateSetupGrid`. Nothing else in the file changes. (2) Tests, in `KitWindowTests` (steps 184-188, 239), with trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: in a kit window, Record experiment twice, a chip swap and Record experiment again write two setups and three experiments, and the reopened window lists them`: over a kit folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitWindowTests\", <a new GUID>)` opened read-write through `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) and loaded through `loadKit` (step 152), as its copy facts open their kits (step 207), a screen running `kitWindowView` on `SetupsFlowStep`: with `LP1`, `QZ` and `QZ2` added through the Items panel's messages, a linear polarizer and a sample added, `LP1` and `QZ` assigned to them (`AssignSlot`), `SetSetupName (ControlCaption \"Bench\")`, `CreateSetup` and the polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`), pressing `recordExperimentButton` twice, then the Obj 1 chip and `QZ2`'s box, then `recordExperimentButton` again leaves the folder holding `Bench.setup-json`, `Bench (2).setup-json` (the swap's new setup, which the standard template cannot name without an analyzer, step 272) holding `QZ2`, and `E1.experiment-json` and `E2.experiment-json` over `'Bench' revision 1` and `E3.experiment-json` over `'Bench (2)' revision 1`; and the folder opened again through `openKitAt` and `loadKit` gives a model whose `kitSetups` hold `Bench` and `Bench (2)` and whose collection holds `E1`, `E2` and `E3`.", "acceptance": "After the kit window proves the slot bar, a constructor window over a kit folder MUST record several experiments over one setup through Record experiment and swap a slot to a new setup through its chip, the files reading back when the kit is reopened, and `AGENTS.md` MUST carry the slot-bar gotcha; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: in a kit window, Record experiment twice, a chip swap and Record experiment again write two setups and three experiments, and the reopened window lists them`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.acceptance: in a kit window, Record experiment twice, a chip swap and Record experiment again write two setups and three experiments, and the reopened window lists them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S84-KIT-WINDOW-QUICK-SWAP"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S8.4 -- The slot bar, quick swap and the direct problem"}
{"number": 285, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [284], "how_to": "What a recorded run is for, the session it belongs to and the notes a reviewer writes on it, as pure Domain data (001 §K '`Experiment` = one recorded run: … a role: `Science | Calibration | Dark | DriftCheck | Diagnostic | Ignored | Planned`; a session'; 001 §E 'notes on experiments, studies and fit runs live in their files'; .spec-md §3.17: case names take a second word; the S9.1 brief: a role with int wire tags, a session and notes). Nothing reads them before step 288. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, directly after `ExperimentId` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentId`), in this order: (1) `ExperimentRole` = `ScienceRun` | `CalibrationRun` | `DarkRun` | `DriftCheckRun` | `DiagnosticRun` | `IgnoredRun` | `PlannedRun`. `member this.value : int` answers 1 to 7 in that order, its disk tag; `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : ExperimentRole option` answers `None` for any other tag (AGENTS.md: a closed set's tag is an int, and no `Unknown*` case); `member this.text : string` answers `Science`, `Calibration`, `Dark`, `Drift check`, `Diagnostic`, `Ignored` and `Planned`; `static member all : ExperimentRole list` lists the seven in tag order. (2) `SessionName of string` with `.value`, the measurement session a run belongs to when the user sets it by hand (S11.1's study splits the rest at its Diagnostic runs): `static member tryCreate (text : string) : SessionName option` keeps the text as given and answers `None` for an empty or white-space text. (3) `ExperimentNotes of string` with `.value`, free text, and `static member none : ExperimentNotes` = `ExperimentNotes \"\"`. No other type, member or option is added. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`, `CanonicalJson.options` gains one converter for `ExperimentRole`, written as step 166's `KitStar` converter is and registered with the others before the `JsonFSharpConverter`: it writes the case's `value` and reads through `ExperimentRole.tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. `SessionName` and `ExperimentNotes` keep the single-case form every other single-case union has, and nothing else in the options changes. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `an experiment role round-trips its wire tag and renders its text`: the tags 1 to 7 in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and 8, the seven texts exactly as above and `all` in tag order; and `a session name keeps its text and refuses a blank one, and notes are free text`: `SessionName.tryCreate \"Day 1 (morning)\"` is `Some (SessionName \"Day 1 (morning)\")`, `\"\"` and `\"   \"` are `None`, and `ExperimentNotes.none.value` is empty. In `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 166), `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes each `ExperimentRole` as its tag (`DarkRun` as `3`) and reads it back, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the role tag 8 with `MalformedJsonErr`.", "acceptance": "After roles, sessions and notes land, `ExperimentRole` MUST hold the seven run roles with int tags 1-7 read back by `tryOfWire` and written as their tag by `CanonicalJson.options`, `SessionName.tryCreate` MUST refuse a blank text and `ExperimentNotes` MUST be free text; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an experiment role round-trips its wire tag and renders its text` and `a session name keeps its text and refuses a blank one, and notes are free text`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.an experiment role round-trips its wire tag and renders its text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-ROLE-SESSION-NOTES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.a session name keeps its text and refuses a blank one, and notes are free text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-ROLE-SESSION-NOTES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-ROLE-SESSION-NOTES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an unknown disk tag is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-ROLE-SESSION-NOTES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentRole", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-ROLE-SESSION-NOTES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.SessionName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-ROLE-SESSION-NOTES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentNotes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-ROLE-SESSION-NOTES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 286, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [285], "how_to": "The name an experiment is stored under, and the kit's template writing it from the experiment's setup (001 §A 'A file that exists many times is named by its own identity … plus its kind extension'; 001 §J 'It names setups and experiments'; the S9.1 brief: experiments are named by the kit's naming template (S8.3) and stored as `<name>.experiment-json`; the S8.3 mapper's request: a one-way member from `NameText`, never both, ELEV006). Nothing stores a name before step 290. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`. (a) `ExperimentError` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentError`) moves to directly after step 285's types, its two cases kept, and gains `InvalidExperimentNameErr of reason : string` (a blank name) and `member this.describe : string`, rendering `the experiment is unknown: <reason>`, `the experiment is unavailable: <reason>` and `the experiment name is not valid: <reason>`; a match over the error anywhere gains the case. (b) `ExperimentName of string` with `.value`: `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<ExperimentName, ExperimentError>` keeps the text as given and refuses an empty or white-space text with `InvalidExperimentNameErr`; `member this.fileStem : FileStem` is `FileStem.ofText this.value` (step 24), so a name keeps the lab's characters (.spec-md §3.11); `member this.nextFreeAmong (taken : ExperimentName list) : ExperimentName` is the `ExperimentName` of `FileStem.firstFreeText this.value` over the taken names' `fileStem`s (step 255), the one suffix sequence items and setups use. (c) `ExperimentId` gains `member this.defaultName : ExperimentName`, `E<n>`: the name an experiment takes when the template cannot name its setup, which is the stem step 146 gives it today, so every such experiment keeps its file name. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs`, after step 271's members: (a) `type NameText with member this.toExperimentName : Result<ExperimentName, ExperimentError>`, `ExperimentName.tryCreate` of its text; no member converts back (ELEV006). (b) `type NamingTemplate with member this.experimentNameAmong (slots : SetupSlot list) (items : Item list) (noteOpt : NamePart option) (taken : ExperimentName list) (unnamed : ExperimentName) : ExperimentName`: `writeName` of `nameReadingOf slots items noteOpt` (steps 269, 271), made an `ExperimentName` by `toExperimentName` and free among `taken` by `nextFreeAmong`, or `unnamed` when the template cannot name the slots; it calls those members as `setupNameAmong` does (step 271), so no second naming rule exists. No other member, cache or option is added. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `an experiment name keeps its text, refuses a blank one, takes the next free suffix and defaults to its id`: `ExperimentName.tryCreate \"CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL\"` keeps the text and its `fileStem` is `FileStem \"CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL\"`; `\"a: b/c\"` has `FileStem \"a_ b_c\"`; `\"\"` and `\"   \"` answer `InvalidExperimentNameErr`; `(ExperimentName \"X\").nextFreeAmong [ ExperimentName \"x\"; ExperimentName \"X (2)\" ]` is `X (3)` and among `[]` `X`; and `(ExperimentId 7).defaultName` is `ExperimentName \"E7\"`; and `every experiment error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it. `NamingTemplateTests` (steps 268-271) gains `an experiment is named by the kit's template from its setup's slots, made free among the kit's experiments, or takes the name it is given`: over step 271's slots, items and `lab` template, the full slots among `[]` give `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL`, among `[ ExperimentName \"cpl-(qz#45-lr#45)-cpl\" ]` give `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL (2)`, with the note `2` give `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`, and with `lpA` holding nothing give the `unnamed` `E3`; and `(NameText \"  \").toExperimentName` answers `InvalidExperimentNameErr`.", "acceptance": "After experiment names land, `ExperimentName` MUST refuse a blank text, take its file stem from the shared name rule and its next free suffix from `FileStem.firstFreeText`, `ExperimentId.defaultName` MUST be `E<n>`, and `NamingTemplate.experimentNameAmong` MUST write the template's name of a setup's slots made free, or answer the name it is given; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an experiment name keeps its text, refuses a blank one, takes the next free suffix and defaults to its id`, `every experiment error renders its condition and its payload` and `an experiment is named by the kit's template from its setup's slots, made free among the kit's experiments, or takes the name it is given`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.an experiment name keeps its text, refuses a blank one, takes the next free suffix and defaults to its id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-NAME"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.every experiment error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-NAME"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.an experiment is named by the kit's template from its setup's slots, made free among the kit's experiments, or takes the name it is given", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-NAME"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-NAME"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentId.defaultName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-NAME"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-NAME"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NameText.toExperimentName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-NAME"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.experimentNameAmong", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-NAME"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 287, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [286], "how_to": "The scan as pure Domain data: one or more blocks, each a product of axes read on one capture (001 §K 'a **scan**: one or more variables (dial 0…360 step 20; φ; incidence × azimuth × observable; λ on a tunable source)'; 001 §Q AT-2 'one experiment per plate, with a multi-variable scan (incidence × azimuth × T / R) that reproduces exactly `a1 @ a2 @ a3`': the optic-axis plate joins A1's four azimuths read in T with A2's incidence × azimuth read in T and R, so an experiment holds more than one product; the S9.1 brief: today's `VariableParameter` / `VariableRange` / `sourceWaveLengthOpt` are generalised, not duplicated). Nothing reads it before step 288. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: (1) `VariableRange` (`Experiments.fs:VariableRange`) gains `member this.sweptValues : SweptValue list`: `n = max 2 points` values, the k-th `min + (max − min) · k / (n − 1)` for k = 0 … n − 1, the grid `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun` computes today (`xs`), so a chart built over it keeps every number. (2) After `ElementLabel` (`Experiments.fs:ElementLabel`), in this order: (a) `ScanAxis = { elementId : ElementId; label : ElementLabel; variable : VariableParameter; range : VariableRange }`, one quantity of one slot over its range: step 261's `VariedElement` with its range, which step 288 deletes; `member this.describe : string` is the varied text of `Experiment.description` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) without its capture, `<label>: vary <variable.label> over <min>…<max> <unit> (<points> pts)`, with the same `%g` and `%d` forms. (b) `ScanSetting = { elementId : ElementId; variable : VariableParameter; value : SweptValue }`, one axis at one value. (c) `ScanPoint = { settings : ScanSetting list; capture : MeasurementMode }`, one configuration: each axis of its block at one value, read on the block's capture. (d) `ScanBlock = { axes : ScanAxis list; capture : MeasurementMode }`, with `member this.points : ScanPoint list`, the product of the axes' `sweptValues` with the first axis outermost and the last innermost, each point carrying the block's capture (so a capture of both branches is the innermost observable, as A2 reads T then R); a block with no axis is one point with no setting, a dark line. (e) `ExperimentScan = { blocks : ScanBlock list; sourceWaveLengthOpt : WaveLength option }`, what an experiment varies, block after block, and the wavelength a tunable source is set to while no axis varies it (spec 0046's `sourceWaveLengthOpt`, now the scan's); `member this.points : ScanPoint list` is the blocks' points in order; `member this.axes : ScanAxis list` the blocks' axes in order; `static member oneAxis (axis : ScanAxis) (capture : MeasurementMode) (sourceWaveLengthOpt : WaveLength option) : ExperimentScan` is one block of that one axis, today's experiment; and `static member darkLine (capture : MeasurementMode) : ExperimentScan` is one block of no axis and no wavelength. No validation, cache, unit conversion or other member is added: a tunable source's limits stay the host's clamp (spec 0046). Tests, in `ExperimentProxyTests`, over test-local element ids `sample` and `analyzer`: `a range sweeps its points evenly from its minimum to its maximum`: `{ min = 0; max = 360; points = 19 }` sweeps 0, 20, …, 360 exactly (dial 0…360 step 20); `{ min = 89; max = 0; points = 3 }` sweeps 89, 44.5 and 0; and a range of one point sweeps its two ends. `a scan block's points are the product of its axes, the first outermost, each read on the block's capture`: the block of `sample`'s R2 over 20…60° (3 points) and `sample`'s R1 over 0…90° (2 points), capture both, has the six points (20, 0), (20, 90), (40, 0), (40, 90), (60, 0), (60, 90) in that order, each with two settings naming `sample` and each `CaptureBoth`; and a block with no axis has one point with no setting. `a scan is its blocks' points in order, so one experiment joins two designs`: the scan of the block `sample`'s R1 over 0…67.5° (4 points) read in T, then the block above, has ten points, the first four `CaptureTransmitted` and the last six `CaptureBoth`, and its `axes` are the three axes in order; `oneAxis` of `analyzer`'s R1 axis read in T at 632.8 nm is one block of that axis keeping the wavelength; and `darkLine CaptureTransmitted` has one point and no wavelength.", "acceptance": "After the scan shapes land, `VariableRange.sweptValues` MUST be chartForRun's evenly spaced grid, `ScanBlock.points` MUST be the product of its axes with the first outermost and its capture on each point, and `ExperimentScan` MUST join its blocks' points in order and carry the tunable source's setting; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a range sweeps its points evenly from its minimum to its maximum`, `a scan block's points are the product of its axes, the first outermost, each read on the block's capture` and `a scan is its blocks' points in order, so one experiment joins two designs`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.a range sweeps its points evenly from its minimum to its maximum", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.a scan block's points are the product of its axes, the first outermost, each read on the block's capture", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.a scan is its blocks' points in order, so one experiment joins two designs", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.VariableRange.sweptValues", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ScanAxis", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ScanSetting", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ScanPoint", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ScanBlock", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentScan", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-SHAPES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 288, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [287], "how_to": "An experiment holds a scan, a role, a session and notes, and the draft builds a scan of any number of axes and blocks (001 §K '`Experiment` = one recorded run: a setup reference and a scan …; a capture (T / R, from the detectors); a role …; a session'; 001 §E notes live in the experiment's file; the S9.1 brief: today's single-variable experiments are one-variable scans). This is one step because the record's fields change every consumer at once (the step 261 precedent). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`. (a) `Experiment` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) becomes `{ id : ExperimentId; setup : SetupReference; scan : ExperimentScan; role : ExperimentRole; sessionOpt : SessionName option; notes : ExperimentNotes; dataFileOpt : DataAttachment option }`: `varied`, `measurement`, `range` and `sourceWaveLengthOpt` are the scan's (step 287), and `VariedElement` (step 261) and `Experiment.variedLabel` are deleted, `ScanAxis` being their successor. `description` keeps its two texts for the scans today's experiments are: one block of one axis is `<axis describe>, capture <capture.label>` (today's varied text exactly), and one block of no axis is step 261's `Dark line on setup <setup.describe>, capture <capture.label>`; any other scan is its blocks' texts joined by `; `, a block's text being its axes' `describe`s joined by ` × ` and then `, capture <capture.label>` (`Dark line, capture <label>` for a block of no axis). (b) `ExperimentDraft` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentDraft`) keeps its fields, the edited axis being `elementId`, `elementLabel`, `variable` and `range`, and gains `outerAxes : ScanAxis list` (the axes of the current block before the edited one, outermost first) and `closedBlocks : ScanBlock list` (the blocks before the current one), both `[]` in `empty`. `member this.axisOpt : ScanAxis option` is the edited axis once an element and a variable are chosen; `member this.scanOpt : ExperimentScan option` is, with it, `closedBlocks` followed by the block of `outerAxes` and the edited axis read on `measurement`, with `sourceWaveLengthOpt`. `ExperimentCollection.canCommit` (`Experiments.fs:canCommit`) matches `draft.axisOpt`, its answers unchanged. (c) `addScanAxis (c : ExperimentCollection) : ExperimentCollection`: with an edited axis, the draft's `outerAxes` gain it and its `elementId`, `elementLabel` and `variable` clear, its range becoming `VariableRange.forVariable VaryR1`; otherwise `c` unchanged. `addScanBlock (c : ExperimentCollection) : ExperimentCollection`: with an edited axis, `closedBlocks` gain the block of `outerAxes` and it read on `measurement`, `outerAxes` empties and the edited axis clears as above; otherwise `c` unchanged. `chooseElement` keeps `outerAxes` and `closedBlocks`, and `newDraft` clears them with the rest. (d) `commit` (`Experiments.fs:commit`, step 261's signature kept) builds from `draft.scanOpt`: an edited experiment takes the setup and the scan and keeps its role, session, notes and data file; an appended one is `ScienceRun`, with no session, `ExperimentNotes.none` and no data file. `commitOverSetups` (step 275) folds it as before. (e) `edit` (`Experiments.fs:edit`) splits the experiment's scan back: `closedBlocks` are every block but the last, the last block's capture is `measurement`, its axes but the last are `outerAxes`, and its last axis is the edited one (none for a block of no axis), with the scan's `sourceWaveLengthOpt`; so editing then committing gives the experiment back. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs`: `requestedWavelengthsOf` (`OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:requestedWavelengthsOf`) answers `SweptWavelengths` from the lowest `min` to the highest `max` of the scan's `VaryWaveLength` axes, each end through `toWaveLength Nanometer` as `requestedWavelengthsFor` reads one range, and `FixedWavelength fixedWavelength` when no axis varies the wavelength; `requestedWavelengthsFor` is unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `loadAndValidate` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`) validates through `MeasuredData.validateAgainstExperiment` (`MeasuredData.fs:validateAgainstExperiment`, unchanged) with the one axis's variable and range for a scan of one block of one axis, and with no variable and `VariableRange.forVariable VaryR1` for a scan of one block of no axis (the range every dark line held, step 50); for any other scan it reads nothing and answers `DataRangeMismatchErr` `an X,Y data file holds one variable, and the scan varies <n> in <m> block(s)` (S9.2's profiles map such files). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json` (steps 146, 261): under schema version 1, `experiment` holds exactly `id`, `setup`, `scan` (an object holding exactly `blocks`, an array, and `sourceWaveLengthOpt`), `role` (an integer from 1 to 7), `sessionOpt` (`null` or a string holding a non-white-space character), `notes` (a string) and `dataFileOpt`; the version stays 1, because no kit of the old shape exists outside test output (.spec-md §7). (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `chartForExperiment` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForExperiment`) runs `chartForRun` over the axis, the capture and the wavelength of a scan of one block of one axis, and answers the empty chart for any other scan until step 293 draws every scan. `SolverHandoffView.fs` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`) calls `loadAndValidate` as before and nothing in it changes. No message, view or other member changes in this step. (6) Every fixture that builds an `Experiment` builds its scan as `ExperimentScan.oneAxis` of the `ScanAxis` its `VariedElement` and range made, with the capture and wavelength it set, or as `ExperimentScan.darkLine` of its capture for a dark line, and sets `role = ScienceRun`, `sessionOpt = None` and `notes = ExperimentNotes.none`, every fact keeping its assertions: in `ExperimentProxyTests`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`, `KitContentFileJsonTests`, `KitLibraryTests`, `ExperimentCopyTests`, `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`, `SetupTests`, `SetupModelTests`, `KitWindowModelTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `InverseConstructorTests` and `KitWindowTests`, whichever of them build one; one the closing build finds anywhere else is re-pointed by the same rule. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `a committed experiment is a one-axis scan of the draft, a science run with no session and no notes`: `commit` of `Bench` revision 1 after `chooseElement` of `lp2` (R1, 0…90°, 10 points, capture T, 632.8 nm) appends an experiment whose scan is `oneAxis` of that axis, read in T at 632.8 nm, `ScienceRun`, no session and `ExperimentNotes.none`, its description the text `an experiment description mentions the element, the variable, and the capture` reads; and `an added axis and an added block commit as one multi-variable scan, and editing splits it back`: `chooseElement` of the sample (R2 over 20…60°, 3 points), `addScanAxis`, `chooseElement` of the sample (R1 over 0…90°, 2 points), capture both, `addScanBlock`, `chooseElement` of `lp2` (R1 over 0…67.5°, 4 points), capture T, then `commit`, appends one experiment whose scan has the blocks [R2 × R1, both] and [R1, T] in that order; `edit` of it gives a draft whose `closedBlocks`, `outerAxes`, edited axis and capture are those, and `commit` again leaves the experiment equal; `addScanAxis` of a draft with nothing chosen changes nothing. `KitContentFileJsonTests` (steps 146, 261): `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text` also round-trips E1 with that two-block scan, `CalibrationRun`, the session `Day 1` and the notes `LR was re-seated`; `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` also refuses `role` 0, `sessionOpt` `\"\"` and an experiment without `scan`. `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`: `requestedWavelengthsOf: a wavelength-sweep experiment requests its range; a dark line is fixed` also finds that a scan whose two blocks vary the wavelength over 300…500 nm and 400…700 nm requests 300…700 nm. `ExperimentDataProxyTests` (step 135) gains `loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan`: over its mock data proxy, the built-in library (`BuiltinCatalogue`) and slots whose detector slot is bound to `PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, an experiment of one axis whose range holds every abscissa of the canned intensity series answers that series, and the same experiment with a second axis answers `DataRangeMismatchErr` naming 2 variables and 1 block.", "acceptance": "After Experiment v2 lands, `Experiment` MUST hold `scan`, `role`, `sessionOpt` and `notes` in place of `varied`, `measurement`, `range` and `sourceWaveLengthOpt`, `VariedElement` MUST be gone, the draft MUST build a scan of several axes and blocks through `addScanAxis` and `addScanBlock`, `edit` MUST split it back, and the experiment file MUST round-trip it under schema version 1; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a committed experiment is a one-axis scan of the draft, a science run with no session and no notes`, `an added axis and an added block commit as one multi-variable scan, and editing splits it back` and `loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` and `requestedWavelengthsOf: a wavelength-sweep experiment requests its range; a dark line is fixed`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.a committed experiment is a one-axis scan of the draft, a science run with no session and no notes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.an added axis and an added block commit as one multi-variable scan, and editing splits it back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.requestedWavelengthsOf: a wavelength-sweep experiment requests its range; a dark line is fixed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.addScanAxis", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.addScanBlock", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentDraft.axisOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentDraft.scanOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.commit", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.edit", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.OutOfBandDiagnostic.requestedWavelengthsOf", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S91-EXPERIMENT-SCAN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 289, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [288], "how_to": "A dial-mounted item is scanned by its raw dial reading (001 §I 'Dial mapping: a rotatable item has a zero and a sign (`DialSign` exists). Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'; 001 §K 'dial 0…360 step 20'; the S8.2 mapper's request: dial scans record readings). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `VariableParameter` (`Experiments.fs:VariableParameter`) gains `VaryDialReading` after `VaryR2`, with `code` `dial`, `label` `Dial reading` and `unitLabel` `°`; `allowedFor` is unchanged, because a kind does not know its item's mounting; `VariableRange.forVariable VaryDialReading` is 0…360° over 19 points. Every match over the variable gains the case, no wildcard arm hiding it (FS0025): `MeasuredData.validateAgainstExperiment` treats it as `VaryR1` (no wavelength check), `OutOfBandDiagnostic.requestedWavelengthsFor` as a fixed wavelength, and the host's arms below. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`, after step 277's members: `type SetupSlot with member this.scanVariablesWith (items : Item list) : VariableParameter list` is `VariableParameter.allowedFor` of the slot's `placement.catalogueKind` with `VaryR1` replaced by `VaryDialReading` when the slot holds (`content.itemOpt`, step 256) an item of `items` whose `dial` is `DialMounted _` (step 222): the angle of such an item is a reading, and the table records readings (step 258's `recordedWith`). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`: the domain-free mirror `VariableChoice` (`ExperimentControls.fs:VariableChoice`) gains `VaryDialReading`, `uiKey` `dial` and `caption` `Dial reading`, and `allVariables` (`ExperimentControls.fs:allVariables`) lists it last, so the bay draws its box under `ConstructorUiId.experimentVariable`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the domain ⇄ Controls mirror maps gain the case; `ExpChooseElement` and the bay's `variableChoices` read `slot.scanVariablesWith model.kitItems` where they read `VariableParameter.allowedFor`; and `chartForRun` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun`) sweeps a `VaryDialReading` of the varied slot as it sweeps `VaryR1`, each swept reading x evaluated at the physical angle `sign.physicalAngleOf item.dialZeroAngle (Angle.degree x)` of the slot's item (steps 255, 258), with `xLabel` `Dial reading (°)`, the vary text `the dial reading over <lo>…<hi>°`, the title `<quantity> vs dial reading` and `AngularXAxis`; a slot whose item is not dial-mounted is never offered the variable. No other variable, option or conversion is added. Tests. `SetupTests` gains `a dial-mounted item's slot scans its dial reading where a fixed one scans R1`: over its `lpA` slot and step 277's items, holding `LP1` (fixed) it scans `[ VaryR1 ]`, holding a test-local `LPd` (`DialMounted DialNegative`, `dialZero` known at 10°) `[ VaryDialReading ]`, and `sampleA` holding `QZd` scans `[ VaryDialReading; VaryR2 ]`; and `VariableRange.forVariable VaryDialReading` sweeps 0, 20, …, 360. `ExperimentControlsTests` (ui-tests) gains `a dial scan draws the run at the physical angle of each reading`: over a table whose analyzer slot holds `LPd` behind a linear polarizer, choosing it offers the `dial` box and no `r1` box, and the draft's chart over readings 0…360° (19 points) equals, point for point within 1e-12, the chart of the same table with a fixed analyzer varied in R1 over the physical angles `DialNegative.physicalAngleOf 10° x`, its x values being the readings. Every other fact passes as written; `ElementMenuTests`, `FsxAcceptanceTests`, `InverseConstructorTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests` and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests` name `VariableChoice` cases and compile as they are, nothing in them changing.", "acceptance": "After the dial reading lands, `VariableParameter.VaryDialReading` MUST be offered for a slot holding a dial-mounted item in place of R1 (`SetupSlot.scanVariablesWith`), its default range MUST be 0-360° in steps of 20, and chartForRun MUST evaluate each reading at its physical angle; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a dial-mounted item's slot scans its dial reading where a fixed one scans R1`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a dial scan draws the run at the physical angle of each reading`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementMenuTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.a dial-mounted item's slot scans its dial reading where a fixed one scans R1", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-DIAL-READING"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a dial scan draws the run at the physical angle of each reading", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S91-DIAL-READING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.scanVariablesWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S91-DIAL-READING"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.VariableChoice", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-DIAL-READING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 290, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [289], "how_to": "Experiments are named by the kit's template and stored as `<name>.experiment-json` (001 §A kit layout `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL.experiment-json`; 001 §J the template names setups and experiments; the S9.1 brief; the S6 mapper's request: `renumberedFor`'s rule carries over to names; the S8.4 mapper's request: the slot bar's `RecordExperiment` names its experiment by the template). This is one step because the record gains a field every consumer builds. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: (a) `Experiment` gains `name : ExperimentName` after `id`, and `ExperimentId.fileStem` (step 146) is deleted: the stem is the name's (step 286). (b) `ExperimentTarget = { setup : SetupReference; name : ExperimentName }`, one experiment to append: its setup revision and its name. `commit (target : ExperimentTarget) (c : ExperimentCollection)` names an appended experiment `target.name` over `target.setup`; an edited experiment takes `target.setup` and keeps its name, so an experiment is never renamed by an edit. `commitOverSetups (targets : ExperimentTarget list)` folds it over the targets in order, as step 275's fold over references. (c) `static member renamedFor (taken : ExperimentName list) (incoming : Experiment list) : Experiment list` on `Experiment`, beside step 203's `renumberedFor`: in order, an incoming experiment keeps its name when no name of `taken` and no name given to an earlier incoming experiment has its `fileStem` ignoring case; otherwise it takes `name.nextFreeAmong` of those; only `name` changes. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs`, after step 286's member: `type NamingTemplate with member this.experimentTargets (setups : Setup list) (items : Item list) (taken : ExperimentName list) (firstId : ExperimentId) : ExperimentTarget list`: for each setup in order, the target of its `reference` named by `experimentNameAmong setup.slots items None (taken followed by the names given so far) id.defaultName`, `id` starting at `firstId` and advancing by `next` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentId`), so the unnamed fallback is the id the experiment receives. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 148, 205, 261): `writeExperiment` writes `ExperimentKitFile` under `experiment.name.fileStem`; `deleteExperiment (name : ExperimentName)` deletes `name.fileStem`; `readExperiments` refuses, as `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file, a file whose experiment's `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case (it compared `id.fileStem`); and `copyExperimentsFrom`, after `renumberedFor`, applies `renamedFor` over the names of `this.proxy.readExperiments ()`, an id the source lacks still being `MissingKitFileErr` of the `ExperimentKitFile` name of its `defaultName`'s stem, so its texts are unchanged. `schema/experiment.schema.json` requires `name`, a string holding a non-white-space character, after `id`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the private function that records the experiments a commit appended (step 278) is unchanged; the three callers name what they append through `model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate.experimentTargets` (step 267) over the setups they commit over, `model.kitItems`, the names of `model.experimentCollection.experiments` and the collection's `nextId`: `ExpCommit` appending over the recorded setup (an edit passes the target of that setup and keeps the name), `RecordExperiment` over the active setup and `GenerateSetupGrid` over the generated setups, each then calling `commit` / `commitOverSetups` with the targets. `ExpRemove` deletes the removed experiment's file through `deleteExperiment` of its name. `RecordExperiment`'s status names the experiment, `Recorded <name.value> over <reference.describe>.`, which for a table the template cannot name is today's `Recorded E2 over 'Bench' revision 1.`. (5) Every fixture that builds an `Experiment` sets `name = <its id>.defaultName`, so every file it writes keeps its `E<n>` name and every fact its assertions (the files of step 288's list). Tests. `KitContentFileJsonTests`: `an experiment is stored under its id` is renamed `an experiment is stored under its name`: `ExperimentKitFile.fileNameOf (ExperimentName \"CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL\").fileStem` is `FileName \"CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL.experiment-json\"` and `(ExperimentId 3).defaultName.fileStem` is `FileStem \"E3\"`; its schema fact also refuses an experiment without `name` and one whose `name` is `\"  \"`. `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`: `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file` is renamed `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the read, naming the file`, its second file holding E1 under the stem `E6` (another name). `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `copied experiments keep their names unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free suffix`: with `taken` [`CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`], incoming experiments named `cpl-(qz#45)-cpl` and `E3` answer `cpl-(qz#45)-cpl (2)` and `E3`, in that order; with `taken` empty they are unchanged; every field but `name` is unchanged; its commit facts pass targets named by `defaultName`, their assertions kept. `NamingTemplateTests` gains `the experiments of new setups are named by the template over each setup's slots, each free among the kit's and the earlier ones`: `lab`'s targets over the setups `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL` and `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL` (made from step 271's slots) with `taken` [`CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`] and `firstId` E4 are `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL (2)` and `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL`, each over its setup's reference, and over a setup the template cannot name the first is `E4`. `ExperimentCopyTests` (steps 205, 240, 261) gains `a copied experiment whose name the target holds takes the next free name`: copying [E1] into a target holding an experiment named `E1` (another id) writes the copy as `E1 (2).experiment-json` and the report names it so. `SetupModelTests`: `a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name` (step 272) also finds `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.experiment-json`, E1 being named so; `GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each` (step 276) finds `LP1-(QZ#0)-LPd.experiment-json` and `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.experiment-json` in place of `E1` and `E2`; and `a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing` finds the second run's experiments as `LP1-(QZ#0)-LPd (2)` and `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd (2)`. Every other fact, the UI facts that find `E<n>.experiment-json` included, passes as written, because their tables hold no item the template needs.", "acceptance": "After experiments are named, `Experiment.name` MUST be the file stem every experiment is written, read, deleted and copied under, a new experiment MUST be named by the kit's template over its setup (made free) or `E<n>`, and a copied experiment whose name the target holds MUST take the next free name; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `copied experiments keep their names unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free suffix`, `the experiments of new setups are named by the template over each setup's slots, each free among the kit's and the earlier ones` and `a copied experiment whose name the target holds takes the next free name`, the count rising by 3, the renamed `an experiment is stored under its name` and `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the read, naming the file` and the changed `a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name`, `GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each` and `a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.copied experiments keep their names unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free suffix", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests.the experiments of new setups are named by the template over each setup's slots, each free among the kit's and the earlier ones", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/NamingTemplateTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.NamingTemplateTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copied experiment whose name the target holds takes the next free name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an experiment is stored under its id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an experiment is stored under its name", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.an experiment file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the read, naming the file", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupModelTests.a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentTarget", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.Experiment.renamedFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.commit", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.commitOverSetups", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentId.fileStem", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.NamingTemplates.NamingTemplate.experimentTargets", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.deleteExperiment", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeExperiment", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readExperiments", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S91-NAMED-FILES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 291, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [290], "how_to": "An experiment's data is a kit file mapped through a named import profile to a selection of its rows (001 §K 'the data attachment: a relative path + hash + import profile + row selection'; 001 §K 'One file → many experiments: split by a key column'; the S9.1 brief: a `DataAttachment` + an import-profile name + a row selection, profiles arriving in S9.2). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, after step 132's `DataAttachmentStatus`: (a) `ImportProfileName of string` with `.value`, the name a kit's import profile is stored and picked under (S9.2 stores the profiles in `.kit-json`): `static member tryCreate (text : string) : ImportProfileName option` keeps the text and answers `None` for an empty or white-space text; `static member intensitySeries : ImportProfileName` = `Intensity series` and `static member ellipsometricSeries : ImportProfileName` = `Ellipsometric series`, the built-in profiles over `DataFileText.parseIntensitySeries` and `parseEllipsometricSeries` (`MeasuredData.fs`), which S9.2 makes profiles under these names. (b) `DataRowKey of string` with `.value`, one value of a profile's experiment-key column. (c) `DataRowSelection` = `AllDataRows` (every row of the file) | `KeyedDataRows of key : DataRowKey` (the rows whose key column holds the key). (d) `MappedAttachment = { attachment : DataAttachment; profile : ImportProfileName; rows : DataRowSelection }`. No int tag is added: the cases are written in the serializer's case form, as `SlotTurn`'s are. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `Experiment.dataFileOpt` becomes `dataOpt : MappedAttachment option`, and `attachDataFile` (`Experiments.fs:attachDataFile`) takes `(data : MappedAttachment)`; `commit` keeps an edited experiment's `dataOpt` and gives an appended one `None`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: (a) `type DetectorKind with member this.builtInProfile : ImportProfileName` answers `intensitySeries` for `Intensity` and `ellipsometricSeries` for `Ellipsometer`. (b) `loadAndValidate` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`) takes `(data : MappedAttachment)` in place of the attachment and reads the file by its profile: `intensitySeries` through `tryLoadIntensity` and `ellipsometricSeries` through `tryLoadEllipsometric`, of `data.attachment`; any other profile name answers `MalformedDataFileErr` `the import profile '<name>' is not available` and reads nothing; `KeyedDataRows key` answers `MalformedDataFileErr` `<path>: an X,Y data file has no key column to select '<key>' by` and reads nothing. The series is then validated against the detector kind and the scan exactly as step 288 left it, so a profile that does not fit the detector is `validateAgainstExperiment`'s `DataUnitsMismatchErr`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage`: `schema/experiment.schema.json` replaces `dataFileOpt` with `dataOpt`, `null` or an object holding exactly `attachment` (the `path` and `contentHash` object step 146 described), `profile` (a string holding a non-white-space character) and `rows` (an object); `KitContentFiles.copyExperimentsFrom` (steps 205, 261) reads each distinct `dataOpt` attachment path and gives each copied experiment the new attachment of its path, its profile and rows kept. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui`: `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`'s `AttachDataFileTo` arm (steps 135, 261) attaches `{ attachment = <the kit's attachment>; profile = (detectorKindOf model.library <the experiment's slots>).builtInProfile; rows = AllDataRows }` and its validation, the one private validation function's, passes the mapped attachment; `dataFileRow` shows `file: <path> (<profile>)`. `SolverHandoffView.fs`'s `validateExperiment` and `handoffFileCaption` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`) read `dataOpt`, the caption adding the profile. (6) Every fixture attachment becomes the `MappedAttachment` of it with `ImportProfileName.intensitySeries` (an ellipsometric fixture `ellipsometricSeries`) and `AllDataRows`, every fact keeping its assertions: in `ExperimentProxyTests`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`, `KitContentFileJsonTests`, `ExperimentCopyTests`, `KitWindowModelTests`, `ExperimentDataProxyTests`, `InverseConstructorTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests` and `KitWindowTests`, whichever of them build one. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `an import profile name refuses a blank text, a row selection names every row or one key, and the two built-in names are the X,Y parsers'`: `ImportProfileName.tryCreate \"Phone ROI CSV\"` keeps the text, `\"\"` and `\"  \"` answer `None`, the two built-in names are `Intensity series` and `Ellipsometric series`, `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey \"CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL\")` differs from `AllDataRows`, and `Intensity.builtInProfile` / `Ellipsometer.builtInProfile` are those two names. `ExperimentDataProxyTests` gains `loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve`: over its mock proxy, step 288's one-axis experiment (its range holding the canned abscissae) mapped by `intensitySeries` answers the canned intensity series; mapped by `ellipsometricSeries` it answers `DataUnitsMismatchErr`; mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` it answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the profile; and with `KeyedDataRows` it answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the key, the last two reading nothing from the mock. `KitContentFileJsonTests`: `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text` also round-trips an attachment mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to the rows keyed `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`; `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` also refuses `dataOpt.profile` `\"\"` and a `dataOpt` without `rows`. `ExperimentProxyTests`: `attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment` binds mapped attachments, its assertions kept. `InverseConstructorTests` (step 135): `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment` also finds the attachment mapped by `Intensity series` over every row. `ExperimentCopyTests` gains `a copy keeps each copied experiment's import profile and row selection`: an experiment whose data is mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to the rows keyed `K1` is copied with the new attachment of its path and that profile and selection.", "acceptance": "After the mapped attachment lands, `Experiment.dataOpt` MUST hold a `MappedAttachment` (attachment, import-profile name, row selection), the file MUST be read by its profile with an unavailable profile or a key selection refused typed, an attach MUST record the detector's built-in profile over every row, and the experiment file MUST round-trip it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an import profile name refuses a blank text, a row selection names every row or one key, and the two built-in names are the X,Y parsers'`, `loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve` and `a copy keeps each copied experiment's import profile and row selection`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` and `attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including the changed `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.an import profile name refuses a blank text, a row selection names every row or one key, and the two built-in names are the X,Y parsers'", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests.a copy keeps each copied experiment's import profile and row selection", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCopyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentCopyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentProxyTests.attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ImportProfileName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.DataRowKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.DataRowSelection", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.MappedAttachment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.attachDataFile", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.DetectorKind.builtInProfile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-MAPPED-ATTACHMENT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 292, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [291], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests"], "how_to": "Building a multi-variable scan as semantic messages (001 §K 'one or more variables'; 001 §P: every user step is a semantic message; .spec-md §4 UI). The bay's buttons that send them are step 296's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `ExpAddScanAxis` (Add variable: the edited axis joins the current block and the editor takes the next) and `ExpAddScanBlock` (Add block: the current block closes and a new one starts), each with a one-line doc. Neither writes the kit, so neither passes the read-only guard of step 185, as the other `Exp*` draft messages do not. `ExpAddScanAxis` is `Experiments.addScanAxis` (step 288) of the collection. `ExpAddScanBlock` first gives the draft the capture the detectors allow (`model.draftCapture`, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:draftCapture`, through `chooseMeasurement`, as `ExpCommit` does) and then `Experiments.addScanBlock`; with no capture it changes nothing. `ExpCommit`, `RecordExperiment` and `GenerateSetupGrid` commit the draft's whole scan through `commit` / `commitOverSetups` (step 288), their texts unchanged. No other message, field or option is added. (2) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs`, `module ExperimentModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended to `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment; its kit is a folder under the class's test directory opened read-write, as `SetupModelTests`' is (step 260), and its table holds the seeded source and detector, a linear polarizer and a sample bound to the 1 mm glass plate (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId`), added and bound as step 263's facts add and bind elements. `Add variable and Add block build the draft's scan, and a commit records it as one experiment`: the sample chosen (`ExpChooseElement`), `ExpChooseVariable VaryR2`, the range 20…60° over 3 points (`ExpSetRangeMin`, `ExpSetRangeMax`, `ExpSetRangePoints`), `ExpAddScanAxis`, the sample chosen again with `ExpChooseVariable VaryR1` over 0…90° in 2 points, `ExpAddScanBlock`, the polarizer chosen with R1 over 0…67.5° in 4 points, then `ExpCommit`: the folder holds one experiment file whose scan read back has the blocks [R2 × R1] and [R1] in that order, each read on the capture the detectors allow, and the draft edits it. `Add variable without a chosen element and variable changes nothing and writes nothing`: after `ExpNew`, `ExpAddScanAxis` and `ExpAddScanBlock` leave the model equal and the folder's files unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the scan messages land, `ExpAddScanAxis` and `ExpAddScanBlock` MUST build the draft's scan through `addScanAxis` / `addScanBlock`, writing nothing, and a commit MUST record the whole scan as one experiment; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Add variable and Add block build the draft's scan, and a commit records it as one experiment` and `Add variable without a chosen element and variable changes nothing and writes nothing`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.Add variable and Add block build the draft's scan, and a commit records it as one experiment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.Add variable without a chosen element and variable changes nothing and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-MESSAGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ExpAddScanAxis", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.ExpAddScanBlock", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-MESSAGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 293, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [292], "how_to": "The experiment chart, the pop-out chart and Export data read the whole scan (the S9.1 brief: the Experiments bay, the experiment chart (`ExperimentChart.fs`, `chartForRun`) and the export path read v2; .spec-md §6: `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun` and the run law are reused). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `chartForRun` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun`, as steps 252, 265, 266 and 289 left it) takes `(model)` and `(scan : Experiments.ExperimentScan)` in place of the chosen element, variable, capture, range, label and wavelength, and `chartForParams` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForParams`), which nothing calls, is deleted. For each block with at least one axis, in order: its last axis is the x axis and its element the varied one whose captures (`model.captureDetectors`) and analyzer check (`noPolarizerOnPath`) apply as today; the x values are the axis's `sweptValues` (step 287), a `VaryR2` axis's range first clamped to [0, `Propagation.r2SweepMaxDegrees`] as today; and the points of its other axes (their product, first outermost) each give one group of series. Each path step is built once per block from the settings that touch it: a polarizer turns to a `VaryR1` setting on it, or to the physical angle of a `VaryDialReading` setting on it (step 289), else its R1; a sample takes its incidence from a `VaryR2` setting on it, its spin from a `VaryR1` or `VaryDialReading` setting on it, else its drawn incidence and R1; every element runs at a `VaryWaveLength` setting, else at `operatingWaveLength model scan.sourceWaveLengthOpt`; a step no setting of the block touches is built once (today's `FixedStep`), so a sample is re-solved only when something it depends on varies. Each group reads every captured branch as today, one series per branch and reading (`Intensity`, `Ψ`, `Δ`). A scan of one block of one axis gives exactly today's chart: series names, labels, title and description. Otherwise a series' name is today's name, then ` — ` and its group's settings as `<axis label>: <variable.label> <%g value><unit>` joined by `, `, then `, block <k>` when the scan has more than one block; the x label joins the distinct x-axis variables' labels with ` / `; `xAxisKind` is `AngularXAxis` when every x-axis variable is an angle (R1, R2, dial) and `NonAngularXAxis` otherwise; the title is today's title of the first block's x axis; and the description names the scan by `Experiment.description`'s block texts (step 288) in place of `varied element: …`. A block with no axis gives no series, and a scan of no series is the empty chart. (2) `model.experimentResult` charts `draft.scanOpt` with its last block read on `model.draftCapture`, empty when either is missing; `chartForExperiment` charts the experiment's scan, so step 288's one-axis limit goes; Export data (`exportDraftRun`, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:exportDraftRun`) and the pop-out window read `experimentResult` as before (`ExperimentExport.fs:ExportedRun` unchanged), so the export carries every series. (3) `AGENTS.md`'s gotcha 'An experiment runs on the light's real path' says, in no more words, that an experiment's chart is its scan's: one series per value of the outer axes and captured branch, over the last axis of each block. No cache, option or other member is added. Tests (`ExperimentControlsTests`, ui-tests, over its table with a sample between a linear polarizer and two detectors, one on each branch): `a two-variable scan draws one series per value of its outer variable, read on each captured branch`: the draft of the sample's R2 over 20…60° (3 points), Add variable (`ExpAddScanAxis`), the sample's R1 over 0…90° (2 points), capture both, charts six intensity series, two per incidence (T and R), each over the x values 0 and 90, named `Intensity (T) — <sample label>: Incidence R2 20°` and so on, and each series' points equal the one-axis draft of R1 over 0…90° with the sample's incidence turned to that value, within 1e-12. `a collected multi-block experiment's chart holds every block's series`: a committed experiment of two blocks (the sample's R1 over 0…67.5° in 4 points read in T, then the block above) charts the first block's one series and the second block's six, the second's names ending `, block 2`. `the export of a two-variable draft carries every series of its chart` : Export data on the two-variable draft exports one run holding the chart's six series. `FsxAcceptanceTests` and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests` pass as written: their one-axis numbers are unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the chart reads the scan, `chartForRun` MUST draw every block of an `ExperimentScan`, one series per value of the outer axes and captured branch over the block's last axis, a one-axis scan giving today's chart exactly, and the draft chart, the collected chart and Export data MUST read it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a two-variable scan draws one series per value of its outer variable, read on each captured branch`, `a collected multi-block experiment's chart holds every block's series` and `the export of a two-variable draft carries every series of its chart`, the count rising by 3, with `FsxAcceptanceTests` unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a two-variable scan draws one series per value of its outer variable, read on each captured branch", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-CHART"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.a collected multi-block experiment's chart holds every block's series", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-CHART"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.the export of a two-variable draft carries every series of its chart", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-CHART"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-CHART"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForParams", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-CHART"], "preserves_obligations": ["S91-SCAN-CHART"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForExperiment", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S91-SCAN-CHART"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 294, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [293], "how_to": "Setting a recorded experiment's role, session and notes as semantic messages that write its file (001 §P `SetExperimentRole`; 001 §E 'notes on experiments … live in their files, so a reviewer's comments come back in the returned folder'; 001 §K role and session). The bay's controls that send them are step 296's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, after `Experiment`: `type Experiment with` `member this.withRole (role : ExperimentRole) : Experiment`, `member this.withSessionOpt (sessionOpt : SessionName option) : Experiment` and `member this.withNotes (notes : ExperimentNotes) : Experiment`, each the experiment with that field; and on `ExperimentCollection` `member this.withStoredExperiment (experiment : Experiment) : ExperimentCollection`, the collection with its experiment of that id replaced, unchanged when it holds none, the draft untouched. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `SetExperimentRole of Experiments.ExperimentId * Experiments.ExperimentRole`, `SetExperimentSession of Experiments.ExperimentId * ControlCaption` (the typed text; a blank text clears the session) and `SetExperimentNotes of Experiments.ExperimentId * ControlCaption`, each with a one-line doc. Each arm is refused by the read-only guard of step 185, which every write message calls. Otherwise, for the collection's experiment of that id (none: the model is unchanged and nothing is written), the changed experiment (`withRole`; `withSessionOpt (SessionName.tryCreate text.value)`; `withNotes (ExperimentNotes text.value)`) is recorded through `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` (step 261 (7)(b)); on success the collection takes it (`withStoredExperiment`), and a failure keeps the model with `kitStatus` `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. An experiment's role, session and notes change nothing else: its scan, setup, name and data stay. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `ExperimentModelTests` (step 292), over its folder kit with E1 committed: `SetExperimentRole, SetExperimentSession and SetExperimentNotes change the stored experiment and its kit file`: `SetExperimentRole (E1, CalibrationRun)`, `SetExperimentSession (E1, ControlCaption \"Day 1\")` and `SetExperimentNotes (E1, ControlCaption \"LR re-seated before this run\")` leave the collection's E1 with that role, `Some (SessionName \"Day 1\")` and those notes, its scan unchanged, and `E1.experiment-json` read back through `readExperiments` holds the same three. `a blank session clears it, and a change to an experiment the kit lacks writes nothing`: then `SetExperimentSession (E1, ControlCaption \"  \")` gives `sessionOpt = None` in the model and the file; `SetExperimentRole (ExperimentId 9, DarkRun)` leaves the model equal and every file's bytes unchanged. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 185, 278): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends the three messages, with the same assertions.", "acceptance": "After the bookkeeping messages land, `SetExperimentRole`, `SetExperimentSession` and `SetExperimentNotes` MUST change the stored experiment's role, session (a blank text clearing it) and notes and write its kit file, refused under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `SetExperimentRole, SetExperimentSession and SetExperimentNotes change the stored experiment and its kit file` and `a blank session clears it, and a change to an experiment the kit lacks writes nothing`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.SetExperimentRole, SetExperimentSession and SetExperimentNotes change the stored experiment and its kit file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests.a blank session clears it, and a change to an experiment the kit lacks writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentModelTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentModelTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitWindowModelTests.a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitWindowModelTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.Experiment.withRole", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.Experiment.withSessionOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.Experiment.withNotes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Experiments.ExperimentCollection.withStoredExperiment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetExperimentRole", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetExperimentSession", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationMsg.SetExperimentNotes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BOOKKEEPING-MESSAGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 295, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [294], "how_to": "Each experiment's data status as one pure Domain badge (001 §K 'Status badges: no data / mapped / validated (points) / excluded points / data changed / out of range'; 001 §E 'A changed or missing data file is flagged'; AGENTS.md: behaviour lives in Domain, the view projects it). The window's `ExperimentFileStatus` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:ExperimentFileStatus`) is that status today, so it MOVES into Domain as the badge and is deleted, one type remaining (AGENTS.md 'A bijection is collapsed'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`, after `loadAndValidate`: `ExperimentDataBadge` = `NoDataBadge` (no data) | `MappedDataBadge of problemOpt : ExperimentDataError option` (mapped: a mapped attachment whose points are not validated, with the reason when the file did not read) | `ValidatedDataBadge of points : MeasuredPointCount` (validated, with its points) | `DataChangedBadge of attachment : DataAttachment * currentOpt : ContentHash option` (data changed since attach: the file's hash now, or `None` when it is missing) | `OutOfRangeBadge of problem : ExperimentDataError` (out of range: a range or units mismatch). `member this.text : string` answers `no data`, `mapped`, `validated (<n> points)`, `data changed` and `out of range`. `static member ofCheck (dataOpt : MappedAttachment option) (statusOpt : DataAttachmentStatus option) (outcomeOpt : Result<MeasuredSeries, ExperimentDataError> option) : ExperimentDataBadge` is the one rule: no data is `NoDataBadge`; a status `AttachedDataChanged current` or `AttachedDataMissing` (step 132) is `DataChangedBadge` of the attachment and `Some current` or `None`; an `Ok series` is `ValidatedDataBadge series.pointCount` (`MeasuredData.fs:pointCount`); an `Error` of `DataRangeMismatchErr` or `DataUnitsMismatchErr` is `OutOfRangeBadge`; any other `Error` is `MappedDataBadge (Some e)`; and no outcome is `MappedDataBadge None`. 001's excluded-points badge needs the experiment's exclusions, which S9.3 adds (its `ExcludePoint`), so it arrives with them. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ExperimentFileStatus` and `ExperimentDataError.fileStatus` are deleted; `experimentDataStatus` (step 136) holds an `ExperimentDataBadge` per experiment; the one private validation function (steps 136, 152, 187) and the `AttachDataFileTo` arm compute it by `ofCheck` from the experiment's `dataOpt`, the `attachmentStatus` read (a `KitError` of that read being `MalformedDataFileErr` of its `describe`, as `ExperimentDataStore` maps one, step 135) and the `loadAndValidate` result; an attach the kit refuses keeps the experiment's data and badge and sets `kitStatus` to `Not attached — <e.describe>`. `model.dataBadgeOf (experiment : Experiments.Experiment) : ExperimentDataBadge` is the map's badge, else `ofCheck experiment.dataOpt None None`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type ExperimentDataBadge with member this.caption : ControlCaption` keeps every caption the window showed: `No data`, `Mapped — not validated`, `Parse error — <e.caption>` for a reason, `Loaded — <n> point(s), schema-valid`, `Data changed since attach — attach it again to validate it`, `Data file missing — <path>` and `Validation error — <e.caption>`; `dataFileRow` shows it. Tests. `ExperimentDataProxyTests` gains `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation`: `ofCheck` of no data is `NoDataBadge` whatever else is given; of a mapped attachment with a changed status `DataChangedBadge` naming the new hash, with a missing one `DataChangedBadge` with `None`, ahead of any outcome; with an `Ok` of the canned intensity series `ValidatedDataBadge` of its `pointCount`; with `DataRangeMismatchErr` and with `DataUnitsMismatchErr` `OutOfRangeBadge`; with `MalformedDataFileErr` `MappedDataBadge (Some _)`; with nothing `MappedDataBadge None`; and the five texts. `InverseConstructorTests` (steps 135, 136, 152): `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status` and `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing` assert `ValidatedDataBadge`, `MappedDataBadge (Some _)`, `OutOfRangeBadge` and `DataChangedBadge` where they asserted the status cases, their captions unchanged; `a picked file the kit cannot attach records a typed attach-failed status and no attachment` is renamed `a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why`: the experiment's `dataOpt` stays `None`, its badge `NoDataBadge`, and `kitStatus` holds the reason. `ScrollExtentTests` passes as written.", "acceptance": "After the data badges land, `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck` MUST be the one rule giving no data / mapped / validated (points) / data changed / out of range from an experiment's mapped attachment, its file's status and its validation, `ExperimentFileStatus` MUST be gone with every caption kept, and an attach the kit refuses MUST be told in the kit status; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including the renamed `a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why` and the changed `attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment`, `attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status`, `attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status` and `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing`, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.a picked file the kit cannot attach records a typed attach-failed status and no attachment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.a picked file the kit cannot attach records no attachment and tells the kit status why", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching a valid intensity file records a typed Loaded status and the attachment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching a malformed intensity file records a typed parse-error status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.attaching an out-of-range intensity file records a typed validation-error status", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests.opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.ExperimentDataBadge", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.ExperimentFileStatus", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"], "preserves_obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.dataBadgeOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ExperimentDataBadge.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S91-DATA-BADGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 296, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [295], "how_to": "The Experiments bay shows and builds v2: the scan's axes and blocks, the edited experiment's role, session and notes, and each row's name, role and data badge (the S9.1 brief: the Experiments bay reads v2; 001 §O 'Automation: every new control gets a stable id'; .spec-md §4 UI: the bay stays domain-free and the button and the test send the same message). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`: (a) `ExperimentRoleMark` = `RoleChosen` | `RoleNotChosen` and `ExperimentRoleOption = { key : ConstructorUiKey; caption : ControlCaption; mark : ExperimentRoleMark }`, one role box. (b) `ExperimentRow` (`ExperimentControls.fs:ExperimentRow`) gains `badge : ControlCaption`, the data badge's text, after `description`. (c) `ExperimentControlsState` (`ExperimentControls.fs:ExperimentControlsState`) gains `scanLines : ControlCaption list` (the closed blocks and the current block's held axes), `scanAvailability : ControlAvailability` (Add variable and Add block), `roleOptions : ExperimentRoleOption list`, `sessionText : ControlCaption`, `notesText : ControlCaption` and `bookkeepingAvailability : ControlAvailability` (present while an experiment is loaded in a writable kit), each empty or withheld in `emptyExperimentControls`. `ExperimentControlsHandlers` (`ExperimentControls.fs:ExperimentControlsHandlers`) gains `addScanAxis : unit -> unit`, `addScanBlock : unit -> unit`, `setRole : ConstructorUiKey -> unit`, `setSession : ControlCaption -> unit` and `setNotes : ControlCaption -> unit`. (d) The view: under the range rows, the scan lines (a `TextBlock` per line in the panel `experimentScanSummary`) and the two buttons `Add variable` and `Add block`, beside Add and New in the box look `actionButton` draws; while `bookkeepingAvailability` is present, a role row of the seven boxes (`optionBoxV`, the chosen one in the chosen colour), a `Session:` field and a `Notes:` field committing on Enter and on losing focus as `numberField` does; each collection row shows its badge text beside its description. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: `experimentScanSummary` (`ExperimentScanSummary`), `experimentAddScanAxisButton` (`ExperimentAddScanAxisButton`), `experimentAddScanBlockButton` (`ExperimentAddScanBlockButton`), `experimentRoleChoice (role : ConstructorUiKey)` (`ExperimentRole_<key>`), `experimentSessionField` (`ExperimentSessionField`), `experimentNotesField` (`ExperimentNotesField`) and `experimentRowBadge (experiment : ConstructorUiKey)` (`ExperimentBadge_<key>`), each a uniquely named static member. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type ExperimentRole with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (`science`, `calibration`, `dark`, `drift-check`, `diagnostic`, `ignored`, `planned`) and `member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `text`). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `model.experimentState` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:experimentState`) fills the fields: each closed block as `Block <k>: <its text>` and the held axes as `This block: <their describes joined by \" × \">` (step 288's texts); `scanAvailability` as `addAvailability`; for the edited experiment the seven roles in tag order, its session's text (empty for none) and its notes, `bookkeepingAvailability` present only when the draft edits an experiment and the kit is writable (step 185's access); each row's `description` `<name> [<role.text>] — <description>` and `badge` `model.dataBadgeOf`'s `text` (step 295). `experimentHandlers` sends `ExpAddScanAxis`, `ExpAddScanBlock` (step 292) and, for the edited experiment's id, `SetExperimentRole` (the role whose `uiKey` is pressed), `SetExperimentSession` and `SetExperimentNotes` (step 294). No other control, option or message is added. Tests (`ExperimentControlsTests`, ui-tests unless named): `the bay's scan, role, session and notes UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the seven ids above are stable (`ExperimentScanSummary`, `ExperimentRole_calibration`, `ExperimentBadge_3`, …). `Add variable and Add block list the held axes and blocks under the range`: over the bay's model, choosing the sample's R2 and pressing `experimentAddScanAxisButton`, then the sample's R1 and `experimentAddScanBlockButton`, shows the summary lines `Block 1: …R2… × …R1…, capture …` in order, and the two buttons are withheld with nothing chosen. `an experiment loaded in the editor shows its role, session and notes, and a press on a role sends it`: with E1 committed and loaded (`ExpEdit`), the role row shows `Science` chosen, the session and notes fields are empty, and pressing `experimentRoleChoice` of `calibration` leaves E1 a `CalibrationRun` with `Calibration` chosen; with no experiment loaded the row is absent. `each collected experiment's row shows its name, its role and its data badge`: E1 committed shows a row reading `E1 [Science] — …` and the badge `no data`. ui-smoke `pressing Add variable between two axes and Add records one two-variable experiment` : pressing the sample's candidate, `ExperimentVariable_r2`, `experimentAddScanAxisButton`, the candidate, `ExperimentVariable_r1` and `experimentAddButton` records one experiment whose scan has two axes in one block. `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`' handler record gains the five fields as `ignore`, every fact keeping its assertions. `ScrollExtentTests`: `Inverse: the Experiments bay with its data-file section leaves everything reachable` also loads an experiment into the editor, so the role row, the two fields and the scan summary are in the bay it scrolls, its assertion kept. `ElementMenuTests` and `InverseConstructorTests` read `experimentState` fields that keep their meaning, and nothing in them changes.", "acceptance": "After the bay reads v2, it MUST show the draft's scan lines with Add variable and Add block, the loaded experiment's role, session and notes sending `SetExperimentRole` / `SetExperimentSession` / `SetExperimentNotes`, and each row's name, role and data badge, under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Add variable between two axes and Add records one two-variable experiment`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the bay's scan, role, session and notes UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `Add variable and Add block list the held axes and blocks under the range`, `an experiment loaded in the editor shows its role, session and notes, and a press on a role sends it` and `each collected experiment's row shows its name, its role and its data badge`, the count rising by 4, and the changed `Inverse: the Experiments bay with its data-file section leaves everything reachable`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementMenuTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.the bay's scan, role, session and notes UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.Add variable and Add block list the held axes and blocks under the range", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.an experiment loaded in the editor shows its role, session and notes, and a press on a role sends it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.each collected experiment's row shows its name, its role and its data badge", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests.pressing Add variable between two axes and Add records one two-variable experiment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.Inverse: the Experiments bay with its data-file section leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.ExperimentRoleMark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.ExperimentRoleOption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.ExperimentRow", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.ExperimentControlsState", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.ExperimentControlsHandlers", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentScanSummary", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentAddScanAxisButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentAddScanBlockButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentRoleChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentSessionField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentNotesField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentRowBadge", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ExperimentRole.uiKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ExperimentRole.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S91-BAY-V2"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 297, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S91m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [296], "how_to": "The section proved end to end through the kit window and a real folder, and the gotcha a later reader needs (001 §K; 001 §E notes in the files; the S9.1 brief; AGENTS.md: wait for deterministic conditions, drive by id). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs` (steps 184, 284) gains the ui-smoke fact `a two-variable experiment recorded through the bay keeps its scan, role, session and notes in its kit file`: over a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write through `openKitAt` and mounted through `kitWindowView` as step 284's fact mounts it, with a sample bound to the 1 mm glass plate added between the seeded source and detector and the Experiments bay open: pressing the sample's candidate, `ExperimentVariable_r2`, `experimentAddScanAxisButton`, the candidate, `ExperimentVariable_r1` and `experimentAddButton`, then `experimentRoleChoice` of `calibration`, and typing `Day 1` into `experimentSessionField` and `LR re-seated` into `experimentNotesField`, each committed by Enter, leaves the folder holding `E1.experiment-json` (the standard template cannot name a table with no item in Prep 1) whose experiment, read back through `readExperiments` of the folder reopened through `openKitAt`, has one block of the two axes, `CalibrationRun`, `Some (SessionName \"Day 1\")` and the notes `LR re-seated`, and the row `ExperimentBadge_1` reads `no data`. (2) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'Names come from the kit's naming template' (step 276), one bullet of at most six lines: **An experiment is a scan over a setup revision** (`Experiments.fs`, spec 0050 S9.1): blocks of axes, each axis one variable of one slot over its range (a dial-mounted item scans its raw reading); a block is the product of its axes, the first outermost, read on its capture; its name comes from the kit's template (else `E<n>`) and is its file's stem; its role, session and notes and its mapped attachment (import profile and row selection) live in its file; its data badge is `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck`. Nothing else in the file changes.", "acceptance": "After the acceptance lands, a two-variable experiment recorded through the kit window's bay MUST be read back from its folder with its scan, role, session and notes, and AGENTS.md MUST carry the gotcha 'An experiment is a scan over a setup revision'; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `a two-variable experiment recorded through the bay keeps its scan, role, session and notes in its kit file`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.a two-variable experiment recorded through the bay keeps its scan, role, session and notes in its kit file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S91-KIT-WINDOW-ACCEPTANCE"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.1 -- Experiments v2: scans, roles, sessions and attachments"}
{"number": 298, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [297], "how_to": "How a lab file is laid out and what its columns hold, as the closed sets an import profile is made of (001 §K 'Column-mapping import wizard: sniff the delimiter, header and BOM, and show a preview; map columns to scan variable(s) (unit; raw dial vs physical), signal, σ, timestamp, capture index, experiment key — or to Mueller elements m00…m33 plus configuration columns'; the S9.2 brief; AGENTS.md: a closed set's disk tag is an int, 1-based, read back by `tryOfWire`, and case names take two words). Nothing reads them before step 299. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`: `ImportProfileName` (step 291) moves, its members unchanged, from after `DataAttachmentStatus` to directly before `NamingTemplate` (step 267), so that the kit file can hold profiles (step 299); `DataRowKey`, `DataRowSelection` and `MappedAttachment` stay where step 291 put them. It gains `static member phoneRoiCsv : ImportProfileName` = `Phone ROI CSV` (the profile over `MuellerDataStore.fs:parseMuellerCsv`) and `static member muellerObservations : ImportProfileName` = `Mueller-matrix observations` (the observation file, step 301), each the one place its text is written, and `static member builtIns : ImportProfileName list`, the four built-in names in the order `intensitySeries`, `ellipsometricSeries`, `phoneRoiCsv`, `muellerObservations`. (2) Directly after `ImportProfileName`, five fieldless unions, each with `member this.value : int` (its disk tag, 1 to n in case order), `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : <the union> option` (`None` for any other tag), `member this.text : string` and `static member all : <the union> list` (the cases in tag order): (a) `DataDelimiter` = `CommaDelimiter` | `SemicolonDelimiter` | `TabDelimiter`, the character between a row's cells, texts `comma`, `semicolon` and `tab`, with `member this.character : char` answering `,`, `;` and the tab character; (b) `HeaderRowChoice` = `HeaderOnFirstRow` | `NoHeaderRow`, whether the first row names the columns, texts `first row is a header` and `no header row`; (c) `ByteOrderMark` = `ByteOrderMarkPresent` | `ByteOrderMarkAbsent`, whether the lab's files start with the UTF-8 byte-order mark, texts `byte-order mark` and `no byte-order mark`: the kit drops a leading mark before anything reads a file (step 128), so the profile records it for the wizard (step 309) and for the files the app writes; (d) `ScanColumnUnit` = `DegreeColumnUnit` | `RadianColumnUnit` | `NanometerColumnUnit` | `MicrometerColumnUnit` | `ElectronVoltColumnUnit` | `WavenumberColumnUnit`, the unit a scan column's numbers are in, texts `°`, `rad`, `nm`, `µm`, `eV` and `cm⁻¹`, with `member this.spectralUnitOpt : Units.UnitOfMeasure option` answering `Nanometer`, `Micrometer`, `ElectronVolt` and `Wavenumber` (`Units.fs:UnitOfMeasure`) for the four spectral cases and `None` for the two angle cases; (e) `ScanReading` = `RawDialReading` | `PhysicalScanValue`, whether a scan column holds the reading on an item's dial or the physical value (001 §I 'experiments record raw dial readings'), texts `raw dial reading` and `physical value`. (3) After them, `DataColumnNumber of int` with `.value`, a column of a lab file counted from 1: `static member tryCreate (number : int) : DataColumnNumber option` answers `None` below 1, and `member this.index : int` is `value - 1`, its position among a row's cells. No other type, member or option is added. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`: `CanonicalJson.options` gains one converter each for `DataDelimiter`, `HeaderRowChoice`, `ByteOrderMark`, `ScanColumnUnit` and `ScanReading`, written as step 166's `KitStar` converter is and registered with the others before the `JsonFSharpConverter`: each writes the case's `value` and reads through its `tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. Nothing else in the options changes. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `the closed sets of an import profile round-trip their disk tags and render their texts`: for each of the five unions, `tryOfWire` of each case's `value` answers the case, the tags run 1 to n in `all`'s order, 0 and n + 1 answer `None`, and the texts are exactly as above; `CommaDelimiter.character` is `,` and `TabDelimiter.character` the tab character; `NanometerColumnUnit.spectralUnitOpt` is `Some Nanometer` and `RadianColumnUnit.spectralUnitOpt` is `None`; `DataColumnNumber.tryCreate 0` is `None` and `(DataColumnNumber 3).index` is 2; and `ImportProfileName.builtIns` holds `Intensity series`, `Ellipsometric series`, `Phone ROI CSV` and `Mueller-matrix observations`, in that order. In `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 166, 285), `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes `SemicolonDelimiter` as `2`, `NoHeaderRow` as `2`, `ByteOrderMarkPresent` as `1`, `WavenumberColumnUnit` as `6` and `RawDialReading` as `1`, each read back equal, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the `DataDelimiter` tag `4` and the `ScanColumnUnit` tag `7` as it refuses the others.", "acceptance": "After the profile's closed sets land, `DataDelimiter`, `HeaderRowChoice`, `ByteOrderMark`, `ScanColumnUnit` and `ScanReading` MUST carry 1-based int disk tags read back by `tryOfWire` and written by `CanonicalJson.options` as those tags, `DataColumnNumber` MUST count from 1, and `ImportProfileName.builtIns` MUST name the four built-in profiles; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the closed sets of an import profile round-trip their disk tags and render their texts`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.the closed sets of an import profile round-trip their disk tags and render their texts", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an unknown disk tag is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.DataDelimiter", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.HeaderRowChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ByteOrderMark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ScanColumnUnit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ScanReading", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.DataColumnNumber", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ImportProfileName.muellerObservations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ImportProfileName.builtIns", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-PROFILE-LAYOUT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 299, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [298], "how_to": "An import profile is a named mapping of a lab file's layout and columns, stored in the kit file (001 §K 'save the mapping as a named import profile in `.kit-json`'; 001 §E 'The kit file holds … the import profiles'; step 122: 'S9.2 the import profiles'; 001 §K 'Raw data is immutable': an experiment names its profile, step 291, so a saved profile is never replaced). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, after `DataColumnNumber` (step 298) and before `NamingTemplate`, in this order: (1) `ScanColumn = { column : DataColumnNumber; valueUnit : ScanColumnUnit; reading : ScanReading }`, a column of a scan variable's values; a profile's scan columns, in column order, give the experiment's scan quantities in order (step 304). (2) `ReadingColumns` = `SignalColumns of signal : DataColumnNumber * sigmaOpt : DataColumnNumber option` (a detector signal and its σ) | `MuellerElementColumns of elements : DataColumnNumber list * throughputOpt : DataColumnNumber option` (the sixteen elements m00…m33 in row order, and the absolute throughput when the elements are normalized): what each row measured. (3) `ColumnRoles = { scan : ScanColumn list; reading : ReadingColumns; timestampOpt : DataColumnNumber option; captureIndexOpt : DataColumnNumber option; observableOpt : DataColumnNumber option; keyOpt : DataColumnNumber option }`, every role a column holds (001 §K): the scan variables, the reading, the capture's timestamp and index, the observable (T or R) and the experiment key that splits one file into experiments (S9.3). (4) `ImportProfileError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `BlankProfileNameErr` (a profile name holding only white space), `BuiltInProfileNameErr` (a built-in profile's name), `DuplicateProfileNameErr` (a name the kit's profiles hold), `SignalColumnCountErr` (a signal mapping with no signal column or more than one), `MixedReadingColumnsErr` (a mapping with a signal and Mueller elements), `RepeatedRoleErr` (a one-column role given to two columns) and `MuellerElementCountErr` (a Mueller mapping that does not give each of m00…m33 exactly one column). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: `the import profile name is blank: <reason>`, `the name belongs to a built-in import profile: <reason>`, `the kit already holds an import profile of that name: <reason>`, `a signal mapping needs exactly one signal column: <reason>`, `a mapping reads a signal or Mueller elements, not both: <reason>`, `a role is given to two columns: <reason>` and `a Mueller mapping needs each of m00…m33 once: <reason>`. (5) `ImportProfile = { name : ImportProfileName; delimiter : DataDelimiter; header : HeaderRowChoice; bom : ByteOrderMark; roles : ColumnRoles }`, one named mapping of a lab file; the four built-in profiles are code and never stored (step 300). (6) `type ImportProfileName with member this.availableAmong (profiles : ImportProfile list) : Result<ImportProfileName, ImportProfileError>`, the one naming rule of a new profile: a name of `builtIns` answers `BuiltInProfileNameErr` and a name ordinal-equal to a held profile's `DuplicateProfileNameErr`, each naming it; any other answers itself. (7) `KitFile` (step 122) gains `importProfiles : ImportProfile list` after `namingTemplate` (step 267), and `KitFile.create` sets it to `[]`, so `KitFolder.namedKitFile` (step 145) and `scratchKit` (step 150) take it unchanged; `member this.withImportProfile (profile : ImportProfile) : Result<KitFile, ImportProfileError>` on `KitFile` is `profile.name.availableAmong this.importProfiles`, whose `Ok` appends the profile. (8) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json` (steps 124, 267): under `if` `schemaVersion` is 1, `importProfiles` joins the required keys as an array of objects, each with exactly the required keys `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character), `delimiter` (an integer 1 to 3), `header` (1 to 2), `bom` (1 to 2) and `roles`, an object with exactly the keys `scan` (an array of objects of exactly `column`, an integer of at least 1, `valueUnit`, 1 to 6, and `reading`, 1 to 2), `reading` (an object) and the four `…Opt` keys (each an integer of at least 1 or `null`); `additionalProperties: false` holds at each level. The schema version stays 1, because kit files of the old shape exist only under test output (.spec-md §7). No up-converter, default-on-read, replace or delete verb is added. Tests. `KitTests` gains `a profile name is refused when a built-in or a kit profile holds it, and a kit file appends a new profile`: over a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column), step 122's `KitFile.create` fixture holds no profile; its `withImportProfile` of `Lab scan` holds exactly it; that kit file's `withImportProfile` of `Lab scan` again answers `DuplicateProfileNameErr` naming `Lab scan`, and of a profile named `Phone ROI CSV` `BuiltInProfileNameErr`; and `(ImportProfileName \"lab scan\").availableAmong [ <Lab scan> ]` answers itself, the comparison being ordinal. `every import profile error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text that contains the reason. `KitFileJsonTests` (steps 124, 267), whose kit file now also holds `importProfiles` of `Lab scan` and a test-local Mueller profile `Polarimeter` (tab, no header row, no byte-order mark; scan columns 1 in degrees and 2 in radians, both physical values; `MuellerElementColumns` of columns 3 to 18 with throughput 19; observable 20; key 21): `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text` lists the top-level keys `author`, `created`, `id`, `importProfiles`, `modified`, `name`, `namingTemplate`, `notes`, `schemaVersion` and `sendExclude` in that order and writes `Polarimeter`'s `delimiter` as `3`; `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds` also refuses the text without `importProfiles`, with a profile whose `delimiter` is `0`, and with a profile that has no `roles`, each with `SchemaValidationErr`. Every other kit-file fact passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the kit file holds import profiles, `ImportProfile` and `ColumnRoles` MUST exist in `Kit.fs`, `KitFile` MUST carry `importProfiles` (empty for a new kit), `KitFile.withImportProfile` MUST append a profile and refuse a built-in's or a held profile's name, and `kit.schema.json` MUST require the profiles; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a profile name is refused when a built-in or a kit profile holds it, and a kit file appends a new profile` and `every import profile error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text` and `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.a profile name is refused when a built-in or a kit profile holds it, and a kit file appends a new profile", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests.every import profile error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests.a kit file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ScanColumn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ReadingColumns", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ColumnRoles", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ImportProfileError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ImportProfile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.ImportProfileName.availableAmong", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit.KitFile.withImportProfile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs", "obligations": ["S92-KIT-PROFILES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 300, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [299], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests"], "how_to": "The built-in profiles, the profile an experiment names, and the points a profile maps a file to, as pure Domain data (001 §K 'Built-in profiles REUSE the existing parsers: `MeasuredData.parseIntensitySeries` / `parseEllipsometricSeries`; `MuellerDataStore.parseMuellerCsv` (the \"Phone ROI CSV\" profile); a Mueller-matrix observation profile'; 001 §K 'Observables: intensity, Ψ / Δ, full Mueller matrices (the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape, normalized + absolute throughput)'; the S9.2 brief). Nothing reads them before step 301. New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`: `module ImportProfiles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ItemEvaluation.fs` (step 245), the last Domain file, because its points hold `MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerRawRow` and `MuellerInverse.fs:MuellerObservation`: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. In this order: (1) The two closed sets of a configuration column, as members on their types, because a file holds them (AGENTS.md: a closed set's disk tag is an int): `type Observable with` (`MuellerInverse.fs:Observable`) `member this.value : int` (1 `TransmittedMueller`, 2 `ReflectedMueller`), `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : Observable option` and `static member tryOfCell (cell : string) : Observable option`, which reads a lab file's observable cell: trimmed, `T` or `R` ignoring case, otherwise its invariant-culture integer through `tryOfWire`, `None` for anything else; and `type SampleCut with` (`MuellerInverse.fs:SampleCut`) `member this.value : int` (1 `ZCut`, 2 `XCut`, 3 `YCut`, 4 `TiltedCut`), `member this.tilt : Angle` (a `TiltedCut`'s angle, `Angle.zero` for the others) and `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) (tilt : Angle) : SampleCut option` (tags 1 to 3 with a zero tilt, 4 as `TiltedCut tilt`, `None` otherwise). `MuellerInverse.fs` itself is not edited. (2) `BuiltInImportProfile` = `IntensitySeriesProfile` | `EllipsometricSeriesProfile` | `PhoneRoiCsvProfile` | `MuellerObservationProfile`, the profiles that are code: `member this.name : ImportProfileName` answers `ImportProfileName.intensitySeries`, `ellipsometricSeries`, `phoneRoiCsv` and `muellerObservations` (step 298); `static member all : BuiltInImportProfile list` lists the four in that order; `static member tryOfName (name : ImportProfileName) : BuiltInImportProfile option`. They are named, never stored, so no int tag is added. (3) `ChosenImportProfile` = `BuiltInProfileChoice of BuiltInImportProfile` | `KitProfileChoice of ImportProfile`, the profile an experiment's name resolves to: `member this.name : ImportProfileName`, and `static member tryOfName (profiles : ImportProfile list) (name : ImportProfileName) : ChosenImportProfile option`, a built-in first, then the first of `profiles` whose name equals it, `None` otherwise. (4) The points: `MeasuredSigma of float` with `.value`, a signal's standard deviation; `RowTimestamp of System.DateTimeOffset` with `.value`, when a row was captured; `ScanCell = { column : ScanColumn; magnitude : Units.UnitMagnitude }`, one scan value as its file wrote it, with `member this.displayValue : SweptValue`, the value in its quantity's display unit (degrees for an angle, nanometres for a wavelength, `Experiments.fs:VariableParameter.unitLabel`): the magnitude for `DegreeColumnUnit` and `NanometerColumnUnit`, `Angle.radiansToDegrees` (`Geometry.fs:Angle`) of it for `RadianColumnUnit`, and `(fromMeters Nanometer (toMeters <spectralUnit> magnitude)).value` (`Units.fs:toMeters`, `fromMeters`) for the other spectral units; `MappedReading` = `SignalReading of signal : MeasuredIntensity * sigmaOpt : MeasuredSigma option` | `MuellerReading of MuellerMatrix`; `MappedRow = { keyOpt : DataRowKey option; scan : ScanCell list; reading : MappedReading; timestampOpt : RowTimestamp option; captureIndexOpt : CaptureIndex option; observableOpt : Observable option }`, one row of a kit profile's mapping (`CaptureIndex` is `MuellerReconstruction.fs:CaptureIndex`, reused); `KeyedObservation = { key : DataRowKey; observation : MuellerObservation }`, one row of the observation file, its key naming the sample it was measured on; and `MappedPoints` = `SeriesPoints of MeasuredSeries` (an `X,Y` built-in's series, `MeasuredData.fs:MeasuredSeries`, reused) | `CapturePoints of MuellerRawRow list` (Phone ROI CSV) | `ObservationPoints of KeyedObservation list` | `ColumnPoints of MappedRow list`, with `member this.pointCount : MeasuredPointCount`, a series' own `pointCount` (`MeasuredData.fs:pointCount`) and the list's length otherwise. (5) The wizard's column choices: `MuellerElementIndex of int` with `.value`, element m<i><j> at 4i + j: `static member tryCreate (index : int) : MuellerElementIndex option` (0 to 15), `static member all : MuellerElementIndex list` (0 to 15 in order) and `member this.text : string` (`m00` … `m33`); `ColumnRoleChoice` = `UnmappedColumnRole` | `ScanColumnRole of valueUnit : ScanColumnUnit * reading : ScanReading` | `SignalColumnRole` | `SigmaColumnRole` | `TimestampColumnRole` | `CaptureIndexColumnRole` | `ObservableColumnRole` | `KeyColumnRole` | `ThroughputColumnRole` | `MuellerElementRole of MuellerElementIndex`, the role the wizard gives one column, with `member this.text : string` (`—`, `scan variable (<valueUnit.text>, <reading.text>)`, `signal`, `σ`, `timestamp`, `capture index`, `observable`, `experiment key`, `throughput`, `m<i><j>`); `ColumnChoice = { column : DataColumnNumber; role : ColumnRoleChoice }`; and `type ColumnRoles with static member tryOfChoices (choices : ColumnChoice list) : Result<ColumnRoles, ImportProfileError>`, the one rule from choices to roles, reading the choices in column order: the scan columns are the `ScanColumnRole` choices; any `MuellerElementRole` or `ThroughputColumnRole` makes the reading `MuellerElementColumns`, its elements ordered by index, a missing or repeated index being `MuellerElementCountErr` naming it and a `SignalColumnRole` or `SigmaColumnRole` beside them `MixedReadingColumnsErr`; otherwise the reading is `SignalColumns`, no or several `SignalColumnRole` being `SignalColumnCountErr`; a second column given `SigmaColumnRole`, `TimestampColumnRole`, `CaptureIndexColumnRole`, `ObservableColumnRole`, `KeyColumnRole` or `ThroughputColumnRole` is `RepeatedRoleErr` naming the role's text and both columns; an `UnmappedColumnRole` column is read by nothing. No other type, member, option or rule is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs`, `module ImportProfileTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. `the built-in import profiles are named once, and a built-in is found before a kit profile`: the names of `BuiltInImportProfile.all` are `ImportProfileName.builtIns`, `tryOfName` inverts `name`, and `Other` answers `None`; `ChosenImportProfile.tryOfName [ <Lab scan> ] (ImportProfileName \"Lab scan\")` is `KitProfileChoice` of it, of `Phone ROI CSV` `BuiltInProfileChoice PhoneRoiCsvProfile` even over a hand-built profile of that name, and of `Nope` `None` (a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column)). `the observable and the cut carry disk tags, and a lab's observable cell reads T, R or the tag`: `TransmittedMueller.value` is 1 and `ReflectedMueller.value` 2, `tryOfWire` inverts them and answers `None` for 3; `tryOfCell` of ` t `, `R`, `2` and `x` answers `TransmittedMueller`, `ReflectedMueller`, `ReflectedMueller` and `None`; the cuts' tags are 1 to 4, `(TiltedCut (Angle 0.3)).tilt` is `Angle 0.3`, `SampleCut.tryOfWire 4 (Angle 0.3)` is `Some (TiltedCut (Angle 0.3))`, `tryOfWire 1 Angle.zero` is `Some ZCut` and `tryOfWire 1 (Angle 0.1)` is `None`. `a scan cell gives its value in its quantity's display unit`: cells of 45 in degrees, 632.8 in nanometres, π/4 in radians and 0.6328 in micrometres display 45, 632.8, 45 and 632.8, the last two to nine places as `MeasuredDataTests` compares (`Assert.Equal(_, _, 9)`). `a column mapping's roles come from one choice per column`: the choices column 1 `ScanColumnRole (DegreeColumnUnit, PhysicalScanValue)`, 2 `SignalColumnRole`, 3 `SigmaColumnRole`, 4 `KeyColumnRole` and 5 `UnmappedColumnRole`, given in reverse order, answer `Lab scan`'s roles; the sixteen element roles over columns 20 down to 5 with `ThroughputColumnRole` on 21 answer `MuellerElementColumns` of columns 20, 19, …, 5 in index order with throughput 21; no signal and two signals answer `SignalColumnCountErr`; a signal beside `m00` answers `MixedReadingColumnsErr`; the sixteen elements without `m12` answer `MuellerElementCountErr` naming `m12`; and two key columns answer `RepeatedRoleErr` naming `experiment key`. `mapped points count what they hold`: `pointCount` of `SeriesPoints` of a two-point intensity series is 2, and of `CapturePoints`, `ObservationPoints` and `ColumnPoints` of three test-local items each 3.", "acceptance": "After `ImportProfiles.fs` lands, the four built-in profiles MUST be named once and resolve before a kit profile of their name, `MappedPoints` MUST hold an X,Y series, Phone ROI capture rows, keyed observations or mapped rows, the observable and the cut MUST carry int disk tags, and `ColumnRoles.tryOfChoices` MUST be the one rule from column choices to roles; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the built-in import profiles are named once, and a built-in is found before a kit profile`, `the observable and the cut carry disk tags, and a lab's observable cell reads T, R or the tag`, `a scan cell gives its value in its quantity's display unit`, `a column mapping's roles come from one choice per column` and `mapped points count what they hold`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.the built-in import profiles are named once, and a built-in is found before a kit profile", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.the observable and the cut carry disk tags, and a lab's observable cell reads T, R or the tag", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.a scan cell gives its value in its quantity's display unit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.a column mapping's roles come from one choice per column", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.mapped points count what they hold", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.BuiltInImportProfile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.ChosenImportProfile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MeasuredSigma", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.RowTimestamp", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.ScanCell", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MappedReading", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MappedRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.KeyedObservation", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MappedPoints", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MuellerElementIndex", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.ColumnRoleChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.ColumnChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.ColumnRoles.tryOfChoices", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.Observable.tryOfCell", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.SampleCut.tryOfWire", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-POINTS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 301, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [300], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests"], "how_to": "The Mueller-matrix observation file, which the app writes and the `Mueller-matrix observations` profile reads (001 §K 'a Mueller-matrix observation profile (§Q, AT-2)'; 001 §Q AT-2 'written as kit data files … through the Mueller-matrix import profile, committed with the kit, and read back through the same profile; the test regenerates them from the seeds and requires the committed files byte-identical'; 'Data identity: the observations the study loads equal the harness's, exactly'; the S9.2 brief: normalized m00…m33 + absolute throughput + the configuration columns, in the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape, and it also WRITES files). New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs`: `module LabFileImport` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `MuellerDataStore.fs`, one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` and no comment; its module doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `type KeyedObservation with static member observationFileText (observations : KeyedObservation list) : Result<KitFileText, ExperimentDataError>` writes the file: the header row `sample,cut,cut_tilt_rad,thickness_m,incidence_rad,azimuth_rad,observable,wavelength_nm,m00,m01,m02,m03,m10,m11,m12,m13,m20,m21,m22,m23,m30,m31,m32,m33,throughput` (the one place it is written), then one row per observation in order: the key's text; the cut's `value` and its `tilt` in radians (step 300); the thickness in metres; the incidence angle's and the azimuth's radians (`IncidenceAngle.value`, `SampleAzimuth.value`); the observable's `value`; the wavelength in nanometres, a `Nm` case's own number; the sixteen elements of `measured.normalized` (`MuellerInverse.fs:normalized`) in row order; and `measured.element 0 0`, the absolute throughput. Cells are joined by `,`, each row ends in `\\n`, and no byte-order mark is written. Every number is `ToString(\"R\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`, the shortest text that reads back to the same double, so the same observations always write the same text. It answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the observation's 1-based position and key, and writes nothing, for a key that is empty or holds `,`, `\"`, a carriage return or a line feed; an `Infinity` thickness; a `Mkm` wavelength, because the file records nanometres (`Fields.fs:WaveLength`); and a matrix whose `normalized` answers an `InversionError`. (2) `type KitFileText with member this.parseMuellerObservations : Result<KeyedObservation list, ExperimentDataError>` reads it: lines are split on `\\n`, a trailing `\\r` trimmed and blank lines skipped; a first line other than the header above is `MalformedDataFileErr` naming it; no row after it is `EmptyDataFileErr`; each row holds 25 cells, its numbers read by `Double.TryParse` with `NumberStyles.Float` and `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`, its cut through `SampleCut.tryOfWire` of the tag and the tilt, its observable through `Observable.tryOfWire` and its key as `DataRowKey` of the cell; the first row that fails is `MalformedDataFileErr` naming its line and cell. The configuration is `{ cut; thickness = Thickness (<metres> * 1.0<meter>); incidenceAngle = IncidenceAngle (Angle <radians>); azimuth = SampleAzimuth (Angle <radians>); observable; waveLength = WaveLength.nm (<nanometres> * 1.0<nm>) }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:MeasurementConfiguration`), the incidence built from its radians, not through `IncidenceAngle.create`, so the stored angle is kept bit for bit; `measured` is the matrix whose element (i, j) is `throughput * <the normalized element>`, its m₀₀ the throughput itself. That is the arithmetic `misreadAbsolute` builds an absolute matrix with (`BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs:misreadAbsolute`), so such a matrix reads back element for element. No other member, option or format is added: the profile reads only this shape, and the app writes only through `observationFileText`. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs`, `module LabFileImportTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its two test-local observations are keyed `Z-cut` and `optic axis (A)`: a `ZCut` plate of `Thickness.mkm 100.0<mkm>` at `IncidenceAngle.create (Angle.degree 45.0<deg>)`, `SampleAzimuth.degree 22.5<deg>`, `ReflectedMueller`, `WaveLength.nm 632.8<nm>`; and a `TiltedCut (Angle 0.3141592653589793)` plate of the same thickness at `IncidenceAngle.normal`, `SampleAzimuth.degree 67.5<deg>`, `TransmittedMueller`, the same wavelength. Each matrix is built as `misreadAbsolute` builds one: a throughput t (0.8125, then 0.03) as m₀₀ and `t * nₖ` for the other elements, with nₖ = (−1)ᵏ (k + 1) / 17 at k = 4i + j. `the observation file writes each observation's configuration, normalized elements and throughput in one row`: the text has three lines, the first being the header, and the first row starts `Z-cut,1,0,`, has 25 cells, its ninth cell `1` (the normalized m₀₀) and its last `0.8125`. `an observation file reads back to the same observations, element for element, and writes back to the same text`: `parseMuellerObservations` of the text answers two keyed observations whose keys and configurations equal the written ones and each of whose sixteen `element i j` equals the written matrix's exactly, and `observationFileText` of them answers the same text. `an observation file of another shape, or one the profile cannot write, is refused`: a header without `m33` answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the header; the header alone answers `EmptyDataFileErr`; a row of 24 cells and a row whose cut tag is `5` answer `MalformedDataFileErr` naming line 2; and writing an observation keyed `a,b`, one of `Thickness.Infinity`, one at `WaveLength.mkm 0.6328<mkm>` and one whose m₀₀ is 0 each answer `MalformedDataFileErr`.", "acceptance": "After the observation file lands, `KeyedObservation.observationFileText` MUST write keyed observations as the header, the configuration, the normalized elements and the throughput in round-trip number text, refusing what it cannot write, and `KitFileText.parseMuellerObservations` MUST read such a file back to the same observations element for element; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the observation file writes each observation's configuration, normalized elements and throughput in one row`, `an observation file reads back to the same observations, element for element, and writes back to the same text` and `an observation file of another shape, or one the profile cannot write, is refused`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.the observation file writes each observation's configuration, normalized elements and throughput in one row", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-OBSERVATION-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.an observation file reads back to the same observations, element for element, and writes back to the same text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-OBSERVATION-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.an observation file of another shape, or one the profile cannot write, is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-OBSERVATION-FILE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LabFileImport.KeyedObservation.observationFileText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "obligations": ["S92-OBSERVATION-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LabFileImport.KitFileText.parseMuellerObservations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "obligations": ["S92-OBSERVATION-FILE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 302, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [301], "how_to": "A kit profile reads a lab file of any delimited shape through its column roles (001 §K 'map columns to scan variable(s) (unit; raw dial vs physical), signal, σ, timestamp, capture index, experiment key — or to Mueller elements m00…m33 plus configuration columns'; the S9.2 brief: 'a custom mapping'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs` (step 301): (1) A private function reads a text into its rows by a delimiter and a header choice, through `CsvFile.Parse` (FSharp.Data, as `MuellerDataStore.fs:parseMuellerCsv` and `SpectralImport.fs` parse) with `separators` the delimiter's `character` as text and `hasHeaders` true for `HeaderOnFirstRow`: every exception is caught and answered `MalformedDataFileErr` with its message, rows whose cells are all blank are skipped as `parseMuellerCsv` skips them, and it answers the header's cells, when there is a header, and the data rows' cells. Step 307's preview calls the same function. (2) `type ImportProfile with member this.mapText (text : KitFileText) : Result<MappedRow list, ExperimentDataError>`: no data row is `EmptyDataFileErr`; each data row is one `MappedRow` (step 300), its cells taken by `DataColumnNumber.index` and trimmed: each scan column a `ScanCell` of its column and the number as a `UnitMagnitude`; `SignalColumns` a `SignalReading` of the signal as `MeasuredIntensity` and the σ as `MeasuredSigma`; `MuellerElementColumns` a `MuellerReading` whose element (i, j) is the column of index 4i + j, times the throughput when a throughput column is given (step 301's rule) and as read otherwise; the timestamp by `DateTimeOffset.TryParse` with `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture` and `DateTimeStyles.AssumeUniversal`, `parseMuellerCsv`'s rule; the capture index by `Int32.TryParse` with `NumberStyles.Integer` into `CaptureIndex`; the observable through `Observable.tryOfCell` (step 300); and the key as `DataRowKey` of the cell. Numbers are read by `Double.TryParse` with `NumberStyles.Float` and `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture`. The first cell that is missing, blank or does not read is `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the 1-based data row, the column and the cell; an unmapped column is read by nothing. No unit heuristics, culture guessing or quoting option is added. Tests, in `LabFileImportTests` (step 301), over test-local profiles written as records: `a column mapping reads each row's scan values, signal, σ and key`: a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column) over `phi,I,sigma,exp\\n0,0.5,0.01,CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL\\n20,0.25,0.01,\"LP-(AIR#0)-LP\"\\n` reads two rows: scan cells of column 1 with magnitudes 0 and 20, signals 0.5 and 0.25 with σ 0.01, and keys `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL` and `LP-(AIR#0)-LP`, the CSV reader removing the quotes. `a semicolon file without a header maps its Mueller elements and throughput`: a profile (semicolon, no header row; scan column 1 in radians as a physical value; `MuellerElementColumns` of columns 2 to 17 with throughput 18; observable 19; key 20) over one row whose sixteen element cells are 1 and fifteen test-local fractions, throughput 0.5 and observable `R` reads one `MuellerReading` whose (0, 0) element is 0.5 and whose (1, 2) element is 0.5 times that cell, with `Some ReflectedMueller`. `a cell the mapping cannot read names its row and column`: a signal cell `n/a` in data row 2 answers `MalformedDataFileErr` holding `2`, the column number and `n/a`; a row with no key cell answers `MalformedDataFileErr`; and a header-only file answers `EmptyDataFileErr`.", "acceptance": "After the column mapping lands, `ImportProfile.mapText` MUST read a lab file through its delimiter, header and column roles into mapped rows, refusing the first unreadable cell with its row and column; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a column mapping reads each row's scan values, signal, σ and key`, `a semicolon file without a header maps its Mueller elements and throughput` and `a cell the mapping cannot read names its row and column`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.a column mapping reads each row's scan values, signal, σ and key", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-COLUMN-MAPPING-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.a semicolon file without a header maps its Mueller elements and throughput", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-COLUMN-MAPPING-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.a cell the mapping cannot read names its row and column", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-COLUMN-MAPPING-READ"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LabFileImport.ImportProfile.mapText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "obligations": ["S92-COLUMN-MAPPING-READ"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 303, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [302], "how_to": "One read of a lab file through any profile, the built-ins calling the existing parsers (001 §K 'Built-in profiles REUSE the existing parsers'; 001 §R 'The strict v1 X,Y path, whose parsers are reused as built-in import profiles'; the S9.2 brief: 'each built-in profile reads its fixture exactly as its parser did'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs`: `type ChosenImportProfile with member this.mapText (text : KitFileText) : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError>`. `IntensitySeriesProfile` is `text.dataFileText.parseIntensitySeries` (`MeasuredData.fs:parseIntensitySeries`, through step 135's `KitFileText.dataFileText`) as `SeriesPoints (IntensityData _)`; `EllipsometricSeriesProfile` is `parseEllipsometricSeries` (`MeasuredData.fs:parseEllipsometricSeries`) as `SeriesPoints (EllipsometricData _)`; `PhoneRoiCsvProfile` is `text.dataFileText.parseMuellerCsv` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:parseMuellerCsv`) as `CapturePoints`, its `MalformedRowErr r` answered `MalformedDataFileErr r`, its `EmptyFileErr r` `EmptyDataFileErr r`, and its two archive cases, which a text parse never answers, `MalformedDataFileErr` of their reason or their archive's path; `MuellerObservationProfile` is `parseMuellerObservations` (step 301) as `ObservationPoints`; and `KitProfileChoice profile` is `profile.mapText` (step 302) as `ColumnPoints`. Each parser is called, never copied, so its rules, diagnostics and numbers are unchanged, and no exception crosses the member. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs`: the module doc's paragraph naming two STRICT schema-v1 shapes and its 'Deliberately NOT in scope' sentence become, in one to three lines, that the two parsers are the bodies of the `Intensity series` and `Ellipsometric series` import profiles (spec 0050 S9.2); no code changes. Tests, in `LabFileImportTests` (step 301): `each built-in profile reads its fixture exactly as its parser did`: over `MeasuredDataTests`' fixture texts written test-locally (`angle_deg,intensity\\n0.0,1.0\\n45.0,0.5\\n90.0,0.0`, `wavelength_nm,psi_deg,delta_deg,aoi_deg\\n633,25,90,70` and the malformed `x,y\\n1.0,2.0\\nfoo,3.0\\n4.0,5.0`) and the Phone ROI text of `MuellerReconstructionTests`' `muellerCsvFixture` (`BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:muellerCsvFixture`, a byte-order mark, the ten-column header and its two rows, written test-locally), `mapText` of `BuiltInProfileChoice IntensitySeriesProfile`, `EllipsometricSeriesProfile` and `PhoneRoiCsvProfile` answers exactly `SeriesPoints` or `CapturePoints` of what `parseIntensitySeries`, `parseEllipsometricSeries` and `parseMuellerCsv` answer for the same text, the malformed file's error included, and `MuellerObservationProfile` over step 301's text answers `ObservationPoints` of `parseMuellerObservations`. `a kit profile reads through its column mapping`: `KitProfileChoice` of `Lab scan` over step 302's text answers `ColumnPoints` of its two rows. `the Phone ROI profile maps the parser's errors onto the data channel`: a Phone ROI text without the `avg_total` column answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming `avg_total`, and the full ten-column header alone `EmptyDataFileErr`. `MeasuredDataTests` and `MuellerReconstructionTests` are not edited.", "acceptance": "After the one read lands, `ChosenImportProfile.mapText` MUST read a lab file through any profile, each built-in calling `parseIntensitySeries`, `parseEllipsometricSeries`, `parseMuellerCsv` or `parseMuellerObservations` and a kit profile its column mapping, with the Phone ROI parser's errors on the data channel; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each built-in profile reads its fixture exactly as its parser did`, `a kit profile reads through its column mapping` and `the Phone ROI profile maps the parser's errors onto the data channel`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasuredData.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.each built-in profile reads its fixture exactly as its parser did", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-ONE-PROFILE-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.a kit profile reads through its column mapping", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-ONE-PROFILE-READ"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests.the Phone ROI profile maps the parser's errors onto the data channel", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LabFileImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LabFileImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-ONE-PROFILE-READ"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.LabFileImport.ChosenImportProfile.mapText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "obligations": ["S92-ONE-PROFILE-READ"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 304, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [303], "how_to": "Mapped points are validated against an experiment's scan and detector by one rule, and the load answers mapped points (001 §K 'Status badges: … validated (points) / … / out of range'; the S9.1 mapper's request: map multi-variable scans (`ScanAxis` / `ScanSetting`) instead of step 288's refusal; 001 §I: a dial-mounted item records raw readings, step 289). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`: the `<Compile>` lines of `ExperimentDataProxy.fs` and `ExperimentDataLoad.fs` move, in that order and with no comment, to directly after `ImportProfiles.fs` (step 300), so the data seam can speak mapped points; no Domain file compiled between their old and new places names them. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, after `MappedPoints`: (a) `ScanQuantity = { elementId : ElementId; label : ElementLabel; variable : VariableParameter; ranges : VariableRange list }`, one quantity a scan varies, with every range an axis gives it, and `member this.admits (value : SweptValue) : bool`, true when some range admits it (`MeasuredData.fs:admits`); (b) `type ExperimentScan with member this.quantities : ScanQuantity list`, the distinct `(elementId, variable)` pairs of `axes` (step 287) in order of first appearance, each with its first axis's label and the ranges of its axes in order, so A1's and A2's azimuth on one plate is one quantity (001 §Q AT-2); (c) `type MappedPoints with member this.validatedFor (detector : DetectorKind) (scan : ExperimentScan) : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError>`, the one validation of mapped points, answering the points unchanged or the first mismatch: `SeriesPoints` is step 288's rule, MOVED out of `loadAndValidate` with its texts, the validated series wrapped again; `CapturePoints` under an `Ellipsometer` is `DataUnitsMismatchErr` `the detector is an ellipsometer (records Ψ/Δ), but the data file is a Phone ROI CSV of intensities`, under a scan of no quantity passes (a dark line has nothing to range-check), under one quantity needs every row's `description.degrees` admitted, the first that is not being `DataRangeMismatchErr` `a description <x>° lies outside every range of <label> <variable.label>`, and under more quantities is `DataRangeMismatchErr` `a Phone ROI CSV holds one variable (its description), and the scan varies <n>`; `ObservationPoints` pass as read, each observation carrying its own configuration, which the study pairs with the experiment (S11.2); `ColumnPoints` with a `SignalReading` under an `Ellipsometer` is `DataUnitsMismatchErr` `the detector is an ellipsometer (records Ψ/Δ), but the mapping reads a signal`, rows whose scan cells do not number the quantities are `DataUnitsMismatchErr` `the import profile maps <k> scan column(s), and the scan varies <n>`, and the i-th cell of a row is the i-th quantity's: an angle unit (`spectralUnitOpt = None`) on a `VaryWaveLength` quantity, a spectral unit on any other, a `RawDialReading` on a quantity other than `VaryDialReading` and a `PhysicalScanValue` on a `VaryDialReading` one are each `DataUnitsMismatchErr` naming the column and the quantity, and a `displayValue` the quantity does not admit is `DataRangeMismatchErr` naming the value, the quantity's `unitLabel` and its label. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `loadAndValidate` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`, steps 261, 291) answers `Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError>`: it reads as step 291 left it (the two built-in names through `tryLoadIntensity` and `tryLoadEllipsometric`, another name and a key selection refused with step 291's texts, reading nothing), wraps the series in `SeriesPoints` and answers its `validatedFor (detectorKindOf library slots) experiment.scan`; its own scan rule is deleted. `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck` (step 295) takes `(outcomeOpt : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError> option)`, `ValidatedDataBadge` holding the points' `pointCount`; nothing else in it changes. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the one private validation function and the attach arm (steps 291, 295) pass the outcome to `ofCheck` as it comes. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs`: `validateExperiment` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`) answers `HandoffReady points.pointCount`; its error arms are unchanged. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` (step 300) gains `a scan's quantities join the axes that vary one slot's variable`: over step 287's test-local `sample` slot, a scan whose first block varies `sample`'s R1 over 0…67.5° and whose second block varies `sample`'s R2 over 20…60° then R1 over 0…90° has two quantities, R1 with both ranges and then R2, and a dark line has none; and `mapped capture rows and column rows are validated against the experiment's scan and detector`: Phone ROI rows at 0° and 45° validate under a one-axis R1 scan over 0…360° and under a dark line, refuse a scan over 0…40° with `DataRangeMismatchErr` naming `45`, refuse the two-quantity scan above and an `Ellipsometer` detector; test-local `Lab scan` rows at 0° and 20° validate under that R1 scan, refuse a `VaryDialReading` scan (`DataUnitsMismatchErr`, a physical column on a dial), a `VaryWaveLength` scan (`DataUnitsMismatchErr`, an angle column on a wavelength) and the two-quantity scan (`DataUnitsMismatchErr`, one scan column for two quantities); and keyed observations pass under any scan. `ExperimentDataProxyTests`: `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation` (step 295) passes `Ok (SeriesPoints (IntensityData <the canned series>))` where it passed the series, its assertions kept, and `loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan` (step 288) and `loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve` (step 291) expect `Ok (SeriesPoints _)` of the series they expected, every error assertion kept. `InverseConstructorTests` and `SolverHandoffWindowTests` pass as written.", "acceptance": "After validation moves onto mapped points, `MappedPoints.validatedFor` MUST be the one rule checking an X,Y series as step 288 did, Phone ROI rows and mapped rows against the scan's quantities (units, raw dial vs physical, ranges) and the detector, with observations passing, and `loadAndValidate` and `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck` MUST carry mapped points; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a scan's quantities join the axes that vary one slot's variable` and `mapped capture rows and column rows are validated against the experiment's scan and detector`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation`, `loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan` and `loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.a scan's quantities join the axes that vary one slot's variable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.mapped capture rows and column rows are validated against the experiment's scan and detector", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.loading data validates a one-axis scan as before and refuses an X,Y file for a multi-variable scan", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.ScanQuantity", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.ExperimentScan.quantities", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MappedPoints.validatedFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentDataLoad.ExperimentDataBadge", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S92-MAPPED-VALIDATION"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.2 -- Import profiles and the column-mapping wizard"}
{"number": 305, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S92h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [304], "how_to": "The strict `X,Y` seam is deleted: the data proxy reads any attached file through its profile and its row selection, and reads a picked file for the wizard (001 §R 'The strict v1 `X,Y` path, whose parsers are reused as built-in import profiles'; the S9.2 brief: 'the fixed-schema attach in `ExperimentDataProxy`, `ExperimentDataStore.createFileBacked` and `ExperimentDataLoad` is replaced by attach-with-profile'; 001 §K 'One file → many experiments: split by a key column'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, after `validatedFor`: `type MappedPoints with member this.selectedBy (rows : DataRowSelection) : Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError>`: `AllDataRows` keeps every point; `KeyedDataRows key` keeps the capture rows whose `experiment` label's text, the observations whose key and the mapped rows whose `keyOpt` equal it, a `SeriesPoints` being `MalformedDataFileErr` `an X,Y data file has no key column to select '<key>' by` (step 291's text, moved here), `ColumnPoints` none of whose rows holds a key `MalformedDataFileErr` `the import profile maps no key column to select '<key>' by`, and an empty selection `EmptyDataFileErr` `no row of the data file holds the key '<key>'`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs`: `ExperimentDataProxy` (`ExperimentDataProxy.fs:ExperimentDataProxy`, step 135) becomes `{ readPickedFile : FileName -> Result<LabFileSource, KitError>; attachDataFile : FileName -> Result<DataAttachment, KitError>; attachmentStatus : DataAttachment -> Result<DataAttachmentStatus, KitError>; readMapped : MappedAttachment -> Result<MappedPoints, ExperimentDataError> }`, still `[<ReferenceEquality>]`: `tryLoadIntensity` and `tryLoadEllipsometric` are deleted. The two new fields' one-line docs: a picked file's absolute name and bytes, read without touching the kit (the wizard's preview, step 308); and the points of an attachment's file read through its import profile, a built-in or the kit's, kept to its row selection. The module doc says so in one to three lines. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `loadAndValidate` is `dataProxy.readMapped data` bound to `validatedFor (detectorKindOf library slots) experiment.scan` (step 304); step 291's name switch and key refusal are deleted from it, because the store resolves the name and `selectedBy` selects. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs`: its `<Compile>` line moves to directly after `LabFileImport.fs` (step 301), with no comment, because it reads through it. In `createFileBacked (kit : KitProxy)` (`ExperimentDataStore.fs:createFileBacked`, step 135): the picked file's read that `attachDataFile` does becomes one private function, and `readPickedFile file` answers its `{ file = file; content = <the bytes> }` or its `KitIoErr`, `attachDataFile` calling the same function; `readMapped data` reads `kit.readKitFile ()`, resolves `ChosenImportProfile.tryOfName kitFile.importProfiles data.profile` (step 300), `None` being `MalformedDataFileErr` `the import profile '<name>' is not available` (step 291's text, moved here), reads `kit.readDataFile data.attachment.path` (step 128), maps its `text` by `mapText` (step 303) and answers `selectedBy data.rows`; a `KitError` of either read is `MalformedDataFileErr` `could not read the data file '<path>' for the import profile '<name>': <e.describe>`, staying within the four-case channel. The private `DataFileKind` and `loadThrough` are deleted; the module doc says, in one to three lines, that the seam reads through the kit and the profile. (5) Every record expression that builds an `ExperimentDataProxy` replaces the two loads with `readMapped` and gains `readPickedFile`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`, `SolverHandoffView.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindow.fs` and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` hold the proxy, build none and call `loadAndValidate` and `createFileBacked` as before, so nothing in them changes. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` gains `a row selection keeps every row or the rows of one key`: over test-local Phone ROI rows labelled `K1`, `K2`, `K1`, observations keyed `K1` and `K2`, and `Lab scan` rows keyed `K1` and `K2`, `AllDataRows` keeps each list whole and `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey \"K1\")` keeps the two, one and one `K1` items; `K3` answers `EmptyDataFileErr`; a series answers `MalformedDataFileErr` naming the key; and rows with no key `MalformedDataFileErr`. `ExperimentDataProxyTests`: its mock, keyed by the attachment's path, answers `readMapped` with canned mapped points (`SeriesPoints` of the canned intensity series for an attachment mapped by `Intensity series`, of the ellipsometric one for `Ellipsometric series`) and `readPickedFile` with canned bytes; `a mock ExperimentDataProxy loads canned intensity and ellipsometric series through their exact signatures` is renamed `a mock ExperimentDataProxy reads canned mapped points and picked files through its exact signature` and `an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError from both fields, never a throw` `an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError, never a throw`, each asserting the same over the new fields; `loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve` is renamed `loading data validates the points the attachment's profile maps`: step 288's one-axis experiment mapped by `Intensity series` answers the canned points validated, and by `Ellipsometric series` `DataUnitsMismatchErr`. `ExperimentDataStoreTests` (step 135), over `createFileBacked` of folder kits under the class's test directory, each folder now initialised through `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (step 125) before its files are placed, because `readMapped` reads the kit file: `createFileBacked round-trips a known intensity file through the step-34 parser`, `createFileBacked round-trips a known ellipsometric file through the step-34 parser` and `createFileBacked delegates parse semantics: an existing but empty file is the parser's EmptyDataFileErr` read through `readMapped` of the attachment mapped by `Intensity series` or `Ellipsometric series` over every row, keeping their names and assertions; `createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error from both fields, never a throw` is renamed `createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error through either X,Y profile, never a throw`; new `createFileBacked reads a data file through the kit's own profile and keeps the rows of its key`: a kit whose kit file holds `Lab scan` and a data file of rows keyed `K1`, `K2`, `K1` answers, for `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey \"K1\")`, `ColumnPoints` of the two `K1` rows; new `createFileBacked refuses a profile the kit lacks and a key an X,Y file cannot select`: the profile `Nope` answers `MalformedDataFileErr` holding `the import profile 'Nope' is not available`, and an `Intensity series` attachment with `KeyedDataRows` `MalformedDataFileErr` holding `no key column`; new `createFileBacked reads a picked file whole without attaching it`: `readPickedFile` of a file written outside the kit answers its name and exact bytes, and the kit's paths are unchanged. `InverseConstructorTests`' `mockIntensity` and `mockEllipsometric` and `SolverHandoffWindowTests`' mocks answer `readMapped` with `SeriesPoints` of the series they answered, keyed by the attachment's path, and `readPickedFile` with an error; `ScrollExtentTests`' `noData` answers both new fields with an error. Every fact of the three classes keeps its assertions. After this step `git grep -n -E \"tryLoadIntensity|tryLoadEllipsometric\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.", "acceptance": "After the strict seam is deleted, `ExperimentDataProxy` MUST read an attachment through `readMapped` (its profile resolved from the built-ins and the kit file, its rows kept by `MappedPoints.selectedBy`) and a picked file through `readPickedFile`, and `git grep -n -E \"tryLoadIntensity|tryLoadEllipsometric\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a row selection keeps every row or the rows of one key`, `createFileBacked reads a data file through the kit's own profile and keeps the rows of its key`, `createFileBacked refuses a profile the kit lacks and a key an X,Y file cannot select` and `createFileBacked reads a picked file whole without attaching it`, the count rising by 4, the renamed `a mock ExperimentDataProxy reads canned mapped points and picked files through its exact signature`, `an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError, never a throw`, `loading data validates the points the attachment's profile maps` and `createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error through either X,Y profile, never a throw`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataProxy.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests.a row selection keeps every row or the rows of one key", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ImportProfileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ImportProfileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.a mock ExperimentDataProxy loads canned intensity and ellipsometric series through their exact signatures", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.a mock ExperimentDataProxy reads canned mapped points and picked files through its exact signature", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError from both fields, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.an unknown path yields a typed ExperimentDataError, never a throw", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.loading data reads it through its import profile and refuses a profile or a row selection the X,Y files cannot serve", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataProxyTests.loading data validates the points the attachment's profile maps", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked round-trips a known intensity file through the step-34 parser", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked round-trips a known ellipsometric file through the step-34 parser", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error from both fields, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked maps a missing file to a typed error through either X,Y profile, never a throw", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked delegates parse semantics: an existing but empty file is the parser's EmptyDataFileErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked reads a data file through the kit's own profile and keeps the rows of its key", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked refuses a profile the kit lacks and a key an X,Y file cannot select", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests.createFileBacked reads a picked file whole without attaching it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentDataStoreTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentDataStoreTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S92-DATA-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ImportProfiles.MappedPoints.select