{"number": 324, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [323], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"], "how_to": "The key split's matched / unmatched table in the Data step, with Apply and Cancel (001 §O 'Data dialog: … the key split with a matched / unmatched table'; 001 §O 'Automation': `DataSplitKeyColumn`; .spec-md §10.3 identify → confirm, §10.5 Apply / Cancel share a row with a gap and distinct positive and negative colours; the S9.3 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs` (step 323): when `model.dataSplitOpt` is `Some s` (step 319), under the Split verb, a bordered vertical panel holding: a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `dataSplitKeyColumn` with `Split <the file's leaf> by '<s.key>' through '<s.profile>'`; one row per group of `s.split.groups`, in order, carrying `dataSplitGroupRow group.key` and reading `<key> — <n> point(s) — ` then, for `ExperimentForGroup name`, `→ <name>`; for `SetupOfferForGroup offer`, a box carrying `dataSplitOfferToggle group.key` labelled `Create <offer.experiment> over '<offer.setup.name>'`, followed by ` (new setup)` when `model.kitSetups` lacks the setup, on the positive background when `s.creating` holds the key and in the verb look otherwise, sending `ToggleSplitOffer group.key`; and for `GroupWithoutMatch problem`, `unmatched — <problem.describe>` in the message colour; then one horizontal row of `Apply split` (`dataSplitApplyButton`, the positive action look, sending `MatchByTemplate`, step 320, disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`) and, after a gap, `Cancel` (`dataSplitCancelButton`, the negative action look, sending `CancelDataSplit`), the `MaterialsWindowView` action buttons step 309 uses. A label never sits in a horizontal `StackPanel` beside a wrapping one (AGENTS.md: dock it in a `DockPanel`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group (step 323), each with a one-line doc: `dataSplitKeyColumn` (`\"DataSplitKeyColumn\"`), `dataSplitApplyButton` (`\"DataSplitApplyButton\"`) and `dataSplitCancelButton` (`\"DataSplitCancelButton\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type DataRowKey with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey` (its text); on `ConstructorUiId`, `static member dataSplitGroupRow (key : DataRowKey) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataSplitGroup_<key>`) and `static member dataSplitOfferToggle (key : DataRowKey) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataSplitOffer_<key>`), as `attachDataFile` is keyed by its experiment; and `type DataSplitError with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its `describe`. No other control or message is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs`, `module DataStepTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended to the compile list after `KitWindowTests.fs` with no comment; its views are mounted over the inverse model (`initInverse`, as `KitWindowTests` builds it, step 184) loaded from a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write, with `E1` committed, as `KitWindowTests` mounts the kit window (step 239), and a test-local `DataSplitState` over `phone.csv` by `experiment` through `Phone ROI CSV` whose groups are `K1` (2 points) matched to `E1`, `K2` (1) offered the new setup `Bench B` and the experiment `K2`, and `K3` (1) unmatched with `SplitKeyNameErr`. `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the Data step's ids so far (`FlowDataStep`, `DataStepPanel`, `DataSplitFileButton`, `DataSplitKeyColumn`, `DataSplitApplyButton`, `DataSplitCancelButton`, `DataSplitGroup_K1`, `DataSplitOffer_K2`). `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row`: `dataSplitKeyColumn` reads `Split phone.csv by 'experiment' through 'Phone ROI CSV'`; the three group rows read `→ E1`, `Create K2 over 'Bench B' (new setup)` and a text starting `unmatched —`; only `K2` has a toggle; `dataSplitApplyButton` and `dataSplitCancelButton` have equal tops, Cancel right of Apply with a gap between. `pressing an offer ticks it, and Cancel forgets the split`: over a `HostWindow` running `Program.mkSimple` of the model with `updateTableAndElementRotation` and `dataStepView`, pressing the toggle's centre leaves `creating` [`K2`] and the toggle on the positive background, and pressing Cancel's centre leaves `dataSplitOpt` `None` and no split panel. With trait `ui-smoke`, `the Data step renders a split and Apply split attaches its matched group`: over a folder kit holding `E1` and its split by `SplitByColumn` of a test-local Phone ROI file whose rows all carry `E1`'s name, the rendered Data step shows the panel, and pressing `dataSplitApplyButton` leaves E1 mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to the rows of its key and the panel gone.", "acceptance": "After the split panel lands, the Data step MUST show a pending split's key column and each group matched, offered (with its toggle) or unmatched (with its reason), with Apply split and Cancel in one row, sending `ToggleSplitOffer`, `MatchByTemplate` and `CancelDataSplit` under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Data step renders a split and Apply split attaches its matched group`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row` and `pressing an offer ticks it, and Cancel forgets the split`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the split panel names its key column and lists each group matched, offered or unmatched, with Apply and Cancel in one row", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing an offer ticks it, and Cancel forgets the split", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step renders a split and Apply split attaches its matched group", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitKeyColumn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitApplyButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitCancelButton", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.DataRowKey.uiKey", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitGroupRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.dataSplitOfferToggle", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.DataSplitError.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-SPLIT-PANEL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 325, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [324], "how_to": "The reviewed experiment's points in the Data step, each with Exclude or Include, and a chart in which an excluded point stays, marked (001 §O 'Data dialog: … per-point exclusion with a reason'; 001 §K 'exclusions carry a reason and stay visible in plots, marked'; the S9.3 brief; .spec-md §4 'UI'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`, after the inline chart: `PointMark` = `KeptPointMark` | `ExcludedPointMark`; `PlottedPoint = { position : ConstructorUiPosition; point : ChartPoint; mark : PointMark }`; and `pointsChartView (id : ConstructorUiId) (points : PlottedPoint list) (xLabel : ControlCaption) (yLabel : ControlCaption) : IView`, documented in one to three lines: a `Canvas` carrying `id`, of the inline chart's size, drawn with the private `PlotWindow.over`, `gridLines`, `axisLines` and `axisLabels` the bay's chart is drawn with (called, not copied; `PlotWindow.over` takes the points as one series); each kept point a filled 5 × 5 `Ellipse` in the first series colour carrying `dataPointDot position`, and each excluded point an unfilled 9 × 9 `Ellipse` ring with a red stroke of 1.5 carrying `dataExcludedPointMark position`, each centred on its point. No line joins the points. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type MappedPointNumber with member this.uiPosition : ConstructorUiPosition` (its value); `type MappedPoints with member this.pointCaptions : ControlCaption list`, one per point in order, numbers by `%g`: an intensity point `x = <x>, I = <intensity>`, an ellipsometric point `λ = <nm> nm, Ψ = <ψ>°, Δ = <δ>°`, a capture row `<label> #<capture index>: <description>° → <avg_total>`, an observation `<key> <T or R>: θ = <incidence>°, φ = <azimuth>°, m00 = <m00>` and a mapped row `<its scan cells' display values joined by \", \">: <signal, or m00>`; and `member this.chartPoints : ExperimentControls.ChartPoint list`, one per point, x its 1-based number and y its reading's first value (the intensity, Ψ in degrees, `avg_total`, the observation's m00, or the mapped signal or m00). On `ConstructorUiId`: `static member dataReviewButton (experimentId : ExperimentId) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataReview_<id>`), `static member dataPointRow (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataPoint_<n>`), `static member dataExcludePointButton (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataExcludePoint_<n>`) and `static member dataIncludePointButton (point : MappedPointNumber) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataIncludePoint_<n>`). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group, each with a one-line doc: `dataReviewPanel` (`\"DataReviewPanel\"`), `dataExclusionReasonField` (`\"DataExclusionReasonField\"`), `dataPointsChart` (`\"DataPointsChart\"`), `dataPointDot (point : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$\"DataPointDot_{point.value}\"`) and `dataExcludedPointMark (point : ConstructorUiPosition)` (`$\"DataPointExcluded_{point.value}\"`). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: each `dataFileRow` gains, after its attach verb, the verb `Review` carrying `dataReviewButton experiment.id` and sending `ReviewExperimentData experiment.id` (step 315), offered read-only too. When `model.reviewedDataOpt` is `Some r`, after the split panel, a bordered panel carrying `dataReviewPanel`: the heading `Points of <name> — <its badge text>` (`model.dataBadgeOf`, step 295); a `DockPanel` whose left child is `Reason:` and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `dataExclusionReasonField` that shows `model.dataDraft.exclusionReason` and sends `SetExclusionReason` on Enter and on losing focus; for `r.points = Ok points`, `ExperimentControls.pointsChartView ConstructorUiId.dataPointsChart` of the `chartPoints` marked `ExcludedPointMark` where the experiment's data excludes the point (`tryFindExclusion`, step 313), with the labels `point` and `reading`, and then one row per point carrying `dataPointRow n`: `#<n>  <its caption>` and, for an excluded point, `excluded — <reason>` in the message colour and the verb `Include` (`dataIncludePointButton n`, sending `IncludePoint`), otherwise the verb `Exclude` (`dataExcludePointButton n`, sending `ExcludePoint (id, n, model.dataDraft.exclusionReason)`), both disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`; for `Error e`, `e`'s caption. No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests` (step 324): `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `DataReviewPanel`, `DataExclusionReasonField`, `DataPointsChart`, `DataPointDot_2`, `DataPointExcluded_2`, `DataReview_1`, `DataPoint_2`, `DataExcludePoint_2` and `DataIncludePoint_2`. New `each mapped point reads as its caption and plots at its number`: the captions and chart points of a two-point intensity series, two Phone ROI rows and one observation (test-local) are as listed above, each x its number. `the review panel lists every point, an excluded one marked with its reason, and plots the excluded points as rings`: over the class's model whose data proxy is a mock answering E1's attachment with the series `0 → 1.0`, `45 → 0.5`, `90 → 0.0` and whose E1 data excludes point 2 for `beam blocked`, after `ReviewExperimentData (ExperimentId 1)`, the panel shows three point rows, row 2 reading `excluded — beam blocked` with `Include` and rows 1 and 3 `Exclude`, and the chart holds `DataPointDot_1`, `DataPointDot_3` and `DataPointExcluded_2` and no `DataPointDot_2`. `pressing Exclude sends the point with the typed reason, and Include takes it back`: over a recording dispatch with the reason field holding `stray light`, pressing `Exclude` of point 3 records `ExcludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 3, ControlCaption \"stray light\")` and pressing `Include` of point 2 records `IncludePoint (ExperimentId 1, MappedPointNumber 2)`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing Review shows the experiment's points and their chart`: in the rendered Data step over that model, pressing `dataReviewButton` of E1 shows `dataReviewPanel` and `dataPointsChart`.", "acceptance": "After the review panel lands, the Data step MUST review an experiment's points with each point's caption, an excluded point listed with its reason and drawn as a ring on the chart beside the kept dots, Exclude sending the typed reason and Include taking an exclusion back, under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Review shows the experiment's points and their chart`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `each mapped point reads as its caption and plots at its number`, `the review panel lists every point, an excluded one marked with its reason, and plots the excluded points as rings` and `pressing Exclude sends the point with the typed reason, and Include takes it back`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.each mapped point reads as its caption and plots at its number", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the review panel lists every point, an excluded one marked with its reason, and plots the excluded points as rings", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing Exclude sends the point with the typed reason, and Include takes it back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing Review shows the experiment's points and their chart", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ExperimentControls.PointMark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/Exper