", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataReviewPanel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataExclusionReasonField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataPointsChart", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataPointDot", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataExcludedPointMark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-REVIEW-PANEL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 326, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93n", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [325], "how_to": "Correcting the reviewed experiment's setup from the Data step, with its audit note and trail (001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact (e.g. \"LR was at −45\"), with a mandatory audit note'; 001 §P `CorrectSetup`; the S9.3 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: the review panel (step 325) ends with a `Setup:` block: the line `Setup: <the experiment's setup.describe>`; a `DockPanel` whose left child is `Audit note:` and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `dataCorrectionNoteField` that shows `model.dataDraft.correctionNote` and sends `SetCorrectionNote` (step 316) on Enter and on losing focus; a `WrapPanel` holding, for each setup of `model.kitSetups` in order whose `reference` is not the experiment's own, the verb `Re-point to <reference.describe>` carrying `dataCorrectSetupChoice setup.name` and sending `CorrectSetup (id, setup.reference, model.dataDraft.correctionNote)`, disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld`; and, when the experiment's `corrections` are not empty, a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `dataCorrectionTrail` with one wrapping line per correction, oldest first: `<previous.describe> → <corrected.describe>: <note>`. The lab file is never shown as changed, because it is not. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group, each with a one-line doc: `dataCorrectionNoteField` (`\"DataCorrectionNoteField\"`) and `dataCorrectionTrail` (`\"DataCorrectionTrail\"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, on `ConstructorUiId` beside `savedSetup` (step 260), with a one-line doc: `static member dataCorrectSetupChoice (name : SetupName) : ConstructorUiId` (`DataCorrectSetup_<name>`). No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests`: `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `DataCorrectionNoteField`, `DataCorrectionTrail` and `DataCorrectSetup_Bench B`. New `the correction panel offers every other setup of the kit and lists the audit trail`: over the class's model whose kit holds the setups `Setup 1` (E1's) and `Bench B`, and whose E1 holds one correction `'Setup 0' revision 1 → 'Setup 1' revision 1: LP1 was at 30`, the reviewed E1 shows `Setup: 'Setup 1' revision 1`, one choice `Re-point to 'Bench B' revision 1` and no choice for `Setup 1`, and the trail's one line. `pressing a setup sends CorrectSetup with the typed audit note`: over a recording dispatch with the note field holding `LR was at -45`, pressing the choice of `Bench B` records `CorrectSetup (ExperimentId 1, <Bench B revision 1>, ControlCaption \"LR was at -45\")`.", "acceptance": "After the correction panel lands, the reviewed experiment MUST show its setup, every other setup of the kit as a re-point choice sending `CorrectSetup` with the typed audit note, and its audit trail, under the stable ids of `ConstructorUiId`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the correction panel offers every other setup of the kit and lists the audit trail` and `pressing a setup sends CorrectSetup with the typed audit note`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the correction panel offers every other setup of the kit and lists the audit trail", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing a setup sends CorrectSetup with the typed audit note", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataCorrectionNoteField", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.dataCorrectionTrail", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.dataCorrectSetupChoice", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-CORRECTION-PANEL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 327, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93o", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [326], "how_to": "The experiment matrix at the top of the Data step, a data badge per experiment in each cell (001 §O 'Experiment matrix view: rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer, with a data badge per cell'; the S9.3 brief; S9.1's badges). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: `type MatrixRowKey with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its sources' labels joined by ` + ` (or `—`), ` · `, then its objects as `<label>@<angle.degreeCaption>` (step 280) joined by ` → ` (or `—`); `type MatrixColumnKey with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, its analyzers' labels joined by ` + ` (or `—`); and on `ConstructorUiId` `static member experimentMatrixEntry (experimentId : ExperimentId) : ConstructorUiId` (`ExperimentMatrixEntry_<id>`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Data step group: `experimentMatrix` (`\"ExperimentMatrix\"`), with a one-line doc. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`: first in the panel, the heading `Experiment matrix:` and a `Grid` carrying `experimentMatrix` over `ExperimentMatrix.ofExperiments model.experimentCollection.experiments model.kitSetups model.kitItems` (step 322): its first row the columns' captions, then one row per matrix row, its caption first and then, per column, a vertical `StackPanel` holding, for each experiment of that cell, a verb carrying `experimentMatrixEntry id` that reads `<name> · <model.dataBadgeOf experiment's text>` and sends `ReviewExperimentData id` (step 315), the reviewed experiment's on the positive background; an empty cell holds nothing. When `unplaced` is not empty, a wrapping line `Not in the matrix (setup missing): <their names joined by \", \">`. With no experiment, the line `(no experiments yet)`. No other control or message is added. Tests, in `DataStepTests`: `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `ExperimentMatrix` and `ExperimentMatrixEntry_1`. New `the matrix shows each experiment in its row and column with its data badge, and lists the unplaced ones`: over the class's model holding E1 over `Setup 1`, E2 over `Bench B` (its polarizer turned) and E3 over `Gone` revision 1, the grid holds the row captions of `Setup 1` and `Bench B`, E1's entry reading `E1 · no data` and E2's `E2 · no data`, and the line naming `E3`; after E1's data is attached through the class's mock, E1's entry reads `E1 · validated (3 points)`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `pressing a matrix entry reviews that experiment`: pressing E2's entry in the rendered Data step reviews E2 and shows `dataReviewPanel`. `ScrollExtentTests`: `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable` (step 323) also holds a pending split of three groups, a reviewed experiment of three points, one excluded, with one correction, and the matrix of three experiments, its assertion kept.", "acceptance": "After the matrix view lands, the Data step MUST open on the experiment matrix, each experiment in the row of its sources and objects with their angles and the column of its analyzers, showing its data badge and reviewing it when pressed, the experiments whose setup the kit lacks listed apart; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing a matrix entry reviews that experiment`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the matrix shows each experiment in its row and column with its data badge, and lists the unplaced ones`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` and `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the Data step UiIds are the stable intent-named ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.the matrix shows each experiment in its row and column with its data badge, and lists the unplaced ones", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests.pressing a matrix entry reviews that experiment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/DataStepTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests.the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.MatrixRowKey.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.MatrixColumnKey.caption", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.ConstructorUiId.experimentMatrixEntry", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.ConstructorUiId.experimentMatrix", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView.dataStepView", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S93-MATRIX-VIEW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 328, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S93p", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [327], "how_to": "The section proved end to end through the kit window and a real folder, and `AGENTS.md` told where data live (the S9.3 brief: update the AGENTS.md 'Main ribbon' gotcha to match; 001 §E 'Exclusions, corrections and mappings live in the experiment file'; AGENTS.md: drive by id and wait for deterministic conditions). Nothing in `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs` changes: the split wizard is the import wizard `ConstructorScene.mount` composes (steps 312, 321), and the Data step is part of `kitWindowView`. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs` (steps 184, 312, 323) gains, with trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: the Data step splits a lab file across the kit's experiments, excludes a point and corrects a setup, all kept in the kit`: over a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write, as `SetupModelTests`' is (steps 260, 263, 272): its items `LP1`, `QZ`, `QZ2`, `Laser` and `LPd`, its kit file holding `NamingTemplate.standard`, its table a linear polarizer holding `LP1`, a sample holding `QZ` turned to R1 45° and a second linear polarizer holding `LPd` before the seeded detector (each by `AssignSlot`), and, after the first polarizer is chosen (`ExpChooseElement`) and `ExpCommit`, the setup `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd` and its experiment `E1`, which the template names `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`, loaded into `initInverse` and mounted as step 312 mounts it (`kitWindowView` over the model, dispatching through `updateTableAndElementRotation`, its shell `KitWindowShell.inert`), and a test-local Phone ROI file written outside the kit, the UTF-8 of `experiment,capture_index,captured_at,description,avg_total` and the rows `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd,0,2026-07-15T12:00:00+00:00,0,869.5`, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd,1,2026-07-15T12:01:00+00:00,45,912.25`, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd-2,0,2026-07-15T12:02:00+00:00,0,870`, `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd,0,2026-07-15T12:03:00+00:00,0,801.5` and `Darkness,0,2026-07-15T12:04:00+00:00,0,12.5`, each ending in `\\n`: pressing `flowDataStep` shows `dataStepPanel`; dispatching `SplitByColumn (<the file>, ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv)`, as the split wizard's Split would, shows `dataSplitKeyColumn`; pressing the centres of `dataSplitOfferToggle` of `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` and then `dataSplitApplyButton` leaves `data/<the file's leaf>` holding the file's bytes, `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd.setup-json` and `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd.experiment-json` written, and `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`'s file mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to the rows of its key; pressing its `experimentMatrixEntry` shows `dataReviewPanel` with two point rows; dispatching `SetExclusionReason (ControlCaption \"saturated\")` and pressing `dataExcludePointButton` of point 2 leaves its file, read back through `readExperiments`, excluding point 2 for `saturated` and its entry reading `excluded points (1 excluded, 1 validated)`; dispatching `SetCorrectionNote (ControlCaption \"QZ was at 0\")` and pressing `dataCorrectSetupChoice` of `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` leaves that experiment over `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` revision 1: `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`'s file holds one correction with that note, its name and its data unchanged; and the lab file's bytes in `data/` are unchanged throughout. Each press waits for its control as step 312's fact does. (2) `AGENTS.md`: in the gotcha **Main ribbon**, the sentence naming the Experiments bay's \"Data files\" section becomes: Attach data file… lives in the Inverse constructor's Data step (DataStepView.fs), not in the Experiments bay; the rest of the bullet is unchanged. After the gotcha 'Lab files are read through import profiles' (step 312), one bullet of at most six lines: **The Data step never edits a lab file** (`DataSplits.fs`, `ExperimentMatrices.fs`, `DataStepView.fs`, spec 0050 S9.3): an exclusion numbers a point of its mapped attachment (`MappedPointNumber`, one per point, with its reason) and a new attachment starts with none; `MappedPoints.keptBy` is the one rule from exclusions to the points validated and fitted; a correction re-points `Experiment.setup` and appends its audit note, the name kept; a split groups a file by its profile's key column (`splitGroups`) and `DataSplit.ofGroups` matches by name, then by the template, else offers the setup the name describes; `MatchByTemplate` attaches the file once, each group as `KeyedDataRows`. Nothing else in the file changes.", "acceptance": "After the end-to-end proof lands, the kit window's Data step MUST split a lab file across a folder kit's experiments (matched and created), review an experiment from the matrix, exclude a point and correct a setup with the experiment files holding each and the lab file unchanged, and AGENTS.md MUST say where Attach data file… lives and carry the gotcha 'The Data step never edits a lab file'; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: the Data step splits a lab file across the kit's experiments, excludes a point and corrects a setup, all kept in the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataStepTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "AGENTS.md"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests.acceptance: the Data step splits a lab file across the kit's experiments, excludes a point and corrects a setup, all kept in the kit", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "obligations": ["S93-DATA-STEP-END-TO-END"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.3 -- One file, many experiments; exclusions, corrections, the Data step and the experiment matrix"}
{"number": 329, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S94a", "touches": ["BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [328], "how_to": "The reference half of `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` moves into the optics-mueller kit (001 §Q AT-1 'Data: … the reference pipeline's scripts, `README.md` and `reference_step1_summary.json` / `reference_step2_linear_summary.json` into `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/`'; 001 §S9 'MOVE `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` into the AT-1 kit folder'; .spec-md §3.20 'The optics-mueller archive moves whole'; the S9.4 brief). `data.zip`, the measured data, moves in step 330, which deletes the folder. This step changes no code and no behaviour, and `MuellerReconstructionTests`' numbers are unchanged. (1) `git mv` each of these seven files from `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` to `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` under the same name: `README.md`, `cpl_cpl_analyzer.py`, `matrix_glue.py`, `matrix_step1_air_fit.py`, `matrix_fit_linear.py`, `reference_step1_summary.json` and `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`. The four scripts and the two summaries keep their bytes; they hold no carriage return, so the `*.py` and `*.json` rules of `.gitattributes` (`.gitattributes:25`, `:35`) change nothing in them. No `.kit-json` or other kit file is written: S12.1 builds the kit around these files. Under `data/`, `.gitignore` ignores only `/data/chroma/` and `/data/*/.oc/` (`.gitignore:333-334`), so `git check-ignore` matches none of the new paths. (2) In the moved `README.md` only what the move makes untrue changes, in the README's own voice: (a) its opening paragraph says that this folder, the optics-mueller kit's `data/reference/`, holds the reference implementation and the reference numerical results that `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` was written against, and that the measured data it inventories is `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip`; (b) every other place that says `data.zip` is here (the paragraph after the provenance table, the `Measured data` table and the inventory sentence under it) names it by that repository path; (c) `Further reading` gains one bullet: `specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md` §Q AT-1 and §S9, which move this folder into the optics-mueller kit. Every other line keeps its text. (3) In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`, the comments that give the summaries' provenance name them at `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/`, and the README beside them as `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md`: the class doc's spec 0044 §8.5 bullet ('`reference_step*_summary.json` in that same folder'), the acceptance-band comment above `stage1Tol` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:stage1Tol`), the comment of `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` that names the README's inventory, the provenance comment of `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values`, and the two of `section 7.2 end-to-end: …` (in its spec 0044 §8.5 paragraph and above `expectedQz`). No code line changes. The other `Data/MuellerMatrix` texts under `Berreman/` change with what they describe: the class doc's bullet on `data.zip` and `loadDataSet`'s doc with the data (step 330), and the doc of `archiveEntryName` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName`) with that member (step 331).", "acceptance": "After the reference files move, `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` MUST hold `README.md`, the four scripts and the two summaries, the scripts and summaries byte for byte, `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` MUST hold only `data.zip`, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST name the summaries at their kit path; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/README.md", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/cpl_cpl_analyzer.py", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_glue.py", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_step1_air_fit.py", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_fit_linear.py", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/reference_step1_summary.json", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/reference_step2_linear_summary.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/cpl_cpl_analyzer.py", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_glue.py", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_step1_air_fit.py", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_fit_linear.py", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/reference_step1_summary.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/reference_step2_linear_summary.json", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.4 -- The optics-mueller lab files move into the kit folder"}
{"number": 330, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S94b", "touches": ["BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [329], "how_to": "The measured data moves out of `data.zip` into the optics-mueller kit byte for byte, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` reads it there, read-only, through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (001 §Q AT-1 'the CSV entries of `data.zip` into `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` … `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` is then deleted, with its `Content` link in `BerremanTests.fsproj` … There is no second copy of the data' and 'The CSVs are read through the existing `MuellerDataStore` parser (`parseMuellerCsv`, the \"Phone ROI CSV\" import profile)'; 001 §K 'Raw data is immutable'; 001 §G 'The two committed reference kits … are read-only to tests'; .spec-md §3.12, §3.20, §3.21 and §7 'moved byte-for-byte … There is no second copy'; the S9.4 brief). After this step nothing reads `data.zip`; the archive-keyed seam the tests stop using is retired in step 331. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' numbers are unchanged. (1) Byte for byte. The lab CSVs are CRLF text, all but `cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv` with a UTF-8 byte-order mark, and the catch-all `* text=auto eol=lf` (`.gitattributes:9`) would store them as LF, so a clone would hold other bytes than the archive and than the SHA-256 a kit records at attach (001 §E). `.gitattributes` therefore gains, after its last rule, a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S9.4 (lab files are kept exactly as recorded) and the rule `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/** -text !eol`, the form of its `*.nb` rule (`.gitattributes:58`). `AGENTS.md`'s 'Line endings: LF' gotcha (`AGENTS.md:513-516`) gains one sentence: the lab files under `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` are the exception, kept byte for byte by that rule (spec 0050 S9.4), and are never converted. (2) The move. Each entry of `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip` is written with the bytes the archive holds: each CSV to `data/optics-mueller/` joined with its archive path, so `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` becomes `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` and the eight exploratory CSVs land in `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/`; and each of the three `data/shapes/*.json` to `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/` under its own name. Before the archive is deleted, each written file's SHA-256 is checked against its entry's (the values in (4)). Then `data.zip` is deleted, with the folders `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` and `Berreman/Data/` it leaves empty. `BerremanTests.fsproj` loses the `ItemGroup` holding the `data.zip` `Content` link and its comment (`BerremanTests.fsproj:52-62`), and the comment above the `OpticalConstructor.Storage` `ProjectReference` (`BerremanTests.fsproj:88-90`), which names `createFileBacked`, gone since spec 0044, and the contract that step 331 retires; the reference stays, because the tests read the parser, the folder `KitProxy` and the Phone ROI CSV profile from Storage. The README (`data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md`, step 329) describes the data where it now is, in its own voice: the opening paragraph says the measured data is this kit's lab files under `data/raw/`; the paragraph after the provenance table says the lab files live in this kit, that `MuellerReconstructionTests` reads them read-only through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (`MuellerDataStore.parseMuellerCsv`), and that no code path references the external checkout; the provenance sentence on line endings says the scripts and summaries were converted to LF while the lab CSVs keep their recorded bytes; the `Measured data` table's row is `data/raw/`, the lab files moved byte for byte out of the former `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip` by spec 0050 S9.4; and the inventory says the folder holds 15 CSVs, seven of them the science data under `data/raw/final/` (the table's entries, now kit paths, keep their texts), the other eight earlier exploratory work under `data/raw/`, and that the archive's three beam-shape descriptions are in `data/reference/shapes/`. Every other line keeps its text. (3) The locator (.spec-md §3.21). New `Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs` in `namespace BerremanTests`, compiled directly before `MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` (one `<Compile>` line in `BerremanTests.fsproj`, no comment): `type CommittedKit = | OpticsMuellerKit`, the committed reference kits under the repository's `data/` folder, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.4 and saying that S10.2 moves it to `BerremanTestSupport`; and `member this.tryFindFolder : KitFolder option`: from `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, each folder upward in turn until one holds `Berreman/Berreman.slnx`, which is the repository root; the answer is `KitFolder (FolderName <root>/data/optics-mueller)` (`KitFolder`, step 122) when that folder exists, and `None` when no folder upward holds the solution or the kit folder is absent. It writes nothing and reads no environment variable. No other case, member or file is added; AT-2's kit adds its case when S12.2 commits that kit. (4) The reads, in `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`. `loadDataSet` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:loadDataSet`) becomes `loadDataSet (file : KitRelativePath) : MuellerRawRow list`: `OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, then `(KitProxy.create folder).readOnlyView.readDataFile file` (steps 126, 128 and 131: a read-only view writes nothing, not even `.oc/`), then `(BuiltInProfileChoice PhoneRoiCsvProfile).mapText` (step 303) of the file's `text`, answering its `CapturePoints` rows; no kit folder, a `KitError`, an `ExperimentDataError` or another `MappedPoints` case fails the test with what it says, as the helper fails today. Its doc says so in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.4. The seven data sets become test-local `KitRelativePath` values bound ahead of the members, each born by `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` (step 123) of its kit path, an `Error` failing the test: `lpLpFile` `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv`, `lpCplFile` `data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv`, `cplLpFile` `data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv`, `cplCplDay1File` `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv`, `cplCplDay2File` `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv`, `darknessChecksFile` `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv`, `bullshitChecksFile` `data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv`, the mapping `MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName` holds. `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values` and `section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly` drop `MuellerDataStore.createArchiveBacked ()`, bind `load` to `loadDataSet` and load each data set's file in place of its case (`load LpLpFamily` becomes `load lpLpFile`, …); every comment of theirs that names the archive store names the kit's lab files, and their bodies and assertions are otherwise unchanged. `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` becomes `the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts`: through `loadDataSet`, `lpLpFile` 209, `lpCplFile` 209, `cplLpFile` 209, `cplCplDay1File` 170, `cplCplDay2File` 57, `darknessChecksFile` 6, `bullshitChecksFile` 2 rows, its comment naming the inventory of `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md` (spec 0042 §6). New fact `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte`: through `(KitProxy.create folder).readOnlyView` over `OpticsMuellerKit.tryFindFolder`, `readDataFile` of each of these kit paths answers a file whose `contentHash` is the `ContentHash` (step 24) of its former archive entry's hex SHA-256: `data/raw/cpl_cpl.csv` `c1cbbde1c7b77acf6d23f972bb85f679e0072779d396a49aaf02b1d92e447eb5`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_big_center.csv` `515d16bb7a375b734038a8dbc6730bb6e726d99bfd11d954b986adf81d47b7b8`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_center.csv` `f2d97088f562cb5e8097b827b6774d1ba88baefd25b15f312515ad77b958d703`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_small_center.csv` `aa18398266782f7cedf15008a8e66beff28f89c81304d68e062d6f8f8216c78b`; `data/raw/cpl_cpl_standard_ellipse.csv` `94b8ef01770a12617f55e1b329d1513670044cee3c0c5e340e9c5826588372e5`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_095.csv` `59a7b7d7f223bf28c4623299df6a530f63787570eb346935b76d468228fbd3bc`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_105.csv` `4fd5b0b5fc09cd291d57732edfd1f582c37119c230c7550d100ebd4a94493336`; `data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv` `53de707ce70b9792d024db41ae39eac8506656916c97b0db1ef9f1512ef50813`; `data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv` `f2f7d28d881b57f5760562d030c12d1e554c7c8cc82d6657e9e4fb5c281c2c9e`; `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv` `9920ae4768558bd865c0190878adf97dde9901e9436a299a0c49e7d48ed39664`; `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv` `fcace7c401940d6b4a84347acd2b2afb925f5ea9c2c57e64fcc6d88e4ad26b2e`; `data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv` `9737ebe6534446ce3d4e1bcbcda222b88fae2d3c58de0cc8db1d322a5c002f39`; `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv` `3b11f42dd67f29a09275b13442849415c82d7a967f5d5933713abb06dfb43cc2`; `data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv` `d014c90144a98eb1949d30716be1f01049ec9763e0e3b94ceb68d2e43c4b1ba8`; `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv` `0fc29a63fd7de90b85842af5020cd79fb1e74ac2d24b49f7c7673cbead82cd81`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_095.json` `f8b15f8069d4986c6a68924349c66b0455b7a976da441adfdf5620af3d9e9425`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_105.json` `e254c679a2861bf5f625a03b5d62c2e6a6f3aac38f29afdfba632521370bedeb`; `data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_v1.json` `76bb56c20c63356640ad286f1f1b109eaa9714f7ea16c2606086705d88854f2d`. The class doc's first sentence names the Phone ROI CSV parser in place of 'the archive-backed `MuellerDataStore`', and its spec 0044 §8 bullet on `data.zip` says the measured data is the optics-mueller kit's lab files, found from the repository root and read read-only through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (spec 0050 S9.4); its other bullets keep their text. The trailing comments of the two `open OpticalConstructor.Storage…` lines are deleted. `muellerCsvFixture`, `malformedMuellerCsv`, `the real parseMuellerCsv parses a committed multi-column CSV fixture into MuellerRawRows (description elevated to Angle)` and `the real parseMuellerCsv maps a malformed file to a typed MuellerDataError, never a throw` are unchanged; the mock data proxy, its three facts and the two `tryLoadFromArchive` facts, which read no archive file, go with the seam in step 331.", "acceptance": "After the lab files move, `data/optics-mueller/data/raw/` MUST hold the fifteen CSVs and `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/` the three shape files, each byte for byte its former `data.zip` entry under the `-text !eol` rule, `Berreman/Data/` and the `data.zip` `Content` link MUST be gone, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST read the kit's lab files read-only through the Phone ROI CSV profile from the repository root; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers unchanged, `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` renamed `the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts` and `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte` added, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": [".gitattributes", "AGENTS.md", "Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl_big_center.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_center.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl_small_small_center.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_cpl_standard_ellipse.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_095.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_scale_105.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/cpl_lr45_standard_ellipse_subset.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_095.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_scale_105.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/shapes/standard_air_ellipse_v1.json", "data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md", "Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "successor": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts", "obligations": ["S94-LAB-FILES-IN-KIT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S94-LAB-FILES-IN-KIT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTests.CommittedKit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs", "obligations": ["S94-LAB-FILES-IN-KIT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.4 -- The optics-mueller lab files move into the kit folder"}
{"number": 331, "anchor": "RETIRE_CONTRACT", "ac": "AC-S94c", "id": "STORE_XDUO_0009", "name": "MuellerDataProxy", "kind": "proxy", "language": "fsharp", "declaring_project": "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [330], "how_to": "The archive-keyed load seam goes, with the data-set identity it was keyed by, the archive path, the two archive error cases and the archive store (001 §R '`MuellerDataSet` (a hard-coded DU of data sets), the archive-keyed `MuellerDataProxy` and `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/`. `parseMuellerCsv` is reused as an import profile'; 001 §S9 'DELETE the `MuellerDataSet` DU and the archive-keyed `MuellerDataProxy`'; 001 §T 'From section 9' (both greps), which this step makes true; .spec-md §0.1, rows `MuellerDataStore.fs` and `MuellerReconstruction.fs`; the S9.4 brief). After step 330 nothing reads them but the facts that test them. This step only deletes: no replacement seam, wrapper, path-keyed variant or compatibility alias is added. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: delete `MuellerDataSet` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:MuellerDataSet`), `MuellerArchivePath` (`:MuellerArchivePath`) and `MuellerDataProxy` (`:MuellerDataProxy`) with their docs, and the cases `ArchiveUnreadableErr` and `DataSetMissingErr` of `MuellerDataError` (`:MuellerDataError`). `MuellerDataError` keeps `MalformedRowErr` and `EmptyFileErr`; its doc becomes one to three lines: a typed failure of parsing a Phone ROI CSV text, never a throw (spec 0050 S9.4 removed the archive cases). The comment block that opens the seam ('Spec 0042 (005, ADD_CONTRACT STORE_XDUO_0009) — the Mueller measured-data LOAD seam …', `MuellerReconstruction.fs:293-320`, which also tells spec 0044 §8.3's re-key from `Experiments.DataFilePath`) becomes one to three lines: the capture rows of a Phone ROI CSV file, read through the Phone ROI CSV import profile (spec 0042; spec 0050 S9.4 deleted the archive-keyed seam). `MuellerExperimentLabel`, `CaptureIndex` and `MuellerRawRow` are unchanged. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs`: delete the `type MuellerDataSet with` extension holding `archiveEntryName` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName`, its doc naming `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/README.md`), `committedArchive`, `tryLoadFromArchive` and `createArchiveBacked` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:createArchiveBacked`) with their docs, and `open System.IO` and `open System.IO.Compression`, which nothing left reads; the `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction` line loses its trailing comment. The module doc becomes one to three lines: the Phone ROI CSV parser, the body of the `Phone ROI CSV` import profile (spec 0042 step 006; spec 0050 S9.2), whose archive store spec 0050 S9.4 deleted. `CaptureCsvRow` and `DataFileText.parseMuellerCsv` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:parseMuellerCsv`) are unchanged, their rules and diagnostics included. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs`: in `ChosenImportProfile.mapText` (step 303) the `PhoneRoiCsvProfile` arm loses its two arms for `ArchiveUnreadableErr` and `DataSetMissingErr`, and its doc the words about them; `MalformedRowErr r` stays `MalformedDataFileErr r` and `EmptyFileErr r` `EmptyDataFileErr r`. (4) In `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` the comment above `MuellerDataStore.fs`'s `<Compile>` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:46-49`, naming the step-005 `MuellerDataProxy` and `createFileBacked`) is deleted and nothing is added. (5) Tests. In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` delete the seam's five facts, `a mock MuellerDataProxy loads canned capture rows through its exact tryLoadDataSet signature`, `an unseeded data set yields a typed MuellerDataError from tryLoadDataSet, never a throw`, `a MuellerDataProxy compares by reference (the ReferenceEquality convention)`, `tryLoadFromArchive maps an absent archive to a typed ArchiveUnreadable, never a throw` and `tryLoadFromArchive maps an archive without the requested entry to a typed DataSetMissing, never a throw`, with `cannedRows`, `makeMockData`, `seededDataMock` and the comment block above them (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:79-105`), and `open System.IO.Compression` and `open System.IO`, which nothing left reads (the `DataSetMissing` fact wrote its throw-away archive under `%TEMP%`). Nothing replaces the five facts: the parser facts (`the real parseMuellerCsv parses a committed multi-column CSV fixture into MuellerRawRows (description elevated to Angle)`, `the real parseMuellerCsv maps a malformed file to a typed MuellerDataError, never a throw`) and step 330's kit facts cover what remains. In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`, the comment in `both proxies compare by reference (the ReferenceEquality convention)` names the `ExperimentDataProxy / MuellerSolverProxy` convention, dropping the retired proxy; no code changes there. After this step `git grep -n -E \"MuellerDataProxy|MuellerDataSet|MuellerArchivePath|ArchiveUnreadableErr|DataSetMissingErr|createArchiveBacked|tryLoadFromArchive|committedArchive|archiveEntryName|tryLoadDataSet\" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -w -E \"LpLpFamily|LpCplFamily|CplLpFamily|CplCplDay1|CplCplDay2|DarknessChecks|BullshitChecks\" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -F \"Data/MuellerMatrix\" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -w \"DataFilePath\" -- Berreman/` find nothing.", "acceptance": "After the retirement, `MuellerDataSet`, `MuellerArchivePath`, `MuellerDataProxy`, `ArchiveUnreadableErr`, `DataSetMissingErr`, `archiveEntryName`, `committedArchive`, `tryLoadFromArchive` and `createArchiveBacked` MUST be gone, with the five facts that test them, `parseMuellerCsv` MUST stay as the Phone ROI CSV profile's body, and `git grep -n -E \"MuellerDataProxy|MuellerDataSet|MuellerArchivePath|ArchiveUnreadableErr|DataSetMissingErr|createArchiveBacked|tryLoadFromArchive|committedArchive|archiveEntryName|tryLoadDataSet\" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -w -E \"LpLpFamily|LpCplFamily|CplLpFamily|CplCplDay1|CplCplDay2|DarknessChecks|BullshitChecks\" -- Berreman/`, `git grep -n -F \"Data/MuellerMatrix\" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -w \"DataFilePath\" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers unchanged and the count falling by 5; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MuellerDataStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/LabFileImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.a mock MuellerDataProxy loads canned capture rows through its exact tryLoadDataSet signature", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.an unseeded data set yields a typed MuellerDataError from tryLoadDataSet, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.a MuellerDataProxy compares by reference (the ReferenceEquality convention)", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.tryLoadFromArchive maps an absent archive to a typed ArchiveUnreadable, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.tryLoadFromArchive maps an archive without the requested entry to a typed DataSetMissing, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerDataSet", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerArchivePath", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerDataProxy", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.MuellerDataError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.MuellerDataStore.archiveEntryName", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.MuellerDataStore.tryLoadFromArchive", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.MuellerDataStore.createArchiveBacked", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"], "preserves_obligations": ["S94-RETIRE-ARCHIVE-SEAM"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S9.4 -- The optics-mueller lab files move into the kit folder"}
{"number": 332, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [331], "how_to": "The uniaxial crystal builder becomes product physics on its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16 'The crystal builders are product physics … promoted into `MuellerInverse.fs` as members of their parameter records, so ONE implementation exists'; the S10.1 brief 'UniaxialParameters gets the uniaxial builder MuellerInverseTests uses'). Two copies exist today, `buildUniaxialGyrotropic` (`MuellerInverseTests.fs:buildUniaxialGyrotropic`) and its body-for-body duplicates `buildLangasite` (`LangasiteInverseTests.fs:buildLangasite`) and the fact-local `buildUniaxial` of `BiaxialInverseTests`' `the triclinic parameter set is a strict generalization of the uniaxial one` (`BiaxialInverseTests.fs:433`); all three go (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs`, `UniaxialParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:UniaxialParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is the deleted builder's: `OpticalProperties.type_3_4_6_Crystal (EpsValue.fromRefractionIndex this.ordinaryIndex) (EpsValue.fromRefractionIndex this.extraordinaryIndex) this.g11 this.g33`, so diag(n_o², n_o², n_e²) and diag(g₁₁, g₁₁, g₃₃) stay the engine's own (`OpticalProperties/Active.fs:type_3_4_6_Crystal`). Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of a uniaxial gyrotropic crystal (classes 3/32/4/422/6/622) with these four constants, through the engine's class 3/4/6 builder (spec 0050 §3.16). `MuellerInverse.fs` opens `OpticalProperties.Active`, which Domain already reaches through its `Analytics` reference (`MaterialLibrary.fs:12` opens it). The module doc's sentence that `OpticalConstructor.Domain` does not reference `OpticalProperties`, so that nothing here names a crystal class (`MuellerInverse.fs:15-20`), becomes: the forward proxy takes a caller-supplied `'Parameters -> OpticalProperties` builder, each parameter record carries its crystal class's builder as `opticalProperties` (spec 0050 §3.16), and no named material lives here. No other line of the file changes. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`: delete `buildUniaxialGyrotropic` with its doc; `forward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`; in `orientForCut carries the optic axis from the surface normal into the surface plane` `props` is `quartz.opticalProperties`. (3) `Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs`: delete `buildLangasite` with its doc; `forward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs`: in `the triclinic parameter set is a strict generalization of the uniaxial one`, delete the local `buildUniaxial`; `uniaxialForward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member evaluates the same expression the three builders did. No test is added or removed. `LangasiteInverseTests`, whose facts drive the uniaxial member through `forward`, is the cheapest class that exercises it.", "acceptance": "After the promotion, `UniaxialParameters.opticalProperties` MUST be the one uniaxial builder, `buildUniaxialGyrotropic`, `buildLangasite` and `BiaxialInverseTests`' local `buildUniaxial` MUST be gone, and the three uniaxial forward models MUST read the member; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.a positive g11 moves the transmission maximum toward smaller analyzer angles", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.n_e and g33 are structurally invisible at z-cut normal incidence", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.the langasite plate measurement determines g11", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.the recovered parameters reproduce all six measured intensities within the noise the data carries", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.the residual Jacobian shows n_o is unobservable against the data's noise floor", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.orientForCut carries the optic axis from the surface normal into the surface plane", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.the triclinic parameter set is a strict generalization of the uniaxial one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.UniaxialParameters.opticalProperties", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.buildUniaxialGyrotropic", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests.buildLangasite", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-UNIAXIAL-BUILDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 333, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [332], "how_to": "The triclinic crystal builder moves onto its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16; the S10.1 brief 'TriclinicParameters gets BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `MuellerInverse.fs`, `TriclinicParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:TriclinicParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is `buildTriclinic`'s (`BiaxialSample.fs:buildTriclinic`): `{ eps = Eps.fromRefractionIndex (this.index1, this.index2, this.index3); mu = Mu.vacuum; rho = Rho.type_1_Crystal this.g11 this.g22 this.g33 this.g23 this.g13 this.g12 }`, the engine's own biaxial permittivity and full symmetric gyration tensor (`OpticalProperties/Active.fs:type_1_Crystal`). Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of a triclinic (class 1) gyrotropic crystal with these nine constants (spec 0050 §3.16). (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs`: delete `buildTriclinic` with its doc and the `open OpticalProperties.Active` line, which nothing left in the file reads; the module doc's first sentence drops 'the builder that turns nine numbers into engine tensors' and keeps the rest of its text. (3) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`: `forward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : TriclinicParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`; in `BiaxialInverseTests` the two `buildTriclinic triclinic` reads (in `the triclinic builder produces a biaxial permittivity and a FULL symmetric gyration tensor` and `orientForCut carries each of the three principal axes onto the surface normal, gyration tensor and all`) become `triclinic.opticalProperties`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member evaluates the same record expression. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s, 5 facts) is the cheapest class whose facts drive the member through `forward`; `BiaxialInverseTests` (997 s) is not selected, as the S10.1 brief directs.", "acceptance": "After the promotion, `TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties` MUST be the one triclinic builder, `BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic` MUST be gone, and both biaxial suites MUST read the member; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.a plate cut perpendicular to an optic axis is a pure circular retarder, and that is what buys the signal", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the order ambiguity is real on the principal cuts and is broken by the optic-axis cuts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible design constrains the gyration tensor FAR better than the idealized thin-plate one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-TRICLINIC-BUILDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 334, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [333], "how_to": "The absorbing triclinic builder moves onto its parameter record (.spec-md §3.16; the S10.1 brief 'AbsorbingTriclinicParameters gets AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) In `MuellerInverse.fs`, `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` (`MuellerInverse.fs:AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`) gains, after `axes`, `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` whose body is `buildAbsorbing`'s (`AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs:buildAbsorbing`) with `p` read as `this`: ε is the complex symmetric matrix with diagonal (n₁², n₂², n₃²) + i(ε″₁₁, ε″₂₂, ε″₃₃) and off-diagonal i·ε″₁₂, i·ε″₁₃, i·ε″₂₃ through `Eps.create`, μ is `Mu.vacuum`, and ρ is the purely imaginary symmetric matrix of the six gyration components through `Rho.create`, the same entries in the same order. Its doc, one to three lines: the engine's optical properties of an absorbing triclinic gyrotropic crystal; ε″ is general in the ε′ frame and ρ stays imaginary (spec 0050 §3.16; specs/0044/.manual/018-absorbing-biaxial-inverse.md). (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`: delete `buildAbsorbing` with its doc and the `open System.Numerics` line, which only the builder read; the module doc's first sentence drops 'the builder that turns fifteen numbers into engine tensors' and keeps the rest. (3) `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs`: `forward` becomes `createBerremanForward (fun (p : AbsorbingTriclinicParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) solverParameters`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the member builds the same complex entries by the same operations. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s, 7 facts) is the cheapest class whose facts drive the member; `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` (946 s) is not selected.", "acceptance": "After the promotion, `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties` MUST be the one absorbing builder, `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing` MUST be gone, and both absorbing suites MUST build their forward models through the member; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing sample attenuates, and every configuration stays physically realizable", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing measurement set recovers all FIFTEEN material constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.all fifteen parameters are observable and the problem is conditioned well enough to solve", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialSample.buildAbsorbing", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ABSORBING-BUILDER"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 335, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [334], "how_to": "The fit machinery gets its product home, and the configuration builder and the observation generator move first (001 §Q AT-2 'Promoted to product (`OpticalConstructor.Optimization`) … `observeWith`'; 001 §S10 first bullet; the S10.1 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs`, `module MuellerFitting` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `MuellerInverseSolver.fs`: one `<Compile Include=\"MuellerFitting.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj`, no comment. Its module doc, one to three lines: the Mueller-matrix fit machinery the inverse-problem suites, the study engine and the Planner share, moved from `BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` by spec 0050 S10.1 (spec 0044 manual tasks 010-016). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) `type MuellerFitError = | ObservationForwardErr of ForwardModelError`, doc one line: a typed failure of generating observations or fitting them, never a throw. Steps 337, 339, 341 and 342 add one case each, in their own words; no other case is added here. (3) `configurationOf` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:configurationOf`) moves with its incidence and azimuth as `float<deg>` (`Berreman.Constants.deg`), because a bare `double` beside our types is ELEV003 / ELEV010 and a measured `float<deg>` is the form `SampleAzimuth.degree` and `Angle.degree` already take (`MuellerInverse.fs:SampleAzimuth`; specs/0048/.manual/002-elevation-ledger.jsonl): `configurationOf (cut : SampleCut) (thickness : Thickness) (incidence : float<deg>) (azimuth : float<deg>) (observable : Observable) (waveLength : WaveLength) : MeasurementConfiguration`, with `incidenceAngle = Angle.degree incidence |> IncidenceAngle.create` and `azimuth = SampleAzimuth.degree azimuth`, the other fields as today. (4) `observeWith` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:observeWith`) moves as `observeWith (forward : ForwardModelProxy<'Parameters>) (truth : 'Parameters) (configurations : MeasurementConfiguration list) : Result<MuellerObservation list, MuellerFitError>`: each configuration in order through `forward.muellerOf c truth`, in the fold `MuellerInverse.forwardModels` uses (`MuellerInverse.fs:forwardModels`); the first `Error e` answers `Error (ObservationForwardErr e)` and evaluates nothing after it; otherwise `Ok` of `{ configuration = c; measured = m }` in configuration order. (5) `Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs`: delete `configurationOf` and `observeWith`, and add to the module `let expectOk (result : Result<'Value, MuellerFitError>) : 'Value` answering the `Ok` value and failing the test with `failwith $\"%A{e}\"` on `Error e`; its doc, one line: a moved product call's value, or the test fails with its typed error (spec 0050 S10.1). It is the one test-side assertion every later move uses. (6) Callers. The local `configuration` helpers of `MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` keep their `double` parameters and pass `(incidenceDeg * 1.0<deg>) (azimuthDeg * 1.0<deg>)` to `configurationOf`. The `observe` helpers of `MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs` become `observeWith forward <truth> configurations |> expectOk`, so their signatures and every fact using them are unchanged. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): a multiplication by `1.0<deg>` is exact, so `Angle.degree` receives the same double, and the forward calls run in the same order. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` is the cheapest class that builds configurations through `configurationOf` and observes them through `observeWith`.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitting.fs` MUST declare `MuellerFitError`, `configurationOf` (incidence and azimuth in `float<deg>`) and `observeWith` (a `Result` whose first forward failure is `ObservationForwardErr`), compiled directly after `MuellerInverseSolver.fs`, `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare neither function and MUST declare `expectOk`, and every suite MUST build its configurations and observations through the product; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.every plate in this design is one a vendor will actually sell", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.a plate cut perpendicular to an optic axis is a pure circular retarder, and that is what buys the signal", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the order ambiguity is real on the principal cuts and is broken by the optic-axis cuts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible design constrains the gyration tensor FAR better than the idealized thin-plate one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.configurationOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.observeWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.expectOk", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.configurationOf", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.observeWith", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-OBSERVE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 336, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [335], "how_to": "The residual closures, the Jacobian adapter and the generic scaling move into `MuellerFitting` (001 §Q AT-2 '`observeWith`, `residualFor`, `throughputResidualFor`; `scalingAround`'; the S10.1 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) Into `MuellerFitting.fs` (step 335), after `observeWith`, with their signatures and bodies unchanged: `residualFor` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:residualFor`), the total, fixed-length 15-per-observation closure with its 1.0e3 penalty; `throughputResidualFor` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:throughputResidualFor`), 16 per observation, the 16th the log-throughput difference; `residualJacobianAt` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:residualJacobianAt`), the `FitQuality.residualJacobian` adapter over `ScaledVector`; and `scalingAround` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:scalingAround`). Every signature already speaks `ForwardModelProxy`, `MuellerObservation`, `ParameterScaling`, `ScaledVector`, `ResidualVector` and `ResidualJacobian`, the last three `[<NumericCarrier>]` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualVector`, `:ScaledVector`, `:ResidualJacobian`), so no shape changes. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. The throughput closure keeps one line saying the log term restores the isotropic absorption that normalization discards (specs/0044/.manual/018-absorbing-biaxial-inverse.md). (2) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes the four; its `fitWithResidual`, `fitObservations` and `fitAbsorbingObservations`, which step 337 moves, call the product closures. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. The generic `scalingAround` has no caller in BerremanTests today: `BiaxialSample.scalingAround`, `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.absorbingScalingAround` and `MuellerInverseTests.scalingAround` build their own one-argument specialisations and shadow it. It moves because 001 §Q AT-2 lists it for the study engine (S11). The shadowing comment above `MuellerInverseTests.scalingAround` ('It deliberately shadows the harness's general `scalingAround`') names `MuellerFitting.scalingAround`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the bodies are unchanged. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` reaches `residualFor` and `residualJacobianAt`, and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` reaches `throughputResidualFor`, the two cheapest classes that do.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitting.fs` MUST declare `residualFor`, `throughputResidualFor`, `residualJacobianAt` and `scalingAround` with unchanged signatures and bodies, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible design constrains the gyration tensor FAR better than the idealized thin-plate one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing measurement set recovers all FIFTEEN material constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.all fifteen parameters are observable and the problem is conditioned well enough to solve", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.residualFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.residualJacobianAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.scalingAround", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.residualFor", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.throughputResidualFor", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.residualJacobianAt", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.scalingAround", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RESIDUAL-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 337, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [336], "how_to": "The search box, the fit record and the three fit runners move into `MuellerFitting` (001 §Q AT-2 '`scalingAround`, `fitWithResidual`, `fitObservations`, `fitAbsorbingObservations`'; the S10.1 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) Into `MuellerFitting.fs`, after `scalingAround`: `SearchBox` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:SearchBox`) with `halfWidth`, unchanged; and the harness's `InverseFit<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:InverseFit`) RENAMED `MuellerFitData<'Parameters>`, because `InverseFit` is already the module `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.InverseFit` (`InverseFit.fs:InverseFit`) and names are unique, not qualified (ELEV014 / ELEV015; the S10.1 brief): the same `[<ReferenceEquality>]` record `{ recovered; solution : NonlinearSolution; scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>; residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector }` with the members `chiSquared` and `rmsResidual`, bodies unchanged. (2) `MuellerFitError` gains `NonlinearFitErr of NonlinearSolverError` (the solve failed). (3) `fitWithResidual (box : SearchBox) (residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector) (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) : Result<MuellerFitData<'Parameters>, MuellerFitError>`: the request is today's (`InverseFitHarness.fs:fitWithResidual`: start at the zero vector, bounds ±`box.halfWidth`, `IterationCount 400`, `StepTolerance 1.0e-12`, through `MuellerInverseSolver.createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt ()`), `Ok` carries the same record, and a solver `Error e` answers `Error (NonlinearFitErr e)`. `fitObservations` and `fitAbsorbingObservations` keep their parameters and answer `fitWithResidual`'s `Result` over `residualFor` and `throughputResidualFor`. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (4) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes `SearchBox`, `InverseFit` and the three runners. `NoisyExperiment.fit`, `fitReportOf` and `predictedRelativeErrors`, which steps 341 and 342 move, take `MuellerFitData<'Parameters>`. (5) Callers unwrap with `expectOk`: `fitObservations … |> expectOk` in `BiaxialInverseTests` (`recoverFromNoisy` and its two fit facts) and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`; `fitAbsorbingObservations … |> expectOk` in `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` and in `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.recoverFromNoisy`; `MuellerInverseTests`' own `fitObservations` wrapper calls `MuellerFitting.fitObservations forward box observations (scalingAround start) |> expectOk` and keeps its tuple, and its `recoverFromNoisy` record literal is the renamed record. The `MuellerInverseTests` comments that place the fit driver in the harness say where it now is: the class doc's 'The fit driver both suites use lives in `InverseFitHarness`' names `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting`, the wrapper's doc 'the shared harness runner' names `MuellerFitting.fitObservations`, and the trailing comment of `open BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness` is deleted. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the request, the solver and the record are unchanged. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` runs `fitObservations` and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` runs `fitAbsorbingObservations`, both through `fitWithResidual`, the two cheapest classes that fit.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitting.fs` MUST declare `SearchBox`, `MuellerFitData<'Parameters>` and the three fit runners answering `Result<MuellerFitData<'Parameters>, MuellerFitError>` (a solver failure being `NonlinearFitErr`), `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them and no type named `InverseFit`, and every suite MUST fit through the product; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing measurement set recovers all FIFTEEN material constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.SearchBox", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.fitWithResidual", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.fitObservations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.fitAbsorbingObservations", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.SearchBox", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFit", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.fitWithResidual", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.fitObservations", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.fitAbsorbingObservations", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-FIT-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 338, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [337], "how_to": "The relative error and the per-parameter recovery errors move into `MuellerFitting` (the S10.1 brief 'RelativeError … recoveryErrors'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) New in `MuellerFitting.fs`, after `fitAbsorbingObservations`: `type QuantityValue = | QuantityValue of double` with `member this.value`, doc one line: a recovered quantity's value in its own physical units (an index, a gyration or ε″ component, a birefringence). It exists because `RelativeError.between` took two bare `double`s beside our type (ELEV010), and steps 341 and 342 read every recovered value through it. (2) `RelativeError` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:RelativeError`) moves with `value`, and `between` becomes `static member between (actual : QuantityValue) (expected : QuantityValue) : RelativeError`, the same `|actual − expected| / |expected|` on the two values. `recoveryErrors` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:recoveryErrors`) moves after it with its signature, each axis's error being `RelativeError.between` of `QuantityValue (a.read recovered)` and `QuantityValue (a.read truth)`. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (3) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes `RelativeError` and `recoveryErrors`. Until step 341 moves them, `statisticsFor`'s `bias` and `worst` call `RelativeError.between` over `QuantityValue` of the same doubles, and `describeErrors` reads the product type. `MuellerInverseTests.relativeError` becomes `RelativeError.between (QuantityValue actual) (QuantityValue expected)`. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the division runs on the same doubles. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` asserts on `recoveryErrors`, the cheapest class that does.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitting.fs` MUST declare `QuantityValue`, `RelativeError` (whose `between` takes two `QuantityValue`s) and `recoveryErrors`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare neither `RelativeError` nor `recoveryErrors`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.QuantityValue", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.RelativeError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.recoveryErrors", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.RelativeError", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.recoveryErrors", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-RELATIVE-ERROR-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 339, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [338], "how_to": "The bench noise model's functions move into Optimization beside their Domain budgets (001 §Q AT-2 'the bench noise model (`NoiseSeed`, …, `UniformDeviateProvider`, `disturb`, `misread`, `misreadAbsolute`, `noisyObserveWith`, `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith`)'; .spec-md §3.23: the data types `AngleUncertainty`, `ElementUncertainty`, `ThroughputUncertainty` and `NoiseParam` have lived in Domain's `ItemModels.fs` since step 213, and S10.1 moves the functions). This step moves the transparent path; step 340 moves the absorbing one. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs`, `module BenchNoise` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `MuellerFitting.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment), opening `OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemModels` for `NoiseParam`. Its module doc, one to three lines: the bench measurement-error model, angle errors filed against the nominal configuration and detector errors on the normalized elements, uniform max errors drawn from a seeded provider; the magnitudes and their sources are specs/0044/.manual/011-noisy-measurement-tests.md and, for the throughput, 019-absorbing-biaxial-noisy-tests.md (moved by spec 0050 S10.1). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) In it: `NoiseSeed` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:NoiseSeed`) with `value`, unchanged. New `type UniformDeviate = | UniformDeviate of double` with `member this.value`, doc one line: one draw, uniform on [−1, +1]; it exists because the provider's field `unit -> double` is ELEV008. `UniformDeviateProvider` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:UniformDeviateProvider`) keeps `[<ReferenceEquality>]` and becomes `{ nextDeviate : unit -> UniformDeviate }`; `fromSeed (seed : NoiseSeed)` keeps `System.Random(seed.value)` and answers `2.0 * rng.NextDouble() - 1.0 |> UniformDeviate` per draw. `disturb` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:disturb`) keeps its signature and its signed `IncidenceAngle + Angle` excursion, its wobble `noise.rotation.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value |> Angle`. `misread` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:misread`) answers `Result<MuellerMatrix, MuellerFitError>`: the same element loop over `m.normalized` (row by row, m₀₀ left at 1, each other element plus `noise.element.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value`), and a normalization `Error e` is `Error (MuellerNormalizationErr e)`. `noisyObserveWith` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:noisyObserveWith`) keeps its five parameters and answers `Result<MuellerObservation list, MuellerFitError>`: one provider from the seed, each nominal configuration in order disturbed, sent through `forward.muellerOf` (an `Error e` is `ObservationForwardErr e`), misread, and filed against the NOMINAL configuration; the first `Error` stops the walk. The draws are taken in exactly today's order, two for `disturb` then fifteen for `misread` per configuration, so a seed gives the same stream bit for bit. (3) `MuellerFitError` gains `MuellerNormalizationErr of InversionError` (a generated matrix could not be normalized). (4) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes `NoiseSeed`, `UniformDeviateProvider`, `disturb`, `misread` and `noisyObserveWith`, and the measurement-error banner above `NoiseSeed` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:59-110`), whose narrative and sources specs/0044/.manual/011 already records (AGENTS.md 'Document a decision once'). Until step 340, its `misreadAbsolute` reads `(draws.nextDeviate ()).value` and its `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith` calls the product `disturb`; `ensembleSeeds` maps the product `NoiseSeed`. (5) Callers. `MuellerInverseTests`: `firstTen` reads `(d.nextDeviate ()).value`, the direct `misread` read pipes `|> expectOk`, and `noisyObserve` is `noisyObserveWith forward quartz noise seed configurations |> expectOk`; the comments that send the reader to 'the commentary above `NoiseParam.decentLab`' or say the model 'lives in `InverseFitHarness`' (the class doc, the banner above `blindStart`, the one above the noisy facts) name `BenchNoise` and specs/0044/.manual/011-noisy-measurement-tests.md. `BiaxialInverseTests.recoverFromNoisy` pipes `noisyObserveWith … |> expectOk`, and its two comments that place the measurement-error model or its commentary in `InverseFitHarness` (the noisy-section banner, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs:233-234`, and the ensemble fact's 'see the commentary in `InverseFitHarness`', `:829-830`) name `BenchNoise` and specs/0044/.manual/011 likewise. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the generator, the draw order and every arithmetic expression are unchanged. No test is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests` (about 456 s) is the one class below `BiaxialInverseTests` that reaches `disturb`, `misread`, `noisyObserveWith` and the provider: `the measurement-error model is reproducible, bounded, and files data against the NOMINAL angles` drives each directly and the ensemble fact drives `noisyObserveWith`.", "acceptance": "After the move, `BenchNoise.fs` MUST declare `NoiseSeed`, `UniformDeviate`, `UniformDeviateProvider`, `disturb`, `misread` and `noisyObserveWith` (the last two answering `Result`s with `MuellerNormalizationErr` and `ObservationForwardErr`), compiled directly after `MuellerFitting.fs`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them and no measurement-error banner; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.the measurement-error model is reproducible, bounded, and files data against the NOMINAL angles", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers every constant, and its scatter IS what one fit's own covariance predicts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.NoiseSeed", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.UniformDeviate", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.UniformDeviateProvider", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.disturb", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.misread", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.noisyObserveWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.NoiseSeed", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.UniformDeviateProvider", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.disturb", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.misread", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.noisyObserveWith", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-NOISE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 340, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [339], "how_to": "The absorbing half of the noise model moves into `BenchNoise` (001 §Q AT-2; .spec-md §3.23), which makes 001 §T 'From section 10' true: `git grep -n -F \"let noisyObserveAbsoluteWith\" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/` finds nothing, as every section from S10.2 on asserts. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) Into `BenchNoise.fs`, after `misread`: `misreadAbsolute` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:misreadAbsolute`) answering `Result<MuellerMatrix, MuellerFitError>`: the throughput draw FIRST (`trueThroughput * (1.0 + noise.throughput.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value)`), then the fifteen element draws in `misread`'s order, each reported element `reportedThroughput * (n.element i j + noise.element.value * (draws.nextDeviate ()).value)` and m₀₀ the reported throughput; a normalization `Error e` is `Error (MuellerNormalizationErr e)`. After `noisyObserveWith`: `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:noisyObserveAbsoluteWith`), the same walk as `noisyObserveWith` with `misreadAbsolute`, answering `Result<MuellerObservation list, MuellerFitError>`. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. `misreadAbsolute` keeps one line saying the throughput draw comes first so a seed reproduces the experiment (specs/0044/.manual/019-absorbing-biaxial-noisy-tests.md). (2) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes both. `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.recoverFromNoisy` pipes `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith forward absorbing noise seed fullConfigurations |> expectOk`. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the draws are taken in the same order by the same arithmetic. No test is added or removed. The absorbing path is reached by `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` alone (946 s, its one ensemble fact), so that class is selected here and nowhere else in S10.1, as the S10.1 brief allows for a function reached nowhere else.", "acceptance": "After the move, `BenchNoise.fs` MUST declare `misreadAbsolute` and `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith` answering `Result`s, `git grep -n -F \"let noisyObserveAbsoluteWith\" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST find nothing (001 §T 'From section 10'), and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` MUST draw its observations through the product; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers the absorption far better than the optical activity", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.misreadAbsolute", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.BenchNoise.noisyObserveAbsoluteWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/BenchNoise.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.misreadAbsolute", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.noisyObserveAbsoluteWith", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ABSOLUTE-NOISE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 341, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [340], "how_to": "The ensemble statistics move into Optimization (001 §Q AT-2 '`RecoveredQuantity`, `RecoveryStatistics`, `statisticsFor`'; the S10.1 brief 'RecoveredQuantity, RecoveryStatistics, NoisyExperiment, statisticsFor, standardErrorOfMean, rowFor'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. Names are `ParameterName`s and values `QuantityValue`s (step 338), because a bare `string` or `double` in a record field or beside our types is ELEV008 / ELEV010. Errors are values (AGENTS.md: 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the harness `failwith`s becomes an `Error` of `MuellerFitError`, and the tests unwrap it with `expectOk`. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs`, `module RecoveryEnsembles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `BenchNoise.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment). Its module doc, one to three lines: what an ensemble of noisy experiments says about each recovered quantity, moved by spec 0050 S10.1 (specs/0044/.manual/011-noisy-measurement-tests.md). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) In it: `RecoveredQuantity<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:RecoveredQuantity`) becomes `{ name : ParameterName; valueIn : 'Parameters -> QuantityValue }`, `ofAxis axis` reading `QuantityValue (axis.read p)` and `derived (name : ParameterName) (valueIn : 'Parameters -> QuantityValue)`. `RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:RecoveryStatistics`) keeps its fields with `mean` and `absoluteScatter` as `QuantityValue`; `describe` renders the same text from their values. `NoisyExperiment<'Parameters>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:NoisyExperiment`) is `{ seed : NoiseSeed; fit : MuellerFitData<'Parameters> }`. New `type EnsembleSize = | EnsembleSize of int` with `value`, doc one line: how many experiments an ensemble holds. `statisticsFor` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:statisticsFor`) keeps its signature and runs today's arithmetic on the same doubles in the same order (the mean by `List.average`, the Bessel-corrected variance, `bias` as `RelativeError.between` of the mean and the truth, `scatter` as `sqrt variance / abs truth`, `worst` the `List.max` of the per-experiment `RelativeError`s), its `mean` and `absoluteScatter` born as `QuantityValue`s. `standardErrorOfMean (size : EnsembleSize) (row : RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>) : RelativeError` is `row.scatter.value / sqrt (float size.value) |> RelativeError`. `rowFor (table : RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters> list) (name : ParameterName) : Result<RecoveryStatistics<'Parameters>, MuellerFitError>` answers the row whose `quantity.name` is `name`, and `Error (UnknownQuantityErr name)` when none is. (3) `MuellerFitError` gains `UnknownQuantityErr of ParameterName` (no ensemble row of that name). (4) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes the three types and the three functions. (5) Callers, test code only. `BiaxialSample.recoveredQuantities`, `MuellerInverseTests.recoveredQuantities` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.reportedQuantities` pass `RecoveredQuantity.derived (ParameterName \"<name>\") (fun p -> QuantityValue (<today's expression>))`. In `MuellerInverseTests`, `BiaxialInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` every `rowFor table <name>` becomes `(rowFor table (ParameterName <name>) |> expectOk)`, and `rowFor table name.value` (`observedScatter`, whose `name` is already a `ParameterName`) becomes `(rowFor table name |> expectOk)`; every `absoluteScatter` compared as a number reads `.value`, and `standardErrorOfMean (List.length <seeds>) row` becomes `standardErrorOfMean (EnsembleSize (List.length <seeds>)) row`. Every band, message and assertion keeps its text. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the statistics are the same operations on the same doubles. No test is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact is the cheapest that drives all six (`BiaxialInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests`, at about 1000 s each, are not selected).", "acceptance": "After the move, `RecoveryEnsembles.fs` MUST declare `RecoveredQuantity` (named by `ParameterName`, valued in `QuantityValue`), `RecoveryStatistics`, `NoisyExperiment`, `EnsembleSize`, `statisticsFor`, `standardErrorOfMean` and `rowFor` (an unknown name being `UnknownQuantityErr`), compiled directly after `BenchNoise.fs`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers every constant, and its scatter IS what one fit's own covariance predicts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.RecoveredQuantity", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.RecoveryStatistics", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.NoisyExperiment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.EnsembleSize", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.statisticsFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.standardErrorOfMean", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.RecoveryEnsembles.rowFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/RecoveryEnsembles.fs", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.RecoveredQuantity", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.RecoveryStatistics", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.NoisyExperiment", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.statisticsFor", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.standardErrorOfMean", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.rowFor", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-ENSEMBLE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 342, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [341], "how_to": "A fit's own account of its uncertainty moves into Optimization, for the Planner's layer 2 (001 §Q AT-2 '`predictedRelativeErrors`, `combinationVariance` (the Planner's layer 2 reuses them, §M)'; the S10.1 brief 'fitReportOf … predictedRelativeErrors, combinationVariance, differenceWeights'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) `fitReportOf` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:fitReportOf`), a function of one of our types, becomes the member `member this.report : FitQuality.FitReport` of `MuellerFitData` in `MuellerFitting.fs` (ELEV013), with its body: `FitQuality.reportFrom` over the residual and the solution as a `DesignVector`, with the final residuals. (2) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs`, `module FitUncertainty` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `RecoveryEnsembles.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment). Its module doc, one to three lines: what a fit's covariance and Jacobian say about the uncertainty of its parameters and of their combinations, moved by spec 0050 S10.1 for the Planner (001 §M). Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (3) In it: `type ParameterWeights = | ParameterWeights of float[]` with `value`, marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"a weight vector over a fit's parameters in its scaling's axis order (R3): read whole against the covariance and the residual Jacobian\")>]` (the S10.1 brief: float[] weight vectors are carriers). `type PredictedVariance = | PredictedVariance of double` with `value`, doc one line: the variance a fit's covariance predicts for a linear combination of its parameters, in scaled units. `predictedRelativeErrors` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:predictedRelativeErrors`) moves with its signature over `MuellerFitData` and body. `combinationVariance (quality : FitQuality.FitReport) (weights : ParameterWeights) : PredictedVariance` is today's `wᵀCw` double sum (`InverseFitHarness.fs:combinationVariance`) on the carrier's array. `differenceWeights (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) (plus : ParameterName) (minus : ParameterName) : Result<ParameterWeights, MuellerFitError>` answers, built without mutation, the vector holding 1.0 at `plus`'s axis, −1.0 at `minus`'s (−1.0 when they coincide, as today) and 0.0 elsewhere; an axis name that is not in `scaling.axes` is `Error (UnknownAxisErr <name>)`. (4) `MuellerFitError` gains `UnknownAxisErr of ParameterName` (no fitted parameter of that name). (5) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes the four. Callers: `fitReportOf first.fit` becomes `first.fit.report` in `MuellerInverseTests` and `BiaxialInverseTests`; in `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact `pairVariance` is `combinationVariance quality (differenceWeights first.fit.scaling (ParameterName \"n_e\") (ParameterName \"n_o\") |> expectOk)`, read as `pairVariance.value` in `pairPrediction` and in the message. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the report, the conversion out of the scaled space and the quadratic form are unchanged. No test is added or removed. `MuellerInverseTests`' ensemble fact drives all four; `BiaxialInverseTests` (997 s) is not selected.", "acceptance": "After the move, `MuellerFitData.report` MUST replace `fitReportOf`, `FitUncertainty.fs` MUST declare `ParameterWeights` (a `[<NumericCarrier>]`), `PredictedVariance`, `predictedRelativeErrors`, `combinationVariance` and `differenceWeights` (an unknown axis being `UnknownAxisErr`), compiled directly after `RecoveryEnsembles.fs`, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST declare none of them; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerInverseTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers every constant, and its scatter IS what one fit's own covariance predicts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitData.report", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.ParameterWeights", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.PredictedVariance", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.predictedRelativeErrors", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.combinationVariance", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.differenceWeights", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.MuellerFitError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.fitReportOf", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.predictedRelativeErrors", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.combinationVariance", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.differenceWeights", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-COVARIANCE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 343, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S101l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [342], "how_to": "The last two harness functions move, and `InverseFitHarness.fs` is left holding only test assertions and formatting (001 §Q AT-2 '`BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` keeps only test assertions (`assertMuellerEqual`, the error formatting) and opens the product modules'; the S10.1 brief 'sumWeights, directionalSensitivity'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one declaration of each moved name exists. (1) Into `FitUncertainty.fs`, after `differenceWeights`: `sumWeights (scaling : ParameterScaling<'Parameters>) (names : ParameterName list) : Result<ParameterWeights, MuellerFitError>` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:sumWeights`), built without mutation, 1.0 at each named axis and 0.0 elsewhere, the first name not in `scaling.axes` being `Error (UnknownAxisErr name)`; new `type DirectionalSensitivity = | DirectionalSensitivity of double` with `value`, doc one line: how hard the residual pushes back along one direction of parameter space, ‖J·v‖ for a unit v; and `directionalSensitivity (jacobian : ResidualJacobian) (direction : ParameterWeights) : DirectionalSensitivity` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:directionalSensitivity`), today's normalization and row sums on the carrier's array. Each moved declaration's doc is cut to its contract in one to three lines (AGENTS.md 'Comments: short, precise, useful'), keeping one line where it guards a hazard the code cannot show. (2) `InverseFitHarness.fs` deletes both and is left with five module bindings and no type, each doc one to three lines: `expectOk` (step 335), `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds` (`InverseFitHarness.fs:describeErrors`, `:describeColumnNorms`, `:assertMuellerEqual`, `:ensembleSeeds`), their bodies unchanged. Its module doc becomes one to three lines: the test-side assertions and formatting the inverse-problem suites share; the machinery they drive is `OpticalConstructor.Optimization`'s `MuellerFitting`, `BenchNoise`, `RecoveryEnsembles` and `FitUncertainty` (spec 0050 S10.1). An `open` nothing in the file reads any more is deleted. (3) `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`: `isotropicAbsorption` answers `ParameterWeights` as `sumWeights scaling [ ParameterName \"e11\"; ParameterName \"e22\"; ParameterName \"e33\" ] |> expectOk`; `anisotropicAbsorption` answers `ParameterWeights`, its array built as today and wrapped where it is born; in `normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it` the three sensitivities are compared and reported through `.value`, every band and message text unchanged. (4) `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`' class doc sentence 'The fit driver, the residual, the scaling, the measurement-error model and the acceptance arithmetic are all shared with `MuellerInverseTests` through `InverseFitHarness`' (`BiaxialInverseTests.fs:94-95`) names the four product modules instead; the rest of that doc keeps its text. Every consumer opens the product module where the compiler asks and changes nothing else unless named here. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the weights hold the same 1.0 / 0.0 entries and the norm is the same sum. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` is the one class that reaches `sumWeights` and `directionalSensitivity`. After this step `git grep -n -E \"^    let |^type \" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` lists exactly `expectOk`, `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds`.", "acceptance": "After the move, `FitUncertainty.fs` MUST declare `sumWeights` (a `Result` over `ParameterName`s), `DirectionalSensitivity` and `directionalSensitivity`, and `git grep -n -E \"^    let |^type \" -- Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs` MUST list exactly `expectOk`, `describeErrors`, `describeColumnNorms`, `assertMuellerEqual` and `ensembleSeeds`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the nineteen s33 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/InverseFitHarness.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.sumWeights", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.DirectionalSensitivity", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.FitUncertainty.directionalSensitivity", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/FitUncertainty.fs", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.sumWeights", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness.directionalSensitivity", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S101-DIRECTION-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.1 -- The bench noise model and the fit harness move into Optimization"}
{"number": 344, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S102a", "touches": ["BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [343], "how_to": "The shared test-support project is born, and S9.4's repository-root kit locator is its first source (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs … move into a shared test-support project, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/`, one `.fsproj` in its own folder. Both `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` reference it, so one compiled copy serves both test suites'; 001 §S10 'create `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/` (own folder, own `.fsproj`, a plain library)'; .spec-md §3.21 'The helper lives in `BerremanTests` until S10 moves it to `BerremanTestSupport`'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `CommittedKit` exists. (1) New `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`, the only project file in its folder (AGENTS.md 'One `.fsproj` per folder'). It is a plain library, not a test project: no `OutputType`, `IsTestProject` or `UseMicrosoftTestingPlatformRunner` property and no test package. Its two property groups are those of `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj` (`OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj:3-14`) without the `AssemblyName` line: `TargetFramework` `net10.0`, `Platforms` `x64` and `IsPackable` `false`; and, for `Release|x64`, `OtherFlags` `--warnaserror+:25 --platform:x64`, `PlatformTarget` `x64` and `NoWarn` `NU5100;NU5110;NU5111;NU1903`. It keeps the SDK's default assembly name, `BerremanTestSupport`. One `ItemGroup` holds `<Compile Include=\"CommittedKits.fs\" />`, and one holds the project reference to `..\\OpticalConstructor\\OpticalConstructor.Domain\\OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` (`KitFolder` is Domain's, step 122). It has no package reference and no comment (AGENTS.md 'No new comments in `.fsproj`'), and like every file this section writes it has LF line endings (AGENTS.md 'Line endings: LF'). (2) `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` gains the entry `<Project Path=\"BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj\">` holding `<Platform Project=\"x64\" />`, in the shape of its neighbours, directly after the `BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj` entry (`Berreman.slnx:17-19`). (3) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs` (the file step 330 creates), and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Its opens, its one case `OpticsMuellerKit` and the body of `tryFindFolder` are unchanged. The locator therefore still walks up from `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory`, the folder of the running test assembly, and writes nothing. The type's doc says, in one to three lines, that these are the committed reference kits under the repository's `data/` folder, found from the folder holding `Berreman/Berreman.slnx` (spec 0050 §3.21, S9.4), and that both test suites share them through `BerremanTestSupport` (S10.2). The sentence saying that S10.2 moves it is deleted. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include=\"CommittedKits.fs\" />`. It gains the project reference to `..\\BerremanTestSupport\\BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` after its last `ProjectReference`, with no comment. (5) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` gains `open BerremanTestSupport` after its last `open` line, and nothing else in it changes. (6) Elevation. Nothing under `Elevation/` and nothing in `.elevation-analyzers.json` changes. The gate driver scopes every solution `.fsproj` whose name does not end in `Tests.fsproj` (`Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1:151`), so it analyzes `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` too. The analyzers apply no rule to that assembly and report zero findings: its name matches neither `inScopePatterns` (`Softellect.Berreman.*`) nor `ownAssemblyPatterns` (`Softellect.*`) (`.elevation-analyzers.json:13-21`), and the same holds for the test projects. No `[<ElevationBoundary>]` or `[<NumericCarrier>]` mark is added to it. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the locator's body is unchanged. No test is added or removed. `MuellerReconstructionTests` is the one class that reaches the locator, through `loadDataSet` and through `the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte`.", "acceptance": "After the project is created, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` MUST be a plain net10.0 x64 library with the assembly name `BerremanTestSupport`, listed in `Berreman.slnx`. It MUST compile `CommittedKits.fs` (namespace `BerremanTestSupport`) and be referenced by `BerremanTests`, and `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST hold no `CommittedKits.fs`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj", "Berreman/Berreman.slnx", "Berreman/BerremanTests/CommittedKits.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the optics-mueller kit holds every file of the former data archive byte for byte", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.the optics-mueller kit's final lab files load through the Phone ROI CSV profile with their documented row counts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.CommittedKit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/CommittedKits.fs", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests.CommittedKit", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S102-KIT-LOCATOR-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs"}
{"number": 345, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S102b", "touches": ["BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [344], "how_to": "The transparent triclinic ground truth moves into `BerremanTestSupport` whole (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs (`BiaxialSample.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`: constants, …) move into a shared test-support project'; 001 §S10 'holding `BiaxialSample` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample`'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `BiaxialSample` module exists. (1) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs`, and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Every declaration moves with its body unchanged, as S10.1 leaves it: `referenceWaveLength`, the three indices and the six gyration components, `triclinic`, `solverParameters`, `scalingAround`, `opticAxisFromLargest`, `opticAxisWaveNormal`, `epsDiagonal`, `rhoImaginary` and `recoveredQuantities`. The builder has been `TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties` since step 333, and `recoveredQuantities` has named `ParameterName`s and read `QuantityValue`s since step 341. Its opens are unchanged. It reads no name of the `BerremanTests` namespace, and `BerremanTestSupport` references no test project. In the module doc, only what the move makes untrue changes. The first sentence's 'every biaxial suite in this assembly shares' (`BiaxialSample.fs:13`) becomes 'every biaxial suite shares', and that paragraph gains one sentence citing spec 0050 S10.2 (001 §Q AT-2): the sample lives in `BerremanTestSupport`, so one compiled copy serves `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`. In the spec R3 sentence, 'in the TEST assembly' (`BiaxialSample.fs:23`) becomes 'in test code'. Every other doc line keeps its text. (2) `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` gains `<Compile Include=\"BiaxialSample.fs\" />` after `CommittedKits.fs`. It also gains the project reference to `..\\OpticalConstructor\\OpticalConstructor.Optimization\\OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj` after the Domain one, because `RecoveredQuantity` and `QuantityValue` are `OpticalConstructor.Optimization`'s (steps 341 and 338). No comment is added. (3) `BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include=\"BiaxialSample.fs\" />` with the comment above it (`BerremanTests.fsproj:40-41`). It also deletes the comment above `<Compile Include=\"InverseFitHarness.fs\" />` (`BerremanTests.fsproj:36-38`), which S10.1 made untrue: after step 343 the harness declares no type and drives no fit. The `InverseFitHarness.fs` line keeps its place. (4) The consumers read the moved module. `open BerremanTests.BiaxialSample` becomes `open BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample`, keeping its trailing comment, in `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` (which step 346 moves). Nothing else in them changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every expression is unchanged, and only its namespace moves. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s) drives `triclinic`, `scalingAround`, `opticAxisWaveNormal`, `solverParameters` and `referenceWaveLength`. `BiaxialInverseTests` (about 997 s) is selected too, because it alone reaches `epsDiagonal`, `rhoImaginary`, `opticAxisFromLargest` and `recoveredQuantities`; the S10.2 brief names both classes.", "acceptance": "After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs` MUST declare the module `BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample` with every declaration and number unchanged. `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST neither hold nor compile `BiaxialSample.fs`, and every consumer MUST open `BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.every plate in this design is one a vendor will actually sell", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.a plate cut perpendicular to an optic axis is a pure circular retarder, and that is what buys the signal", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the order ambiguity is real on the principal cuts and is broken by the optic-axis cuts", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible measurement set recovers all NINE constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.the feasible design constrains the gyration tensor FAR better than the idealized thin-plate one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.the triclinic builder produces a biaxial permittivity and a FULL symmetric gyration tensor", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.orientForCut carries each of the three principal axes onto the surface normal, gyration tensor and all", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.an optic axis is reachable from the x-cut and unreachable from the z-cut, which is what the steep configurations are for", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests.an ensemble of noisy experiments recovers all nine constants, and the birefringences survive far better", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests|T:BerremanTests.BiaxialSample", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S102-BIAXIAL-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs"}
{"number": 346, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S102c", "touches": ["BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [345], "how_to": "The absorbing ground truth and its measurement design move into `BerremanTestSupport` whole, beside their transparent twin (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs (… `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`: constants, `buildAbsorbing`, the cuts, `a1` / `a2` / `a3`, `perturbedStart`, `searchBox`) move into a shared test-support project'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `AbsorbingBiaxialSample` module exists. (1) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Every declaration moves with its body unchanged, as S10.1 leaves it: the six ε″ components, `absorbing`, `absorbingScalingAround`, `plate`, `waveLength`, `opticAxisCut`, `otherOpticAxisCut`, `configuration`, `a1`, `a2`, `a3`, `fullConfigurations`, `perturbedStart` and `searchBox`. The builder has been `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.opticalProperties` since step 334, `configuration` has passed `float<deg>` angles to `MuellerFitting.configurationOf` since step 335, and `SearchBox` has been `MuellerFitting`'s since step 337. The file keeps `open BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample` (step 345). No `open` of a `BerremanTests` module remains in it: `open BerremanTests.InverseFitHarness` is deleted, because after S10.1 nothing in the file reads the harness and `BerremanTestSupport` references no test project. In the module doc, the first paragraph gains one sentence citing spec 0050 S10.2 (001 §Q AT-2): the sample and its design live in `BerremanTestSupport`, so one compiled copy serves `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`. Every other doc line keeps its text. (2) `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` gains `<Compile Include=\"AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs\" />` after `BiaxialSample.fs`. No reference and no comment is added. (3) `BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include=\"AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs\" />`, so its compile list holds no ground-truth file. (4) In `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs`, `open BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialSample` becomes `open BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample`, keeping its trailing comment. Nothing else in them changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every expression is unchanged, and `fullConfigurations` holds the same 44 configurations in the same order. No test is added or removed. `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s) reads every moved declaration that `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` (946 s, not selected) reads, and it reaches the rest through `configuration` and `fullConfigurations`.", "acceptance": "After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` MUST declare the module `BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample` with every declaration and number unchanged and no `open` of a `BerremanTests` module. `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST neither hold nor compile `BiaxialSample.fs` or `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, and both absorbing suites MUST open `BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BerremanTests.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the scaled parameter space round-trips all fifteen coordinates and a unit step moves exactly one", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.absorption and refraction do NOT share principal axes, which is what makes this crystal triclinic-absorbing", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the REAL part of rho has no first-order effect, so circular dichroism is not expressible through it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing sample attenuates, and every configuration stays physically realizable", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.normalized data is markedly blind to isotropic absorption, and absolute throughput restores it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.the absorbing measurement set recovers all FIFTEEN material constants from a perturbed start", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.all fifteen parameters are observable and the problem is conditioned well enough to solve", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.AbsorbingBiaxialSample", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}, {"symbol": "BerremanTests|T:BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialSample", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"], "preserves_obligations": ["S102-ABSORBING-SAMPLE-MOVE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs"}
{"number": 347, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S102d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [346], "how_to": "`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` references the shared test-support project, so one compiled copy of the ground truth, the designs and the kit locator serves both test suites (001 §Q AT-2 'Both `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` reference it, so one compiled copy serves both test suites'; 001 §S10 'referenced by `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`'; the S10.2 brief). `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` gains the project reference to `..\\..\\BerremanTestSupport\\BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` after its last `ProjectReference`, the `OpticalConstructor.TestWindows.App` one (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj:268`), with no comment (AGENTS.md 'No new comments in `.fsproj`'). This step adds the reference 001 §Q AT-2 requires and changes no source file of the suite, so no `ui-tests` class holds a changed fact and that gate is not selected; what the reference can affect, the suite's build and load, is what `build` and `ui-smoke` prove. The reference brings no assembly besides `BerremanTestSupport` itself, because `OpticalConstructor.Domain` and `OpticalConstructor.Optimization` already reach the suite through `OpticalConstructor.Ui` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj:176-178`). The test projects stay outside the elevation gate's scope (`Elevation/Run-ElevationGate.ps1:151`), so the gate analyzes nothing new here. No test and no package is added. `ui-smoke` runs whole (`whole_suite: light`, about 27 s) and shows that the headless host still loads, discovers and runs the suite with the new reference.", "acceptance": "After the reference is added, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj` MUST reference `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`, so that `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` build against one `BerremanTestSupport` assembly. ui-smoke MUST pass, its count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.2 -- BerremanTestSupport: the shared ground truth and designs"}
{"number": 348, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103a", "touches": ["BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [347], "how_to": "The reference pipeline's transcribed expectations get ONE home in test support, which `MuellerReconstructionTests` and AT-1 (S12.1) share (001 §Q AT-1 'the transcribed expected literals move from the §7.2 test body into one shared reference module, which both tests open. The test reads no file for its expectations (spec 0044 §8.5)'; 001 §S10 third bullet 'move its expected literals into one shared reference module'; the S10.3 brief 'dataMatrixTol moves with them'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §6 row '§7.2 pipeline: `MuellerReconstructionTests` §7.2 → product staged path', deleted at the source: 'The hand-composed body'): after the step every expected literal of the Stage-1 and section 7.2 facts exists once, in `MuellerReference`. (1) New `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs`: `module MuellerReference` in `namespace BerremanTestSupport`, the shape of `BiaxialSample.fs` (step 345), compiled after `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` through one `<Compile Include=\"MuellerReference.fs\" />` line in `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj`, with no comment and no reference added (Domain since step 344, Optimization since step 345). The module opens only what its values need. Its doc, one to three lines: the optics-mueller reference pipeline's full-precision results, transcribed from `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/reference_step1_summary.json` and `reference_step2_linear_summary.json` (step 329), which `MuellerReconstructionTests` and AT-1 assert against, so no test reads a file for its expectations (spec 0044 §8.5; spec 0050 S10.3). Each value is born elevated (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin … This holds for test fixtures too'), and each value's doc, one line, names its summary key. In this order: (a) The two bands, moved from the class bindings `stage1Tol` and `dataMatrixTol` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:stage1Tol`, `:dataMatrixTol`) with their values `1.0e-12` and `1.0e-9` and their docs, and the comment block above `stage1Tol` (the spec 0044 §8.5 / §9 bands and their observed figures) with its text as step 329 leaves it. (b) The Stage-1 constants of `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values`, from `reference_step1_summary.json`: `darkMean` = `DarkMean 869.666` (`dark_mean_avg_total`); `lpAnalyzerZero` = `Angle.degree 155.44011830109392<deg>` (`lp_lp_anchor.zero_angle_deg`); `cplAnalyzerZero` = `Angle.degree 96.99613336321012<deg>` (`cpl_analyzer_from_lp_cpl.zero_angle_deg`); `cplAnalyzerRetardance` = `Retardance.degree 83.66804489441891<deg>` (`cpl_analyzer_from_lp_cpl.retardance_raw_deg`, the magnitude stage 1 derives); `cplSourceAxisOffset` = `Angle.degree 39.31100224361002<deg>` and `cplSourceRetardance` = `Retardance.degree 82.55344158462403<deg>` (`cpl_source_from_cpl_lp.source_theta_relaxed_model.theta_rel_deg` and `.retardance_deg`). Each of these degree literals comes back bit for bit from `.degrees` (checked when this spec was authored), so every comparison stays exact. (c) The section 7.2 values, from `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`: `qzMatrix`, `lrMatrix` and `combinedMatrix`, the `MuellerMatrix`es of `qz_matrix`, `lr_matrix` and `combined_matrix`, built from the literals the fact's `expectedQz`, `expectedLr` and `expectedComb` hold today (`RealMatrix4x4.create … |> MuellerMatrix`); `cascadeFrobenius`, `cascadeMeanAbs` and `cascadeMaxAbs`, the `MatrixDeviation`s 0.5714178795538456, 0.11328628636347338 and 0.26806464658062423 (`combined_vs_product_matrix.frobenius_norm`, `.mean_abs_entry_diff`, `.max_abs_entry_diff`); and `cascadeLargestDeltaPositions : Set<MuellerRowIndex * MuellerColumnIndex>`, the 0-indexed positions (3, 3) and (3, 1) of the two largest `delta_matrix` magnitudes, with the fact's spec 0044 note on them cut to one to three lines. (d) `excludedPoints : ExcludedPoint list`, the one point of the reference's `EXCLUDED_POINTS` (`Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_glue.py:22`, in `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` from step 329): experiment `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`, description 140°, capture index 17. It is the caller's data to the reconstruction (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:ExcludedPoint`, spec 0042 §0). (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` reads each of them as `MuellerReference.<name>` (`BerremanTestSupport` is open since step 344). It deletes `stage1Tol`, `dataMatrixTol` and the comment block above them. `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values` compares `darkMean` with `MuellerReference.darkMean.value` and each angle or retardance through `.degrees` of its `MuellerReference` value, in the same order and at `MuellerReference.stage1Tol`; its provenance comment says, in one to three lines, that the expected values are `MuellerReference`'s (spec 0050 S10.3). The section 7.2 fact deletes `expectedQz`, `expectedLr`, `expectedComb`, its local `excluded` and its three metric literals, and reads their `MuellerReference` values. It compares at `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` and checks its two largest-delta positions, now enumerated as `(MuellerRowIndex i, MuellerColumnIndex j)`, against `MuellerReference.cascadeLargestDeltaPositions`; its comments that name the summary say the values are `MuellerReference`'s. `buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)` reads `MuellerReference.excludedPoints` in place of its local copy of the same point (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy': a re-transcribed constant is a defect). The class doc's spec 0044 §8.5 bullet adds that the expectations live in `BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference` (spec 0050 S10.3); no other comment changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every computed value and every expected value is the same double, so each assertion compares the same numbers. No test is added or removed. The test support project is outside the ELEV analyzers' scope (`.elevation-analyzers.json:13-21`, as step 344 records), so nothing under `Elevation/` changes.", "acceptance": "After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` MUST declare `BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference` holding the two bands, the six Stage-1 constants, the three section 7.2 matrices, the three cascade metrics, the two largest-delta positions and the excluded point, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST hold none of these literals and read them from the module; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BerremanTestSupport.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-REFERENCE-MODULE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-REFERENCE-MODULE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-REFERENCE-MODULE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs", "obligations": ["S103-REFERENCE-MODULE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number": 349, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [348], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests"], "how_to": "Stage 1 of the reference pipeline, which `MuellerReconstructionTests` composes by hand, becomes the first half of the study's staged Mueller path in `OpticalConstructor.Optimization` (001 §Q AT-1 'the stage pipeline that §7.2 composes by hand (`loadDataSet`, `reduceAirTraces`, `unwrapFit`, stage-1 constants, …) is promoted into product code as the study's staged Mueller path, and §7.2 is re-pointed to call it'; 001 §S10 third bullet; the S10.3 brief 'the stage-1 constants (freeCosineFit, sourceCplFromLpFrame, the analyzer zeros and retardances)' and 'The test-only failure helpers (unwrapFit throws) become typed errors'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §6 row '§7.2 pipeline: `MuellerReconstructionTests` §7.2 → product staged path', deleted at the source: 'The hand-composed body'): after the step `reduceAirTraces`, `lpFrameCoeffs` and `unwrapFit` exist nowhere in the test. Errors are values (AGENTS.md 'do not throw across a public boundary'): what the test `failwith`s becomes a typed error. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs`, `module StagedMuellerPath` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Optimization`, compiled directly after `FitUncertainty.fs` (step 342): one `<Compile Include=\"StagedMuellerPath.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj`, no comment. It opens what it needs (`OpticalConstructor.Domain` for `Library.PolarizerKind`, `ItemModels` for `DialSign` since step 212, `MuellerReconstruction`). Module doc, one to three lines: the optics-mueller reference pipeline (spec 0042 §7.2) as the study's staged Mueller path, a pure function of the lab files' capture rows and a `MuellerSolverProxy`, promoted from `MuellerReconstructionTests` by spec 0050 S10.3. Each declaration's doc is one to three lines naming the reference script function it mirrors. In this order: (a) `StagedMuellerCaptureData`, the capture rows of the seven lab files as the Phone ROI CSV profile reads them (step 303): `lpLpRows`, `lpCplRows`, `cplLpRows`, `cplCplDay1Rows`, `cplCplDay2Rows`, `darknessRows` and `bullshitCheckRows`, each a `MuellerRawRow list`. (b) `StagedMuellerError`, doc one line (a typed failure of the staged path, never a throw): `EmptyCaptureSetErr of reason : string` (a set of capture rows the path needs holds none; the reason names it) and `AirCalibrationFitErr of family : Family * error : SolverError` (the stage-1 AIR cosine fit of that family failed; `MuellerReconstruction.fs:Family`, `:SolverError`). Steps 351 and 352 add their own cases; no other case is added here. (c) `StageOneCalibrationData = { darkMean : DarkMean; lpZero : Angle; cplZero : Angle; cplAnalyzerRetardance : Retardance; cplSourceModel : SourceCplModel }`, the stage-1 constants (`matrix_step1_air_fit.py`), with the stage-2 models built from them (`matrix_glue.py` `load_step1_models`) as members, moved from the section 7.2 fact's `analyzerLp`, `analyzerCpl` and `sourceCpl` with their values: `member this.lpAnalyzer : AnalyzerModel` (`Library.IdealLinear`, `zeroDial = this.lpZero`, `DialNegative`, no retarder); `member this.cplAnalyzer : AnalyzerModel` (`Library.IdealCircularLeft`, `zeroDial = this.cplZero`, `DialPositive`, `thetaRelOpt = Some (Angle.degree 45.0<deg>)`, `retardanceOpt = Some (Retardance.degree (- this.cplAnalyzerRetardance.degrees * 1.0<deg>))`, the fact's expression, so the same double); and `member this.cplSource : SourceModel` (`CplSource (this.cplSourceModel.thetaRel, this.cplSourceModel.retardance)`). (d) Private, moved from the test: `reduceAirTraces` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:reduceAirTraces`, the reference `load_air_traces` + `prepare_normalized_traces`) with its dark mean as `DarkMean` (ELEV003P, ELEV010P), read through `.value` where it subtracts, its body otherwise unchanged; and the LP-frame fit (`:lpFrameCoeffs`, the reference `fit_lp_frame_coeffs`), whose `CosineCoefficient * CosineCoefficient` answer is ELEV011, as a helper answering `Result<SourceCplModel, SolverError>`: the same phased 2-column solve through the proxy, each coefficient bound as a `CosineCoefficient` where it is read from the solution (ELEV001), then `sourceCplFromLpFrame` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:sourceCplFromLpFrame`). (e) `calibrateStageOne (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (captures : StagedMuellerCaptureData) : Result<StageOneCalibrationData, StagedMuellerError>`, the stage-1 part of today's section 7.2 body in its order: no darkness row answers `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the darkness checks; the dark mean is the mean `avgTotal` of `darknessRows`; `freeCosineFit` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:freeCosineFit`) of `reduceAirTraces` over `lpLpRows` gives `lpZero`, and over `lpCplRows` gives `cplZero` and `cplAnalyzerRetardance` (its `visibility.retardance`); the LP-frame fit over `cplLpRows`, phased on `lpZero`, gives `cplSourceModel`. A failed solve answers `AirCalibrationFitErr` of `LpLp`, `LpCpl` or `CplLp` with its `SolverError`, and nothing after it runs. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath` and deletes `reduceAirTraces`, `lpFrameCoeffs` and `unwrapFit`. After the seven kit file values (step 330) it binds `let opticsMuellerCaptures () : StagedMuellerCaptureData`, each field `loadDataSet` of its file, its doc one line. `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values` calls `calibrateStageOne (createMathNetSvd ()) (opticsMuellerCaptures ())`, an `Error` failing the fact with its `%A`, and compares `stageOne.darkMean.value` and, through `.degrees`, `lpZero`, `cplZero`, `cplAnalyzerRetardance`, `cplSourceModel.thetaRel` and `cplSourceModel.retardance` with the `MuellerReference` values as step 348 left the comparison. The section 7.2 fact makes the same call and takes `darkMean`, `lpAnalyzer`, `cplAnalyzer` and `cplSource` from it, with `LpSource`, in place of its hand-written Stage 1 and Stage 2 blocks; it binds one `opticsMuellerCaptures ()` and reads every lab file's rows from it, the call included. Its Stage 3 and its assertions are unchanged in this step. `loadDataSet` stays: it is the test's read of the committed kit (IO), and the promoted path is pure over the rows it reads (the S10.3 brief 'a pure function over the parsed capture rows'). `degree` stays, for `freeCosineFit recovers a synthetic cosine zero and visibility within tolerance (always-run)`. (3) Tests. New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs`, `module StagedMuellerPathTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests` (the shape of `MeasuredDataTests.fs`), appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, opening `OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction`, `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath` and what its facts need, each fact over the real `createMathNetSvd ()` and fixed-literal rows: `stage one answers a typed error naming the empty darkness checks, never a throw`: all seven row lists empty answer `EmptyCaptureSetErr` whose reason names the darkness checks; `stage one answers a typed error naming the family whose AIR cosine fit fails`: one darkness row and no other row answer `AirCalibrationFitErr (LpLp, SingularDesignErr _)`, the empty LP-LP AIR trace being an empty design. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every number is computed by the same float operations in the same order. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged.", "acceptance": "After stage one is promoted, `StagedMuellerPath.fs`, compiled directly after `FitUncertainty.fs`, MUST declare `StagedMuellerCaptureData`, `StagedMuellerError` (`EmptyCaptureSetErr`, `AirCalibrationFitErr`), `StageOneCalibrationData` with its `lpAnalyzer`, `cplAnalyzer` and `cplSource` members, and `calibrateStageOne`, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST declare none of `reduceAirTraces`, `lpFrameCoeffs` and `unwrapFit` and take its stage-1 constants from `calibrateStageOne`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `stage one answers a typed error naming the empty darkness checks, never a throw` and `stage one answers a typed error naming the family whose AIR cosine fit fails`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.stage one answers a typed error naming the empty darkness checks, never a throw", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.stage one answers a typed error naming the family whose AIR cosine fit fails", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerCaptureData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StageOneCalibrationData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.calibrateStageOne", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGE-ONE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number": 350, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [349], "how_to": "`buildDesign` hands each kept row's label reading to its per-row projection, so no projection reads a label again and the staged path (step 351) is total without an arm for an `Error` that cannot occur (AGENTS.md 'Errors are values'; the S10.3 brief 'The test-only failure helpers … become typed errors'). Since step 270, `buildDesign` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:buildDesign`) keeps a row only when `NamingTemplate.standard.readName r.experiment.nameText` reads it, and the section 7.2 fact's `prepareRow` reads the same label again and fails the fact on an `Error` that no kept row can give. (1) In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`, `buildDesign`'s first parameter becomes `prepareRow : MuellerRawRow -> NameReading -> StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity`. Each row's label is read once. A row is kept, in row order and with its reading, when the reading's `matrixKind` equals `kind`, the label is no AIR#0 label and the row is no excluded point, as today; each kept row is projected by `prepareRow row reading`. The rows kept, their order and the system are unchanged. Its doc says so in one to three lines (spec 0050 S10.3). No other declaration changes. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact's `prepareRow` takes `(reading : NameReading)` after its row and its φ is `reading.objectPhi`; its own read of the label and the failure on that read's `Error` (step 270) are deleted. `buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)`'s stub projection takes an ignored `NameReading` after its row; its rows, its assertions and its numbers are unchanged. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the reading `buildDesign` hands over is the reading the fact made itself, so every row has the same φ and every design row the same entries. No test is added or removed. No other consumer of `buildDesign` exists: the S10.3 path adopts this form in step 351.", "acceptance": "After the change, `buildDesign`'s projection MUST have the type `MuellerRawRow -> NameReading -> StokesVector * RealVector4 * DetectorIntensity` and receive each kept row's reading, and no projection in `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST read a label; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, its count unchanged; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.buildDesign keeps only the requested kind, dropping AIR rows and the excluded contaminated point (always-run)", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-DESIGN-READING"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-DESIGN-READING"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.buildDesign", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-DESIGN-READING"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number": 351, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [350], "how_to": "Stages 2 and 3 of the reference pipeline join stage 1 in `StagedMuellerPath`, and the section 7.2 fact keeps only its assertions (001 §Q AT-1 '… `familyGain`, `correctSignal`, `buildDesign`, `reconstruct`) is promoted into product code as the study's staged Mueller path, and §7.2 is re-pointed to call it'; 001 §S10 third bullet; the S10.3 brief 'It returns typed stage-1 constants, the reconstructed matrices with rank and residual' and 'sec 7.2 calls the promoted path, and its body keeps only assertions'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §6 row '§7.2 pipeline: `MuellerReconstructionTests` §7.2 → product staged path', deleted at the source: 'The hand-composed body'): after the step the hand-composed Stage 3 exists once, in product code. (1) In `StagedMuellerPath.fs` (step 349): (a) `StagedMuellerError` gains `ObjectReconstructionErr of kind : MatrixKind * error : SolverError` (the stage-3 solve of that object failed; `MuellerReconstruction.fs:MatrixKind`). (b) After `calibrateStageOne`, `StagedMuellerData = { stageOne : StageOneCalibrationData; gains : GainCalibration; cplCplDay1Gain : InterpolatedGain; qz : ReconstructedMatrix; lr : ReconstructedMatrix; qzLr : ReconstructedMatrix }`, doc one to three lines: the stage-1 constants, the AIR gain rules (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:GainCalibration`, whose `cplCpl` is the day-2 `Day2Single`), the day-1 CPL-CPL interpolation (`:InterpolatedGain`), and M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} with their rank and residual (`:ReconstructedMatrix`). (c) `reconstructStaged (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) (excluded : ExcludedPoint list) (captures : StagedMuellerCaptureData) : Result<StagedMuellerData, StagedMuellerError>`, the rest of today's section 7.2 body moved with its rules and values, in this order: `calibrateStageOne`, its error passing through; the CPL-LP split time, the earliest `capturedAt` of `bullshitCheckRows` (the reference `assign_gain_model` reads the first check), no row answering `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming the bullshit checks; the nine AIR blocks, each the rows of its file whose `experiment` equals its label, in this order: `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2` and `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R` of `lpLpRows`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2` and `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2R` of `lpCplRows`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2R` of `cplLpRows`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR` of `cplCplDay1Rows` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2` of `cplCplDay2Rows` (the labels `assign_gain_model` selects, `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_fit_linear.py:94-144`), the first block with no row answering `EmptyCaptureSetErr` naming its label, where the fact divides 0 by 0 or throws today; each block's gain by the fact's `fitAirGain` and the day-1 block times by its `meanTime`, with the sources (`LpSource`, `stageOne.cplSource`) and analyzers (`stageOne.lpAnalyzer`, `stageOne.cplAnalyzer`) its `calibration` and `day1Cal` use; the five families' projections as its `prepareRow` and `families` build them, in step 350's form; and, for `Qz`, `Lr` and `QzLrProduct` in that order, the five families' `buildDesign` systems over `excluded`, concatenated in family order and solved by `reconstruct`, the first failure answering `ObjectReconstructionErr` with the kind and the `SolverError`. The nine labels are literals of the path, born as `MuellerExperimentLabel`s: they are the reference procedure's gain rules, which S11.1 turns into session data (001 §L 'familyGain becomes their first implementation'). The excluded points are the caller's data (spec 0042 §0; 001 §Q AT-1 'the excluded frame [is] applied as data'). Helpers are private or local and meet ELEV003P, ELEV010P and ELEV013. (2) `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` gains, after the cascade values, the nine AIR gains of `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`'s `gain_summary`, each an `AirGain` with a one-line doc naming its key: `lpLpGainA` 45028.89958338373 (`lp_lp.gain_air2`), `lpLpGainB` 44514.55313613668 (`lp_lp.gain_air2r`), `lpCplGainA` 64241.39738340334 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2`), `lpCplGainB` 63009.84001492676 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2r`), `cplLpGainPre` 36886.57620207925 (`cpl_lp.gain_pre_air2`), `cplLpGainPost` 40015.20947516168 (`cpl_lp.gain_post_air2r`), `cplCplDay1GainStart` 34623.69085844701 and `cplCplDay1GainEnd` 37056.15607055087 (`cpl_cpl_day1.gain_start`, `.gain_end`) and `cplCplDay2Gain` 36225.080943100205 (`cpl_cpl_day2.gain`). `dataMatrixTol`'s doc gains one line: it also bands the AIR gains, whose worst observed deviation was 2.9e-11 (`lp_cpl.gain_air2`) when spec 0050 was authored, 2026-11-04, so the band is about 34 times looser (spec 0044 §9). (3) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact calls `reconstructStaged (createMathNetSvd ()) MuellerReference.excludedPoints (opticsMuellerCaptures ())`, an `Error` failing the fact with its `%A`, and deletes every binding of its body that is neither an assertion nor its formatting (the stage-1 call of step 349, `airRowsOf`, `fitAirGain`, `meanTime`, `splitTime`, `day1Start`, `day1End`, `calibration`, `day1Cal`, `prepareRow`, `families` and `reconstructKind`); `worstElementDeviation` and `describeDeviation` stay. Its assertions read `staged.qz`, `staged.lr` and `staged.qzLr` (rank 16 each; the matrices within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol`), and its cascade check reads `cascadeProduct staged.lr.matrix staged.qz.matrix` until step 352. It gains one assertion that reports all nine deviations, as the matrix assertion does: each AIR gain of `staged.gains` (`lpLp.gainA`, `lpLp.gainB`, `lpCpl.gainA`, `lpCpl.gainB`, `cplLp.gainPre`, `cplLp.gainPost` and the `Day2Single` gain of `cplCpl`, a `Day1Interp` failing the fact) and of `staged.cplCplDay1Gain` (`gainStart`, `gainEnd`) is within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of its `MuellerReference` value. Its leading comment says, in one to three lines, that it runs the promoted staged path (spec 0050 S10.3) over the kit's lab files; its spec 0044 §8.4 and §8.5 paragraphs keep their text, and the comments of the moved code go with it. (4) Tests, in `StagedMuellerPathTests` (step 349), over test-local synthetic captures whose AIR rows are, per label, nine readings at 0°, 20°, …, 160° with `avgTotal` 2 + cos 2α at fixed literal times, one darkness row and one bullshit-check row, so stage 1 solves: `the staged path answers a typed error naming an AIR block that holds no capture row`: the LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP files hold only their first block (`LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2`) and the day files nothing, so `reconstructStaged` answers `EmptyCaptureSetErr` whose reason holds `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`; `the staged path answers a typed error naming the object whose solve fails`: all nine blocks and no science row answer `ObjectReconstructionErr (Qz, SingularDesignErr _)`, the empty QZ design reaching the real `createMathNetSvd ()`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the path computes every gain, projection and solve by the same float operations in the same order; a probe this spec ran at authoring through the same functions reproduced the summary's nine gains within 2.9e-11 and its row counts (QZ 228, LR 227, QZ+LR 228). The gain assertion compares values the fact already computes, and `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged (001 §W: no new inverse-physics test).", "acceptance": "After the staged path is promoted, `StagedMuellerPath.reconstructStaged` MUST answer the stage-1 constants, the nine AIR gains and M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} with their rank and residual, or a typed `StagedMuellerError`, and the section 7.2 fact MUST call it, hold only assertions and their formatting, and find every gain within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference`'s; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the staged path answers a typed error naming an AIR block that holds no capture row` and `the staged path answers a typed error naming the object whose solve fails`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.the staged path answers a typed error naming an AIR block that holds no capture row", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.the staged path answers a typed error naming the object whose solve fails", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.reconstructStaged", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"], "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs"}, {"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-STAGED-PATH"], "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs"}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number": 352, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S103e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [351], "how_to": "The product check, the combined QZ+LR matrix against the cascade M_LR · M_QZ, becomes part of the staged path's answer, with the product-check RMSE ratio the reference reports (001 §L 'the product check for series objects (M_comb against M_LR · M_QZ)'; 001 §Q AT-1 'Assertions: … the product-check RMSE ratio'; the S10.3 brief 'the cascade comparison' and 'It returns … the product check'; S11.4 reuses it). The reference computes `fit_rmse`, the combined matrix's own RMSE over its rows, and `product_rmse`, the cascade's prediction RMSE over the same rows (`Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/matrix_fit_linear.py:372-373`, in `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` from step 329), and its report prints `product / fit` (`:334`). (0) The residual RMSE of a solution over a least-squares system gets one implementation, which the SVD proxy and the product check share (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy … A duplicated function body … is a defect'): `createMathNetSvd` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:createMathNetSvd`) computes `‖A·x − b‖ / √m` inline today, in its `residual`, `rows` and `rmse` bindings. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs` the record `LeastSquaresSystem` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:LeastSquaresSystem`) gains `member this.residualRmseAt (solution : RealVector) : ResidualRmse`: `RealMatrix.create` of its design rows' values times `solution`, minus `RealVector.create` of `rhs`, the difference's `norm` divided by `sqrt` of the row count, the expression `createMathNetSvd` evaluates, in its order (`ResidualRmse` is declared above the record, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:ResidualRmse`). Its doc, one to three lines: the residual RMSE of a solution over this system's rows, the one the solver reports and the product check reuses (spec 0050 S10.3). In `createMathNetSvd` those three bindings become `system.residualRmseAt (RealVector x)`; its checks, its errors and the rest of its body are unchanged, so every solver RMSE is the same double, as `the real createMathNetSvd proxy solves a known over-determined full-rank system`, `reconstruct recovers a seeded MuellerMatrix from a synthetic full-rank design at rank 16 (always-run)`, `freeCosineFit recovers a synthetic cosine zero and visibility within tolerance (always-run)` and the section 7.2 fact, which read it through the proxy, show. No other declaration of the file changes. (1) In `StagedMuellerPath.fs`, before `StagedMuellerData`: (a) `ProductRmseRatio of float` with `member this.value`, doc one line, and `static member between (productRmse : ResidualRmse) (fitRmse : ResidualRmse) : ProductRmseRatio` (`productRmse.value / fitRmse.value`), the one place the ratio is formed, as `RelativeError.between` is (step 338). (b) `ProductCheckData = { cascade : MuellerMatrix; difference : MatrixDiff; fitRmse : ResidualRmse; productRmse : ResidualRmse }` with `member this.rmseRatio : ProductRmseRatio` (`ProductRmseRatio.between this.productRmse this.fitRmse`). (c) `productCheckOf (lr : MuellerMatrix) (qz : MuellerMatrix) (combined : ReconstructedMatrix) (combinedSystem : LeastSquaresSystem) : ProductCheckData`: `cascade` is `cascadeProduct lr qz` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:cascadeProduct`, in its operand order), `difference` is `frobeniusDiff combined.matrix cascade` (`:frobeniusDiff`), `fitRmse` is `combined.rmse` and `productRmse` is `combinedSystem.residualRmseAt cascade.vecColumnMajor` (part 0). (2) `StagedMuellerData` gains `productCheck : ProductCheckData` after `qzLr`; `reconstructStaged` keeps the `QzLrProduct` system it solves and fills the field with `productCheckOf lr.matrix qz.matrix qzLr` of that system, after the three solves. (3) `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath` and gains, after the gains, `combinedFitRmse` = `ResidualRmse 0.10162659513724465` (`combined_check.fit_rmse`), `productRmse` = `ResidualRmse 0.12833930975940816` (`combined_check.product_rmse`) and `productCheckRmseRatio` = `ProductRmseRatio.between productRmse combinedFitRmse`. `dataMatrixTol`'s doc gains one line: it also bands the ratio, whose observed deviation was 5.7e-13 when spec 0050 was authored, 2026-11-04. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact's cascade check reads `staged.productCheck` and its own `cascadeProduct` and `frobeniusDiff` calls go: the three metrics are `staged.productCheck.difference`'s, compared with `MuellerReference`'s at `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` as before, and the two largest-delta positions compare `staged.qzLr.matrix` with `staged.productCheck.cascade`. It gains one assertion: `staged.productCheck.rmseRatio` is within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference.productCheckRmseRatio`, its message naming the two RMSEs and the two ratios. (5) Test, in `StagedMuellerPathTests`: `the product check compares the combined matrix with the cascade and the RMSEs over the combined rows`: with `lr` = `Propagation.identityMueller`, `qz` = the diagonal Mueller matrix diag(1, 0.5, 0.5, 1), `combined` = `{ matrix = Propagation.identityMueller; rank = MatrixRank 16; rmse = ResidualRmse 0.1 }` and the system of the two design rows `kron4 (StokesVector.create [ 1.0; 0.0; 0.0; 0.0 ]) (RealVector4.create [ 1.0; 0.0; 0.0; 0.0 ])` and the same two constructors over [ 0.0; 1.0; 0.0; 0.0 ] (they read M₀₀ and M₁₁, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:kron4`) with the right-hand side 1.0 and 0.8, `productCheckOf` answers a `cascade` equal to `qz` element by element, a `difference` whose `maxAbs` is 0.5 and whose `frobenius` is √0.5, `fitRmse` 0.1, `productRmse` √0.045 and a `rmseRatio` of √0.045 / 0.1, each within 1e-12. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): the three metrics and the two positions are computed from the same matrices by the same calls, and every solver RMSE by the same operations. A probe this spec ran at authoring reproduced the summary's `fit_rmse`, `product_rmse` and their ratio within 2.3e-14, 2.9e-14 and 5.7e-13, so the new assertion holds at `dataMatrixTol`. `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the product check lands, `LeastSquaresSystem.residualRmseAt` MUST compute `‖A·x − b‖ / √m` and `createMathNetSvd` MUST report its RMSE through it, `productCheckOf` MUST answer the cascade M_LR · M_QZ, its difference from M_{QZ+LR}, the combined fit's RMSE and the cascade's RMSE over the combined rows, and their ratio, `reconstructStaged` MUST carry it, and the section 7.2 fact MUST read it, finding the ratio within `MuellerReference.dataMatrixTol` of `MuellerReference.productCheckRmseRatio`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the product check compares the combined matrix with the cascade and the RMSEs over the combined rows`, the count rising by 1; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s35 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests.the product check compares the combined matrix with the cascade and the RMSEs over the combined rows", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StagedMuellerPathTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StagedMuellerPathTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.LeastSquaresSystem.residualRmseAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.ProductRmseRatio", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.ProductCheckData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.productCheckOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerData", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"], "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs"}, {"symbol": "BerremanTestSupport.MuellerReference", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S103-PRODUCT-CHECK"], "path": "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs"}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S10.3 -- The staged Mueller pipeline and its reference values are promoted"}
{"number": 353, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTestSupport", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [352], "how_to": "The three crystal-parameter records move ahead of the material library, so that a material version can hold one of them as its physics (.spec-md §3.16 'A material version can hold one of the three parameter records as its physics (S11)'; the S11.1 brief 'Material physics form'). `MaterialEntry` is declared in `MaterialLibrary.fs`, which `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` compiles long before `MuellerInverse.fs`, where the records live today (`MuellerInverse.fs:UniaxialParameters`, `:TriclinicParameters`, `:AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`), so the records and the builders S10.1 put on them (steps 332-334, `opticalProperties`) move. This departs from .spec-md §3.16's location for the builders ('promoted into `MuellerInverse.fs` as members of their parameter records'), and the departure is recorded here: §3.16's own next bullet needs the records before `MaterialLibrary.fs`, and ONE implementation of each builder still exists. This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'): after the step each record and each builder is declared once. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs`, `module CrystalPhysics` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `DispersionModels.fs` and before `MaterialLibrary.fs`: one `<Compile Include=\"CrystalPhysics.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: the crystal-parameter records a material version can hold as its physics, each with its engine builder (spec 0050 S11.1, .spec-md §3.16). It opens what the moved bodies read (the engine's `Fields`, `MaterialProperties` and `OpticalProperties.Active`, as `MuellerInverse.fs` opens them). It holds `UniaxialParameters`, `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` in that order, each with its doc, its fields and its `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` exactly as steps 332-334 leave them. `MuellerObservation`, declared between two of them today, stays in `MuellerInverse.fs`. (2) Each record's `axes` stays in `MuellerInverse.fs`, because `ParameterAxis` is declared there and `ParameterName` in `ItemModels.fs` (step 212), both after `MaterialLibrary.fs`: directly after `ParameterAxis`, three type extensions `type UniaxialParameters with static member axes : ParameterAxis<UniaxialParameters> list = …`, the same for `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`, each with the doc and the body it has today. Every `UniaxialParameters.axes` call therefore reads as today wherever `MuellerInverse` is open. `MuellerInverse.fs` opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics`, and its module doc's sentence that each parameter record carries its crystal class's builder (step 332) adds that the records live in `CrystalPhysics` (spec 0050 S11.1). No other line of the file changes. (3) The files that name a record open `OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics` where the compiler asks and change nothing else: `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs`, `LangasiteInverseTests.fs`, `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs` and `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, and `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` (steps 345-346). The Optimization fit wrappers are generic in `'Parameters` (`MuellerFitting.fs`, step 337) and name no record. No alias, re-export or second declaration remains (ELEV014), so `git grep -n -E \"type (UniaxialParameters|TriclinicParameters|AbsorbingTriclinicParameters) =\" -- Berreman/` finds only `CrystalPhysics.fs`. The edits also name `Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`, the paths the repository census still gives the two files steps 345-346 moved; nothing is written there. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'): the builders and the axes are the same expressions, and no BerremanTests fact is added or removed. `LangasiteInverseTests` (the uniaxial builder and axes), `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s, the triclinic ones) and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (about 177 s, the absorbing ones) are the cheapest classes that drive each moved record. (4) Test, in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs`, which reaches the records from the module ahead of the material library: `{F_BUILDERS}`: over test-local records written as literals, the uniaxial record's `opticalProperties.eps` is diagonal (n_o², n_o², n_e²), the triclinic record's is diagonal (n₁², n₂², n₃²), and the absorbing record's has ε₁₁ = n₁² + i·ε″₁₁ and ε₁₂ = i·ε″₁₂ (steps 332-334's builders), each within 1e-15.", "acceptance": "After the move, `UniaxialParameters`, `TriclinicParameters` and `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` with their `opticalProperties` MUST be declared only in `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs`, compiled directly after `DispersionModels.fs`, and their `axes` MUST stay static members declared in `MuellerInverse.fs`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests`, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each crystal record's builder composes its permittivity from its own fields`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests", "BerremanTests.LangasiteInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/LangasiteInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.each crystal record's builder composes its permittivity from its own fields", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.UniaxialParameters", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.TriclinicParameters", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.AbsorbingTriclinicParameters", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics.UniaxialParameters", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics.TriclinicParameters", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics.AbsorbingTriclinicParameters", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-RECORDS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 354, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [353], "how_to": "A material's physics becomes a union that can hold more than the complexity tree, with one case for now, so that the next step adds the crystal case without touching every reader again (the S11.1 brief 'a new case beside the existing complexity tree'; .spec-md §3.2 'A material's physics is its complexity', which this widens). This is one step because the record field's type changes every consumer at once (the step 13 precedent). No behaviour changes. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: directly after `MaterialComplexity` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialComplexity`), `MaterialPhysics` = `ComplexityPhysics of complexity : MaterialComplexity`, with `member this.toProperties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp` answering the complexity's `toProperties`. `MaterialEntry` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`) replaces `complexity : MaterialComplexity` (step 13) with `physics : MaterialPhysics`, and its `properties` member is `this.physics.toProperties`; its doc says the physics is the entry's data and `properties` its engine composition. (2) The members the readers share, each with one arm here: in `LibraryFacets.fs`, beside `MaterialComplexity.anisotropy` (`LibraryFacets.fs:anisotropy`), `type MaterialPhysics with member this.anisotropy : Anisotropy`; in `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs`, beside `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:isEditable`), `type MaterialPhysics with member this.editableComplexityOpt : MaterialComplexity option`, `Some` of the complexity when its `isEditable` holds and `None` otherwise (an option rather than a flag, ELEV012); in `OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs`, beside `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` (`NkDispersionChart.fs:gyrationComponentsOfComplexity`) and `MaterialComplexity.muKind`, `type MaterialPhysics with member this.gyrationComponents : GyrationComponent list` (the complexity's `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity`) and `member this.muKind : MuKind` (the complexity's `muKind`). (3) Readers. `MaterialStore.fs`: `MaterialEntry.versionPayload` (step 68) becomes `VersionPayload<MaterialPhysics, MaterialMetadata>` with `physics = this.physics`, so the version rule compares the physics structurally as it compared the complexity. `LibraryFacets.fs`: the private `constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt` and `magneticOpt` match `entry.physics` (`ComplexityPhysics complexity` → today's body), the anisotropy facet extracts `entry.physics.anisotropy`, and the transparency facet matches `ComplexityPhysics _` around today's rule. `OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs`: `ReachableMaterial.ofEntry` (`OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:ofEntry`) matches the physics, `ComplexityPhysics complexity` → `ReachableMaterial.definedSegmentsOf complexity`. `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` (step 25): `ofMaterialEntry` writes `MaterialPayload` of the physics' complexity and `toMaterialEntry` reads it back as `ComplexityPhysics`, so every entry file, catalogue file, snapshot and stored payload keeps its bytes and its hash (`BuiltInCatalogueParityTests` and `BuiltInCatalogueIntegrityTests` stay green unchanged). `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs` (`entryFromTabulated`, `entryOfAxis`) and `Report.fs` (`dtoToEntry`) build `physics = ComplexityPhysics …`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs`: `ViewOnlyMaterial of reason : ControlCaption * shown : MaterialComplexity` (step 13) carries `shown : MaterialPhysics`; `previewProperties`, `previewGyrationComponents` and `previewMuKind` read `shown.toProperties`, `shown.gyrationComponents` and `shown.muKind`; `initMaterialEditor` seeds through `entry.physics.editableComplexityOpt`: `Some complexity` → `ofComplexity` as today, its `Error e` giving `ViewOnlyMaterial (e.caption, entry.physics)`, and `None` → `ViewOnlyMaterial (ControlCaption \"this entry's physics is not editable term data — view-only\", entry.physics)`; `entryUnder` builds `physics = ComplexityPhysics complexity`. `MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `editableSelection` and the view panel's editability read `entry.physics.editableComplexityOpt` (`Some _` is editable), and both chart call sites read `shownEntry.physics.anisotropy`. `MaterialEditorWindow.fs`: its module doc names the physics. (4) Every test fixture that builds a `MaterialEntry` writes `physics = ComplexityPhysics c` for `complexity = c`, and every test read of `.complexity` reads the physics' complexity through a match; no assertion changes: in `OpticalConstructor.Tests` `MaterialProxyTests.fs`, `SampleProxyTests.fs`, `MaterialComplexityTests.fs`, `MaterialImportTests.fs`, `LibraryFacetsTests.fs`, `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs`, `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `ExportImportTests.fs`, `LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs`, `EntryFileJsonTests.fs`, `CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs`, `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs` and `BuiltinCatalogue.fs`; in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`, `MaterialsWindowTests.fs`, `NkDispersionChartTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`, `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` and `MaterialsControlsTests.fs`, whichever of them build or read one. A comment or message in an edited file that names the entry's `complexity` field names its physics. No other type, member or option is added. (5) Tests. `MaterialComplexityTests`: `a complexity physics composes, classifies and offers its complexity as the complexity does`: for a constant isotropic complexity and a uniaxial dispersive one, `ComplexityPhysics` of each answers `toProperties.getProperties` at 600 nm equal to the complexity's, `anisotropy` equal to the complexity's, and `editableComplexityOpt` `Some` of it; a complexity whose active aspect is `PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw` (step 10) answers `None`. `NkDispersionChartTests`: `a complexity physics charts the gyration components and the mu kind of its complexity`: for a uniaxial-active complexity the physics answers `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` of it and its `muKind`. `MaterialEditorWindowTests`' `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry` reads the view-only case's shown physics where it read its complexity, its assertions otherwise unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the physics union lands, `MaterialEntry` MUST hold `physics : MaterialPhysics` with `properties` its `toProperties`, `MaterialPhysics` MUST hold the one case `ComplexityPhysics`, and every entry file MUST keep its bytes and hash; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a complexity physics composes, classifies and offers its complexity as the complexity does`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a complexity physics charts the gyration components and the mu kind of its complexity` and the changed `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CatalogueImportInMemoryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BuiltinCatalogue.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.a complexity physics composes, classifies and offers its complexity as the complexity does", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests.a complexity physics charts the gyration components and the mu kind of its complexity", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialPhysics", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialEntry.complexity", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialEntry.physics", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryFacets.MaterialPhysics.anisotropy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialComplexityEditor.MaterialPhysics.editableComplexityOpt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.NkDispersionChart.MaterialPhysics.gyrationComponents", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.NkDispersionChart.MaterialPhysics.muKind", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialEditorView.EditorMode", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs", "obligations": ["S111-MATERIAL-PHYSICS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 355, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [354], "how_to": "A material version holds one of the three crystal-parameter records as its physics, beside the complexity tree, and composes its engine properties through the S10.1 builders; the editor, the facets and the entry-file schema follow (the S11.1 brief 'Material physics form'; .spec-md §3.16). The editor follows as it followed the published gyration law (step 10): the ladder edits complexity trees, so a crystal entry opens view-only; a crystal material reaches the library through its entry file (import and drop, S3.1-S3.2) and through Promote to library (S11.5). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `CrystalPhysics.fs` (step 353), after the three records: `CrystalParameters` = `UniaxialCrystal of UniaxialParameters` | `TriclinicCrystal of TriclinicParameters` | `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal of AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`, with `member this.opticalProperties : OpticalProperties` (each case its record's `opticalProperties`) and `member this.toProperties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp`, `this.opticalProperties.dispersive` (`Dispersion.fs`, `OpticalProperties.dispersive`): the same tensors at every wavelength. It is stored in the serializer's case form, as `SlotTurn` is (step 256), so no int tag is added. (2) `MaterialLibrary.fs`: `MaterialPhysics` (step 354) gains `CrystalParameterPhysics of crystal : CrystalParameters`, and `toProperties` answers `crystal.toProperties` for it. (3) Each shared member gains its arm. `LibraryFacets.fs`: `type CrystalParameters with member this.anisotropy : Anisotropy` (`Uniaxial` for `UniaxialCrystal`, `Biaxial` for the two triclinic cases) and `member this.transparency : Transparency` (`Transparent` for the uniaxial and the triclinic crystal, `Absorbing` for the absorbing one), and `MaterialPhysics.anisotropy` answers the crystal's. `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs`: `editableComplexityOpt` answers `None`. `NkDispersionChart.fs`: `gyrationComponents` answers `allGyrationComponents` and `muKind` `ScalarMuKind`, μ being the vacuum's in every builder. So `initMaterialEditor` opens a crystal entry as `ViewOnlyMaterial` with step 354's caption, its preview charting `shown.toProperties`, and the Materials window offers no Edit for it, with no change to either view. (4) `LibraryFacets.fs`: the private `constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt` and `magneticOpt` answer `None` for a crystal, and the transparency facet extracts `crystal.transparency` for it; the dispersion facet already reads `MaterialEntry.dispersion`, which is `ConstantMaterial` for a crystal; the dispersion-model, gyration-class, handedness and magnetic facets do not apply, because they classify the ladder's value trees and a crystal's gyration is parameters. `OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs`: `ofEntry` answers no defined segment for a crystal, so it never flags, as a constant complexity does not. (5) Entry files. `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `LibraryEntryPayload` (step 25) gains `CrystalMaterialPayload of CrystalParameters`, whose `kind` is `MaterialEntryKind`; `ofMaterialEntry` writes it for a crystal and `MaterialPayload` for a complexity; `toMaterialEntry` reads either; every other decoder answers `EntryKindMismatchErr` for it as for `MaterialPayload`, and every other complete match over the payload gains the case. `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-material.schema.json` (step 30): under version 1 the payload's case tag is `MaterialPayload` or `CrystalMaterialPayload`, written as the schema writes the existing tag, the crystal inside it bound by the serializer (`MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one). The schema version stays 1: no stored file changes, because every existing material keeps `MaterialPayload` (.spec-md §7: no migration, no stored data predates the case). The database stores the canonical payload (step 69), so nothing else in Storage changes. No editor for crystal parameters, no wire tag and no other member is added. (6) Tests, over test-local records written as literals (a uniaxial crystal n_o 1.544, n_e 1.553, g11 3.0e-5, g33 −1.0e-5; a triclinic one; an absorbing triclinic one with fifteen distinct values). `MaterialComplexityTests`: `a crystal-parameter material composes its record's engine properties at every wavelength`: for each case an entry of `CrystalParameterPhysics` answers, at 400, 600 and 800 nm, `properties.getProperties` equal to its record's `opticalProperties` (ε, μ and ρ through the file's tolerance helpers, 1e-15) and `dispersion` `ConstantMaterial`; `a crystal-parameter physics offers no editable complexity, so its entry opens view-only`: a crystal answers `editableComplexityOpt = None` and a constant isotropic complexity `Some` of itself. `LibraryFacetsTests`: `a crystal-parameter material classifies its anisotropy and transparency from its crystal, and the ladder's facets do not apply`, over entries built as `materialEntryWith` builds them, with a crystal physics:anisotropy `Uniaxial` / `Biaxial` / `Biaxial`, transparency `Transparent` / `Transparent` / `Absorbing`, dispersion `Constant`, and the dispersion-model, gyration-class, handedness and magnetic facets not applicable. `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`: `a crystal-parameter material never flags out of band`: a wavelength sweep over 300-900 nm flags nothing for a crystal entry. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`: `a crystal-parameter material's builder and decoder are inverse`: `ofMaterialEntry` then `toMaterialEntry` answers each crystal entry, its content's payload being `CrystalMaterialPayload`, and `toSample` of it `EntryKindMismatchErr`. `EntryFileJsonTests`: `a crystal-parameter material entry file round-trips each crystal record`: each crystal content goes `sealed`, `fileText`, `parseEntry MaterialEntryKind` and answers an equal envelope whose decoder answers the entry, the text naming `CrystalMaterialPayload`. `MaterialProxyTests` (`MaterialProxyContract`, steps 66, 69, so both stores run it): `a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics`: a minted absorbing crystal material saved through `saveMaterial` resolves at version 1 to an equal entry and is listed by `listMaterials ActiveOnly`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`: `a crystal-parameter entry opens the editor view-only and previews its crystal's properties`: `initMaterialEditor` over a uniaxial crystal entry gives `ViewOnlyMaterial`, its `previewProperties.getProperties` at 600 nm equal to the crystal's `opticalProperties`, and its `previewGyrationComponents` equal to `allGyrationComponents`.", "acceptance": "After the crystal case lands, an entry of `CrystalParameterPhysics` MUST compose its record's builder at every wavelength, classify by its crystal's anisotropy and transparency, never flag out of band, open view-only, and round-trip its entry file as `CrystalMaterialPayload` while every existing file keeps its bytes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a crystal-parameter material composes its record's engine properties at every wavelength`, `a crystal-parameter physics offers no editable complexity, so its entry opens view-only`, `a crystal-parameter material classifies its anisotropy and transparency from its crystal, and the ladder's facets do not apply`, `a crystal-parameter material never flags out of band`, `a crystal-parameter material's builder and decoder are inverse`, `a crystal-parameter material entry file round-trips each crystal record` and `a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics` under `MaterialProxyTests` and `MaterialProxySqliteTests`, the count rising by 8; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a crystal-parameter entry opens the editor view-only and previews its crystal's properties`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-material.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.a crystal-parameter material composes its record's engine properties at every wavelength", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.a crystal-parameter physics offers no editable complexity, so its entry opens view-only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests.a crystal-parameter material classifies its anisotropy and transparency from its crystal, and the ladder's facets do not apply", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.a crystal-parameter material never flags out of band", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.OutOfBandDiagnosticTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a crystal-parameter material's builder and decoder are inverse", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a crystal-parameter material entry file round-trips each crystal record", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests.a crystal-parameter material is stored and resolved at its version by its physics", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxySqliteTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.a crystal-parameter entry opens the editor view-only and previews its crystal's properties", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.CrystalPhysics.CrystalParameters", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/CrystalPhysics.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialPhysics", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryFacets.CrystalParameters.anisotropy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryFacets.CrystalParameters.transparency", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles.LibraryEntryPayload.CrystalMaterialPayload", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S111-CRYSTAL-MATERIAL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 356, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [355], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests"], "how_to": "Sessions' gain models become data, and `MuellerReconstruction.familyGain` with its `GainCalibration` cases becomes their first implementation (001 §L 'Sessions and gain models as data: … per session the gain is free, anchored to its AIR runs, or interpolated between two AIR repeats … These rules replace the hand-written family rules: `MuellerReconstruction.familyGain` becomes their first implementation'; the S11.1 brief 'moved, not copied'; .spec-md §6 row 'Gain rules'). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'): after the step `familyGain`, `GainCalibration`, `RepeatPairGain`, `SplitGain`, `CplCplGain` and `InterpolatedGain` exist nowhere, and each of their rules exists once, in the gain model. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs`, `module Studies` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ImportProfiles.fs` (step 300), the last Domain file, because a study names experiments, items, materials, the crystal axes and AIR gains declared before it: one `<Compile Include=\"Studies.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: a study, a named set of one kit's experiments fitted together, with its unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials (spec 0050 S11.1). In this order: (a) `StudyError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `EmptyGainAnchorsErr` (an anchored gain model names no AIR run), `MissingAnchorGainErr` (a gain model names an AIR run whose gain is not given) and `FreeSessionGainErr` (a free session gain is fitted, so no AIR rule derives it), with `member this.describe : string` in step 39's form: `the gain model names no AIR run: <reason>`, `the AIR run's gain is not known: <reason>` and `the session gain is fitted, not derived from AIR runs: <reason>`. Later S11.1 steps add cases, each with its line. (b) `AirRepeatPair = { opening : ExperimentName; closing : ExperimentName }`, the AIR runs that open and close a drifting session. (c) `SessionGainModel` = `FreeSessionGain` | `AnchoredSessionGain of anchors : ExperimentName list` | `InterpolatedSessionGain of repeats : AirRepeatPair`, stored in the serializer's case form (step 256's `SlotTurn` precedent), no int tag. (d) `AirAnchorGain = { run : ExperimentName; gain : AirGain; capturedAt : System.DateTimeOffset }`, one AIR run's fitted gain and the mean capture time of its rows (the reference `fit_air_gain`). (e) `GainInterpolation = { gainStart : AirGain; timeStart : System.DateTimeOffset; gainEnd : AirGain; timeEnd : System.DateTimeOffset }`, `MuellerReconstruction.fs:InterpolatedGain` moved and renamed, its fields unchanged. (f) `SessionGainRule` = `SteadyGainRule of gain : AirGain` | `InterpolatedGainRule of interpolation : GainInterpolation`, with `member this.gainAt (t : System.DateTimeOffset) : AirGain`: the steady gain, or `familyGain`'s `Day1Interp` arm moved verbatim (the span in `TotalSeconds`, weight 0 for a span ≤ 0 and otherwise `(t − timeStart) / span` clamped to [0, 1], then `AirGain ((1.0 - weight) * gainStart.value + weight * gainEnd.value)`). (g) `type SessionGainModel with member this.ruleWith (anchors : AirAnchorGain list) : Result<SessionGainRule, StudyError>`, each anchor found by its `run`: `FreeSessionGain` → `FreeSessionGainErr`; an anchored model with no run → `EmptyGainAnchorsErr`; a run `anchors` lacks → `MissingAnchorGainErr` naming it (the first, in model order); one run → `SteadyGainRule` of its gain (`familyGain`'s `Day2Single`, and each side of its `SplitGain`); two → `SteadyGainRule (AirGain (0.5 * (a.value + b.value)))` (`familyGain`'s `meanPair`, moved); more → `SteadyGainRule` of their sum over their count; `InterpolatedSessionGain` → `InterpolatedGainRule` of the opening run's gain and time and the closing run's. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs`: delete `RepeatPairGain`, `InterpolatedGain`, `CplCplGain` (`Day1Interp`, `Day2Single`), `SplitGain`, `GainCalibration` and `familyGain` with their docs (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:familyGain`). The Stage-3 section comment and `correctSignal`'s doc name the session's gain rule (`SessionGainRule.gainAt`, spec 0050 S11.1) where they name `familyGain`. `AirGain`, `scalarGain`, `darkSubtract`, `DarkMean`, `airIdentityPred` and `correctSignal` stay. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs` (steps 349-352) opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies`. (a) The nine AIR block literals become `ExperimentName`s, born as names because in a kit the AIR runs are experiments of those names and a gain model anchors to experiments by name (001 §L); a block's rows are those whose `experiment.nameText.toExperimentName` (steps 270, 286) answers `Ok` of its name. (b) Each block's `AirAnchorGain` is its name, the gain `fitAirGain` fits over it and the time `meanTime` computes over it, for all nine. (c) The five families' gain rules become six gain models resolved through `ruleWith` over the nine anchors: LP-LP `AnchoredSessionGain [ LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2; LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R ]`, LP-CPL `[ LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2; LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2R ]`, CPL-LP before the split `[ CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2 ]` and from the split on `[ CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2R ]`, CPL-CPL day 1 `InterpolatedSessionGain { opening = CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL; closing = CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR }` and CPL-CPL day 2 `AnchoredSessionGain [ CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2 ]`; a refusal is the new `StagedMuellerError` case `SessionGainErr of error : StudyError`, which no committed data reaches. (d) Each science row's signal is `correctSignal darkMean r.avgTotal (rule.gainAt r.capturedAt)` with its family's rule, a CPL-LP row captured strictly before the split time taking the pre rule and every other CPL-LP row the post rule, as `SplitGain` did. (e) `StagedMuellerData` replaces `gains : GainCalibration` and `cplCplDay1Gain : InterpolatedGain` with `airGains : AirAnchorGain list`, the nine in the reference order (LP-LP, LP-CPL and CPL-LP each `-2` then `-2R`, then `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR` and `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`), and its doc says so. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`: the section 7.2 fact's gain assertion reads each gain from `staged.airGains` by run name against its `MuellerReference` value (`lpLpGainA` for `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `lpLpGainB` for `-2R`, …, `cplCplDay1GainStart` for `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `cplCplDay1GainEnd` for `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR`, `cplCplDay2Gain` for `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`), a run missing from the list failing the fact; its band, its numbers and the rest of the fact are unchanged. The fact `Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred, correctSignal and every per-family familyGain rule (always-run)` keeps its `scalarGain`, `darkSubtract`, `correctSignal` and `airIdentityPred` pins, loses its `familyGain` block, whose rules moved, and is renamed `Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred and correctSignal (always-run)`. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4): every row divides by the gain the same operations compute (one run's gain itself, two runs' `0.5 * (a + b)`, the interpolation's same expression). `MuellerReconstructionTests`' count is unchanged. (5) Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs`, `module StudySessionTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, carrying the moved block's literals at fixed literal times: `a session anchored to one AIR run takes its gain, and to more the mean of their gains`: anchors of 10 and 20 answer a steady 15 equal by `=` to `AirGain (0.5 * (10.0 + 20.0))`, 4 and 6 answer 5, one anchor of 42 answers 42, three anchors of 1, 2 and 6 answer 3, and the CPL-LP split as two one-run sessions of 100 and 200 answers 100 and 200 at any time; `a session interpolated between two AIR repeats weighs their gains by time and clamps outside them`: opening 30 at 10:00 and closing 50 at 14:00 answer 40 at 12:00, 30 at 10:00, 50 at 14:00, 30 at 09:00 and 50 at 15:00, within 1e-12; `a free gain has no AIR rule, and an anchored model with no run or a missing run is refused`: `FreeSessionGain` answers `FreeSessionGainErr`, `AnchoredSessionGain []` `EmptyGainAnchorsErr`, and an anchored or interpolated model naming a run the anchors lack `MissingAnchorGainErr` whose reason holds that name; `every study error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text holding it.", "acceptance": "After the gain models land, `SessionGainModel.ruleWith` MUST resolve a free, anchored or interpolated model by `familyGain`'s moved rules, `familyGain`, `GainCalibration`, `RepeatPairGain`, `SplitGain`, `CplCplGain` and `InterpolatedGain` MUST be gone, and `StagedMuellerPath` MUST divide each row by its session's rule and answer the nine AIR gains as `airGains`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a session anchored to one AIR run takes its gain, and to more the mean of their gains`, `a session interpolated between two AIR repeats weighs their gains by time and clamps outside them`, `a free gain has no AIR rule, and an anchored model with no run or a missing run is refused` and `every study error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, with `Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred and correctSignal (always-run)` in place of the familyGain fact, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerReconstruction.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred, correctSignal and every per-family familyGain rule (always-run)", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "successor": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.Stage-3 signal reduction pins darkSubtract, scalarGain, airIdentityPred and correctSignal (always-run)", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests.section 7.2 end-to-end: the Stage 1 to 2 to 3 pipeline reconstructs M_QZ, M_LR and M_{QZ+LR} at rank 16 and reproduces the reference pipeline exactly", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a session anchored to one AIR run takes its gain, and to more the mean of their gains", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a session interpolated between two AIR repeats weighs their gains by time and clamps outside them", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a free gain has no AIR rule, and an anchored model with no run or a missing run is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.familyGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.GainCalibration", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.RepeatPairGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.SplitGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.CplCplGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerReconstruction.InterpolatedGain", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.AirRepeatPair", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SessionGainModel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.AirAnchorGain", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.GainInterpolation", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SessionGainRule", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SessionGainModel.ruleWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerData", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.StagedMuellerPath.StagedMuellerError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/StagedMuellerPath.fs", "obligations": ["S111-GAIN-MODELS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 357, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [356], "how_to": "A study's experiments fall into session blocks, split automatically at the Diagnostic runs or set by hand, and a session's dark comes from the Dark runs (001 §L 'Sessions and gain models as data: auto-split at Diagnostic experiments, or by hand; … dark from the Dark runs'; the S11.1 brief 'Sessions, auto-split at DiagnosticRun experiments or set by hand'; step 285: a hand-set `SessionName` is the session a run belongs to, the rest split at the Diagnostic runs). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after `SessionGainModel.ruleWith` (step 356): (1) `StudySession = { name : SessionName; experiments : ExperimentName list }`, one session block. (2) `static member splitAll (experiments : Experiment list) : StudySession list`, over the experiments in the order given: an experiment whose `sessionOpt` is `Some s` (`SetExperimentSession`, step 294) joins the session named `s`; a `DiagnosticRun` (step 285) with no hand-set session belongs to no session and closes the current automatic block; every other experiment joins the current automatic block. Each non-empty automatic block is a session named `Session <k>`, `k` the smallest positive integer whose `SessionName` neither a hand-set session of the list nor an earlier block holds, so two Diagnostic runs in a row, or one at either end, make no empty session. The sessions are ordered by the position of their first experiment, each holding its experiments in list order. (3) `member this.darkRunsIn (experiments : Experiment list) : ExperimentName list`: the session's `DarkRun` experiments in its order, or, when it holds none, every `DarkRun` experiment of `experiments` in their order, because one darkness file can serve every session (the optics-mueller kit's `darkness_checks.csv`, step 330). Reading the dark level from those runs' data is the forward model's (S11.2). No other type, member or option is added. Tests, in `StudySessionTests` (step 356), over test-local experiments built as `ExperimentProxyTests`' fixtures build them, differing only in name, role and session: `experiments split into sessions at each diagnostic run, and a hand-set session gathers its own`: E1 (Science), E2 (Calibration), D1 (Diagnostic), E3 (Science), E4 (Science, hand-set `Day 2`), E5 (Dark) and D2 (Diagnostic) split into `Session 1` [E1; E2], `Session 2` [E3; E5] and `Day 2` [E4], in that order; the same list with E1 hand-set to `Session 1` gives `Session 1` [E1], `Session 2` [E2] and `Session 3` [E3; E5] and `Day 2` [E4], ordered by first experiment; and a list of only Diagnostic runs gives no session. `a session's dark comes from its own dark runs, or else from every dark run of the study`: in the first split, `Session 2`'s dark runs are [E5], and `Session 1`'s and `Day 2`'s are every Dark run of the list, [E5]; a session holding two Dark runs answers its own two.", "acceptance": "After sessions land, `StudySession.splitAll` MUST gather hand-set sessions, split the rest at each Diagnostic run into `Session <k>` blocks ordered by their first experiment, and `darkRunsIn` MUST answer a session's own Dark runs or else every Dark run; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `experiments split into sessions at each diagnostic run, and a hand-set session gathers its own` and `a session's dark comes from its own dark runs, or else from every dark run of the study`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.experiments split into sessions at each diagnostic run, and a hand-set session gathers its own", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.a session's dark comes from its own dark runs, or else from every dark run of the study", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudySession", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudySession.splitAll", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudySession.darkRunsIn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SESSIONS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 358, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [357], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests"], "how_to": "The study as Domain data, and CreateStudy's pure half (001 §L '`Study` grows from the experiment collection: a named set of experiments inside ONE kit, plus: the unknowns (owner + scope); sessions; fit settings; its append-only fit runs', the scope table, 'Weights and ablation: a weight per experiment or per detector; enable / disable per experiment'; 001 §E 'notes on … studies … live in their files'; 001 §P `CreateStudy`; the S11.1 brief). Fit runs are their own files (S11.3). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. Every case name has two words and no `bool` appears. In `Studies.fs`, after `StudySession` (step 357), in this order: (1) `StudyName of string` with `.value`, `static member tryCreate (text : string) : Result<StudyName, StudyError>` keeping the text and refusing an empty or white-space one with `InvalidStudyNameErr`, and `member this.fileStem : FileStem` = `FileStem.ofText this.value` (step 24), the stem of its `<name>.study-json` (001 §A). (2) `StudyNotes of string` with `.value` and `static member none`. (3) `ParameterScope` = `ItemScope` | `MaterialScope` | `SessionBlockScope` | `ExperimentScope` (001 §L 'Scope is the sharing rule'): `member this.value : int` 1 to 4 in that order, `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : ParameterScope option`, `member this.text : string` (`Item`, `Material`, `Session`, `Experiment`) and `static member all`. The session case is `SessionBlockScope`, after 001's 'one value per session block', because STL declares a `SessionScope` case and DU case names are unique among ours (AGENTS.md, ELEV016; the lower assembly keeps its name). (4) `StudyParameterRef` = `ItemParameterRef of item : ItemId * name : ParameterName` | `MaterialParameterRef of material : MaterialVersionId * name : ParameterName`, with `member this.name : ParameterName` and `member this.describe : string` (`item <GUID> <name>` or `material <GUID> v<n> <name>`). (5) `ScopedParameter = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; scope : ParameterScope }`, a scope the study sets. (6) `ParameterLink = { follower : StudyParameterRef; leader : StudyParameterRef }`, 'CPL2.δ = CPL1.δ': the follower takes the leader's value (001 §L 'Explicit links … are constraints'). (7) `SessionGainSetting = { session : SessionName; model : SessionGainModel }`. (8) `FitMode` = `JointFit` | `StagedFit` (001 §L 'Fit modes'; S11.3 runs them), with `value` 1-2, `tryOfWire`, `text` (`Joint`, `Staged`) and `all`. (9) `ResidualWeight of float` with `.value`, `static member tryCreate (value : float) : Result<ResidualWeight, StudyError>` refusing a NaN, infinite, zero or negative value with `InvalidResidualWeightErr`, and `static member unit` (1.0). (10) `ExperimentWeightSetting = { experiment : ExperimentName; weight : ResidualWeight }` and `DetectorWeightSetting = { detector : ItemId; weight : ResidualWeight }`. (11) `StudyFitSettings = { mode : FitMode; experimentWeights : ExperimentWeightSetting list; detectorWeights : DetectorWeightSetting list; disabled : ExperimentName list }`, with `static member initial` (`JointFit`, no weight, nothing disabled). (12) `OpenedMaterial = { version : MaterialVersionId; name : EntryName; crystal : CrystalParameters; parameters : Parameter list }`, the study-local working copy of an opened material version (001 §I 'a study OPENS a material version, which creates a study-local working copy, stored in the study file'), which step 361 fills. (13) `Study = { name : StudyName; experiments : ExperimentName list; materials : OpenedMaterial list; scopes : ScopedParameter list; links : ParameterLink list; sessionGains : SessionGainSetting list; settings : StudyFitSettings; notes : StudyNotes }`. Experiments are named by `ExperimentName`, because a kit stores each under its name (step 290). (14) `static member create (name : StudyName) (experiments : ExperimentName list) (held : Study list) (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`: `DuplicateStudyNameErr` naming both when a held study's `name.fileStem` equals the name's ignoring case (every `<name>.study-json` shares the kit root, step 223's rule for items); `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming the first name no kit experiment has; otherwise the study holding the names in order, each once, with nothing opened, scoped or linked, no gain setting, `StudyFitSettings.initial` and `StudyNotes.none`. (15) `member this.sessionsIn (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : StudySession list`: `StudySession.splitAll` of the study's experiments as `kitExperiments` holds them, in study order. (16) `member this.gainModelOf (session : SessionName) : SessionGainModel`: the setting's model, or `FreeSessionGain`. `StudyError` gains `InvalidStudyNameErr` (`the study name is not valid: <reason>`), `DuplicateStudyNameErr` (`the kit already has a study of that name: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` (`the kit has no such experiment: <reason>`) and `InvalidResidualWeightErr` (`the residual weight is not valid: <reason>`). No wire converter is added here: the study file (step 359) adds the two. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs`, `module StudyTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local experiments built as in `StudySessionTests`: `a study name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`: `StudyName.tryCreate \"QZ:LR\"` keeps the text and its `fileStem` is `FileStem \"QZ_LR\"`, and `\"\"` and `\"  \"` answer `InvalidStudyNameErr`; `a parameter scope and a fit mode round-trip their wire tags and render their text`: the tags 1-4 and 1-2 in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and 5 (and 3), the texts as above and `all` in tag order; `a residual weight refuses a non-finite or non-positive value`: 0.5 and 2 are kept, and NaN, +∞, 0 and −1 answer `InvalidResidualWeightErr`; `a study is created over the kit's experiments in order, each once, with the initial settings, and refuses a held name or an experiment the kit lacks`: over E1, E2 and E3, `create` of `QZ-LR` with [E2; E1; E2] answers [E2; E1] with the initial settings; with a held study `qz-lr` it answers `DuplicateStudyNameErr`; with [E1; E9] `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming E9; `a study's sessions split its experiments in study order, and a session without a setting has a free gain`: a study of [E3; D1; E1] (D1 Diagnostic) answers `Session 1` [E3] and `Session 2` [E1], and `gainModelOf` of each is `FreeSessionGain`. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the four new cases.", "acceptance": "After the study's shape lands, `Studies.fs` MUST declare `StudyName`, `StudyNotes`, `ParameterScope` (with `SessionBlockScope`), `StudyParameterRef`, `ScopedParameter`, `ParameterLink`, `SessionGainSetting`, `FitMode`, `ResidualWeight`, the weight settings, `StudyFitSettings`, `OpenedMaterial` and `Study`, and `Study.create` MUST refuse a held name and an unknown experiment; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule`, `a parameter scope and a fit mode round-trip their wire tags and render their text`, `a residual weight refuses a non-finite or non-positive value`, `a study is created over the kit's experiments in order, each once, with the initial settings, and refuses a held name or an experiment the kit lacks` and `a study's sessions split its experiments in study order, and a session without a setting has a free gain`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a study name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a parameter scope and a fit mode round-trip their wire tags and render their text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a residual weight refuses a non-finite or non-positive value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a study is created over the kit's experiments in order, each once, with the initial settings, and refuses a held name or an experiment the kit lacks", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a study's sessions split its experiments in study order, and a session without a setting has a free gain", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyName", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyNotes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ParameterScope", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyParameterRef", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ScopedParameter", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ParameterLink", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.SessionGainSetting", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.FitMode", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ResidualWeight", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ExperimentWeightSetting", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.DetectorWeightSetting", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyFitSettings", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.OpenedMaterial", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.create", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.sessionsIn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.gainModelOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-SHAPE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 359, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [358], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests"], "how_to": "A study persists as its own kit file, `<name>.study-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema, and recording it snapshots and pins the material versions it opens (001 §A 'Kit extensions … .study-json'; 001 §E 'Library closure snapshot', 'Writes are atomic'; 001 §P '`KitProxy` … studies'; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 146's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`) and step 226's shape for items; no second parser or writer is written. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. (1) `Studies.fs`, after `Study` (step 358): `StudyFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; study : Study }`, the `.study-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1; `type Study with member this.studyFile : StudyFile` (one direction, ELEV006); and `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list`, each opened material's `EntryVersionReference { entryId = version.materialId.toLibraryEntryId; version = version.version }` in study order (steps 24, 137): what the kit snapshots and pins. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/item.schema.json` (step 226), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/study.json`: `schemaVersion` a positive integer, checked unconditionally; only under `if` it is 1 (`then`), the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `study`, and `study` holds exactly `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character, the pattern `\\S`), `experiments` (an array of non-empty strings), `materials`, `scopes`, `links` and `sessionGains` (arrays), `settings` (an object holding exactly `mode`, an integer from 1 to 2, `experimentWeights` and `detectorWeights`, arrays, and `disabled`, an array of non-empty strings) and `notes` (a string). The inner shapes are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/item.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateStudyFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateItemFile` (step 226) does. (3) `CanonicalJson.options` (`CanonicalJson.fs`) gains two converters, for `ParameterScope` and `FitMode`, written as step 285's `ExperimentRole` converter is and registered beside it before the `JsonFSharpConverter`: each writes the case's `value` and reads through `tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. `SessionGainModel`, `StudyParameterRef` and `CrystalParameters` keep the serializer's case form, and nothing else in the options changes. (4) `KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 146, 226-228): `type StudyFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` (`nodeOf this` rendered by `canonicalFileText`); `type KitFileText with member this.parseStudyFile : Result<StudyFile, StorageError>` (`parseVersionedText validateStudyFile StudyKitFile.extension StudyFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value`, steps 123-124); on the `KitProxy` extension `member this.writeStudy (study : Study) : Result<unit, KitError>`, which writes `study.studyFile.fileText` with `writeKindFile StudyKitFile study.name.fileStem`, a rendering error being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file, and `member this.readStudies () : Result<Study list, KitError>`, which parses every stem `listKindFiles StudyKitFile` answers, a refusal or a file whose study's `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason and refusing the whole read, ordered by the name's text (ordinal); and on the `KitLibraryContext` extension `member this.recordStudy (study : Study) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>`: `this.snapshotReferences study.libraryReferences` (step 139), then `this.kit.proxy.writeStudy study`, a `KitError` wrapped as `KitLibraryKitErr`. Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) `writeStudy` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`. No delete, rename, cache or other member is added. There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. (5) Tests. Their study is test-local: `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2, with an opened absorbing crystal material written as an `OpenedMaterial` record literal over a test-local probe whose one parameter, `n3`, is an `UnknownParameter` with a prior, one `ScopedParameter` (`ExperimentScope`), one `ParameterLink`, one gain setting of each `SessionGainModel` case, both weights, E2 disabled and two lines of notes. `KitContentFileJsonTests`: `a study is stored under its name`: `StudyKitFile.fileNameOf (StudyName \"QZ-LR\").fileStem` is `FileName \"QZ-LR.study-json\"`; `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`: `studyFile`, `fileText`, `parseStudyFile` answer an equal file; the text holds no `\\r`, ends with exactly one `\\n`, lists its top-level keys as `schemaVersion` then `study` in ordinal order, writes the fit mode and the scope as their tags, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text; `a study file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: the text with `schemaVersion` 2, with its body and alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = StudyKitFile.extension`, found 2 and expected 1; `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds`: without `study`, with an extra top-level key, with `study.name` `\"  \"` and with `study.settings.mode` 3 each answer `SchemaValidationErr`, and `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`. `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 166, 285): `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes each `ParameterScope` and `FitMode` as its tag (`SessionBlockScope` as `3`) and reads it back, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the scope tag 5 and the mode tag 3 with `MalformedJsonErr`. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs`, `module KitStudyFileTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, whose facts each make a folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, \"KitStudyFileTests\", <a new GUID>)` and a `KitProxy.create` over it with `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (step 227's precedent): `a kit's study files round-trip, each stored under its name`: `QZ-LR` and `LR` written answer `LR.study-json` and `QZ-LR.study-json` in the folder and `readStudies` answers `LR` then `QZ-LR`; `a study file that does not read or holds another name refuses the read, naming the file`: `Broken.study-json` holding `{` and `Other.study-json` holding `QZ-LR`'s text each make `readStudies` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file; `a read-only kit refuses a study write and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView` `writeStudy` answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and the folder's bytes are unchanged. `KitLibraryTests` (step 139), over its built-in library, its recorder of pins and its in-memory kit opened read-write: `recording a study snapshots and pins its opened material versions, then writes its file`: a user absorbing crystal material saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial` and held by `QZ-LR` as an `OpenedMaterial` record literal of its version, recorded through `recordStudy`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding that material's version 1 and its category, `paths` holding `library/<its GUID>@v1.material-json` and `QZ-LR.study-json`, the recorder holding that version, and `kit.proxy.readStudies ()` answering the study; `a read-only kit records no study`: under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` `recordStudy` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the study file lands, `StudyFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseStudyFile` reads back equal against `schema/study.schema.json`, `KitProxy.writeStudy` / `readStudies` MUST store each study under its name and refuse a bad file whole, and `KitLibraryContext.recordStudy` MUST snapshot and pin the opened material versions before it writes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study is stored under its name`, `a study file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a study file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds`, `a kit's study files round-trip, each stored under its name`, `a study file that does not read or holds another name refuses the read, naming the file`, `a read-only kit refuses a study write and writes nothing`, `recording a study snapshots and pins its opened material versions, then writes its file` and `a read-only kit records no study`, the count rising by 9, and the widened `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/study.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a study is stored under its name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a study file round-trips through its canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a study file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or malformed study file is refused before it binds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an unknown disk tag is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests.a kit's study files round-trip, each stored under its name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests.a study file that does not read or holds another name refuses the read, naming the file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests.a read-only kit refuses a study write and writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStudyFileTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStudyFileTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.recording a study snapshots and pins its opened material versions, then writes its file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests.a read-only kit records no study", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.studyFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.libraryReferences", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.SchemaValidation.validateStudyFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.StudyFile.fileText", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitFileText.parseStudyFile", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.writeStudy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitProxy.readStudies", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Storage.KitContentFiles.KitLibraryContext.recordStudy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-FILE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 360, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [359], "how_to": "AddExperimentsToStudy's pure half (001 §P `AddExperimentsToStudy`; 001 §L 'a named set of experiments inside ONE kit'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. On `Study` in `Studies.fs`: `member this.withExperiments (names : ExperimentName list) (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`. It answers `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming the first name no kit experiment has, and changes nothing then; otherwise the study whose experiments are its own, in place, followed by each given name it does not hold yet, in the given order and each once. Every other field is unchanged: a study's scopes, links and gain settings name parameters and sessions, not the experiment list. No removal member is added; disabling an experiment is step 365's. Tests, in `StudyTests` (step 358): `adding experiments appends the new ones in order and keeps those the study holds`: a study of [E2] given [E3; E2; E1; E3] answers [E2; E3; E1], its other fields equal; `adding an experiment the kit lacks changes nothing`: given [E1; E9] it answers `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` naming E9.", "acceptance": "After AddExperimentsToStudy's pure half lands, `Study.withExperiments` MUST append the names the study lacks in order, each once, and refuse a name the kit lacks with nothing changed; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `adding experiments appends the new ones in order and keeps those the study holds` and `adding an experiment the kit lacks changes nothing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.adding experiments appends the new ones in order and keeps those the study holds", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-ADD-EXPERIMENTS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.adding an experiment the kit lacks changes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-ADD-EXPERIMENTS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withExperiments", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-ADD-EXPERIMENTS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 361, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [360], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests"], "how_to": "A study opens a material version into a working copy whose every component is a parameter, generated from the material's crystal record, shared by every sample made of it (001 §I 'Material parameters as unknowns: a study OPENS a material version, which creates a study-local working copy, stored in the study file, with `Unknown` components; every sample made of it shares them (`MaterialScope`)'; 001 §N 'Parameter-axis generation: … publishes its `ParameterAxis` list. Case 1b's generated axes equal `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` — an exact test'; 001 §P `OpenMaterial`; the S11.1 brief 'Generated axes', 'the EXACT test'; .spec-md §3.16 'its generated axes are that record's `axes`'). A complexity tree publishes no parameter axis in this spec: its eps is formula, table or constant data the ladder edits, so a material is fitted through its crystal-parameter form (step 355). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after step 360's member: (1) `type ParameterAxis<'Parameters> with member this.parameterValueOf (p : 'Parameters) : ParameterValue` (`this.read p` as a `ParameterValue`, the one conversion from an axis read to a parameter's number) and `member this.writeValue (value : ParameterValue) (p : 'Parameters) : 'Parameters` (`this.write value.value p`, the one conversion back). (2) `type CrystalParameters with member this.parameterAxes : ParameterAxis<CrystalParameters> list`: the axes of its record (`UniaxialParameters.axes`, `TriclinicParameters.axes` or `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes`, step 353) in their order, each lifted onto the crystal by a private helper per case: the same `name` and the same field case (`RefractionIndexField`, `RhoValueField`, `EpsValueField`), its access reading the record of a crystal of the same case and writing back a crystal of that case; a crystal of another case reads as `this` reads and is written back unchanged, because the axes are generated from `this` and a study applies them to its own working copy only. The list is generated, never hand-written. (3) On `OpenedMaterial` (step 358): `static member openFrom (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<OpenedMaterial, StudyError>`, for a `CrystalParameterPhysics crystal` the working copy `{ version; name = entry.name; crystal; parameters }` whose parameters are, per generated axis in order, `{ name = axis.name; state = KnownParameter (axis.parameterValueOf crystal) }`, and for a `ComplexityPhysics` `MaterialWithoutParametersErr` naming the entry; `member this.withParameterState (name : ParameterName) (state : ParameterState) : Result<OpenedMaterial, StudyError>`, `UnknownStudyParameterErr` naming the material and the name when no component has it, `InvalidStudyParameterErr` carrying the `ItemError.describe` of `{ name = name; state = state }.validate` (step 221) when the state breaks its rules, and otherwise that component's state replaced in place (freeing a component is its `UnknownParameter` state, 001 §I); and `member this.currentCrystal : CrystalParameters`, the crystal with each component written through its generated axis at its parameter's current number (a known or calibrated value, an unknown's start), in order. (4) On `Study`: `member this.openMaterial (version : MaterialVersionId) (entry : MaterialEntry) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr` naming the version when `materials` holds it, `openFrom`'s error passing through, and otherwise the study with the working copy appended; `member this.withMaterialParameterState (version : MaterialVersionId) (name : ParameterName) (state : ParameterState) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, `UnknownStudyMaterialErr` naming the version when it is not opened, and otherwise its copy's `withParameterState` in place. (5) `type Sample with member this.openedMaterialsIn (study : Study) : OpenedMaterial list`: the study's working copies whose version the sample's `structure.referencedMaterialVersions` (step 61) holds, in study order, so every sample made of an opened material reads the same copy (`MaterialScope`); the forward model reads it (S11.2). `StudyError` gains `MaterialWithoutParametersErr` (`the material publishes no parameter to fit: <reason>`), `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr` (`the study already opens that material version: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyMaterialErr` (`the study opens no such material version: <reason>`), `UnknownStudyParameterErr` (`the study has no such parameter: <reason>`) and `InvalidStudyParameterErr` (`the parameter state is not valid: <reason>`). No cache, conversion or other member is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs`, `module StudyMaterialTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over test-local entries of each crystal case (fifteen distinct literal values for the absorbing probe) and a test-local `MaterialVersionId`: `the generated axes of an opened absorbing triclinic material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` (the exact test): the opened copy's `crystal.parameterAxes` has the fifteen names of `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` in its order and the same field case at each position; at each position the generated read of `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal probe` equals the record axis's read of `probe` exactly, and the generated write of 2.5 times that value answers `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal` of the record axis's write of it; and the copy's parameters are those fifteen names, each `KnownParameter` at the probe's value; `an opened uniaxial or triclinic material generates its record's axes the same way`: the same over a uniaxial (4 axes) and a triclinic (9) entry; `a material whose physics is a complexity tree, or one opened twice, is refused`: a constant isotropic complexity entry answers `MaterialWithoutParametersErr`, and opening the absorbing version twice `MaterialAlreadyOpenErr`; `freeing a component makes it an unknown in place, and the working copy's crystal reads each parameter's current value`: setting `n3` to an `UnknownParameter` starting at 1.70 within [1.60, 1.80] changes that parameter in place, the copy's `currentCrystal` reading index3 1.70 and every other field the probe's; a name the copy lacks answers `UnknownStudyParameterErr` and reversed bounds `InvalidStudyParameterErr`, the study unchanged; `every sample made of an opened material shares its working copy`: a plate sample whose substrate is the opened version and a film sample whose `Repeated` cell names it each answer [the copy], and a sample of another version answers []. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the five new cases.", "acceptance": "After OpenMaterial's pure half lands, `OpenedMaterial.openFrom` MUST turn a crystal-parameter version into a working copy whose parameters follow the record's generated axes, refusing a complexity tree, and the generated axes of an opened `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters` material MUST equal `AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes` in names, order, field kinds and read / write on a probe; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the generated axes of an opened absorbing triclinic material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes`, `an opened uniaxial or triclinic material generates its record's axes the same way`, `a material whose physics is a complexity tree, or one opened twice, is refused`, `freeing a component makes it an unknown in place, and the working copy's crystal reads each parameter's current value` and `every sample made of an opened material shares its working copy`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.the generated axes of an opened absorbing triclinic material equal AbsorbingTriclinicParameters.axes", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.an opened uniaxial or triclinic material generates its record's axes the same way", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.a material whose physics is a complexity tree, or one opened twice, is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.freeing a component makes it an unknown in place, and the working copy's crystal reads each parameter's current value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests.every sample made of an opened material shares its working copy", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMaterialTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMaterialTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ParameterAxis.parameterValueOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ParameterAxis.writeValue", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.CrystalParameters.parameterAxes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.OpenedMaterial.openFrom", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.OpenedMaterial.withParameterState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.OpenedMaterial.currentCrystal", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.openMaterial", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withMaterialParameterState", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Sample.openedMaterialsIn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-OPEN-MATERIAL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 362, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [361], "how_to": "The study's unknowns, each with its scope, and the owners each scope gives it (001 §L 'the unknowns (owner + scope)' and the scope table: ItemScope 'One value for every experiment using the item', MaterialScope 'One value for every sample of an opened material', SessionScope 'One value per session block (gain)', ExperimentScope 'One value per run'; 001 §I 'Intensity detector | Gain (session-scoped)'; the S11.1 brief 'each with an owner (item / material / session / experiment) and a scope'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, after step 361's members: (1) `UnknownOwner` = `ItemOwner of ItemId` | `MaterialOwner of MaterialVersionId` | `SessionOwner of SessionName` | `ExperimentOwner of ExperimentName`: what holds one value of an unknown; it is derived and never stored, so it carries no tag. (2) `StudyUnknown = { parameter : StudyParameterRef; scope : ParameterScope; unknown : UnknownParameterData }` (step 221's start, bounds and prior). (3) `type Study with member this.scopeOf (parameter : StudyParameterRef) : ParameterScope`: the study's `ScopedParameter` for it, or the default: `MaterialScope` for a material component, `SessionBlockScope` for an item parameter named `gain` (the one `IntensityDetectorModel` publishes, step 215), `ItemScope` for every other item parameter. (4) `member this.unknownsWith (used : Item list) : StudyUnknown list`: for each item of `used` in order, each of its parameters whose state is `UnknownParameter`, then for each opened material in order each component whose state is `UnknownParameter`, each with `scopeOf`; a parameter that is a link's follower is left out, because it takes its leader's value (001 §L). `used` is the items the study's experiments use (`Experiment.itemsUsedBy`, step 261), which the caller passes. (5) `type StudyUnknown with member this.owners (sessions : StudySession list) (users : ExperimentName list) : UnknownOwner list`: under `ItemScope` or `MaterialScope` its one owner, the `ItemOwner` of its item or the `MaterialOwner` of its material; under `SessionBlockScope` one `SessionOwner` per session holding a user, in session order; under `ExperimentScope` one `ExperimentOwner` per user, in order. `users` is the enabled experiments of the study whose setups use the unknown's item or a sample made of its material, which the forward model knows (S11.2). The fitter's vector holds one value per owner of each unknown (S11.2-S11.3). No other type or member is added. Tests, in `StudyTests`, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 223) over the built-in circular-polarizer and intensity-detector models: CPL1 with `c2.retardance` unknown, CPL2 with `c2.retardance` and `c2.fastAxisOffset` unknown, a Phone with `gain` unknown, and an opened absorbing material with `n1` and `e11` unknown: `the study's unknowns are its items' and opened materials' unknown parameters, with their scopes, leaving out link followers`: `unknownsWith [ CPL1; CPL2; Phone ]` answers CPL1 `c2.retardance` (ItemScope), CPL2's two (ItemScope), Phone `gain` (SessionBlockScope), `n1` and `e11` (MaterialScope), in that order; with a `ScopedParameter` making CPL1's `ExperimentScope` it answers that scope; with a link (a record literal) whose follower is CPL2's `c2.retardance` that parameter is left out. `an unknown's owners are its item or material, one per session holding a user, or one per user`: over sessions `Session 1` [E1; E2] and `Session 2` [E3], CPL1's unknown has the one `ItemOwner`, `n1` the one `MaterialOwner`, Phone's `gain` with users [E1; E3] `SessionOwner` of both sessions and with users [E2] only `Session 1`, and an `ExperimentScope` unknown with users [E3; E1] the owners E3 then E1.", "acceptance": "After the unknowns land, `Study.unknownsWith` MUST list the used items' and opened materials' unknown parameters with their scopes (a detector's `gain` session-scoped by default) and leave out link followers, and `StudyUnknown.owners` MUST give one owner per item or material, per session holding a user, or per user; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the study's unknowns are its items' and opened materials' unknown parameters, with their scopes, leaving out link followers` and `an unknown's owners are its item or material, one per session holding a user, or one per user`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.the study's unknowns are its items' and opened materials' unknown parameters, with their scopes, leaving out link followers", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.an unknown's owners are its item or material, one per session holding a user, or one per user", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.UnknownOwner", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyUnknown", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.scopeOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.unknownsWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyUnknown.owners", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-UNKNOWNS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 363, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [362], "how_to": "SetParameterScope's pure half (001 §P `SetParameterScope`; 001 §L 'Scope is the sharing rule'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. On `Study` in `Studies.fs`: `member this.withParameterScope (scoped : ScopedParameter) (used : Item list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`. It refuses, changing nothing: a parameter the study does not have, an item parameter of no item of `used` holding that name (`Item.tryFindParameter`, step 222) or a material component of no opened copy, with `UnknownStudyParameterErr` naming its `describe`; a scope its kind does not take, with `ScopeNotAllowedErr` naming the parameter and the scope's `text`: an item parameter takes `ItemScope`, `SessionBlockScope` or `ExperimentScope`, and a material component `MaterialScope` only, because 'One value for every sample of an opened material' is a material's sharing rule; and a parameter that is a link's follower or leader, with `ScopeNotAllowedErr` naming the link, so a link always joins parameters of one scope (step 364). Otherwise it answers the study whose `scopes` hold the given entry in place of that parameter's earlier one, or appended. Every other field is unchanged. `StudyError` gains `ScopeNotAllowedErr` (`the parameter cannot take that scope: <reason>`). Tests, in `StudyTests`, over step 362's items and opened material: `setting a parameter's scope replaces its entry in place or adds it, and the default applies until then`: Phone `gain` set to `ExperimentScope` appends its entry and `scopeOf` answers it; set again to `ItemScope` it replaces the entry in place, the list still one long; CPL1's `c2.retardance` answers `ItemScope` before any entry. `a scope is refused for a parameter the study does not use, for a linked parameter, and MaterialScope fits a material component only`: a parameter of an item outside `used`, a name CPL1 lacks, CPL1's `c2.retardance` under `MaterialScope`, `n1` under `ItemScope` and, in a study holding a test-local link (a record literal) whose follower is CPL2's `c2.retardance`, that parameter under `ExperimentScope` each answer their error, the study unchanged. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case.", "acceptance": "After SetParameterScope's pure half lands, `Study.withParameterScope` MUST replace or add a parameter's scope entry, and MUST refuse a parameter the study does not use, a linked parameter and a scope the parameter's kind does not take; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `setting a parameter's scope replaces its entry in place or adds it, and the default applies until then` and `a scope is refused for a parameter the study does not use, for a linked parameter, and MaterialScope fits a material component only`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.setting a parameter's scope replaces its entry in place or adds it, and the default applies until then", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SET-SCOPE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a scope is refused for a parameter the study does not use, for a linked parameter, and MaterialScope fits a material component only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SET-SCOPE"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SET-SCOPE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withParameterScope", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SET-SCOPE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SET-SCOPE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 364, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [363], "how_to": "LinkParameters' pure half (001 §L 'Explicit links (\"CPL2.δ = CPL1.δ\") are constraints'; 001 §P `LinkParameters`). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. On `Study` in `Studies.fs`: `member this.withLink (link : ParameterLink) (used : Item list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`. It refuses, changing nothing: either parameter the study does not have (step 363's rule), with `UnknownStudyParameterErr` naming it; and, with `InvalidParameterLinkErr` naming both `describe`s and the broken rule, a follower equal to its leader, a follower that already follows or leads a link, a leader that follows a link (no chain, so every follower reads its leader directly), and two parameters whose `scopeOf` (step 362) differ, because a link equates one value per owner. Otherwise it answers the study with the link appended; nothing else changes. No unlink member is added. `StudyError` gains `InvalidParameterLinkErr` (`the link is not valid: <reason>`). Tests, in `StudyTests`, over step 362's items: `linking CPL2's retardance to CPL1's makes it follow and leaves it out of the unknowns`: linking CPL2's `c2.retardance` (follower) to CPL1's (leader) appends the link, and `unknownsWith` then lists CPL1's retardance and leaves CPL2's out. `a link to itself, a chain, a second link of one follower, a missing parameter or differing scopes is refused`: CPL1's retardance linked to itself; then, with that first link held, CPL1's `c2.retardance` following CPL2's `c2.fastAxisOffset` (a leader made a follower), CPL2's `c2.fastAxisOffset` following CPL2's `c2.retardance` (a chain through a follower), CPL2's retardance following CPL2's `c2.fastAxisOffset` (a second link of one follower), a name CPL1 lacks, and CPL2's `c2.fastAxisOffset` following Phone's `gain` (`ItemScope` against `SessionBlockScope`) each answer their error, the study unchanged. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case.", "acceptance": "After LinkParameters' pure half lands, `Study.withLink` MUST append a link between two parameters of one scope and MUST refuse a self link, a chain, a second link of a follower, a missing parameter and differing scopes; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `linking CPL2's retardance to CPL1's makes it follow and leaves it out of the unknowns` and `a link to itself, a chain, a second link of one follower, a missing parameter or differing scopes is refused`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.linking CPL2's retardance to CPL1's makes it follow and leaves it out of the unknowns", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a link to itself, a chain, a second link of one follower, a missing parameter or differing scopes is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withLink", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-LINKS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 365, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [364], "how_to": "A study's per-session gain models, fit settings, weights, enablement and notes, as pure updates (the S11.1 brief 'Per session a gain model …', 'Fit settings (joint / staged, S11.3), weights per experiment or per detector, enable / disable per experiment, and notes'; 001 §L 'Weights and ablation'; 001 §E notes). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`: (1) `ExperimentEnablement` = `EnabledInStudy` | `DisabledInStudy`, a two-case union in place of a flag; it is not stored, the study keeps its `disabled` list. (2) On `Study`, each refusal changing nothing: `member this.withSessionGainModel (session : SessionName) (model : SessionGainModel) (kitExperiments : Experiment list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`: `UnknownStudySessionErr` naming the session when `sessionsIn kitExperiments` (step 358) holds none of that name, `GainAnchorOutsideSessionErr` naming the run when an anchor or a repeat is no experiment of that session, and otherwise the setting replaced in place or appended; `member this.withFitMode (mode : FitMode) : Study`; `member this.withExperimentWeight (experiment : ExperimentName) (weight : ResidualWeight) : Result<Study, StudyError>` and `member this.withExperimentEnablement (experiment : ExperimentName) (enablement : ExperimentEnablement) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, each `UnknownStudyExperimentErr` for an experiment the study does not hold; the weight replaced in place or appended; `DisabledInStudy` adding the name to `disabled` once and `EnabledInStudy` removing it; `member this.withDetectorWeight (detector : ItemId) (weight : ResidualWeight) (used : Item list) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, `UnknownStudyItemErr` for an item outside `used`, else replaced or appended; `member this.withNotes (notes : StudyNotes) : Study`. (3) `member this.enabledExperiments : ExperimentName list`, the study's experiments without the disabled ones, in order; and `member this.residualWeightOf (experiment : ExperimentName) (detector : ItemId) : ResidualWeight`, the experiment's weight times the detector's, each `ResidualWeight.unit` when unset, the weight the residual rows of that experiment take (S11.2). `StudyError` gains `UnknownStudySessionErr` (`the study has no such session: <reason>`), `GainAnchorOutsideSessionErr` (`the AIR run is not in that session: <reason>`) and `UnknownStudyItemErr` (`the study uses no such item: <reason>`). No threshold or other setting is added. Tests, in `StudyTests`, over a study of E1, E2, D1 (Diagnostic) and E3 and step 362's items: `a session's gain model is set for a session of the study, anchored within it`: `Session 1`'s model set to `AnchoredSessionGain [ E2 ]`, then to `InterpolatedSessionGain { opening = E1; closing = E2 }`, leaves one setting holding the second, and `gainModelOf` answers it while `Session 2`'s stays `FreeSessionGain`; `fit mode, weights, enablement and notes are set in place, and an unset weight reads one`: `StagedFit`, an experiment weight of 2 on E1 set twice (the second 4), a detector weight of 0.5 on the Phone, E2 disabled twice then enabled, E3 disabled, and notes give one weight entry of 4, `residualWeightOf E1 Phone` 2, `residualWeightOf E3 CPL1` 1, `enabledExperiments` [E1; E2; D1] and the notes; `a setting naming an experiment, item or session the study lacks is refused`: a session `Day 9`, an anchor E3 for `Session 1`, a weight or enablement for E9 and a detector weight for an item outside `used` each answer their error, the study unchanged. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases.", "acceptance": "After the settings land, a study MUST set a session's gain model only for a session it has with anchors inside it, set its fit mode, weights, enablement and notes in place, and answer `enabledExperiments` and `residualWeightOf`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a session's gain model is set for a session of the study, anchored within it`, `fit mode, weights, enablement and notes are set in place, and an unset weight reads one` and `a setting naming an experiment, item or session the study lacks is refused`, the count rising by 3, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a session's gain model is set for a session of the study, anchored within it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.fit mode, weights, enablement and notes are set in place, and an unset weight reads one", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests.a setting naming an experiment, item or session the study lacks is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.ExperimentEnablement", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withSessionGainModel", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withFitMode", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withExperimentWeight", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withExperimentEnablement", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withDetectorWeight", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.withNotes", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.enabledExperiments", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.Study.residualWeightOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-SETTINGS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 366, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S111n", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [365], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests"], "how_to": "The five study messages as one semantic union with a pure update over what logic receives, tested over in-memory kits (001 §P 'Every user step is a semantic message: … `CreateStudy`, `AddExperimentsToStudy`, `OpenMaterial`, `SetParameterScope`, `LinkParameters` … The same messages back the buttons, so tests drive by meaning'; 001 §P 'Logic receives a `KitContext`'; the S11.1 brief 'The messages are pure updates, with tests over in-memory kits'; .spec-md §4 'Every user step is a semantic Elmish message. The button and the test send the same message'). The study view that sends them is S11.5's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.1. In `Studies.fs`, last: (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyContext = { studies : Study list; experiments : Experiment list; setups : Setup list; items : Item list; resolveMaterial : MaterialVersionId -> Result<MaterialEntry, StudyError> }`, the kit's studies, experiments, setups and items as the window last read them and the library's resolution of a material version (the `*Context` convention; the composer maps its store's failure to `MaterialUnavailableErr`), with `member this.itemsUsedBy (study : Study) : Item list`, `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` (step 261) of the study's experiments as `experiments` holds them, over `setups` and `items`. (2) `StudyMsg` = `CreateStudy of name : StudyName * experiments : ExperimentName list` | `AddExperimentsToStudy of study : StudyName * experiments : ExperimentName list` | `OpenMaterial of study : StudyName * material : MaterialVersionId` | `SetParameterScope of study : StudyName * scoped : ScopedParameter` | `LinkParameters of study : StudyName * link : ParameterLink`, each case documented. (3) `member this.applyTo (context : StudyContext) : Result<Study, StudyError>`, the study the message creates or changes: `CreateStudy` is `Study.create` over `context.studies` and `context.experiments` (step 358); every other case finds its study in `context.studies` by name, `UnknownStudyErr` naming it when none has it, then answers `withExperiments` (step 360), `openMaterial` of `context.resolveMaterial`'s entry (step 361), `withParameterScope` or `withLink` over `context.itemsUsedBy` of the study (steps 363, 364). A refusal answers its error and changes nothing. The caller records the answered study through `KitLibraryContext.recordStudy` (step 359) and replaces it in its list. `StudyError` gains `UnknownStudyErr` (`the kit has no such study: <reason>`) and `MaterialUnavailableErr` (`the material version could not be read: <reason>`). No other message, field or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs`, `module StudyMessageTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Each fact builds an in-memory kit as `KitLibraryTests` does (step 139): `KitProxy.createInMemory`, `KitContext.openKit` read-write with a stepping clock and a `KitLibraryContext` over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`'s import seam; it records step 362's CPL1, CPL2 and Phone through `recordItem` (step 228), one setup holding them through `recordSetup` (step 260) and E1, E2 and E3 over it through `recordExperiment`, and saves a user absorbing crystal material through the set's `materials.saveMaterial`; the context's lists are what the kit reads back, and `resolveMaterial` reads `materials.resolveVersion`, `Ok None` and `Error _` answering `MaterialUnavailableErr`. Each answered study is recorded through `recordStudy`. `CreateStudy and AddExperimentsToStudy write the study file over the kit's experiments`: `CreateStudy (QZ-LR, [ E1 ])`, then `AddExperimentsToStudy (QZ-LR, [ E2; E1 ])` over the refreshed list, leave `readStudies` answering `QZ-LR` over [E1; E2]. `OpenMaterial snapshots the material version into the kit and stores its working copy in the study file`: `OpenMaterial (QZ-LR, <its version>)` leaves `paths` holding `library/<its GUID>@v1.material-json` and `readStudies`' study holding the working copy with its fifteen known parameters. `SetParameterScope and LinkParameters change the stored study`: `SetParameterScope (QZ-LR, Phone gain → ExperimentScope)` and `LinkParameters (QZ-LR, CPL2 c2.retardance → CPL1 c2.retardance)` leave the read-back study holding that scope entry and that link. `a refused study message records nothing`: `AddExperimentsToStudy (LR, [ E1 ])` with no study `LR` answers `UnknownStudyErr`, `OpenMaterial` of a version the library lacks `MaterialUnavailableErr`, and `paths` and every file's bytes are unchanged. `StudySessionTests`' `every study error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After the study messages land, `StudyMsg` MUST hold `CreateStudy`, `AddExperimentsToStudy`, `OpenMaterial`, `SetParameterScope` and `LinkParameters`, and `StudyMsg.applyTo` MUST answer the created or changed study through the pure updates, or a typed refusal that changes nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `CreateStudy and AddExperimentsToStudy write the study file over the kit's experiments`, `OpenMaterial snapshots the material version into the kit and stores its working copy in the study file`, `SetParameterScope and LinkParameters change the stored study` and `a refused study message records nothing`, the count rising by 4, and the widened `every study error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s36 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.CreateStudy and AddExperimentsToStudy write the study file over the kit's experiments", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.OpenMaterial snapshots the material version into the kit and stores its working copy in the study file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.SetParameterScope and LinkParameters change the stored study", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests.a refused study message records nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyMessageTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyMessageTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudySessionTests.every study error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudySessionTests.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyContext.itemsUsedBy", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyMsg.applyTo", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Studies.StudyError", "op": "change_shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Studies.fs", "obligations": ["S111-STUDY-MESSAGES"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.1 -- Studies: unknowns, scopes, links, sessions and opened materials"}
{"number": 367, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [366], "how_to": "The forward model of an experiment (001 §N 'The forward model of an experiment = slots + scan point + parameters → predicted reading') evaluates a RECORDED setup in Domain, and three rules it needs live today inside the table's run in the UI, so they MOVE into Domain and the table calls them (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). Nothing the table draws, lays out or runs changes. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs`, after `layout` (`BeamLayout.fs:layout`): `type PlacedElement with member this.incidenceOn (placement : ElementPlacement) : IncidenceAngle`, the body of the private extension `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:incidenceOn` moved verbatim (the angle between the element's drawn face normal, `r1Axis (RayModel.orientedToBeam d placement)`, and its arriving beam `d`, capped at `Propagation.r2SweepMaxDegrees`, and 0° for the root, which has no arriving beam), its doc kept with spec 0046 and spec 0050 S11.2 cited; and `type BeamTree.BeamBranch with member this.propagationBranch : Propagation.Branch`: `TransmittedBeam` is `BranchTransmitted` and `ReflectedBeam` `BranchReflected` (`Propagation.fs:Branch`), the mapping `chartForRun` writes inline today. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs`, after `SetupSlot.inLightOrder` (step 257): `type SetupSlot with static member boundSourceIn (slots : SetupSlot list) (library : LibraryProxy) : SourcePreset option`, the body of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:boundSource` moved: in slot order, the first `LightSource` slot whose `placement.valueId` `library.tryGetEntry` answers as a `SourceItem`, that preset; `None` when no slot does. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs`, after `read`: `type Library.SourcePreset with static member operatingWaveLengthOf (sourceOpt : SourcePreset option) (requested : WaveLength option) : WaveLength`, the body of `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:operatingWaveLength` moved: a `TunableBetween` source's `requested` wavelength clamped to its limits, or its own wavelength when nothing is requested; a `FixedLine` source's own wavelength whatever is requested; 600 nm without a source. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the private `incidenceOn` extension is deleted and `chartForRun` calls the Domain member on the same placed element; `chartForRun`'s inline branch match becomes `step.branch.propagationBranch`; `model.boundSource` is `SetupSlot.boundSourceIn model.elements model.library`; and `operatingWaveLength model requested` is `SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf model.boundSource requested`. Their docs say in one line that the rule is Domain's. No other UI line changes, so every chart, caption and status is as it was. Tests. In `BeamLayoutTests`, `the drawn incidence is the angle between an element's drawn face normal and its arriving beam`: over elements laid out by `BeamLayout.layout` from the file's own placement helper on the main beam, a sample at R2 30° meets its beam at 30°, an untilted one at 0°, the root answers 0°, and a sample at R2 89.5° is capped at 89°, each within 1e-9; and `TransmittedBeam.propagationBranch` is `BranchTransmitted` and `ReflectedBeam.propagationBranch` `BranchReflected`. In `SetupTests` (step 256), `the bound source is the first light-source slot bound to a source preset`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()` and the file's slot fixtures, the slots [an unbound source; a source bound to the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` preset; a source bound to `PresetIds.heNe633`] answer the HeNe preset, and slots with no bound source answer `None`. In `ExperimentRunTests`, `the run's wavelength is a tunable source's clamped request, a fixed line's own, or 600 nm without a source`: the HeNe preset with its tuning set to `TunableBetween` limits of 400 nm and 700 nm (a record copy) answers 500 nm for a request of 500 nm, 700 nm for 900 nm, 400 nm for 300 nm and its own wavelength for `None`; the HeNe preset as it is answers 632.8 nm whatever is requested; `None` answers 600 nm.", "acceptance": "After the move, `PlacedElement.incidenceOn`, `BeamBranch.propagationBranch`, `SetupSlot.boundSourceIn` and `SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf` MUST be declared in Domain, and `chartForRun`, `boundSource` and `operatingWaveLength` MUST call them with no copy left in the UI; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the drawn incidence is the angle between an element's drawn face normal and its arriving beam`, `the bound source is the first light-source slot bound to a source preset` and `the run's wavelength is a tunable source's clamped request, a fixed line's own, or 600 nm without a source`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, every chart unchanged and the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests.the drawn incidence is the angle between an element's drawn face normal and its arriving beam", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/BeamLayoutTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.BeamLayoutTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests.the bound source is the first light-source slot bound to a source preset", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SetupTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.the run's wavelength is a tunable source's clamped request, a fixed line's own, or 600 nm without a source", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.BeamLayout.PlacedElement.incidenceOn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.BeamLayout.BeamBranch.propagationBranch", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/BeamLayout.fs", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.Setups.SetupSlot.boundSourceIn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Setups.fs", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.incidenceOn", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.boundSource", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.operatingWaveLength", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-RUN-GEOMETRY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 368, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [367], "how_to": "The second half of the run rules the forward model needs: how a slot binds for a run and what the source emits, written today inside `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun` (steps 252 and 265) and `model.runEmission` (step 266), MOVE into Domain and the table calls them (001 §N 'One item-model evaluator'; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move'; step 251: `boundWith` is 'the door S8.2's slots and S11.2's forward model call'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs`, which opens `Setups`, after `ItemModelChoice.boundWith` (step 251): (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] SlotRunParam = { library : LibraryProxy; materials : MaterialProxy; items : Item list; choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option; valuesOf : Item -> ParameterValues }`: the library a bare slot is bound in, the material store a stack sample resolves through (`MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialProxy`), the kit's items, an item's model as the window's stores resolve it (`model.tryItemModelChoice`, step 263) and the numbers an item is evaluated with. (2) `SlotRunError`, an `*Error` union: `SlotItemErr of error : SetupError` | `SlotEvaluationErr of error : ItemEvaluationError`, with `member this.describe : string` answering the inner error's `describe` unchanged. (3) `type SetupSlot with member this.runElementWith (param : SlotRunParam) : Result<BoundOpticalElement option, SlotRunError>`, the binding `chartForRun` does once per path step today, by the slot's `placement.catalogueKind`: a `LightSource`, `Detector`, `Lens`, `FlatMirror` or `CurvedMirror` slot answers `Ok None` (a source emits, a detector reads, and a mirror or a lens only steers the ray, as the run law has always treated them); a `LinearPolarizer`, `CircularPolarizer` or `Sample` slot holding `ItemInSlot (id, _)` takes the item of that id in `param.items`, else `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the id, then its `param.choiceOf`, else `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the item's label and that its model is not in the library, then `choice.boundWith param.materials (param.valuesOf item)` (step 251), its error as `SlotEvaluationErr`; such a slot of `EmptySlotContent` is its library binding: a polarizer slot bound to a `PolarizerItem p` is `BoundPolarizerPreset p.behavior`, a sample slot bound to a `SampleItem s` is `BoundOpticalElement.ofStackSample param.materials (ParameterValues.defaultsOf s.parameterAxes) s` (step 252), and an unbound slot, any other entry or a binding `library.tryGetEntry` does not answer (`Ok None` or `Error`) is `Ok None`, as today. The reasons are the ones `chartForRun` gives today (steps 263, 265). `member this.runStepOf (mueller : MuellerMatrix) : ExperimentRun.RunStep`: an `ObjectStep` for a `Sample` slot and an `ElementStep` for any other (step 265). `static member runEmissionOf (slots : SetupSlot list) (param : SlotRunParam) : Result<SourceEmission, SlotRunError>`, `model.runEmission`'s rule (step 266): the first `LightSource` slot holding an item emits `choice.emissionWith (param.valuesOf item)` (step 246), the item and its model found as above and an evaluation error answered as `SlotEvaluationErr`; without such a slot, `SourceEmission.ofValues (ParameterValues.defaultsOf SourcePreset.lightSourceAxes)` (step 252's default). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `chartForRun` binds each path step's slot through `slot.runElementWith` over `{ library = model.library; materials = model.materials; items = model.kitItems; choiceOf = model.tryItemModelChoice; valuesOf = fun item -> ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters }` and makes each evaluated matrix its step through `slot.runStepOf`; `model.runEmission` is `SetupSlot.runEmissionOf model.elements` over the same param, its error's `describe` as its `ControlCaption`. The failure charts keep their texts: `SlotEvaluationErr (SampleMaterialErr e)` shows `Sample materials failed to resolve` with `e.runFailureCaption`, every other error `The run cannot be evaluated` with its `describe`. The inline bindings are deleted, so one rule binds a slot, and every chart's numbers and texts are unchanged. Tests, in `ItemEvaluationTests` (step 245), with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])` and `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, over slots built as `SetupTests`' fixtures build them (step 256) and items made by `ItemDraft` (step 223): `a slot runs as its item through the given values, else as its library binding, and a source, detector, mirror or lens slot is no run element`: a linear-polarizer slot bound to `PresetIds.polarizerLp` with no item binds its `BoundPolarizerPreset`; the same slot holding a real-LP item (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`) whose `valuesOf` answers an `extinctionRatio` of 0.01 evaluates at 0° and 600 nm to `BoundOpticalElement.ofOpticalForm` of those values, within 1e-12; a sample slot bound to `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` evaluates as `ofStackSample` at its defaults; a source, a detector and a flat-mirror slot answer `Ok None`; and `runStepOf` makes an `ObjectStep` of the sample slot and an `ElementStep` of the polarizer. `a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve answers SlotItemErr`: a polarizer slot holding an item id outside `items`, and one holding an item whose `choiceOf` answers `None`, each answer `SlotItemErr` of `UnknownSlotItemErr`. `the run's source emits its item's state through the given values, and the default set without a source item`: a source slot holding a HeNe item (`BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633`) whose `valuesOf` answers a degree of polarization 1 at azimuth 30° emits that `SourceEmission`; slots with no source item emit the default emission; and a `degreeOfPolarization` of 1.5 answers `SlotEvaluationErr` of `ParameterOutOfRangeErr`.", "acceptance": "After the move, `SetupSlot.runElementWith`, `runStepOf` and `runEmissionOf` MUST bind a slot and emit the source in Domain, and `chartForRun` and `model.runEmission` MUST call them with no inline binding left; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot runs as its item through the given values, else as its library binding, and a source, detector, mirror or lens slot is no run element`, `a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve answers SlotItemErr` and `the run's source emits its item's state through the given values, and the default set without a source item`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, every chart unchanged and the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a slot runs as its item through the given values, else as its library binding, and a source, detector, mirror or lens slot is no run element", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.a slot whose item the kit lacks or whose model does not resolve answers SlotItemErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests.the run's source emits its item's state through the given values, and the default set without a source item", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemEvaluationTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemEvaluationTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SlotRunParam", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SlotRunError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SetupSlot.runElementWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SetupSlot.runStepOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation.SetupSlot.runEmissionOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemEvaluation.fs", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.chartForRun", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.TableAndElementRotationView.TableAndElementRotationModel.runEmission", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-SLOT-RUN"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 369, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [368], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests"], "how_to": "The study's pre-fit checks are `SolverHandoffView`'s three checks, moved into Domain (001 §R '`SolverHandoffView`'s stub screen, replaced by the study view. Its three validation checks are reused as the study's pre-fit checks'; .spec-md §6 row 'Pre-fit checks'; the S11.2 brief 'SolverHandoffView calls the moved checks until S11.5 deletes it'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs`, `module PrefitChecks` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ExperimentMatrices.fs` (step 322), the last Domain file, because the checks read setups, experiments and the data seam: one `<Compile Include=\"PrefitChecks.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: an experiment's checks before a fit (spec 0050 S11.2; spec 0038 Part L). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In order: (a) `SlotSpecification` = `SpecifiedSlot` | `UnspecifiedSlot`, and `type SetupSlot with member this.specification : SlotSpecification`: specified when it holds an item or its placement is bound (`valueId`), the rule `SolverHandoffView.fs:unspecifiedElements` reads (step 261). (b) `PrefitError`, an `*Error` union: `UnspecifiedSlotsErr of reason : string` (a slot other than a sample's is unspecified, or the experiment's setup does not resolve), `MissingDataErr of reason : string` (no data is attached), `UnreadableDataErr of error : ExperimentDataError` (the attached file does not read through its profile: a `MalformedDataFileErr` or an `EmptyDataFileErr`, `MeasuredData.fs:ExperimentDataError`) and `InconsistentDataErr of error : ExperimentDataError` (its points do not fit the scan: a `DataRangeMismatchErr` or a `DataUnitsMismatchErr`), with `member this.describe : string`: `a slot is not specified: <reason>`, `no data is attached: <reason>`, `the data file does not read: <the error's reason>` and `the data does not fit the scan: <the error's reason>`. (c) `type Experiment with member this.prefitCheckWith (library : LibraryProxy) (dataProxy : ExperimentDataProxy) (setups : Setup list) : Result<MappedPoints, PrefitError>`, the three checks of `SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment` in order, each with the reason text the view gives today (steps 261, 291, 304): (1) `this.slotsIn setups` (step 261), a `SetupError` answering `UnspecifiedSlotsErr` of its `describe`, then the slots of `SetupSlot.inLightOrder` (step 257) that are not `Sample` slots and are `UnspecifiedSlot`, answering `UnspecifiedSlotsErr` naming their roles' `text`; (2) `this.dataOpt` of `None` answers `MissingDataErr`; (3) `ExperimentDataLoad.loadAndValidate library dataProxy slots this data` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`: read through the profile, the exclusions removed by `keptBy`, then `validatedFor`, steps 304 and 314), whose `Ok points` is answered as it is, the kept and validated points a fit reads, a `MalformedDataFileErr` or `EmptyDataFileErr` as `UnreadableDataErr` and a `DataRangeMismatchErr` or `DataUnitsMismatchErr` as `InconsistentDataErr`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs`: `validateExperiment` answers `experiment.prefitCheckWith library dataProxy setups` mapped onto the screen's `ExperimentHandoffStatus` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:ExperimentHandoffStatus`): `Ok points` is `HandoffReady points.pointCount`, `UnspecifiedSlotsErr r` `UnspecifiedElements` and `MissingDataErr r` `MissingDataFile`, each of its reason as a `ControlCaption`, `UnreadableDataErr e` `DataFileParseError e.caption` and `InconsistentDataErr e` `DataFileValidationError e.caption`; the private `unspecifiedElements` member is deleted and `handoffSetupCaption` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:handoffSetupCaption`) tags a slot through its `specification`. The status union stays the screen's display until S11.5 deletes the view. Every caption the screen shows is unchanged, so `SolverHandoffWindowTests` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`), which calls `validateExperiment`, runs with every fact and fixture as it is. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs`, `module PrefitCheckTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, setups made by `Setup.create` (step 256) of slots built as `SetupTests` builds them (a source bound to `PresetIds.heNe633`, a linear polarizer, a sample and a detector holding an intensity-detector item, `ItemModelIds.intensityDetectorModelId`), test-local experiments built as `StudySessionTests` builds them (step 357) with a `oneAxis` `VaryR1` scan of the polarizer over 0…90° in 4 points, and a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy` record whose `readMapped` answers by attachment path and whose other fields answer errors: `a slot other than a sample's must hold an item or a binding, and a setup the kit lacks is named`: with the polarizer slot empty, `UnspecifiedSlotsErr` whose reason names `Prep 1` and not `Obj 1`; with it holding a linear-polarizer item, the slot check passes although the sample is empty; an experiment whose setup is `'Missing' revision 1` answers `UnspecifiedSlotsErr` naming it. `an experiment without data fails the data check`: `dataOpt = None` answers `MissingDataErr`. `a data file that does not read is unreadable, and points outside the scan are inconsistent`: `readMapped` answering a `MalformedDataFileErr` or an `EmptyDataFileErr` answers `UnreadableDataErr` carrying it, and an intensity series holding x = 120 answers `InconsistentDataErr` of a `DataRangeMismatchErr`. `a ready experiment answers its kept, validated points`: a series at 0, 30, 60 and 90 with point 2 excluded (`PointExclusion`, step 313) answers `Ok` of the three points 0, 60 and 90. `every pre-fit error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct payload renders its text with it.", "acceptance": "After the move, `Experiment.prefitCheckWith` MUST run the three checks in Domain and answer the kept, validated points or a typed `PrefitError`, and `SolverHandoffView.validateExperiment` MUST call it with every caption unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a slot other than a sample's must hold an item or a binding, and a setup the kit lacks is named`, `an experiment without data fails the data check`, `a data file that does not read is unreadable, and points outside the scan are inconsistent`, `a ready experiment answers its kept, validated points` and `every pre-fit error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.a slot other than a sample's must hold an item or a binding, and a setup the kit lacks is named", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.an experiment without data fails the data check", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.a data file that does not read is unreadable, and points outside the scan are inconsistent", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.a ready experiment answers its kept, validated points", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.every pre-fit error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.SlotSpecification", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.SetupSlot.specification", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.PrefitError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.Experiment.prefitCheckWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SolverHandoffView.validateExperiment", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.SolverHandoffView.unspecifiedElements", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"], "preserves_obligations": ["S112-PREFIT-CHECKS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 370, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [369], "how_to": "Before a fit, an experiment's data is flagged when it changed since it was attached or since the last fit run read it (001 §E 'A changed or missing data file is flagged on open and before each fit (\"data changed since attach / since the last fit run\")'; the S11.2 brief 'Add S4.2's \"data changed since attach / since the last fit run\" flag'). The since-attach half is S4.2's check (`DataAttachment.statusAgainst`, step 132; `KitProxy.attachmentStatus`, step 134); the since-fit half compares the attachment with the attachments a fit run read, which S11.3's fit runs record. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `PrefitChecks.fs`, after `prefitCheckWith` (step 369): (1) `DataChangeFlag` = `DataUnchangedFlag` | `ChangedSinceAttachFlag of current : ContentHash` | `ChangedSinceFitFlag of current : ContentHash` | `MissingDataFileFlag`, with `member this.text : string`: `data unchanged`, `data changed since attach`, `data changed since the last fit run` and `data file missing`. It is derived, never stored, so it carries no tag. (2) `type MappedAttachment with member this.changeWith (status : DataAttachmentStatus) (fitted : DataAttachment list) : DataChangeFlag`, over the status S4.2's check answers for this attachment: `AttachedDataMissing` is `MissingDataFileFlag`; `AttachedDataChanged current` is `ChangedSinceAttachFlag current`; `AttachedDataUnchanged` is `ChangedSinceFitFlag` of `this.attachment.contentHash` when `fitted` holds an attachment of the same `path` whose `contentHash` differs, and `DataUnchangedFlag` otherwise. `fitted` is the attachments the study's last fit run read, empty before its first. No other member or option is added. Tests, in `PrefitCheckTests` (step 369), over test-local attachments and hashes: `a data file is flagged when it went missing, changed since attach, or changed since the last fit run read it`: `AttachedDataMissing` answers `MissingDataFileFlag`; `AttachedDataChanged h2` answers `ChangedSinceAttachFlag h2`, also when `fitted` holds the path at another hash; `AttachedDataUnchanged` with `fitted` empty, holding the path at the same hash or holding only other paths answers `DataUnchangedFlag`, and with `fitted` holding the path at another hash `ChangedSinceFitFlag` of the attachment's hash; and the four `text`s are as above.", "acceptance": "After the flag lands, `MappedAttachment.changeWith` MUST flag a missing file, a change since attach and a change since the last fit run, in that precedence; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a data file is flagged when it went missing, changed since attach, or changed since the last fit run read it`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests.a data file is flagged when it went missing, changed since attach, or changed since the last fit run read it", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PrefitCheckTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.PrefitCheckTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-DATA-CHANGE"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.DataChangeFlag", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-DATA-CHANGE"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.PrefitChecks.MappedAttachment.changeWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/PrefitChecks.fs", "obligations": ["S112-DATA-CHANGE"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 371, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [370], "actions": ["ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests"], "how_to": "What a detector records, and each measured point paired with what fixes its prediction (001 §K 'Observables: intensity, Ψ / Δ, full Mueller matrices (the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape, normalized + absolute throughput). A study mixes them'; step 304: '`ObservationPoints` pass as read, each observation carrying its own configuration, which the study pairs with the experiment (S11.2)'). (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs`, `module StudyForward` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `PrefitChecks.fs` (step 369), the last Domain file, because the forward model reads studies, setups, items, the evaluator and the data seam: one `<Compile Include=\"StudyForward.fs\" />` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`, no comment. Module doc, one to three lines: the forward model of an experiment and the study residual (spec 0050 S11.2). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In order: (a) `StudyForwardError`, an `*Error` union, its first case `UnpairedPointsErr of reason : string` (a mapped point the experiment's scan cannot place), with `member this.describe : string`: `the data cannot be placed on the scan: <reason>`. Later steps add their cases, each with its line. (b) `RecordedReading` = `RecordedSignal of MeasuredIntensity` (an intensity detector's signal) | `RecordedPsiDelta of PsiDelta` (an ellipsometer's Ψ and Δ, `AnalysisFunctions.fs:PsiDelta`) | `RecordedMueller of MuellerMatrix` (a polarimeter's ABSOLUTE Mueller matrix, its m₀₀ the throughput, as S9.2's Mueller readings hold it, steps 301-302): what a detector records, predicted or measured. (c) `MeasuredRow` = `SettingsRow of settings : ScanSetting list * waveLengthOpt : WaveLength option * measured : RecordedReading` (a point taken at those scan settings, step 287, at its own wavelength when it carries one) | `ObservationRow of observation : MuellerObservation` (a point carrying its own configuration, `MuellerInverse.fs:MuellerObservation`). (d) `type MappedPoints with member this.measuredRowsFor (scan : ExperimentScan) : Result<MeasuredRow list, StudyForwardError>`: the points in their order, each placed by the rules `validatedFor` checks (step 304) over `scan.quantities` (step 304), a quantity set as `{ elementId; variable; value }` with the value `validatedFor` admits for the point, through the same conversion: a `SeriesPoints (IntensityData s)` point is `SettingsRow` of the one quantity at its x, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of its intensity; a `SeriesPoints (EllipsometricData s)` point is `SettingsRow` of the scan's `VaryR2` quantity at its angle of incidence when it carries one and the scan has that quantity (else no setting), `Some` of its wavelength, and `RecordedPsiDelta` of its Ψ and Δ; a `CapturePoints` row is `SettingsRow` of the one quantity at its `description` in degrees, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of its `avgTotal`; a `ColumnPoints` row is `SettingsRow` of the quantities, cell i the i-th quantity at the cell's `displayValue`, no wavelength, and `RecordedSignal` of a `SignalReading`'s signal (its σ is not read: a study weighs runs and detectors, 001 §L) or `RecordedMueller` of a `MuellerReading`; an `ObservationPoints` observation is `ObservationRow` of it. Under a scan of no quantity (a dark line, step 287) a series point, capture row or column row has no setting. A series point or capture row under more than one quantity, and a column row whose cells do not number the quantities, answer `UnpairedPointsErr` naming the point's number and the counts. No cache or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs`, `module StudyForwardTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local scans of `ScanAxis` records on test-local element ids: `each kind of mapped point is placed on the scan it was taken over`: under a one-axis `VaryR1` scan of a polarizer, an intensity series at x 0 and 30 gives two `SettingsRow`s setting the polarizer's `VaryR1` to 0 and 30, no wavelength, their intensities; under a one-axis `VaryDialReading` scan, a capture row of description 20° sets the dial reading to 20 with its `avgTotal`; under a two-axis scan (the polarizer's `VaryR1` outer, a sample's `VaryR2` inner), a column row of cells 10 and 45 sets both in that order, and its `MuellerReading` is `RecordedMueller`; an ellipsometric point at 500 nm with an angle of incidence of 60° under that scan sets the sample's `VaryR2` to 60 with `Some` 500 nm and its Ψ and Δ; observations give one `ObservationRow` each, in order; under a dark-line scan a series point has no setting. `a point the scan cannot place is refused`: under the two-axis scan an intensity series point, a capture row and a column row of one cell each answer `UnpairedPointsErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct payload renders its text with it.", "acceptance": "After the readings land, `MappedPoints.measuredRowsFor` MUST place every kind of mapped point on its experiment's scan or refuse it with `UnpairedPointsErr`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `each kind of mapped point is placed on the scan it was taken over`, `a point the scan cannot place is refused` and `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.each kind of mapped point is placed on the scan it was taken over", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a point the scan cannot place is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.RecordedReading", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.MeasuredRow", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.MappedPoints.measuredRowsFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-MEASURED-ROWS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 372, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [371], "how_to": "The parameter vector a fit searches, laid out by the generated axes: one value per owner of each unknown (step 362: 'The fitter's vector holds one value per owner of each unknown (S11.2-S11.3)'; 001 §N 'Parameter-axis generation'; 001 §L scopes; the S11.2 brief 'a parameter vector laid out by the generated axes'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `measuredRowsFor` (step 371): (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] StudyForwardContext = { kit : StudyContext; library : LibraryProxy; materials : MaterialProxy; experimentData : ExperimentDataProxy; choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option; solverParameters : SolverParameters }`: what a study's forward model reads, the kit as the study messages see it (step 366), the library and material stores, the data seam (step 305), an item's model as the window's stores resolve it (step 263) and the solver parameters a cut plate is solved with, passed rather than defaulted as `MuellerInverse.fs:createBerremanForward` asks. (2) `StudyRunUse` = `ResidualRunUse` | `DarkLevelRunUse` | `UnreadRunUse`, and `type ExperimentRole with member this.studyUse : StudyRunUse` (step 285's roles, no wildcard arm): `ScienceRun`, `CalibrationRun` and `DriftCheckRun` give residual rows, `DarkRun` gives its session's dark level (001 §L 'dark from the Dark runs'), and `DiagnosticRun`, `IgnoredRun` and `PlannedRun` are not read. It is derived, never stored, so it carries no tag. (3) `type Study with member this.fittedRunsIn (experiments : Experiment list) : Experiment list`: the study's `enabledExperiments` (step 365) whose role's use is `ResidualRunUse`, as `experiments` holds them, in study order. (4) `StudyVectorEntry = { unknown : StudyUnknown; owner : UnknownOwner }` (step 362), one value of the vector. (5) `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"the study's parameter vector: built whole for every residual evaluation and handed whole to the fit\")>] StudyParameterVector = StudyParameterVector of float[]` with `.value`, `static member ofParameterValues (values : ParameterValue list) : StudyParameterVector` and `member this.valueAt (index : int) : ParameterValue`. (6) `StudyParameterLayout = { entries : StudyVectorEntry list; sessions : StudySession list }` with `member this.startVector : StudyParameterVector`, each entry's `unknown.unknown.start` (step 221) in order. (7) `type Study with member this.parameterLayoutWith (context : StudyForwardContext) : StudyParameterLayout`: `sessions` is `this.sessionsIn context.kit.experiments` (step 358); for each of `this.unknownsWith (context.kit.itemsUsedBy this)` (steps 362, 366) in order, one entry per owner of `unknown.owners sessions users` (step 362), in its order, `users` being the names of `this.fittedRunsIn context.kit.experiments` whose slots (`slotsIn context.kit.setups`, step 261; a run whose setup does not resolve uses nothing) hold the unknown's item for an `ItemParameterRef`, or, for a `MaterialParameterRef`, an item whose `context.choiceOf` is `StackSampleChoice (_, sample)` with `sample.openedMaterialsIn this` (step 361) holding a copy of that version. No bound, scaling or option is added: the fit's are S11.3's. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over test-local items made by `ItemDraft` (step 223): CPL1 (`ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId`, `c2.retardance` unknown from π / 2 within [1, 2]), a Phone (`ItemModelIds.intensityDetectorModelId`, `gain` unknown from 1 within [0.1, 10]) and QZ (a `StackSampleChoice` of a test-local plate sample whose substrate is a test-local uniaxial crystal version), a study opening that version with `n_o` unknown from 1.54 within [1.5, 1.6] (step 361), setups made by `Setup.create` of slots built as `SetupTests` builds them holding CPL1, QZ and the Phone, test-local experiments E1 and E2 (Science, `Session 1`), D1 (Diagnostic) and E3 (Science), a `StudyContext` record of them and a `choiceOf` answering each item's choice: `the vector holds one value per owner of each unknown, in the unknowns' order, and starts at each unknown's start`: the layout's entries are CPL1 `c2.retardance` with its `ItemOwner`, the Phone `gain` with `SessionOwner` `Session 1` then `Session 2`, and `n_o` with its `MaterialOwner`, in that order, and `startVector` is [π / 2; 1; 1; 1.54]; with a scope making CPL1's retardance `ExperimentScope` its owners are E1, E2 and E3 in that order. `a disabled run, a run that is not fitted and a run whose setup does not use an unknown own none of its values`: with E2 disabled (`withExperimentEnablement`, step 365) the experiment-scoped retardance has the owners E1 and E3; E1 made a Dark run owns none of them; and a run over a setup holding no QZ is no user of `n_o`, which keeps its one `MaterialOwner` through the others.", "acceptance": "After the layout lands, `Study.parameterLayoutWith` MUST hold one entry per owner of each of the study's unknowns, in the unknowns' order, owned only through enabled fitted runs that use them, and `startVector` MUST be their starts; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the vector holds one value per owner of each unknown, in the unknowns' order, and starts at each unknown's start` and `a disabled run, a run that is not fitted and a run whose setup does not use an unknown own none of its values`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.the vector holds one value per owner of each unknown, in the unknowns' order, and starts at each unknown's start", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a disabled run, a run that is not fitted and a run whose setup does not use an unknown own none of its values", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardContext", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyRunUse", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.ExperimentRole.studyUse", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.fittedRunsIn", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyVectorEntry", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyParameterVector", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyParameterLayout", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.parameterLayoutWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-VECTOR-LAYOUT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 373, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [372], "how_to": "The numbers one experiment is evaluated with at one parameter vector: each item's values and each opened material's crystal (001 §L 'Scope is the sharing rule'; 001 §I 'every sample made of it shares them (`MaterialScope`)'; step 361: `Sample.openedMaterialsIn` — 'the forward model reads it (S11.2)'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `parameterLayoutWith` (step 372): (1) `ExperimentAssignment = { itemValues : Map<ItemId, ParameterValues>; crystals : Map<MaterialVersionId, CrystalParameters> }`, with `member this.valuesOf (item : Item) : ParameterValues`, its entry or `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters` (step 245) for an item the map lacks; `member this.crystalOf (material : OpenedMaterial) : CrystalParameters`, its entry or the copy's `currentCrystal` (step 361); and `member this.materialProxyOver (materials : MaterialProxy) : MaterialProxy`, `materials` with `resolveVersion` answering, for a version `crystals` holds, the entry the store answers with its `physics` replaced by `CrystalParameterPhysics` of the assignment's crystal (step 355), every other version and field passing through, so a stack sample made of an opened material is solved with the study's working copy. (2) `type StudyParameterLayout with member this.assignmentFor (study : Study) (items : Item list) (experiment : ExperimentName) (vector : StudyParameterVector) : Result<ExperimentAssignment, StudyForwardError>`: `VectorLengthErr` naming both lengths when the vector does not hold one value per entry; otherwise an entry's owner holds the experiment when it is an `ItemOwner` or a `MaterialOwner`, a `SessionOwner s` whose session of `this.sessions` lists it, or the `ExperimentOwner` of it, and (a) each of `items` takes `ParameterValues.ofParameters item.parameters` with each entry k on one of its parameters whose owner holds the experiment set by `withValue name (vector.valueAt k)` (step 245); (b) each of `study.materials` takes its `currentCrystal` with each such entry on one of its components written through the generated axis of that name (`crystal.parameterAxes`, `writeValue`, step 361); (c) then each of `study.links` (step 364) sets its follower to its leader's value in this assignment: an item parameter's `valueOf`, or a component read through its generated axis's `parameterValueOf`, written as in (a) or (b). `StudyForwardError` gains `VectorLengthErr of reason : string`, rendered `the parameter vector does not fit the study: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 372's fixture and its layout: `an experiment's items take the vector's value for the owner that holds it, and every other parameter its own`: at [0.7; 2; 3; 1.6], E1's assignment gives CPL1 `c2.retardance` 0.7 and the Phone `gain` 2 and `darkOffset` its own 0, E3's gives `gain` 3, and every other parameter of each item is its own value. `an opened material's crystal takes its components from the vector, and a link's follower takes its leader's value`: E1's crystal of the opened version is the uniaxial copy with `n_o` 1.6 and its other three components the copy's; with CPL2 added (`c2.retardance` known at 1.2) and linked to follow CPL1's (step 364), CPL2's value is 0.7 at E1 and its known 1.2 in an assignment taken before the link. `a stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy`: `materialProxyOver`'s `resolveVersion` of the opened version answers the entry whose physics is `CrystalParameterPhysics` of E1's crystal, and of another version the store's entry unchanged. `a vector of another length is refused`: a vector of three values answers `VectorLengthErr` naming 3 and 4. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers `VectorLengthErr`.", "acceptance": "After the assignment lands, `StudyParameterLayout.assignmentFor` MUST give each item the vector's value for the owner holding the experiment and its own value otherwise, each opened material its crystal from the vector, each link's follower its leader's value, and `materialProxyOver` MUST resolve an opened version to the working copy; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an experiment's items take the vector's value for the owner that holds it, and every other parameter its own`, `an opened material's crystal takes its components from the vector, and a link's follower takes its leader's value`, `a stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy` and `a vector of another length is refused`, the count rising by 4, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an experiment's items take the vector's value for the owner that holds it, and every other parameter its own", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an opened material's crystal takes its components from the vector, and a link's follower takes its leader's value", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a stack sample made of an opened material resolves to the study's working copy", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a vector of another length is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.ExperimentAssignment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyParameterLayout.assignmentFor", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-ASSIGNMENT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 374, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [373], "how_to": "The forward model of an experiment at a scan point: its setup's slots, the point's settings and the study's numbers give the predicted reading, through S8.1's evaluator (001 §N 'The forward model of an experiment = slots + scan point + parameters → predicted reading: intensity → S₀ · gain + dark; polarimeter → Mueller elements + throughput; ellipsometer → Ψ / Δ'; step 251: a detector's 'gain, dark offset and noise belong to S11.2's forward model'). The noise budget a detector publishes is not read: nothing is simulated here. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs`, after `read`: `type RunStep with static member productOf (steps : RunStep list) : MuellerMatrix`, the steps' matrices multiplied in light order from `Propagation.identityMueller` (each `step.mueller * product`). (2) In `StudyForward.fs`, after `assignmentFor` (step 373): (a) `type ParameterValue with member this.darkMean : DarkMean`, the number as a dark level in the detector's own units (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:DarkMean`; a `ReadingParameter`, step 214). (b) `DetectorReadout` = `IntensityDetectorReadout of gain : ParameterValue * dark : DarkMean` | `PolarimeterDetectorReadout` | `EllipsometerDetectorReadout`. (c) `BoundPathStep = { slot : SetupSlot; element : BoundOpticalElement; branch : Propagation.Branch; drawnIncidence : IncidenceAngle; dial : ItemDial; dialZero : Angle }`. (d) `BoundExperiment = { experiment : Experiment; emission : SourceEmission; operatingWaveLength : WaveLength; path : BoundPathStep list; detectorItem : ItemId; readout : DetectorReadout }`. (e) `type Experiment with member this.boundWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (assignment : ExperimentAssignment) (darkOpt : DarkMean option) : Result<BoundExperiment, StudyForwardError>`: the slots are `this.slotsIn context.kit.setups` (step 261; a `SetupError` answers `ForwardSetupErr`), each `drawnWith context.kit.items` (step 258), laid out by `BeamLayout.layout` of their `layoutElement`s; `param` is `{ library = context.library; materials = assignment.materialProxyOver context.materials; items = context.kit.items; choiceOf = context.choiceOf; valuesOf = assignment.valuesOf }` (steps 368, 373); the emission is `SetupSlot.runEmissionOf slots param`; the operating wavelength `SourcePreset.operatingWaveLengthOf (SetupSlot.boundSourceIn slots context.library) this.scan.sourceWaveLengthOpt` (step 367); the detector is the first `DetectorSlotRole` slot of `SetupSlot.inLightOrder slots` (step 257) holding an item whose `context.choiceOf` is a `LibraryModelChoice` of a detector form (step 215), else `StudyDetectorErr` naming the setup reference, and its readout is, for `IntensityDetectorModel`, `IntensityDetectorReadout` of the item's `ParameterName.gain` value and `darkOpt`, or else the item's `ParameterName.darkOffset` value's `darkMean`; for `MuellerPolarimeterModel`, `PolarimeterDetectorReadout`; for `EllipsometerModel`, `EllipsometerDetectorReadout`; the path is the detector's placed `path` (`BeamLayout.fs:PathStep`), each step's slot bound by `runElementWith param` (step 368) and kept when it answers `Some element`, with `step.branch.propagationBranch`, its placed element's `incidenceOn slot.placement` (step 367), and its item's `dial` and `dialZero` value's `angle` (`FixedMounting` and `Angle.zero` for a slot without an item). Every `SlotRunError` answers `ForwardSlotErr`. (f) `type BoundExperiment with member this.readingAt (settings : ScanSetting list) (waveLengthOpt : WaveLength option) : Result<RecordedReading, StudyForwardError>`: the wavelength is `waveLengthOpt`, else a `VaryWaveLength` setting's value in nanometres, else `operatingWaveLength`; each path step is evaluated by `element.muellerAt` (step 247) at `{ rotation; incidence; branch }` and made its run step by `slot.runStepOf` (step 368), its rotation a `VaryR1` setting on its slot in degrees, else a `VaryDialReading` setting's reading in degrees through its dial, else its slot's `DialTurn reading` through its dial, else `slot.placement.r1` (a reading through a `DialMounted sign` dial being `sign.physicalAngleOf dialZero reading`, step 255, and through `FixedMounting` the reading itself), and its incidence a `VaryR2` setting on its slot in degrees, else `drawnIncidence`; then `IntensityDetectorReadout (gain, dark)` reads `RecordedSignal` of S₀ · gain + dark, S₀ being the intensity `ExperimentRun.read Intensity this.emission steps` gives (step 252); `EllipsometerDetectorReadout` reads `RecordedPsiDelta` of the Ψ and Δ `ExperimentRun.read Ellipsometer` gives; `PolarimeterDetectorReadout` reads `RecordedMueller (RunStep.productOf steps)`. An `ItemEvaluationError` answers `ForwardSlotErr (SlotEvaluationErr e)`. `StudyForwardError` gains `ForwardSetupErr of error : SetupError`, `ForwardSlotErr of error : SlotRunError` and `StudyDetectorErr of reason : string`, rendered `the experiment's setup does not resolve: <describe>`, `a slot cannot be evaluated: <describe>` and `the setup has no detector item: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests. In `ExperimentRunTests`, `a path's Mueller matrix is the product of its steps in light order`: [`ElementStep A`; `ObjectStep B`; `ElementStep C`] of three distinct test-local matrices is C · B · A, and [] is the identity. In `StudyForwardTests`, with materials from `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])` and `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, over setups of slots built as `SetupTests` builds them: a HeNe source item, a linear-polarizer item at R1 0° (prep), a real-LP item (`ItemModelIds.realLinearPolarizerModelId`, analyzer) and a detector item, each assignment from `assignmentFor` or a test-local `ExperimentAssignment`: `an intensity detector reads S0 times its gain plus its dark level along the setup's path`: with an intensity detector item at `gain` 2 and `darkOffset` 0.1, a `VaryR1` setting of the analyzer at 60° reads S₀ · 2 + 0.1 within 1e-12, S₀ being `ExperimentRun.read Intensity` over the default emission and the two polarizers' matrices from `runElementWith` and `muellerAt` at 0° and 60°; with `darkOpt = Some (DarkMean 0.3)` the dark is 0.3. `a scan setting turns, tilts or retunes the path, and a dial reading turns its slot through the vector's zero`: the analyzer as a `DialMounted DialNegative` item whose `dialZero` is 10° in the assignment reads a `VaryDialReading` setting of −20° as the analyzer at 30°, and its recorded `DialTurn` of −20° without a setting likewise; a sample slot holding a glass-plate item (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1) between the polarizers, under a `VaryR2` setting of 40°, is evaluated at incidence 40°; a `VaryWaveLength` setting of 500 reads as evaluated at 500 nm, and `waveLengthOpt` of 450 nm wins over it. `a polarimeter reads its path's Mueller matrix, and an ellipsometer Psi and Delta of the arriving state`: a polarimeter detector item (`ItemModelIds.muellerPolarimeterModelId`) reads `RecordedMueller` of the analyzer's matrix times the prep's within 1e-12, and an ellipsometer item (`ItemModelIds.ellipsometerModelId`) the Ψ and Δ of `ExperimentRun.read Ellipsometer` over the same steps. `a setup without a detector item, or whose setup or slot item does not resolve, is refused`: a detector slot holding no item answers `StudyDetectorErr`; an experiment over `'Missing' revision 1` answers `ForwardSetupErr`; an analyzer slot holding an item the kit lacks answers `ForwardSlotErr` of `SlotItemErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers the three new cases.", "acceptance": "After the forward model lands, `Experiment.boundWith` and `BoundExperiment.readingAt` MUST predict an intensity detector's S₀ · gain + dark, a polarimeter's path Mueller matrix and an ellipsometer's Ψ and Δ at each scan setting through S8.1's evaluator, and refuse a setup without a detector item or with an unresolved setup or slot item; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a path's Mueller matrix is the product of its steps in light order`, `an intensity detector reads S0 times its gain plus its dark level along the setup's path`, `a scan setting turns, tilts or retunes the path, and a dial reading turns its slot through the vector's zero`, `a polarimeter reads its path's Mueller matrix, and an ellipsometer Psi and Delta of the arriving state` and `a setup without a detector item, or whose setup or slot item does not resolve, is refused`, the count rising by 5, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests.a path's Mueller matrix is the product of its steps in light order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentRunTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentRunTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an intensity detector reads S0 times its gain plus its dark level along the setup's path", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a scan setting turns, tilts or retunes the path, and a dial reading turns its slot through the vector's zero", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a polarimeter reads its path's Mueller matrix, and an ellipsometer Psi and Delta of the arriving state", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a setup without a detector item, or whose setup or slot item does not resolve, is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.ExperimentRun.RunStep.productOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentRun.fs", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.ParameterValue.darkMean", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.DetectorReadout", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundPathStep", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundExperiment", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Experiment.boundWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundExperiment.readingAt", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-FORWARD-MODEL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 375, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [374], "how_to": "A Mueller observation carries its own configuration, and the study pairs it with the experiment (step 304): its object is a plate of an opened crystal, solved through the spec 0044 Berreman forward at that configuration (001 §K 'the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape'; 001 §N '`MuellerInverse.orientForCut` + `createBerremanForward` for cut plates — REUSED'; .spec-md §3.16: the study engine evaluates the crystal-parameter records). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`: (1) After `readingAt` (step 374), `type MeasurementConfiguration with member this.elementOrientation : ElementOrientation`: `{ rotation = this.azimuth.angle; incidence = this.incidenceAngle; branch }`, `BranchTransmitted` for `TransmittedMueller` and `BranchReflected` for `ReflectedMueller` (`MuellerInverse.fs:MeasurementConfiguration`), so that `ElementOrientation.sampleAzimuth` and `observable` (step 250) give the configuration's back. (2) `BoundExperiment` (step 374) gains `observedCrystalOpt : CrystalParameters option` and `solverParameters : SolverParameters`, and `Experiment.boundWith` takes the study as its second parameter, `(context : StudyForwardContext) (study : Study) (assignment : ExperimentAssignment) (darkOpt : DarkMean option)`, to fill them: `solverParameters` is `context.solverParameters`; `observedCrystalOpt` is `assignment.crystalOf` (step 373) of the one copy `sample.openedMaterialsIn study` (step 361) answers when the setup's `ObjectSlotRole` slots (step 257) hold exactly one item, whose `context.choiceOf` is a `StackSampleChoice (_, sample)` made of exactly one opened material, and `None` otherwise. Step 374's facts pass the study. (3) `type BoundExperiment with member this.predictedReadingOf (row : MeasuredRow) : Result<RecordedReading, StudyForwardError>`: a `SettingsRow (settings, waveLengthOpt, _)` reads `readingAt settings waveLengthOpt`; an `ObservationRow o` under `PolarimeterDetectorReadout` with `Some crystal` reads `RecordedMueller` of `BoundCutPlate (CutPlate.ofForward (MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (fun (c : CrystalParameters) -> c.opticalProperties) this.solverParameters) crystal o.configuration.cut o.configuration.thickness)` (steps 250, 355; `MuellerInverse.fs:createBerremanForward`) evaluated by `muellerAt o.configuration.elementOrientation o.configuration.waveLength`, its `ItemEvaluationError` answering `ForwardSlotErr (SlotEvaluationErr e)`; with `None` it answers `ObservationPlateErr` naming the experiment, and under another readout `ReadingMismatchErr` naming the readout. `StudyForwardError` gains `ObservationPlateErr of reason : string` and `ReadingMismatchErr of reason : string`, rendered `the observation has no single plate of one opened crystal: <reason>` and `the reading is not what the detector records: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 374's setups with a polarimeter detector item and an object item made of a test-local plate sample of an opened uniaxial version (n_o 1.544, n_e 1.553, zero gyration in the assignment), with `SolverParameters.defaultValue`: `an observation is predicted as a cut plate of its object's opened crystal at its own configuration`: an `XCut` 1 mm observation at incidence 20°, azimuth 30° and 600 nm, transmitted, reads `RecordedMueller` equal element by element exactly to `(MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) SolverParameters.defaultValue).muellerOf` of its configuration and those parameters, and the reflected one likewise; `elementOrientation`'s `sampleAzimuth` and `observable` give the configuration's back; and a `SettingsRow` reads as `readingAt` does. `an observation without one opened plate, or under a detector that is no polarimeter, is refused`: an object made of no opened material, and a setup holding two object items, answer `ObservationPlateErr`; an observation under an intensity detector answers `ReadingMismatchErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After the observations land, `BoundExperiment.predictedReadingOf` MUST predict an observation as the cut plate of its experiment's one opened crystal through `createBerremanForward` at the observation's configuration, exactly as the spec 0044 forward does, and read a settings row as `readingAt`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an observation is predicted as a cut plate of its object's opened crystal at its own configuration` and `an observation without one opened plate, or under a detector that is no polarimeter, is refused`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an observation is predicted as a cut plate of its object's opened crystal at its own configuration", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.an observation without one opened plate, or under a detector that is no polarimeter, is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.MeasurementConfiguration.elementOrientation", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundExperiment.predictedReadingOf", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.BoundExperiment", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Experiment.boundWith", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-OBSERVATIONS"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 376, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Optimization", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [375], "how_to": "The residual entries of one measured row, per kind, REUSING the semantics of `MuellerInverse.observationResidual` / `residualVector` for Mueller matrices (the S11.2 brief; 001 §K 'the 0044 `MuellerObservation` shape, normalized + absolute throughput'). The log-throughput term the study needs lives inside `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor` (step 336), which Domain cannot reference, so it MOVES into `MuellerInverse.fs` beside `observationResidual` and the fit calls it (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs`, after `residualVector` (`MuellerInverse.fs:residualVector`): `throughputResidual (measured : MuellerMatrix) (model : MuellerMatrix) : Result<ResidualVector, InversionError>`, the one entry ln m₀₀(model) − ln m₀₀(measured), and `NonPositiveIntensityErr` of the measured, then the model's, m₀₀ when it is not above zero or not finite (the refusal `normalized` makes, `MuellerInverse.fs:InversionError`); its doc says it is the term that keeps isotropic absorption in the data and points at `throughputResidualFor`'s doc for why. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs`: `throughputResidualFor` takes each observation's term from `throughputResidual o.measured model`, an `Error` giving `1.0e3` where its local `logThroughput` gave `None`; the local helper is deleted. The same `log` and the same subtraction run, so every BerremanTests number is bit-identical. (3) In `StudyForward.fs`, after `predictedReadingOf` (step 375): `RowResidual = { elements : ResidualVector; throughputOpt : ResidualVector option }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ResidualVector`), and `type RecordedReading with member this.residualAgainst (measured : RecordedReading) : Result<RowResidual, StudyForwardError>`, `this` being the prediction: two signals give the one element `predicted − measured`; two Ψ / Δ readings give the elements Ψ_p − Ψ_m and `Math.IEEERemainder (Δ_p − Δ_m, 2π)`, in radians, so a Δ near ±180° is not a 2π jump; two Mueller matrices give the elements `observationResidual measured predicted` (`MuellerInverse.fs:observationResidual`, the 15 normalized differences) and the throughput `throughputResidual measured predicted`; an `InversionError` answers the new `RowResidualErr of error : InversionError`, and readings of different kinds `ReadingMismatchErr` (step 375) naming both. `RowResidualErr` renders `the residual cannot be formed: <the error>` (each `InversionError` case's payload). No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`: `a signal row's entry is the predicted signal less the measured`: a predicted 2.5 against a measured 2 gives [0.5]. `a Psi and Delta row's entries are their differences, Delta's taken on the circle`: Ψ 30° against 28° and Δ 179° against −179° give 2° and −2°, in radians, within 1e-12. `a Mueller row's entries are the normalized element differences and the log-throughput ratio`: a predicted ideal-LP matrix scaled by 0.8 against a measured one scaled by 0.5 gives the elements `observationResidual` gives (15 zeros here) and the throughput [ln 0.8 − ln 0.5] within 1e-15, and a measured retarder (`MuellerReconstruction.retarderMueller`) against it the 15 entries `observationResidual` gives. `a reading of another kind than the row's, or a Mueller matrix without positive throughput, is refused`: a signal against a Mueller matrix answers `ReadingMismatchErr`, and a measured matrix of m₀₀ 0 answers `RowResidualErr` of `NonPositiveIntensityErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers `RowResidualErr`. BerremanTests' `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, the cheapest class running `throughputResidualFor`, runs unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the row residual lands, `MuellerInverse.throughputResidual` MUST be the one log-throughput term, called by `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor` with its numbers bit-identical, and `RecordedReading.residualAgainst` MUST give a signal's difference, Ψ and the wrapped Δ, and a Mueller matrix's 15 normalized differences with its log-throughput ratio; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a signal row's entry is the predicted signal less the measured`, `a Psi and Delta row's entries are their differences, Delta's taken on the circle`, `a Mueller row's entries are the normalized element differences and the log-throughput ratio` and `a reading of another kind than the row's, or a Mueller matrix without positive throughput, is refused`, the count rising by 4, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a signal row's entry is the predicted signal less the measured", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a Psi and Delta row's entries are their differences, Delta's taken on the circle", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a Mueller row's entries are the normalized element differences and the log-throughput ratio", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a reading of another kind than the row's, or a Mueller matrix without positive throughput, is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MuellerInverse.throughputResidual", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MuellerInverse.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Optimization.MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor", "op": "change_behavior", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.RowResidual", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.RecordedReading.residualAgainst", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-ROW-RESIDUAL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 377, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112k", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [376], "how_to": "The study's pre-fit validation: every run a fit reads checked by the moved checks and flagged by the data-change check (001 §R 'Its three validation checks are reused as the study's pre-fit checks'; 001 §E 'flagged … before each fit'; steps 369 and 370). A failed check is reported, not raised: the study view (S11.5) lists each. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `residualAgainst` (step 376): (1) `ExperimentPrefit = { experiment : Experiment; check : Result<MappedPoints, PrefitError>; changeOpt : DataChangeFlag option }`: one run's checked points or its typed failure, and its data's change flag (`None` without data, whose check already answers `MissingDataErr`). (2) `type Study with member this.prefitWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (fitted : DataAttachment list) : Result<ExperimentPrefit list, StudyForwardError>`: the study's `enabledExperiments` (step 365) whose role's `studyUse` (step 372) is `ResidualRunUse` or `DarkLevelRunUse`, in study order, each found by name in `context.kit.experiments` (else `MissingStudyRunErr` naming it), its `check` `prefitCheckWith context.library context.experimentData context.kit.setups` (step 369), and its `changeOpt` for an attached run `data.changeWith` (step 370) of `context.experimentData.attachmentStatus data.attachment` (step 305), a `KitError` answering `StudyRunKitErr`. `fitted` is the attachments the study's last fit run read, empty before its first. `StudyForwardError` gains `MissingStudyRunErr of reason : string` and `StudyRunKitErr of error : KitError`, rendered `the kit has no such experiment: <reason>` and `the kit cannot report the data's status: <describe>`. No other member is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 374's setups, a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy` record answering `readMapped` and `attachmentStatus` by attachment path, and a study of E1 (Science, attached, unchanged), K1 (Dark, attached, changed since attach), X1 (Diagnostic, attached), E2 (Calibration, no data), E3 (Science, attached, disabled) and P1 (Planned): `a study's pre-fit checks every run a fit reads, in study order, with its data-change flag`: with `fitted` holding E1's path at another hash, `prefitWith` answers E1 (`Ok` of its points, `ChangedSinceFitFlag`), K1 (`Ok`, `ChangedSinceAttachFlag`) and E2 (`MissingDataErr`, `None`), in that order, and nothing for X1, E3 or P1. `a study naming an experiment the kit lacks, or a data status the kit cannot read, is refused`: a study naming E9, which the kit lacks, answers `MissingStudyRunErr` naming it, and an `attachmentStatus` answering a `KitIoErr` answers `StudyRunKitErr`. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After the study's pre-fit lands, `Study.prefitWith` MUST check every enabled run a fit reads, in study order, with its data-change flag, and leave out diagnostic, ignored, planned and disabled runs; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study's pre-fit checks every run a fit reads, in study order, with its data-change flag` and `a study naming an experiment the kit lacks, or a data status the kit cannot read, is refused`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a study's pre-fit checks every run a fit reads, in study order, with its data-change flag", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a study naming an experiment the kit lacks, or a data status the kit cannot read, is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.ExperimentPrefit", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.prefitWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-PREFIT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 378, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112l", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [377], "how_to": "What a study's residual reads, gathered once from its pre-fit: each fitted run's measured rows and each session's dark level from its Dark runs (001 §L 'dark from the Dark runs'; step 357: 'Reading the dark level from those runs' data is the forward model's (S11.2)'; step 314: `keptBy` is 'the one a study's residual reads in S11'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, after `prefitWith` (step 377): (1) `StudyRun = { experiment : Experiment; rows : MeasuredRow list }`; `SessionDark = { session : SessionName; dark : DarkMean }` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:DarkMean`); `StudyData = { runs : StudyRun list; darks : SessionDark list }` with `member this.darkOf (session : SessionName) : DarkMean option`. (2) `type Study with member this.dataWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) : Result<StudyData, StudyForwardError>`: the first prefit whose `check` is an `Error` answers `PrefitFailedErr` naming its experiment; `runs` are the prefits whose role's use is `ResidualRunUse`, in order, each its checked points' `measuredRowsFor experiment.scan` (step 371); `darks` hold, for each session of `this.sessionsIn context.kit.experiments` (step 358) listing a run, the mean of the signals of every row of `session.darkRunsIn` over the prefits' experiments (step 357: its own Dark runs, else every Dark run the fit reads), each row a `RecordedSignal` (else `DarkReadingErr` naming the run), as a `DarkMean`; a session with no Dark run has none, and its intensity runs take their detector's `darkOffset` (step 374). `StudyForwardError` gains `PrefitFailedErr of experiment : ExperimentName * error : PrefitError` and `DarkReadingErr of reason : string`, rendered `the experiment is not ready for a fit: <name>: <the error's describe>` and `a dark run does not record a signal: <reason>`. No cache or option is added. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, over step 377's fixture with every check passing: `a study's data holds each fitted run's kept rows in study order`: E1's rows and E2's are in `runs` in that order, E1's three intensity points with point 2 excluded giving two rows, and K1 is not a run. `a session's dark level is the mean signal of its own dark runs, else of every dark run, and none without a dark run`: with K1 in `Session 1` holding signals 0.2 and 0.4, `Session 1`'s dark is 0.3; with a second session E4 holding no Dark run of its own, its dark is the mean over every Dark run the fit reads; with K1 disabled no session has a dark. `a failed pre-fit check or a dark run that records no signal is refused`: a prefit whose check is `MissingDataErr` answers `PrefitFailedErr` naming E2, and a Dark run whose rows are `RecordedPsiDelta` answers `DarkReadingErr` naming it. `every forward error renders its condition and its payload` covers the two new cases.", "acceptance": "After the study's data lands, `Study.dataWith` MUST hold each fitted run's kept rows in study order and each session's dark level as the mean signal of its Dark runs, else of every Dark run, and refuse a failed check or a Dark run without signals; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a study's data holds each fitted run's kept rows in study order`, `a session's dark level is the mean signal of its own dark runs, else of every dark run, and none without a dark run` and `a failed pre-fit check or a dark run that records no signal is refused`, the count rising by 3, and the widened `every forward error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a study's data holds each fitted run's kept rows in study order", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a session's dark level is the mean signal of its own dark runs, else of every dark run, and none without a dark run", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a failed pre-fit check or a dark run that records no signal is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.every forward error renders its condition and its payload", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyRun", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.SessionDark", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyData", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.dataWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.StudyForwardError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-DATA"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
{"number": 379, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S112m", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [378], "how_to": "The study residual: one weighted vector over every enabled fitted run of the study, against its data, at a parameter vector laid out by the generated axes (the S11.2 brief; 001 §L 'Weights and ablation: a weight per experiment or per detector; enable / disable per experiment'; 001 §K 'A study mixes them'; step 365: `residualWeightOf` is 'the weight the residual rows of that experiment take (S11.2)'). The engines that minimise it are S11.3's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `StudyForward.fs`, last: `type Study with member this.residualWith (context : StudyForwardContext) (layout : StudyParameterLayout) (data : StudyData) (vector : StudyParameterVector) : Result<ResidualVector, StudyForwardError>`: for each run of `data.runs` in order, its assignment `layout.assignmentFor this context.kit.items run.experiment.name vector` (step 373), the dark `data.darkOf` gives the session of `layout.sessions` listing it (step 378), `run.experiment.boundWith context this assignment darkOpt` (step 375), its weight `this.residualWeightOf run.experiment.name bound.detectorItem` (step 365), and for each row `bound.predictedReadingOf row` (step 375) `residualAgainst` the row's measured reading (step 376), every entry multiplied by the weight. The vector is every run's element entries, run after run and row after row, followed by every Mueller row's throughput entry in the same order: the layout of `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor` (step 336), so a study of polarimeter observations at unit weight is that harness vector, which S12.2 asserts on AT-2 (001 §Q AT-2 'Model identity'). The first error stops the walk. A disabled run, a run that is not fitted and a Dark run add no entry, because `data.runs` holds none of them (steps 377, 378). No cache, scaling or penalty is added: S11.3's engines decide what an error costs. Tests, in `StudyForwardTests`, each study's data made by `prefitWith` and `dataWith` over a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy`: `a mixed study's residual holds every run's entries in study order, the Mueller throughputs last`: a study of an intensity run (two rows, its session holding a Dark run of signal 0.25), an ellipsometer run (one row) and a polarimeter observation run (one row of an opened uniaxial plate) gives 20 entries: the two signal differences with the dark 0.25, Ψ and Δ, the 15 normalized differences, then the one throughput entry, each equal to `residualAgainst` of `predictedReadingOf` the row within 1e-12. `a run's weight multiplies its entries, and a disabled run adds none`: the intensity run at an experiment weight of 3 (`withExperimentWeight`) and its detector at 0.5 (`withDetectorWeight`) has its two entries times 1.5 and the others unchanged; with the ellipsometer run disabled the residual holds 18 entries, the same others. `a polarimeter study's residual is the throughput residual of its observations`: a study opening a uniaxial version with its four components unknown, its one plate run holding three observations (`XCut` 1 mm transmitted at incidence 0°, the same reflected at 20°, a `ZCut` 0.5 mm transmitted at 10°) at a vector of the crystal's values, equals entry by entry, within 1e-12 relative, `MuellerFitting.throughputResidualFor (MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (fun (p : UniaxialParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) SolverParameters.defaultValue)` of those observations over `scalingAround UniaxialParameters.axes` of any scale centred on the same parameters, at the zero scaled vector.", "acceptance": "After the residual lands, `Study.residualWith` MUST give one vector over every enabled fitted run, run after run, each entry times the run's weight, the Mueller throughputs last, equal for a polarimeter study to `throughputResidualFor`'s; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a mixed study's residual holds every run's entries in study order, the Mueller throughputs last`, `a run's weight multiplies its entries, and a disabled run adds none` and `a polarimeter study's residual is the throughput residual of its observations`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a mixed study's residual holds every run's entries in study order, the Mueller throughputs last", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a run's weight multiplies its entries, and a disabled run adds none", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-RESIDUAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests.a polarimeter study's residual is the throughput residual of its observations", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyForwardTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyForwardTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-RESIDUAL"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.StudyForward.Study.residualWith", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/StudyForward.fs", "obligations": ["S112-STUDY-RESIDUAL"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S11.2 -- The forward model of an experiment and the study residual"}
